// ===== 元の問題バンク（クイズ用ベース）=====
const BANK = [
  {"d":"D1","q":"エージェントとワークフローの本質的な違いはどれか。","qEn":"What is the essential difference between an agent and a workflow?","o":["エージェントは経路を事前に固定し、ワークフローは経路を実行時に決定する","エージェントは経路を実行時に決定し、ワークフローは経路を事前に固定する","エージェントは単一のプロンプトで完結し、ワークフローは複数ステップに分割して処理する","エージェントとワークフローはどちらも経路を実行時にモデルが動的に決定する"],"oEn":["An agent fixes its path in advance; a workflow decides the path at runtime","An agent decides its path at runtime; a workflow fixes the path in advance","An agent is a single self-contained prompt; a workflow splits the work into multiple steps","Both agents and workflows have the model decide the path dynamically at runtime"],"a":1,"e":"ワークフローは定義済みコードパス、エージェントはモデルが手順とツールを動的に選ぶ。エージェントが経路を事前に固定するという説明は逆で、両者とも実行時にモデルが経路を決めるという説明も、ワークフローの定義に反する。","eEn":"A workflow is a predefined code path; an agent has the model dynamically choose steps and tools. Saying agents fix the path in advance is backwards, and claiming workflows also let the model choose the path at runtime contradicts their definition."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"エージェント ループの継続/終了を判断する標準的な手段はどれか。","qEn":"What is the standard way to decide whether an agent loop continues or ends?","o":["stop_reason（tool_use なら継続、end_turn なら終了）","role フィールド（assistant なら継続、user なら終了）","finish_reason（length なら継続、stop なら終了）","usage.output_tokens の値（0 なら継続、正の値があれば終了）"],"oEn":["stop_reason (tool_use = continue, end_turn = end)","role field (assistant = continue, user = end)","finish_reason (length = continue, stop = end)","usage.output_tokens value (0 = continue, positive = end)"],"a":0,"e":"自然言語で終了判定するのはアンチパターン。stop_reason で機械的に判断する。roleは発言者を示すだけで継続判断には使えず、finish_reasonはClaude APIの応答項目ではない。output_tokensの値も終了条件とは無関係である。","eEn":"Judging termination via natural language is an anti-pattern; decide mechanically via stop_reason. role only identifies the speaker, finish_reason is not a field in Claude API responses, and output_tokens says nothing about whether the loop should end."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"サブエージェントを使う主な利点はどれか。","qEn":"What is the main benefit of using subagents?","o":["コンテキストの分離と専門タスクへの特化","親コンテキストの完全な共有と履歴の一元管理","モデル呼び出し回数の削減とトークン課金の一括化","推論速度の向上と応答レイテンシの短縮"],"oEn":["Context isolation and specialization for focused tasks","Full sharing of the parent context and unified history management","Fewer model calls and consolidated token billing","Faster inference and reduced response latency"],"a":0,"e":"各サブエージェントが独立した窓を持ち、親の文脈を汚染しない。探索的調査に有効。親の文脈を完全に共有すると分離の利点が失われ、呼び出し回数もサブエージェントを増やすほど増えるため、削減にはならない。","eEn":"Each subagent has its own window and does not pollute the parent context; useful for exploratory research. Fully sharing the parent's context would remove the isolation benefit, and more subagents means more model calls, not fewer."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"サブエージェントへ文脈を渡す正しい方法はどれか。","qEn":"What is the correct way to pass context to a subagent?","o":["共有メモリ領域に書き込み参照させる","親エージェントのシステムプロンプトを継承させる","会話履歴のIDを渡して自動で復元させる","プロンプトに必要な文脈を明示的に含める"],"oEn":["Have it read from a shared memory region","Let it inherit the parent agent's full system prompt and history","Pass a conversation ID and have it auto-restore","Explicitly include the needed context in the prompt"],"a":3,"e":"サブエージェントは隔離文脈を持ち親履歴を自動継承しない。明示的な受け渡しが必要。文脈が隔離されているため、共有メモリや履歴IDによる自動復元、システムプロンプトの継承に頼っても、必要な文脈は渡らない。","eEn":"Subagents have isolated context and do not auto-inherit parent history; explicit passing is required. Because a subagent's context is isolated, relying on shared memory, history IDs for auto-restore, or an inherited system prompt does not deliver the needed context."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"サブタスク数が入力ごとに変わる複雑な処理に最適なパターンはどれか。","qEn":"Which pattern best fits complex processing where the number of subtasks varies per input?","o":["プロンプトチェイニング","ルーティング（分類振り分け）","評価者・最適化者ループ","オーケストレーター・ワーカー"],"oEn":["Prompt chaining","Routing (classify)","Evaluator-Optimizer","Orchestrator-Workers"],"a":3,"e":"サブタスク数が事前に決まらない場合、オーケストレーターが動的に分割・統合する。プロンプトチェイニングは手順が固定された逐次処理、ルーティングは入力を分類して専門の処理へ振り分けるだけで、いずれもサブタスク数を動的に決めない。","eEn":"When the subtask count isn't fixed in advance, an orchestrator dynamically splits and integrates. Prompt chaining is a fixed sequence and routing only classifies input to a specialist path; neither decides the number of subtasks dynamically."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"不可逆・高リスクな操作に対する最も有効な安全設計はどれか。","qEn":"What is the most effective safety design for irreversible, high-risk operations?","o":["サンドボックス内でドライラン実行に限定する","操作前後に自動スナップショットを取得する","ヒューマン・イン・ザ・ループ（承認ステップ）","リトライ回数を増やして操作の冪等性を確保する"],"oEn":["Restrict to dry-run execution inside a sandbox","Take automatic snapshots around the operation","Human-in-the-loop (an approval step)","Increase retries to ensure operation idempotency"],"a":2,"e":"送金やファイル削除など影響の大きい操作の前に人の承認を挟む。ドライランやスナップショットは実行の可否を人に委ねず、送金のような外部への影響は元に戻せない。リトライや冪等性は重複を防ぐだけである。","eEn":"Insert human approval before high-impact operations like transfers or file deletion. Dry runs and snapshots do not hand the go/no-go decision to a person, and external effects like transfers cannot be undone; retries and idempotency only prevent duplicates."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"解けないタスクでループが暴走しコストが急増した。最初に追加すべきものはどれか。","qEn":"A loop ran away on an unsolvable task and costs spiked. What should you add first?","o":["温度を下げて出力の一貫性を高める設定変更","停止条件（最大反復回数・トークン上限・タイムアウト）","出力を逐次要約するサブエージェントの導入","各ツールへの詳細な説明文と入力スキーマ検証の追加"],"oEn":["Lower the temperature to make the outputs more consistent","Stopping conditions (max iterations, token cap, timeout)","Introduce a subagent that incrementally summarizes the output","More detailed tool descriptions and strict input-schema validation"],"a":1,"e":"無限ループ防止には完了・反復上限・タイムアウトのいずれかで確実に停止させる。温度を下げても、要約サブエージェントやスキーマ検証を足しても、ループ自体は終わらない。コスト急増の根本は停止条件の欠如である。","eEn":"To prevent infinite loops, stop reliably via completion, an iteration cap, or a timeout. Lowering temperature, adding a summarizing subagent, or adding schema validation does not end the loop; the root cause is the missing stop condition."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"評価者・最適化者パターンが適するのはどれか。","qEn":"When is the Evaluator-Optimizer pattern appropriate?","o":["サブタスクが互いに独立し完全並列で実行できるタスク","明確な評価基準があり反復で品質が向上するタスク","入力ごとに必要な手順数が動的に変わるタスク","一度の生成で確定し検証が不要な低リスクタスク"],"oEn":["Tasks whose subtasks are mutually independent and can run fully in parallel","Tasks with clear evaluation criteria where iteration improves quality","Tasks where the number of required steps varies per input","Low-risk tasks settled in one pass that need no verification"],"a":1,"e":"生成と評価を分離し反復改善する。翻訳の精緻化や複雑な検索が典型。互いに独立したサブタスクの並列実行は並列化、手順数が動的に変わるタスクはオーケストレーター・ワーカーの領域であり、一度で確定するタスクには反復が不要である。","eEn":"Separate generation and evaluation to iterate; typical for refining translations or complex search. Independent parallel subtasks fit parallelization, tasks with a dynamic number of steps fit orchestrator-workers, and one-shot tasks need no iteration."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"ハブ＆スポーク型のオーケストレーションの特徴はどれか。","qEn":"What characterizes hub-and-spoke orchestration?","o":["ワーカーが隣接ノードへ結果を順に受け渡す","調整役を持たず各エージェントが自律的に動く","各ワーカーが対等に協調し合意で意思決定する","調整役が全通信を仲介し分解・委譲・統合を担う"],"oEn":["Each worker passes its results sequentially to the adjacent node in a chain","There is no coordinator; each agent acts autonomously and independently","All workers cooperate as equals and proceed purely by consensus-based decision-making","A coordinator mediates all communication and handles split, delegate, integrate"],"a":3,"e":"中央の調整役がタスクを分解し各ワーカーへ委譲、結果を統合する。隣接ノードへ順に渡すのはパイプライン型、調整役を置かずに自律や合意で動くのはピア型で、ハブ＆スポークの中央仲介とは異なる。","eEn":"A central coordinator splits the task, delegates to workers, and integrates the results. Passing results to adjacent nodes is a pipeline, and agents acting autonomously or by consensus without a coordinator is peer-to-peer; neither is hub-and-spoke."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"PostToolUseフックの典型的な用途はどれか。","qEn":"What is a typical use of a PostToolUse hook?","o":["ユーザーがプロンプトを送信した時点で入力を検査する","ツール結果を処理前に正規化・変換する","ツール呼び出し前に引数を検証する","ツールの実行可否をポリシーで判定する"],"oEn":["Inspect the user's input at the moment a prompt is submitted","Normalize/transform tool results before processing","Validate the arguments before the tool is called","Decide whether a tool may run based on policy"],"a":1,"e":"Unix時刻やISO 8601、数値コードの統一などデータ正規化に使う。引数の検証や実行可否の判定は、ツール実行前に動くPreToolUseの役割である。プロンプト送信時の入力検査はUserPromptSubmitが担う。","eEn":"Used for data normalization such as unifying Unix time, ISO 8601, or numeric codes. Validating arguments and deciding whether a tool may run belong to PreToolUse, which fires before the tool runs; inspecting input when a prompt is submitted is UserPromptSubmit's job."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"前提ゲート（強制）の例として正しいものはどれか。","qEn":"Which is a correct example of a prerequisite gate (enforcement)?","o":["顧客識別が完了するまでprocess_refundを遮断する","残高照会を先に行うよう、プロンプトでモデルに依頼する","在庫確認を先に済ませる手順を、システムプロンプトに詳しく書いて促す","認証の確認を忘れないよう、応答の末尾で毎回注意を促す"],"oEn":["Block process_refund until customer identification completes","Ask the model in the prompt to run the balance inquiry first","Describe in detail in the system prompt that the stock check should come first","Remind the model at the end of every response not to forget the auth check"],"a":0,"e":"プログラム的強制により、前段完了まで後段操作を確実にブロックする。プロンプトでの依頼や、システムプロンプトへの手順の記述、注意喚起は、モデルが従うことを期待する誘導にすぎず、手順が飛ばされる確率をゼロにできない。","eEn":"Programmatic enforcement reliably blocks later operations until earlier steps complete. Asking in the prompt, writing the procedure into the system prompt, or adding reminders only guides the model and cannot reduce the chance of a skipped step to zero."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"ReActパターンの特徴はどれか。","qEn":"What characterizes the ReAct pattern?","o":["全ての行動手順を事前に詳細計画し一括で順に実行する","推論と行動を交互に行い思考を言語化しながらツールを使う","推論過程を内部に隠し最終結果だけを出力する","複数の思考経路を並列に展開し多数決で選ぶ"],"oEn":["Plan all action steps in advance and execute them in one batch","Alternate reasoning and acting, verbalizing thought while using tools","Hide the reasoning internally and output only the final result","Expand multiple reasoning paths in parallel and pick by majority vote"],"a":1,"e":"「考える→行動する→観測する」を繰り返し複雑タスクの精度を上げる。事前に全手順を計画して一括実行するのはPlan-and-Execute型、複数の思考経路を並列に展開して多数決で選ぶのはSelf-Consistency型で、推論と行動を交互に繰り返すReActとは異なる。","eEn":"Repeat think → act → observe to improve accuracy on complex tasks. Planning every step upfront and executing in one pass is plan-and-execute, and exploring parallel reasoning paths with majority voting is self-consistency; neither alternates reasoning and acting like ReAct."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"エージェントのコスト増大の主因はどれか。","qEn":"What is the main cause of rising agent cost?","o":["ツール定義のJSONスキーマを毎回添付すること","システムプロンプトを毎回わずかに書き換える処理","ループ反復ごとに蓄積するコンテキストの再送信","応答を待つ間のネットワーク遅延の累積"],"oEn":["Attaching the tools' JSON schema on every request","Slightly rewriting the entire system prompt on every single turn","Re-sending context that accumulates each loop iteration","Accumulated network latency while awaiting responses"],"a":2,"e":"各ターンで履歴全体を送るため入力トークンが累積。キャッシュや圧縮で緩和。ツール定義は毎回同じ大きさで蓄積せず、ネットワーク遅延は待ち時間に影響しても課金には影響しない。主因は反復ごとに膨らむ履歴である。","eEn":"Sending the whole history each turn accumulates input tokens; mitigate with caching or compaction. Tool definitions stay the same size each turn rather than accumulating, and network latency affects wait time, not billing; the main driver is the history that grows with every iteration."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"権限最小化（Least Privilege）原則とは。","qEn":"What is the principle of least privilege?","o":["タスク遂行に必要な最小限の権限のみ付与する","役割ごとに標準化した権限セットを一律に付与する","利用頻度の高い権限を既定で有効にしておく","将来必要になり得る権限をまとめて先に付与する"],"oEn":["Grant only the minimum permissions needed to do the task","Grant a standardized permission set uniformly per role","Enable frequently used permissions by default","Grant upfront any permissions that might be needed later"],"a":0,"e":"過剰権限は事故時の被害を拡大する。読み取りで足りるなら書き込みを与えない。役割ごとの権限セットの一律付与、利用頻度の高い権限の既定有効化、将来分の先行付与は、いずれも必要なものだけに絞る原則に反して過剰権限を生む。","eEn":"Excess permissions widen the damage when accidents happen; if read suffices, don't grant write. Uniform role-based sets, enabling frequently used permissions by default, and granting future permissions up front all create excess permissions, against the principle of granting only what is needed."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【まとめ】D1の設計判断で一貫して問われる軸はどれか。","qEn":"[Summary] What axis is consistently asked about in D1 design decisions?","o":["プログラム的に固定すべきか、モデルに委ねるべきか","単一エージェントで担うか複数エージェントで分担するか","同期的に処理するか非同期的に処理するか","オープンソースか商用モデルを採用するか"],"oEn":["Whether to fix it in code or delegate to the model","Whether to handle it with one agent or split across several agents","Whether to process synchronously or asynchronously","Whether to adopt an open-source or a commercial model"],"a":0,"e":"予測可能性が要る部分はコードで固定、柔軟性が要る部分のみモデルへ委ねる。単一か複数のエージェントか、同期か非同期か、オープンソースか商用かは個別の論点で、設計判断を貫く軸ではない。","eEn":"Fix in code where predictability is needed; delegate to the model only where flexibility is needed. Single versus multiple agents, sync versus async, and open-source versus commercial models are separate topics, not the axis running through design decisions."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ツール選択の主たる根拠となるのはどれか。","qEn":"What is the main basis for tool selection?","o":["戻り値の例示","登録された順番","引数の型定義","ツールの説明文"],"oEn":["The tool's return examples","The tool's registration order","The tool's argument types","The tool's description"],"a":3,"e":"名前・説明・パラメータ記述はプロンプトと同じ重み。説明の質が使用精度を決める。登録順や戻り値の例は選択の根拠にならず、引数の型定義は呼び出し方を決めるもので、どのツールを選ぶかは説明文から判断される。","eEn":"Name, description, and parameter docs carry the same weight as a prompt; description quality drives accuracy. Registration order and return-value examples are not the basis for selection; argument types govern how to call a tool, while the choice of tool comes from its description."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"MCP（Model Context Protocol）が解決する課題はどれか。","qEn":"What problem does MCP (Model Context Protocol) solve?","o":["ツール呼び出し時のトークン超過エラー","エージェント間の権限昇格リスクの管理","モデルごとのプロンプト形式の非互換性","ツール連携の個別実装が乱立するN×M問題"],"oEn":["Frequent token-overflow errors that occur during tool calls","Managing privilege-escalation risk between agents","The incompatibility of prompt formats that differ from model to model","The N×M problem of proliferating per-integration implementations"],"a":3,"e":"共通プロトコルで一度作ったサーバーを複数クライアントで再利用できる。トークン超過や権限昇格、モデルごとのプロンプト形式の違いは、MCPが標準化の対象とするツール連携の接続方式とは別の課題である。","eEn":"A common protocol lets a server built once be reused across multiple clients. Token overflow, privilege escalation, and per-model prompt formats are different problems from the tool-integration connection method that MCP standardizes."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"MCP（Model Context Protocol）が公開する3つの主要要素はどれか。","qEn":"What are the three main elements MCP (Model Context Protocol) exposes?","o":["ツール・リソース・プロンプト","リソース・セッション・ログ","ツール・メモリ・エージェント","プロンプト・スキーマ・キャッシュ"],"oEn":["Tools, resources, prompts","Resources, sessions, logs","Tools, memory, agents","Prompts, schemas, caches"],"a":0,"e":"ツールは実行操作、リソースは参照データ、プロンプトは定型テンプレート。セッション、ログ、メモリ、エージェント、スキーマ、キャッシュは、MCPサーバーが公開する3要素には含まれない。","eEn":"Tools are executable operations, resources are reference data, prompts are reusable templates. Sessions, logs, memory, agents, schemas, and caches are not among the three elements an MCP server exposes."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ローカルの社内DBにClaude Codeから接続する最適なトランスポートはどれか。","qEn":"What is the best transport to connect Claude Code to a local internal DB?","o":["gRPC（遠隔呼び出し）","WebSocket（双方向）","HTTP/SSE（サーバー送信）","stdio（標準入出力）"],"oEn":["gRPC (remote call)","WebSocket (bidirectional)","HTTP/SSE (server-sent)","stdio (standard I/O)"],"a":3,"e":"同一マシン上の連携にはstdioが単純・高速。攻撃面も狭い。gRPCとWebSocketはMCPの標準トランスポートではなく、HTTP/SSEはリモートサーバー向けで、同一マシンではポートの待ち受けが余計に必要になる（2026年10月時点）。","eEn":"For same-machine integration, stdio is simple, fast, and has a narrow attack surface. gRPC and WebSocket are not standard MCP transports, and HTTP/SSE targets remote servers, requiring extra listening ports on a single machine (as of October 2026)."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ツールのエラーをモデルに返す利点はどれか。","qEn":"What is the benefit of returning tool errors to the model?","o":["後続の全処理を安全に中断し状態保存できる","エラー内容をユーザーに即座に通知できる","モデルが原因を理解し自己修正・再試行できる","失敗したツールを自動的に無効化できる"],"oEn":["All downstream processing can be halted and state saved","The error can be reported to the user immediately","The model understands the cause and can self-correct or retry","The failing tool can be disabled automatically"],"a":2,"e":"例外で即停止せず構造化エラーを返すと、引数修正や再試行を促せる。処理の全中断や失敗したツールの自動無効化は、モデルに修正の機会を与えない。ユーザーへの即時通知も自己修正にはつながらない。","eEn":"Returning a structured error instead of halting lets the model fix arguments and retry. Halting everything or auto-disabling the failed tool gives the model no chance to correct itself, and notifying the user does not by itself enable self-correction."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"MCP（Model Context Protocol）エラーのerrorCategoryに含まれる分類はどれか。","qEn":"Which classifications are part of MCP (Model Context Protocol) errorCategory?","o":["transient / validation / permission","fatal / recoverable / ignorable / deferred","syntax / runtime / semantic","network / timeout / retryable"],"oEn":["transient / validation / permission","fatal / recoverable / ignorable / deferred","syntax / runtime / semantic","network / timeout / retryable"],"a":0,"e":"一時的・検証・権限などに分類し、isRetryableで再試行可否を示す。retryableは分類ではなくisRetryableで示す再試行可否の情報であり、networkやtimeoutは一時的エラーの原因にすぎない。","eEn":"Classified as transient/validation/permission, with isRetryable indicating retry eligibility. retryable is not a category but the retry eligibility carried by isRetryable, and network or timeout are merely causes of a transient error."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"tool_choiceの「any」の挙動はどれか。","qEn":"What is the behavior of tool_choice 'any'?","o":["モデルが判断し必要なら呼ぶ","必ずいずれかのツールを呼ぶ","複数ツールを同時に必ず呼ぶ","呼ぶ前に必ず確認を求める"],"oEn":["The model decides and calls if needed","Always calls one of the tools","Always calls multiple tools at once","Asks for confirmation before any call"],"a":1,"e":"autoはテキストも返す、anyは必ずツール、強制は特定ツールを名指し。モデルの判断で必要なときだけ呼ぶのはautoの挙動で、anyは複数ツールの同時呼び出しや事前確認を求めるものではない。","eEn":"auto may return text, any always calls a tool, forced names a specific tool. Calling a tool only when the model deems it necessary is the behavior of auto; any neither forces multiple simultaneous calls nor asks for confirmation first."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"プロジェクトレベルのMCP（Model Context Protocol）設定ファイルはどれか。","qEn":"Which is the project-level MCP (Model Context Protocol) config file?","o":["./.mcp.json","./mcp.config.js","./mcp.yaml","./.mcprc.json"],"oEn":["<project>/.mcp.json","./mcp.config.js","./mcp.yaml","./.mcprc.json"],"a":0,"e":".mcp.jsonはバージョン管理でチーム共有。~/.claude.jsonは個人・実験用。mcp.config.js、mcp.yaml、.mcprc.jsonは、Claude Codeがプロジェクト設定として読み込むMCP設定ファイル名ではない（2026年10月時点）。","eEn":".mcp.json is version-controlled for team sharing; ~/.claude.json is for personal/experimental use. mcp.config.js, mcp.yaml, and .mcprc.json are not file names Claude Code reads as project-level MCP configuration (as of October 2026)."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"MCP（Model Context Protocol）サーバーの認証情報の正しい扱いはどれか。","qEn":"What is the correct handling of MCP (Model Context Protocol) server credentials?","o":[".mcp.json にトークンを直接書いてリポジトリで共有する","トークンをシステムプロンプトに埋め込んでモデルに渡す","起動フラグ --token で毎回コマンド渡しする","環境変数展開（${GITHUB_TOKEN}等）を使う"],"oEn":["Write the token directly into .mcp.json and share it via the repository","Embed the token in the system prompt and pass it to the model","Pass them each time via a --token launch flag","Use env-var expansion (e.g. ${GITHUB_TOKEN})"],"a":3,"e":"秘密を埋め込まず環境変数で扱う。漏えいは重大リスク。.mcp.jsonに直書きするとリポジトリ経由で漏れ、システムプロンプトに入れると会話ログや出力に露出する。起動フラグで渡すとシェルの履歴やプロセス一覧に残る。","eEn":"Don't embed secrets; handle them via environment variables. Leakage is a serious risk. Hard-coding the token in .mcp.json leaks it through the repository, and putting it in the system prompt exposes it in conversation logs and outputs. Passing it as a launch flag leaves it in shell history and process listings."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"組み込みツールGrepとGlobの違いはどれか。","qEn":"What is the difference between the built-in Grep and Glob tools?","o":["Grepはファイル名検索、Globは全文検索","Grepは内容検索、Globはパスパターン一致","Grepは正規表現置換、Globはディレクトリ作成","Grepはパス一致、Globは内容検索"],"oEn":["Grep searches filenames; Glob does full-text search","Grep searches file content; Glob matches path patterns","Grep replaces via regex; Glob creates directories","Grep matches paths; Glob searches content"],"a":1,"e":"Grepは中身を探す、Globは名前で探す。Grepがファイル名検索でGlobが全文検索という説明は逆で、Globにディレクトリ作成の機能はなく、Grepは置換も行わない。","eEn":"Grep finds by content; Glob finds by name. Describing Grep as filename search and Glob as full-text search is backwards; Glob cannot create directories and Grep does not perform replacement."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"認証と認可の正しい区別はどれか。","qEn":"What is the correct distinction between authentication and authorization?","o":["認証はセッション管理、認可はログ記録","認証はトークン発行、認可はトークン失効","認証は暗号化、認可は復号処理のこと","認証は本人確認、認可は権限確認"],"oEn":["Authn manages user sessions; authz records access logs","Authn issues tokens; authz revokes tokens","Authn is encryption; authz is decryption","Authn checks identity; authz checks permission"],"a":3,"e":"認証=誰か、認可=何ができるか。両者を区別して設計する。セッション管理やログ記録、トークンの発行や失効、暗号化や復号は、本人確認と権限確認の区別を表す定義ではない。","eEn":"Authentication = who you are; authorization = what you can do. Design them separately. Session management and logging, token issuance and revocation, and encryption and decryption do not define the distinction between identity verification and permission checks."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ツールが18個ある場合と4-5個の場合の違いはどれか。","qEn":"What differs between having 18 tools versus 4-5 tools?","o":["個数は選択精度に影響しない","多いほど選択信頼性が低下する","多いほど応答速度が向上する","少ないほど誤呼び出しが増える"],"oEn":["Tool count does not affect selection accuracy","More tools lower selection reliability","More tools improve response speed","Fewer tools cause more misfires"],"a":1,"e":"役割が重複するツールはモデルを迷わせる。明確で少数のツールが精度を高める。個数は選択精度に影響し、多いほど応答速度が上がるわけでもない。少数の明確なツールのほうが誤呼び出しは減る。","eEn":"Overlapping tools confuse the model; few, clear tools improve accuracy. Tool count does affect selection accuracy, more tools do not speed up responses, and a few clear tools reduce mistaken calls rather than increase them."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【まとめ】D2が一貫して問う設計原則はどれか。","qEn":"[Summary] What design principle does D2 consistently ask about?","o":["広い権限・柔軟な定義・自由な出力","最小権限・明確な定義・構造化結果","高速化・並列化・キャッシュ活用","多数のツール・詳細なログ・冗長化"],"oEn":["Broad permissions, flexible definitions, free output","Least privilege, clear definitions, structured results","Speedup, parallelization, cache utilization","Many tools, highly detailed logging, and redundancy"],"a":1,"e":"権限を絞り、定義を明確にし、結果を構造化する。三者が堅牢な連携の基盤。広い権限や自由な出力は逆の方向で、高速化・並列化・キャッシュや多数のツール・詳細なログ・冗長化は、連携設計の原則とは別の論点である。","eEn":"Limit permissions, clarify definitions, structure results—these three underpin robust integration. Broad permissions and free-form output run in the opposite direction, while speed, parallelism, caching, many tools, detailed logs, and redundancy are separate concerns from integration design principles."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"CLAUDE.mdの役割はどれか。","qEn":"What is the role of CLAUDE.md?","o":["実行時に動的読み込みするツール定義のカタログファイル","会話ごとに自動生成される一時的なキャッシュ","プロジェクト固有の指示・規約を常時与えるメモリ","モデルの応答例を蓄積する学習用データセット"],"oEn":["A catalog file listing tool definitions loaded dynamically at runtime","A temporary cache that is auto-generated for each new conversation","A memory that always supplies project-specific instructions and conventions","A training dataset that accumulates the model's response examples"],"a":2,"e":"ビルド手順や規約を記述し、各セッションで自動的に読み込まれる。ツール定義のカタログや一時キャッシュ、学習用データセットではなく、プロジェクトの指示を毎回与えるための記述ファイルである。","eEn":"It records build steps and conventions and is loaded automatically each session. It is not a tool-definition catalog, a temporary cache, or a training dataset; it is a file that supplies project instructions every session."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"CLAUDE.md設定階層の正しい並びはどれか。","qEn":"What is the correct order of the CLAUDE.md config hierarchy?","o":["組織・リポジトリ・ブランチ設定","システム・チーム・個人プロファイル","グローバル・ローカル・一時設定","ユーザー・プロジェクト・ディレクトリ"],"oEn":["Org, repository, branch settings","System, team, personal profile","Global, local, temporary session","User, project, directory"],"a":3,"e":"ユーザーは個人専用、プロジェクトはチーム共有、ディレクトリは局所規約。CLAUDE.mdにはブランチ単位や一時セッション単位の階層はなく、読み込み位置で決まるのはユーザー・プロジェクト・ディレクトリの3層である。","eEn":"User is personal, project is team-shared, directory is local convention. CLAUDE.md has no branch-level or temporary-session tier; its three levels are determined by where the file is loaded from: user, project, and directory."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"フックとスラッシュコマンドの違いはどれか。","qEn":"What is the difference between hooks and slash commands?","o":["フックはUI描画用、スラッシュコマンドはAPI呼び出し用","フックは自動発火、スラッシュコマンドは手動呼び出し","フックは手動登録、スラッシュコマンドは自動検出される","フックは同期実行、スラッシュコマンドは非同期実行"],"oEn":["Hooks render the UI; slash commands call APIs","Hooks auto-fire; slash commands are invoked manually","Hooks are registered manually; slash commands are auto-detected","Hooks run synchronously; slash commands run asynchronously"],"a":1,"e":"フックはイベント駆動で確実に走り、コマンドは利用者が明示的に起動する。フックはUI描画用ではなく、スラッシュコマンドもAPI呼び出し用ではない。手動と自動を入れ替えた説明は逆で、同期・非同期が両者を分ける違いでもない。","eEn":"Hooks run reliably on events; commands are explicitly invoked by the user. Hooks are not UI rendering and slash commands are not API calls; swapping manual and automatic reverses the real relationship, and sync versus async does not separate them."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"大規模なアーキテクチャ変更に適すモードはどれか。","qEn":"Which mode suits large architectural changes?","o":["プラン モード","対話チャット","オート編集","ヘッドレス実行"],"oEn":["Plan mode","Chat mode","Auto-edit","Headless"],"a":0,"e":"プランモードで変更前に探索・設計し手戻りを防ぐ。オート編集は設計の前に変更へ進むため大規模変更では手戻りが出やすく、ヘッドレス実行は人の介在なしに走らせる用途である。","eEn":"Plan mode lets you explore and design before changing, avoiding rework. Auto-edit proceeds to changes before design, causing rework on large changes, and headless execution is meant for running without human involvement."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"ヘッドレスモードがCI/CDに適する理由はどれか。","qEn":"Why is headless mode suited to CI/CD?","o":["リッチなUIでログを可視化できる","GPUを占有して並列処理を高速化できる","人の介在なしにコマンドとして実行できる","対話プロンプトを逐次表示して確認できる"],"oEn":["It visualizes logs and output in a rich interactive UI","It monopolizes the GPU to speed up parallel processing","It runs as a command without human intervention","It can display interactive prompts step by step for confirmation"],"a":2,"e":"プルリクの自動レビューやコード生成をパイプラインに組み込める。リッチなUIや対話プロンプトの逐次表示は人が操作する前提の機能で、GPUの占有による並列化もCI/CDに適する理由ではない。","eEn":"It embeds automated PR review and code generation into the pipeline. A rich UI and step-by-step interactive prompts assume a human operator, and GPU-based parallelism is not why it suits CI/CD."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"スキルとCLAUDE.mdの違いはどれか。","qEn":"What is the difference between a Skill and CLAUDE.md?","o":["スキルはオンデマンド呼び出し、CLAUDE.mdは常時読み込み","スキルはグローバル固定、CLAUDE.mdはセッション限定","スキルは自動発火、CLAUDE.mdは手動でのみ有効化される","スキルは常時読み込み、CLAUDE.mdはオンデマンド呼び出し"],"oEn":["A Skill is invoked on demand; CLAUDE.md is always loaded","A Skill is globally fixed; CLAUDE.md is session-scoped","A Skill auto-fires; CLAUDE.md is enabled only manually","A Skill is always loaded; CLAUDE.md is invoked on demand"],"a":0,"e":"スキルはタスク特化ワークフローを必要時に呼ぶ。CLAUDE.mdは普遍的標準。CLAUDE.mdは手動でのみ有効になるものでもセッション限定でもなく、各セッションで自動的に読み込まれる。常時読み込みとオンデマンドを入れ替えた説明も逆である。","eEn":"A Skill calls a task-specific workflow when needed; CLAUDE.md is the universal standard. CLAUDE.md is not manual-only or session-limited; it loads automatically each session, and swapping always-loaded with on-demand is backwards."},
  {"d":"D3","q":".claude/rules のパススコープの仕組みはどれか。","qEn":"How does the path scope of .claude/rules work?","o":["ファイル拡張子の自動判定で読み込み","ディレクトリ深さの閾値で読み込み","YAMLのpathsグロブで条件読み込み","gitignore と同じ除外規則で読み込み"],"oEn":["Loading by automatic file-extension detection","Loading by a directory-depth threshold","Conditional loading via YAML paths globs","Loading by the same exclusion rules as gitignore"],"a":2,"e":"型別に全域へ適用できる。場所でなく型で適用。拡張子の自動判定やディレクトリ深さの閾値、gitignoreの除外規則では読み込み条件を決められず、条件はYAMLのpathsに書いたグロブで指定する。","eEn":"Apply by type across the codebase—by type, not by location. Auto-detecting extensions, directory-depth thresholds, or gitignore-style exclusion rules cannot set the load condition; it is specified with globs in the YAML paths field."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"SKILL.mdのcontext: forkの意味はどれか。","qEn":"What does context: fork in SKILL.md mean?","o":["親文脈をそのまま引き継いで実行する","隔離されたサブ文脈で実行する","複数プロセスに分岐して並列実行する","実行結果を親に自動マージする"],"oEn":["Run inheriting the parent context as-is","Run in an isolated sub-context","Fork into processes and run in parallel","Auto-merge the results back into the parent"],"a":1,"e":"隔離文脈で実行し、allowed-toolsでツール制限、argument-hintで引数を促す。親文脈をそのまま引き継ぐ実行は逆の挙動で、複数プロセスへ分岐して並列実行する意味でもない。","eEn":"Runs in isolated context; allowed-tools limits tools and argument-hint prompts for arguments. Inheriting the parent context as-is is the opposite behavior, and it does not mean branching into multiple processes for parallel execution."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"権限の推奨許可方針はどれか。","qEn":"What is the recommended permission-granting policy?","o":["全操作を実行前に一律で承認フローに回す","読み取りは狭く、書き込みは広く、破壊的は自動許可","読み取りは広く、書き込みは狭く、破壊的は承認必須","頻度の高い操作から順に権限を緩めていく"],"oEn":["Route every operation through a uniform pre-approval flow","Read narrowly, write broadly, destructive auto-allowed","Read broadly, write narrowly, destructive requires approval","Loosen permissions starting from frequent operations"],"a":2,"e":"リスクの非対称性に応じて配分する。調査は安全だが変更は事故を生む。全操作を一律に承認へ回すと低リスクの調査まで止まり、破壊的操作を自動許可にするのは危険である。頻度だけで権限を緩める基準もリスクを見ていない。","eEn":"Allocate by risk asymmetry: investigation is safe, but changes cause incidents. Routing every operation to approval stalls even low-risk investigation, auto-allowing destructive operations is dangerous, and loosening by frequency alone ignores risk."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"カスタム スラッシュ コマンドの定義方法はどれか。","qEn":"How do you define a custom slash command?","o":["設定ファイルにコマンド名と本文をJSONで登録する","専用のPythonスクリプトを実装し関数をコマンドとして公開する","コマンド用ディレクトリにMarkdownファイルを置く","起動時フラグでコマンド定義のパスを指定する"],"oEn":["Register the command name and body as JSON in a config file","Implement a dedicated Python script exposing it as a command","Place a Markdown file in the commands directory","Specify the path to the command definition via a launch flag"],"a":2,"e":"ファイル名がコマンド名、本文がプロンプト。$ARGUMENTS等で引数も使える。JSONでの登録やPythonスクリプトの実装、起動フラグでのパス指定は、カスタムコマンドの定義方法ではない（2026年10月時点）。","eEn":"The filename is the command name and the body is the prompt; arguments work via $ARGUMENTS, etc. Registering in JSON, writing a Python script, or passing a path via a startup flag is not how custom commands are defined (as of October 2026)."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"非対話モードで構造化出力を得るオプションはどれか。","qEn":"Which option gets structured output in non-interactive mode?","o":["--format=text --pretty-print","--stream --raw / --no-color","--structured --emit yaml / --schema-file","--output-format json / --json-schema"],"oEn":["--format=text --pretty-print","--stream --raw / --no-color","--structured --emit yaml / --schema","--output-format json / --json-schema"],"a":3,"e":"-p/--printで非対話実行し、JSON出力やスキーマ強制でスクリプト連携する。--format=text --pretty-print、--structured --emit yaml、--stream --rawは、Claude Codeに存在する構造化出力のオプションではない（2026年10月時点）。","eEn":"Run non-interactively with -p/--print and integrate via JSON output or schema enforcement. --format=text --pretty-print, --structured --emit yaml, and --stream --raw are not Claude Code options for structured output (as of October 2026)."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"テスト駆動開発（TDD）をClaude Codeで行う流れはどれか。","qEn":"What is the flow for doing TDD with Claude Code?","o":["コードを生成後に網羅的なテストを追加させる","先に詳細な設計書を書かせ、それを実装コードへ自動変換させる","実装とテストを一度のプロンプトで同時生成させる","先にテストを書かせ、それを満たすコードを生成させる"],"oEn":["Generate the code first, then add exhaustive tests afterward","Write a design doc first, then auto-convert it into implementation code","Generate the implementation and tests together in a single prompt","Write tests first, then generate code that satisfies them"],"a":3,"e":"失敗するテストを基準に進める。テストが客観的な完了条件になる。コード生成後にテストを足す流れや、実装とテストの同時生成、設計書の自動変換は、先に失敗するテストを基準に据えるTDDの順序ではない。","eEn":"Proceed against failing tests; the tests become an objective completion criterion. Adding tests after the code, generating code and tests together, or converting a design document automatically are not the TDD order, which starts from a failing test as the yardstick."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"settings.jsonの役割はどれか。","qEn":"What is the role of settings.json?","o":["実行時のトークン使用量を計測する設定","モデルの重みとハイパーパラメータを定義する","権限・フック・環境設定をファイルで管理する","会話履歴とツール出力を保存する記録専用ファイル"],"oEn":["A setting that measures runtime token consumption","Define the model's weights and hyperparameters at load time","Manage permissions, hooks, and environment settings via a file","A file for storing conversation history and tool outputs"],"a":2,"e":"プロジェクト単位とユーザー単位で持て、共有設定と個人設定を分離できる。トークン使用量の計測、モデルの重みやハイパーパラメータの定義、会話履歴の保存は、settings.jsonの役割ではない。","eEn":"It can be held per project and per user, separating shared and personal settings. Measuring token usage, defining model weights and hyperparameters, and storing conversation history are not the role of settings.json."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【まとめ】D3が一貫して問う判断軸はどれか。","qEn":"[Summary] What decision axis does D3 consistently ask about?","o":["確実性が必要な処理も柔軟な処理も全てフックと権限で固定して完全に自動化する","確実性が要る処理はフックや権限で固定、柔軟性が要る処理はモデルに委ねる","処理の種類を問わず全ての判断をモデルに一任し設定を最小化する","コストが最も安いモデルを常に選ぶことだけを基準にする"],"oEn":["Fix both certainty-needing and flexible work entirely with hooks and permissions to fully automate","Fix certainty-needing work with hooks/permissions; delegate flexible work to the model","Delegate every decision to the model regardless of type and minimize configuration","Always pick the cheapest available model as the sole deciding criterion"],"a":1,"e":"CLAUDE.mdで文脈を、権限とフックでガードレールを与える配分が核心。全てをフックと権限で固定すると柔軟性を失い、全てをモデルに委ねると確実性を担保できない。コストの安さだけを基準にする選び方も、設計判断の軸にならない。","eEn":"The core is allocating context via CLAUDE.md and guardrails via permissions and hooks. Fixing everything with hooks and permissions loses flexibility, delegating everything to the model loses certainty, and choosing only the cheapest model is not a design axis."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"プロンプトで「明確さ」が最重要とされる理由はどれか。","qEn":"Why is clarity considered most important in prompting?","o":["曖昧な指示はモデルの解釈を分散させ精度を下げるから","明確な指示はモデルの学習データを更新できるから","詳細な指示はトークン消費を抑え応答速度を高めるから","曖昧な指示はコンテキスト窓を余分に消費するから"],"oEn":["Vague instructions scatter the model's interpretation and lower accuracy","Clear instructions let the model update its training data","Detailed instructions reduce token use and improve response speed","Vague instructions consume extra context window capacity"],"a":0,"e":"何を・どの形式で・どこまで求めるかを具体化し誤解の余地を消す。指示の明確さが学習データを更新することはなく、詳細な指示がトークン消費を抑えるわけでもない。曖昧さの問題は、余分な窓の消費ではなく解釈のばらつきである。","eEn":"Specify what, in what format, and how far, to eliminate room for misinterpretation. Clear instructions do not update the model's training data, detailed instructions do not reduce token use, and the problem with vagueness is divergent interpretation, not extra context-window use."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"一貫した出力を得る最有効な手段の一つはどれか。","qEn":"What is one of the most effective ways to get consistent output?","o":["長いコンテキストの投入","出力トークン数の上限拡大","少数例示（フューショット）","システムプロンプトの詳細化"],"oEn":["Long context input","Raise output token cap","Few-shot examples","Detailed system prompt"],"a":2,"e":"2-4例で選択理由を示し、曖昧ケースの判断を汎化させる。長いコンテキストの投入や出力トークン上限の拡大は出力の一貫性を直接高めず、システムプロンプトの詳細化は例示ほど判断基準を具体的に示せない。","eEn":"Show 2-4 examples with reasons to generalize judgment on ambiguous cases. Feeding long context or raising the output token cap does not directly make output consistent, and a more detailed system prompt shows decision criteria less concretely than examples."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"構文エラーを排し確実な構造化出力を得る方法はどれか。","qEn":"How do you eliminate syntax errors and get reliable structured output?","o":["temperatureを0に固定","tool_use＋JSONスキーマ","正規表現による出力の後処理抽出","プロンプト内でJSON形式の出力を依頼"],"oEn":["Fix temperature to zero","tool_use + JSON schema","Post-process output with regex","Ask for JSON in the prompt"],"a":1,"e":"スキーマで形式を強制すれば構文エラーが排除され確実。temperatureを0にしても、プロンプトでJSONを依頼しても、構文エラーは排除されない。正規表現による後処理抽出は崩れた出力を事後に拾うだけで確実性がない。","eEn":"Forcing the format via schema eliminates syntax errors and ensures reliability. Setting temperature to 0 or asking for JSON in the prompt does not eliminate syntax errors, and regex post-extraction only salvages broken output after the fact."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"値の捏造（幻覚）を防ぐスキーマ設計はどれか。","qEn":"Which schema design prevents fabricating values (hallucination)?","o":["列挙型で選択候補を限定する","説明文をフィールドに付与する","nullableフィールドを使う","既定値を全フィールドに設定する"],"oEn":["Limit choices with an enum","Add descriptions to fields","Use nullable fields","Set defaults on every field"],"a":2,"e":"値が無い場合にnullを許せば、無理に値を埋める捏造を防げる。列挙型の限定や説明文の付与は値の選び方を導くだけで、値が存在しない場合の逃げ道にならない。全フィールドへの既定値の設定は、かえって値を埋めてしまう。","eEn":"Allowing null when no value exists prevents forced fabrication of values. Restricting values with an enum or adding descriptions only guides value choice and gives no escape when the value is absent, and setting defaults on every field fills them in instead."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"拡張可能な分類を実現するenumの工夫はどれか。","qEn":"What enum technique enables extensible classification?","o":["自由記述のフィールドだけで分類を表現する","enumに全候補を事前列挙する","数値コードのみで分類を表現する","enum＋\"other\"＋detail"],"oEn":["Use only a free-text field","Pre-list all cases in the enum","Use numeric codes for classes","enum + \"other\" + detail"],"a":3,"e":"許可値に制限しつつotherで未知パターンに対応する。自由記述のみでは分類がばらつき、全候補の事前列挙は未知のパターンに対応できない。数値コードのみでは意味が読み取れず拡張も管理しにくい。","eEn":"Restrict to allowed values while handling unknown patterns via 'other'. Free text alone makes categories inconsistent, listing every candidate upfront cannot handle unknown patterns, and numeric codes alone hide meaning and are hard to extend."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"スキーマ検証で防げないものはどれか。","qEn":"What can schema validation NOT prevent?","o":["必須フィールドの欠落や列挙値の範囲外といった構造上の形式的な誤り","JSON構文の破綻や閉じ括弧の欠落による解析不能","文字列型のフィールドに数値が混入するような型違反","意味エラー（calculatedとstatedの不一致等）"],"oEn":["Missing required fields or out-of-range enum values","Broken JSON syntax or a missing closing brace that blocks parsing","Type violations like a number in a string field","Semantic errors (e.g. calculated vs stated mismatch)"],"a":3,"e":"スキーマは構文・型・必須は防げるが、意味的な矛盾は別途検証が必要。必須フィールドの欠落、列挙値の範囲外、JSON構文の破綻、型違反は、スキーマ検証で検出できるため防げないものには当たらない。","eEn":"Schemas catch syntax/type/required issues, but semantic contradictions need separate verification. Missing required fields, out-of-range enum values, broken JSON syntax, and type violations can all be caught by schema validation, so they are not what it fails to prevent."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"Message Batches APIの特徴はどれか。","qEn":"What characterizes the Message Batches API?","o":["即時応答で追加料金が発生する同期処理API","50%節約・最大24時間・SLA保証なし","常にリアルタイムのストリーミング配信","料金が2倍で優先処理される高速枠"],"oEn":["A synchronous API with instant response, premium pricing","50% savings, up to 24h, no SLA guarantee","Always real-time streaming delivery","A fast tier at double price with priority processing"],"a":1,"e":"夜間レポートや週次監査など待てる処理向け。リクエスト内マルチターンは不可。バッチは即時応答の同期処理でも常時のストリーミングでもなく、料金を2倍にして優先処理される枠でもない。","eEn":"For deferrable work like nightly reports or weekly audits; no multi-turn within a request. Batches are neither a synchronous API with immediate responses nor real-time streaming, nor a double-priced priority tier."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"肯定形の指示が推奨される理由はどれか。","qEn":"Why are positive (affirmative) instructions recommended?","o":["肯定形のほうが出力トークンを節約できるから","「するな」より「せよ」のほうが従いやすい","肯定形は禁止事項を書かずに済むから","否定形はモデルの推論速度を大きく下げるから"],"oEn":["Affirmative form saves output tokens","'Do' is easier to follow than 'don't'","Affirmative form avoids writing prohibitions","Negative form greatly slows the model's reasoning"],"a":1,"e":"否定形は解釈が不安定。望ましい行動を直接示す。肯定形が出力トークンを節約するわけでも、禁止事項を書かずに済むわけでもない。否定形が推論速度を大きく下げるという根拠もない。","eEn":"Negative forms are unstable to interpret; state the desired behavior directly. Positive phrasing does not save output tokens or remove the need to state prohibitions, and negative phrasing has no basis for greatly slowing inference."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"システム プロンプトの役割はどれか。","qEn":"What is the role of the system prompt?","o":["直近のユーザー発言だけに一時的な指示を与える","会話履歴を要約してトークンを節約する機能","モデルの役割・制約・基本方針を会話全体に設定する","ツールの一覧と各引数のスキーマを定義する"],"oEn":["Give a temporary instruction only to the most recent user message","Summarize the conversation history to conserve context tokens","Set the model's role, constraints, and policy for the whole conversation","Define the tool list and the schema of each tool argument"],"a":2,"e":"口調・専門性・禁止事項を定義。個別メッセージより上位の文脈として作用する。直近の発言だけへの一時的な指示や、履歴の要約によるトークン節約は別の仕組みで、ツールの一覧とスキーマはtoolsパラメータで定義する。","eEn":"It defines tone, expertise, and prohibitions, acting as context above individual messages. Temporary instructions for the latest message and token savings via history summaries are separate mechanisms, and tool lists and schemas are defined in the tools parameter."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"XMLタグをプロンプトで使う利点はどれか。","qEn":"What is the benefit of using XML tags in prompts?","o":["推論の途中経過をログに保存できる","入力トークン数を自動的に圧縮できる","モデルの出力を必ずXML形式に固定できる","指示・文脈・例の境界を明確に区切れる"],"oEn":["Save the intermediate reasoning steps to an external log","Automatically compress the input token count","Force the model's output into XML format","Clearly delimit instructions, context, and examples"],"a":3,"e":"モデルが各部分を正確に識別できる。Claudeは構造化タグの解釈に強い。XMLタグは入力トークンを圧縮せず、推論の途中経過をログに保存するものでもない。出力をXMLに固定する強制力もなく、あくまで区切りを明確にする記法である。","eEn":"The model identifies each part accurately; Claude is strong at interpreting structured tags. XML tags do not compress input tokens or log reasoning, and they cannot force XML output; they are simply notation that clarifies boundaries."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"プレフィルの効果はどれか。","qEn":"What is the effect of prefilling?","o":["会話履歴を圧縮して文脈量を削減する","モデルの温度を内部的に自動調整する","応答冒頭を固定し形式逸脱や前置きを抑える","応答末尾に定型の署名文を自動的に付与する"],"oEn":["Compress conversation history to reduce context size","Internally auto-tune the model's sampling temperature","Fix the response opening to curb format deviation and preamble","Automatically append a fixed template signature to the response's end"],"a":2,"e":"{を入れてJSON出力を強制するなど、出だしを決めて誘導する。プレフィルは会話履歴の圧縮やtemperatureの調整、応答末尾への署名文の付与を行う機能ではなく、応答の冒頭だけに作用する。","eEn":"Guide by setting the start, e.g. inserting { to force JSON output. Prefill does not compress history, adjust temperature, or append a signature; it acts only on the start of the response."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"思考の連鎖（CoT）を常用すべきでない場面はどれか。","qEn":"When should you NOT routinely use Chain of Thought (CoT)?","o":["多段の論理推論を要する課題","制約が多い計画立案タスク","単純で即答できるタスク","複雑な数式の段階的計算"],"oEn":["Problems needing multi-step logical reasoning","Planning tasks with many constraints","Simple tasks answerable instantly","Step-by-step computation of complex formulas"],"a":2,"e":"推論を強制するとトークンとレイテンシが無駄に増える。複雑タスクに限定する。多段の論理推論、制約の多い計画立案、複雑な数式の段階的計算は、途中の思考が精度を高める場面なので、思考の連鎖が効果を発揮する。","eEn":"Forcing reasoning wastes tokens and latency; limit it to complex tasks. Multi-step logical reasoning, constraint-heavy planning, and step-by-step complex calculations are where intermediate thinking raises accuracy, so chain of thought pays off."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"独立レビューインスタンスが自己レビューより優れる点はどれか。","qEn":"How is an independent review instance better than self-review?","o":["生成時の推論文脈を持たず微妙な問題を客観検出できる","同一モデルを使うため出力が完全に一致する","レビュー専用の追加プロンプトを設計する手間が一切不要になる","生成時の推論文脈を共有して速く判断できる"],"oEn":["Without generation context, it objectively detects subtle issues","Using the same model makes the outputs match exactly","It removes all need to design a separate review prompt","Sharing the generation reasoning lets it judge much faster"],"a":0,"e":"生成者は自分の判断を疑いにくい。独立インスタンスは客観的。同じ推論文脈を共有すると生成者の思い込みを引き継ぐため客観性が下がり、レビュー用のプロンプト設計が不要になるわけでもない。出力が完全に一致することも利点ではない。","eEn":"The generator rarely doubts its own judgment; an independent instance is objective. Sharing the generator's reasoning context carries over its assumptions and lowers objectivity, review prompts still need design, and identical output would not be an advantage."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【まとめ】D4が一貫して強調する原則はどれか。","qEn":"[Summary] What principle does D4 consistently emphasize?","o":["明確・簡潔・例示・形式指定で曖昧さを排す","常に詳細な背景説明を可能な限り多く盛り込む","出力形式を指定せず自然文で受け取る","推論はモデルの自由な解釈に委ねる"],"oEn":["Eliminate ambiguity via clarity, brevity, examples, and format specs","Always pack in the maximum amount of detailed background context possible","Specify no output format and accept plain natural prose","Leave the reasoning to the model's free interpretation"],"a":0,"e":"役割・文脈・タスク・形式を揃え、評価セットで測定しながら反復改善する。背景説明を際限なく盛り込むと要点がぼやけ、出力形式を指定しないと後処理が不安定になる。推論をモデルの自由な解釈に委ねる方針は曖昧さを排す原則に反する。","eEn":"Align role, context, task, and format, and iterate while measuring with an eval set. Piling on background blurs the point, leaving the output format unspecified makes downstream handling unstable, and leaving reasoning to free interpretation contradicts the principle of removing ambiguity."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"コンテキスト窓とは何か。","qEn":"What is the context window?","o":["モデルが一度に処理できる入出力トークンの総量","モデルの事前学習に用いた訓練データ全体の総量","同時に呼び出せるツールの最大登録数","1秒あたりに生成できるトークンの数"],"oEn":["The total input/output tokens the model can process at once","The total amount of data used to pretrain the model","The maximum number of tools you can register at once","The number of tokens it can generate per second"],"a":0,"e":"窓を超える情報は扱えない。長い対話や大規模文書では管理が必須。事前学習データの総量やツールの最大登録数、1秒あたりの生成トークン数は、それぞれ別の指標で、窓の大きさを表すものではない。","eEn":"Information beyond the window can't be handled; management is essential for long dialogues or large documents. The total training data, the maximum number of registered tools, and tokens generated per second are separate metrics, not the size of the window."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"「lost in the middle」現象とは何か。","qEn":"What is the 'lost in the middle' phenomenon?","o":["入力の先頭付近に置いた情報ほど無視される","長文の中間部の情報が参照されにくくなる","長文になると出力が途中で打ち切られる","末尾の情報ほど誤って要約される"],"oEn":["Information placed near the start is most often ignored","Mid-text information becomes less likely to be referenced","With long text, output gets cut off partway","Information near the end is most often mis-summarized"],"a":1,"e":"重要情報は冒頭や末尾に置く。中間に埋めると見落とされやすい。先頭や末尾の情報はむしろ参照されやすく、出力が途中で打ち切られる現象や末尾の誤要約は、中間部の見落としとは別の問題である。","eEn":"Put key info at the start or end; buried in the middle it's easily missed. Information at the start or end is actually easier to use, and truncated output or mis-summarized endings are different problems from overlooking the middle."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"頻繁に更新される製品情報に基づき回答させる最適手法はどれか。","qEn":"What is the best method to answer based on frequently updated product info?","o":["RAG（検索拡張生成）","モデルの再ファインチューニング","システムプロンプトへの直書き","少数例の追加提示"],"oEn":["RAG (retrieval-augmented generation)","Periodic re-fine-tuning of the model","Hard-coding facts into the prompt","Adding a few in-context examples"],"a":0,"e":"実行時に最新情報を取得して文脈に加える。再訓練不要で更新に即応、出典提示も可能。再ファインチューニングは更新のたびに再訓練が要り、システムプロンプトへの直書きは情報量が増えるほど保守できない。少数例の提示は最新情報の供給手段ではない。","eEn":"Fetch the latest info at runtime and add it to context; no retraining, instant updates, and citable. Re-fine-tuning needs retraining at every update, hardcoding into the system prompt becomes unmaintainable as information grows, and few-shot examples are not a way to supply current information."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"数日にわたるタスクでセッションをまたいで状態を保持する手段はどれか。","qEn":"How do you retain state across sessions for a multi-day task?","o":["システムプロンプトへの全履歴の埋め込み","メモリツール（外部ストアへの永続化）","コンテキスト窓の拡張だけで保持する","毎回プロンプトを冒頭から再送する"],"oEn":["Embedding the full history into the system prompt","Memory tool (persistence to an external data store)","Retaining it via context-window expansion alone","Resending the prompt from the top each time"],"a":1,"e":"コンテキスト窓を超えて情報を保存し再参照する。長期タスクの一貫性を支える。システムプロンプトへの履歴埋め込みや毎回の再送は窓を圧迫して上限に達し、窓の拡張だけではセッションをまたいだ保持にならない。","eEn":"Store info beyond the context window and re-reference it; supports consistency on long tasks. Embedding history in the system prompt or resending it each time eats into the window until it hits the limit, and enlarging the window alone does not persist state across sessions."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"一時的なAPI失敗への最適な信頼性対策はどれか。","qEn":"What is the best reliability measure for transient API failures?","o":["失敗時に即座に処理全体を中断する","固定間隔での上限なしの再試行","指数バックオフ付きリトライ（上限あり）","temperatureを上げて再送する"],"oEn":["Immediately abort the whole process on failure","Unlimited retries at a fixed interval","Retry with exponential backoff (capped)","Raise temperature and resend the request"],"a":2,"e":"待機を挟んだ再試行が有効。上限を設け恒久的障害での無限再試行を防ぐ。失敗のたびに全体を中断すると一時的な障害でも処理が失敗し、固定間隔で上限なく再試行すると負荷が集中して恒久障害では終わらない。temperatureを上げても通信障害は解消しない。","eEn":"Retrying with waits is effective; cap attempts to avoid infinite retries on permanent failures. Aborting everything on each failure turns a transient fault into a total failure, unlimited fixed-interval retries concentrate load and never end on permanent faults, and raising temperature does not fix an API failure."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"依存先の連続障害時に全体遅延を防ぐパターンはどれか。","qEn":"Which pattern prevents overall delay during a dependency's consecutive failures?","o":["タイムアウトの延長","無制限のリトライ","サーキット ブレーカー","同期的な逐次呼び出しの徹底"],"oEn":["Extending the timeout","Unlimited retries","Circuit breaker","Serial blocking calls"],"a":2,"e":"連続失敗時に呼び出しを一時遮断し、障害連鎖と負荷集中を防ぐ。タイムアウトの延長や無制限のリトライは、障害中の依存先への待機と負荷をかえって増やし、全体の遅延を悪化させる。","eEn":"On consecutive failures it temporarily cuts off calls, preventing cascades and load concentration. Extending timeouts or retrying without limit adds waiting and load against a failing dependency, making the overall delay worse."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"アクセス失敗と有効な空結果の正しい区別はどれか。","qEn":"What is the correct distinction between an access failure and a valid empty result?","o":["どちらもエラーとして扱い全処理を中断する","両者を区別せず同じ再試行ロジックにかける","アクセス失敗は再試行判断が必要、空結果はそのまま受容","空結果は必ず再試行し、アクセス失敗はそのまま受容する"],"oEn":["Treat both as errors and immediately abort the process","Apply the same retry logic to both cases without distinguishing them","Access failure needs retry judgment; an empty result is accepted as-is","Always retry empty results and accept access failures as-is"],"a":2,"e":"空を成功と偽装するのはアンチパターン。取れなかったのか、無かったのかを区別する。どちらもエラー扱いで全処理を中断すると、有効な空結果まで失敗にしてしまう。空結果を必ず再試行しアクセス失敗を受容する対応は、区別を逆にしている。","eEn":"Disguising an empty as success is an anti-pattern; distinguish 'couldn't fetch' from 'nothing there'. Treating both as errors and halting turns valid empty results into failures, and retrying empties while accepting access failures reverses the distinction."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"エスカレーションの適切な契機はどれか。","qEn":"What is an appropriate trigger for escalation?","o":["人の要求・ポリシー欠如・進展不能","モデルの確信度が閾値を下回った時","応答トークン数が上限に達した時","処理時間が想定より長引いた時"],"oEn":["Human request, missing policy, or no progress","When the model's confidence drops below a threshold","When response tokens hit the limit","When processing takes longer than expected"],"a":0,"e":"感情ベースや自己申告確信度は代理指標として不適。校正が不正確。応答トークン数の上限到達や処理時間の長期化は、顧客の要求や方針の空白、進展不能とは無関係な技術的指標で、エスカレーション判断の根拠にならない。","eEn":"Emotion-based or self-reported confidence are poor proxies; their calibration is inaccurate. Hitting a response token cap or a long processing time are technical indicators unrelated to the customer's request, a policy gap, or being stuck, and are no basis for escalation."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"プロンプトキャッシュが最も効果的な条件はどれか。","qEn":"When is prompt caching most effective?","o":["毎回大きく異なる長い可変部を大量に送信する場合","呼び出すツールの数が非常に多い場合","固定の接頭辞が大きく同一内容を繰り返し送る","出力トークンが極端に短くなる場合"],"oEn":["Sending a large, entirely different variable part every single time","When the number of tools called is very large","A large fixed prefix with the same content sent repeatedly","When the output tokens become extremely short"],"a":2,"e":"固定部分を先頭に、可変部分を後方に置くとヒット率が最大化する。毎回大きく異なる可変部を送ると接頭辞が一致せずキャッシュに当たらない。ツールの数や出力の短さは、キャッシュの効き目を決める条件ではない。","eEn":"Putting the fixed part first and the variable part later maximizes the hit rate. Sending a large, different variable part each time breaks the prefix match so the cache is missed, and the number of tools or the shortness of output does not determine cache effectiveness."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"集計精度の罠（97%が隠すもの）とは何か。","qEn":"What is the aggregate-accuracy trap (what 97% hides)?","o":["特定の型だけを過剰に最適化する","サンプル数が少なく分散が大きくなる","全体精度が特定の型別の不調を覆い隠す","全体精度が実際の値より低く算出されてしまう"],"oEn":["It over-optimizes for just one specific type","A small sample size makes the variance large","Overall accuracy masks poor performance on a specific type","Overall accuracy gets computed lower than it truly is in reality"],"a":2,"e":"全体97%でも特定フィールド型では低精度のことがある。層化無作為抽出で測る。サンプル数が少なく分散が大きくなる問題や、全体精度が実際より低く出るという説明は、集計値が部分的な不調を隠すという罠とは別である。","eEn":"97% overall can hide low accuracy on a specific field type; measure with stratified sampling. High variance from small samples, or overall accuracy being computed lower than reality, differs from the trap where an aggregate hides localized weakness."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"複数情報源を統合する際の矛盾統計の扱いはどれか。","qEn":"How should you handle conflicting statistics when integrating multiple sources?","o":["多数派の数値に統一する","常に最大値を提示する","出典付きで両論併記する","新しい方の値だけ採用"],"oEn":["Unify to the majority figure","Always present the single maximum value","Present both sides with citations","Adopt only the newer value"],"a":2,"e":"claim-sourceマッピングを統合まで保持し、出典付きで矛盾を提示する。多数派への統一や最大値の提示、新しい値だけの採用は、どの出典がどの数値を主張したかを失わせ、矛盾の存在そのものを読み手から隠す。","eEn":"Keep the claim-source mapping through integration and present the conflict with citations. Unifying to the majority, always showing the maximum, or adopting only the newer value loses which source claimed which number and hides the contradiction from the reader."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"探索中に文脈を削減する手段はどれか。","qEn":"What reduces context during exploration?","o":["/compact","/verbose","/expand","/reset-all"],"oEn":["/compact [instructions]","/verbose","/expand","/reset-all"],"a":0,"e":"探索中の文脈を圧縮。scratchpadファイルで境界を越えて保持も可能。/verbose、/expand、/reset-allは、文脈を要約して小さくするコマンドではない（2026年10月時点）。","eEn":"Compacts context during exploration; a scratchpad file can also retain it across boundaries. /verbose, /expand, and /reset-all are not commands that summarize and shrink the context (as of October 2026)."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"グレースフル デグラデーションとは何か。","qEn":"What is graceful degradation?","o":["全機能を通常どおり完全な状態で維持する","システム全体を自動で再起動して復旧する","障害を検知した時点で全機能を即座に完全停止する","一部障害時も機能を縮退させつつ動作を続ける"],"oEn":["Maintain every function fully in a normal state","Automatically restart the whole system to recover","Immediately shut down all functions the moment a fault is detected","Keep operating with reduced function during partial failure"],"a":3,"e":"全停止を避け部分的に動かす。可用性を保つ設計思想。全機能を通常どおり維持するのは障害時に不可能で、障害検知で全機能を即座に停止するのは縮退ではなく全停止である。自動再起動は復旧手段であり、縮退運転ではない。","eEn":"Avoid a full stop and keep partially running; a design philosophy for availability. Keeping every function at full capacity is impossible during a failure, stopping everything on detection is a full outage rather than degradation, and automatic restart is a recovery method, not degraded operation."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【まとめ】D5が一貫して問う設計判断はどれか。","qEn":"[Summary] What design decision does D5 consistently ask about?","o":["文脈を常に最大化して全履歴を保持し続け精度だけを最優先する","観測やログを完全に排し内部状態を一切記録せずに動かす","文脈を最小十分に保ち効率化し、検証・再試行・観測で信頼性を担保する","検証や再試行を全て省き応答速度だけを最大限に高める"],"oEn":["Always maximize the context and retain the entire history in order to prioritize accuracy above everything else","Remove observability and logging and run without recording internal state at all","Keep context minimally sufficient and ensure reliability via verification, retries, and observability","Skip all verification and retries entirely to maximize raw response speed alone"],"a":2,"e":"過剰な文脈は希薄化とコストを招く。非決定性は検証層・冪等性・フォールバックで囲む。文脈を常に最大化すると希薄化とコスト増を招き、観測を排したり検証と再試行を省いたりすると、非決定的な出力を扱う信頼性を担保できない。","eEn":"Excess context causes dilution and cost; wrap non-determinism with verification, idempotency, and fallback. Always maximizing context causes dilution and cost, and dropping observability or skipping verification and retries leaves no way to ensure reliability with non-deterministic output."}];

// ===== 模擬試験 固定セット（各100問×4。クイズとは独立）=====

// ===== 模試セットを認定レベルに再構成 =====
// 公式比率 D1:27 / D2:18 / D3:20 / D4:20 / D5:15 を維持。各セットは重複しない100問。
// 実際のセット2〜4は、依存（EXTRA/dedupe/hashStr/isAdvancedQ）の定義後に下方で構築する。
const EXAM_WEIGHTS = { D1: 27, D2: 18, D3: 20, D4: 20, D5: 15 };

const RAW_SETS = { 1: null, 2: null, 3: null, 4: null };
const SET_READY = { 1: true, 2: true, 3: true, 4: true };

// ===== クイズ用 追加問題（資料2の記述式を4択化）=====
const EXTRA = [
  {"d":"D1","q":"エージェントの観測可能性（Observability）が重要な理由はどれか。","o":["各ツール呼び出しの実行速度を向上させるため","実行に必要なトークン数を大きく削減するため","非決定的な実行経路を後から追跡し失敗を診断するため","エージェントの応答の文体を統一するため"],"a":2,"e":"各ステップのツール呼び出しと推論をログ化する。観測可能性がないと失敗原因を特定できない。", "qEn": "Why is agent observability important?", "oEn": ["To improve the execution speed of every single tool call across the board","To greatly reduce the number of tokens needed for execution","To trace non-deterministic paths afterward and diagnose failures","To unify the writing style of the agent's responses"], "eEn": "Log the tool calls and reasoning of each step. Without observability, the cause of a failure cannot be identified."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"エージェントの「環境」を設計することがなぜ中核なのか。","o":["環境がモデルの学習データを自動更新するから","環境を変えると課金単価が下がるから","環境設定を変えるとモデルの重みを直接書き換えられるから","能力が与えられた環境とツールに規定されるから"],"a":3,"e":"エージェントの能力は、与えられた環境とツールで決まる。何を観測し何に作用できるかは環境の設計次第だからだ。環境設定でモデルの重みを書き換えることはできず、学習データが自動更新されることもない。", "qEn": "Why is designing the agent's environment central?", "oEn": ["Because the environment automatically updates the model's training data","Because changing the environment lowers the billing unit price","Because changing environment settings lets you rewrite the model weights directly","Because capability is determined by the environment and tools provided"], "eEn": "An agent's capabilities are set by the environment and tools it is given, because they decide what it can observe and act on. Changing environment settings cannot rewrite the model's weights, and it does not update training data automatically."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"短期メモリと長期メモリの正しい区別はどれか。","o":["短期も長期も同じコンテキスト窓内に格納される","短期はコンテキスト窓内で揮発的、長期は窓外の永続ストア","短期は要約で保持、長期はキャッシュに保持する","短期はディスクに保存し、長期はGPUメモリ上に常駐させる"],"a":1,"e":"短期メモリはコンテキスト窓内にあるため、セッションが終わると消える。長期メモリは窓の外のファイルやDBなど永続ストアに置き、必要時に呼び出す。両方が同じコンテキスト窓内に格納されるなら、長期の永続性を満たさない。", "qEn": "Which is the correct distinction between short-term and long-term memory?", "oEn": ["Both short-term and long-term memory are stored in the same context window","Short-term is volatile in the window; long-term is a persistent store outside it","Short-term is kept as a summary; long-term is kept in a cache","Short-term is saved to disk, and long-term stays permanently resident in GPU memory"], "eEn": "Short-term memory lives inside the context window, so it disappears when the session ends. Long-term memory sits in a persistent store outside the window, such as files or a database, and is recalled when needed. If both lived in the same window, nothing would be persistent."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"エージェントの再現性を高める手法はどれか。","o":["会話履歴をランダムに間引いて応答の多様性を高める","呼び出すツールの数を大幅に増やし探索範囲を広げる","temperatureを下げ、ツール結果とプロンプトを固定する","temperatureを上げて、ツールの出力を実行ごとに変化させる"],"a":2,"e":"非決定性はtemperatureと動的環境から生じる。テスト時は固定し安定させる。", "qEn": "Which technique improves agent reproducibility?", "oEn": ["Randomly thin out the conversation history to increase response diversity","Greatly increase the number of tools called to broaden the search range","Lower the temperature and fix tool results and the prompt","Raise the temperature and have tool outputs change on each run"], "eEn": "Non-determinism comes from temperature and the dynamic environment. Fix them to stabilize during testing."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"目標漂流（Goal Drift）を防ぐ手段はどれか。","o":["目標の定期的な再確認と計画への固定","会話履歴を毎ターン全消去する","temperatureを段階的に上げていく","利用可能なツールを都度増やしていく"],"a":0,"e":"目標の定期的な再確認と計画への固定で、長いループでも当初の目標からのずれを検知して戻せる。会話履歴を毎ターン全消去すると目標そのものまで失い、temperatureを上げると出力のばらつきが増えるだけでずれは抑えられない。", "qEn": "Which technique prevents goal drift?", "oEn": ["Recheck the goal regularly and fix it in the plan","Fully erase the conversation history every turn","Keep raising the temperature gradually, step by step","Add available tools each time"], "eEn": "Re-checking the goal regularly and anchoring it to the plan lets the agent notice drift and return to the original objective. Clearing the whole conversation history every turn would lose the goal itself, and raising temperature only adds variance without preventing drift."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"冪等性（Idempotency）が重要な理由はどれか。","o":["リトライ回数の上限を自動で決めるため","ツールの戻り値を毎回キャッシュするため","再試行時の重複実行による副作用を防ぐため","同じ処理を複数回並列に実行して高速化するため"],"a":2,"e":"冪等な操作は、同じ操作を繰り返しても結果が変わらない。そのため再試行で重複実行されても副作用が出ず、リトライを安全にできる。同じ処理を複数回並列に実行して高速化することは、冪等性の目的ではない。", "qEn": "Why is idempotency important?", "oEn": ["To automatically decide the retry limit","To cache tool return values every time","To prevent side effects from duplicate execution on retry","To speed things up by running the same process several times in parallel"], "eEn": "An idempotent operation gives the same result no matter how many times it runs, so a retry that repeats the call causes no duplicate side effects. Running the same job several times in parallel to speed it up is not the purpose of idempotency."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"エージェントをステートレスに保つ利点はどれか。","o":["会話の文脈を長期間保持しやすくなる","利用トークン数が常に一定に保たれる","水平スケールと障害からの復旧が容易になる","モデルの応答精度が自動的に向上する"],"a":2,"e":"状態を外部に持つステートレスなエージェントは、どのインスタンスでも処理を引き継げる。そのため水平スケールと障害復旧が容易になる。会話の文脈を長期間保持しやすくなるわけではなく、保持したい文脈は外部ストアに置く必要がある。", "qEn": "What is the benefit of keeping agents stateless?", "oEn": ["It becomes easier to retain conversation context over a long period","The number of tokens used is always kept constant","Horizontal scaling and failure recovery become easier","The model's response accuracy improves automatically"], "eEn": "A stateless agent keeps its state outside, so any instance can pick up the work. That makes horizontal scaling and failure recovery easy. It does not make it easier to hold conversation context for a long time; context that must be kept has to go in an external store."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"ホットパス最適化とは何か。","o":["処理経路ごとに担当モデルを毎回切り替える","全ての処理経路を一律に同じ優先度で扱う","最頻出の処理経路を優先的に高速化・低コスト化する","最も稀にしか通らない処理経路から順に優先して最適化する"],"a":2,"e":"ホットパス最適化は、最も頻繁に通る処理経路を優先して高速化・低コスト化する。頻度が高い経路ほど改善効果が全体に及ぶため費用対効果が高い。最も稀にしか通らない処理経路から優先すると、効果の小さい所に労力を使うことになる。", "qEn": "What is hot path optimization?", "oEn": ["Switching the model in charge for each processing path every time","Treating all processing paths uniformly with the same priority","Speeding up and cutting the cost of the most frequent processing path first","Optimizing in priority order, starting with the processing paths used most rarely"], "eEn": "Hot-path optimization speeds up and cheapens the most frequently used path first, because improving a busy path pays off across the whole system. Starting from the path that is rarely taken would spend effort where the benefit is smallest."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"コンテキスト汚染（Context Pollution）とは何か。","o":["コンテキスト窓が上限に達し入力が切り詰められる現象","無関係・誤った情報が蓄積し後続判断を歪める現象","無関係な情報を自動で検出し即座に除去する仕組み","重要な情報ほど文脈の中間に埋もれる現象"],"a":1,"e":"コンテキスト汚染は、無関係な情報や誤った情報が蓄積して後続の判断を歪める現象。窓が上限に達して入力が切り詰められる現象は窓の溢れの問題で別物であり、重要な情報ほど文脈の中間に埋もれる現象とも区別される。", "qEn": "What is context pollution?", "oEn": ["A phenomenon where the context window reaches its upper limit and the input gets truncated","A phenomenon where irrelevant or wrong information piles up and skews later decisions","A mechanism that automatically detects irrelevant information and removes it immediately","A phenomenon where more important information gets buried in the middle of the context"], "eEn": "Context pollution is when irrelevant or wrong information piles up and distorts later decisions. Input being truncated because the window hit its limit is a separate overflow problem, and important details getting lost in the middle of the context is also a different phenomenon."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"探索 vs 活用の調整とは何か。","o":["短期記憶を使うか長期記憶を使うかの切り替え","確実性を重視するか柔軟性を重視するかの判断","処理を並列で走らせるか逐次で走らせるかを選ぶ配分","新たな手段を試すか既知の有効手段を使うかの配分"],"a":3,"e":"探索と活用の調整は、新しい手段を試すか、既知の有効な手段を使うかの配分を決めること。短期記憶と長期記憶の切り替えや、確実性と柔軟性の判断、並列か逐次かの選択とは別の論点。", "qEn": "What is balancing exploration versus exploitation?", "oEn": ["Switching between using short-term memory and long-term memory","A judgment about whether to prioritize certainty or flexibility","An allocation that chooses between running processing in parallel or sequentially","An allocation between trying new approaches and using known effective ones"], "eEn": "Balancing exploration and exploitation means deciding the allocation between trying new approaches and using known effective approaches. It is a different issue from switching between short-term and long-term memory, judging certainty versus flexibility, or choosing parallel versus sequential."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"単一障害点（SPOF）を避ける設計はどれか。","o":["監視を止めて障害を隠す","全処理を単一ノードに集約する","冗長化とフォールバックの導入","依存コンポーネントを一箇所に統合する"],"a":2,"e":"単一障害点を避けるには、冗長化とフォールバックを入れて、一部が止まっても全体が動くようにする。全処理を単一ノードに集約したり、依存先を一箇所に統合したりすると、そこが新たな単一障害点になる。", "qEn": "Which design avoids a single point of failure (SPOF)?", "oEn": ["Stop monitoring to hide failures","Consolidate all processing onto a single node","Introduce redundancy and fallbacks","Integrate dependent components in one place"], "eEn": "To avoid a single point of failure, introduce redundancy and fallbacks so that the whole keeps running even if a part stops. Consolidating all processing on a single node or integrating dependencies in one place creates a new single point of failure there."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"フォールバック設計とは何か。","o":["利用可能なツールを無制限に増やすこと","失敗した処理の履歴をすべて破棄すること","主経路が失敗した際の代替処理を用意すること","主経路が失敗した際に処理全体を即座に中断すること"],"a":2,"e":"フォールバック設計は、主経路が失敗したときに別手段への切替や人へのエスカレーションなど代替処理を用意しておく設計で、可用性を支える。失敗時に処理全体を即座に中断すると代替がなく、履歴をすべて破棄しても失敗の原因は消えない。", "qEn": "What is fallback design?", "oEn": ["Increasing the available tools without limit","Discarding the entire history of failed processing","Preparing alternative processing for when the primary path fails","Aborting the whole process when the primary path fails"], "eEn": "Fallback design prepares an alternative for when the main path fails, such as switching to another method or escalating to a person, and it supports availability. Stopping the whole process immediately leaves no alternative, and discarding the failure history does not remove the cause."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"保守的デフォルト設計とは何か。","o":["不確実時には安全側の行動を選ぶ既定方針","行動をランダムに選択して決定する方針","不確実な状況ほど積極的に権限を拡大する既定方針","入力に関係なく毎回処理を停止する方針"],"a":0,"e":"保守的デフォルト設計は、不確実なときに安全側の行動を選ぶ既定の方針。行動をランダムに選ぶ、不確実なほど権限を広げる、入力に関係なく毎回停止するという方針は、安全でも実用的でもない。", "qEn": "What is conservative default design?", "oEn": ["A default policy of choosing the safe-side action under uncertainty","A policy of choosing actions at random","A default policy of aggressively expanding permissions the more uncertain things are","A policy of halting processing every time regardless of input"], "eEn": "Conservative default design is a default policy of choosing the safe-side action when uncertain. Policies of choosing actions at random, expanding permissions the more uncertain things are, or halting every time regardless of input are neither safe nor practical."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"サブゴール分解の利点はどれか。","o":["タスク全体を一括処理でき呼び出し回数が減る","モデルの推論速度が必ず向上するという利点","実行ステップ数を常に一定に固定できる利点","小さく検証可能な中間目標により完遂率が上がる"],"a":3,"e":"サブゴール分解は、大きな目的を小さく検証できる中間目標に分けるため、途中で誤りを見つけやすく完遂率が上がる。一括処理で呼び出し回数が減るわけではなく、推論速度の向上やステップ数の固定も保証されない。", "qEn": "What is the benefit of subgoal decomposition?", "oEn": ["The whole task can be processed in one batch, reducing the number of calls","The benefit that the model's inference speed always improves","The benefit that the number of execution steps can always be fixed","Small, verifiable intermediate goals raise the completion rate"], "eEn": "Subgoal decomposition splits a large objective into small, verifiable intermediate goals, which makes errors easier to find along the way and raises the completion rate. Batch processing does not reduce the number of calls, and neither faster inference nor a fixed number of steps is guaranteed."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"中間チェックポイントを設ける利点はどれか。","o":["処理全体を一度も中断せず一気に完了できる点","モデルへの入力トークン量を常に一定に保てる点","長時間タスクの途中状態を保存し再開・検証できる","中間結果を破棄して常に最初からやり直せる点"],"a":2,"e":"中間チェックポイントは長時間タスクの途中状態を保存するので、失敗しても途中から再開でき、その時点の結果を検証できる。中間結果を破棄して常に最初からやり直す運用は、チェックポイントの目的と逆である。", "qEn": "What is the benefit of establishing intermediate checkpoints?", "oEn": ["The whole process can be completed in one go without ever being interrupted","The amount of input tokens to the model can always be kept constant","A long task's intermediate state can be saved, resumed, and verified","Intermediate results can be discarded and work can always restart from scratch"], "eEn": "A checkpoint saves the intermediate state of a long task, so after a failure the work can resume from that point and the partial result can be verified. Throwing away intermediate results and always restarting from scratch is the opposite of what checkpoints are for."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"権限昇格を慎重に扱う理由はどれか。","o":["過剰権限が事故時の被害を拡大するから","昇格処理がトークン消費量を決めるから","権限設定がUIの見た目を左右するから","権限が多いほど処理速度が向上するから"],"a":0,"e":"権限が過剰だと、誤動作や侵害が起きたときに被害が広がるため、昇格は慎重に扱う。トークン消費量の決定やUIの見た目は権限と関係がなく、権限が多いほど処理が速くなることもない。", "qEn": "Why should privilege escalation be handled carefully?", "oEn": ["Because excessive privileges magnify the damage in an incident","Because the escalation process determines token consumption","Because permission settings affect the look of the UI","Because the more privileges there are, the faster processing becomes"], "eEn": "If privileges are excessive, damage spreads when a malfunction or breach occurs, so escalation should be handled carefully. Token consumption and the look of the UI are unrelated to privileges, and more privileges do not make processing faster."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"動的サブタスク生成のリスクはどれか。","o":["トークン消費が常に固定されること","処理が必ず高速化してしまうこと","サブタスク間の依存が完全に消えること","無制限な分解による爆発的なステップ増加"],"a":3,"e":"動的にサブタスクを生成すると、分解が無制限に続いてステップ数が爆発的に増えるおそれがある。トークン消費が一定になる、必ず高速化する、サブタスク間の依存が消えるといったことは起きない。", "qEn": "What is the risk of dynamic subtask generation?", "oEn": ["Token consumption always being held fixed at one constant level","Processing always becoming faster","Dependencies between subtasks disappearing completely","Explosive growth in steps from unlimited decomposition"], "eEn": "If subtasks are generated dynamically, decomposition may continue without limit and the number of steps may grow explosively. Token consumption does not become constant, processing is not always faster, and dependencies between subtasks do not disappear."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"結果の信頼度スコアを返す利点はどれか。","o":["下流が確信度に応じた扱いを選べる","トークン課金を自動で削減できる利点","処理が必ず高速化されるという利点","出力の形式を常に統一できるという利点"],"a":0,"e":"信頼度スコアがあれば、下流の処理が確信度に応じて扱いを選べる。低スコアは追加検証へ、高スコアはそのまま利用へ分岐できる。出力形式の統一やトークン課金の削減は、スコアを返すことの利点ではない。", "qEn": "What is the benefit of returning a confidence score for results?", "oEn": ["Downstream can handle each result by its confidence","The benefit that token billing is reduced automatically","The benefit that processing is always made faster","The benefit that the output format can always be unified"], "eEn": "With a confidence score, downstream steps can choose how to treat each result: low scores go to extra verification and high scores can be used directly. Unifying the output format or cutting token charges is not what a confidence score provides."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"決定の確信度を活用する方法はどれか。","o":["低確信時に追加検証や人へのエスカレーションを発火させる","確信度の高低にかかわらず常に処理を停止する方法","確信度を無視して次の行動をランダムに決める方法","確信度の値に応じて課金額を自動的に増減させて調整する方法"],"a":0,"e":"確信度が低いときに、追加の検証や人へのエスカレーションを発動させれば、誤った判断を減らせる。確信度にかかわらず常に停止したり、無視してランダムに行動したり、課金額を増減させたりしても意味がない。", "qEn": "Which is a way to make use of decision confidence?", "oEn": ["Trigger additional verification or human escalation when confidence is low","A method of always stopping processing regardless of whether confidence is high or low","A method of ignoring confidence and choosing the next action at random","A method of adjusting by automatically raising or lowering the billed amount according to the confidence value"], "eEn": "If you trigger additional verification or escalation to a human when confidence is low, you can reduce wrong decisions. Always stopping regardless of confidence, ignoring it and acting at random, or raising and lowering the billed amount is pointless."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"サンドボックスを用意する理由はどれか。","o":["本番に影響を与えず危険な行動を検証するため","実行履歴を保存せず毎回破棄しておくため","本番のツール権限を無条件に最大まで引き上げるため","本番環境の処理速度を直接高速化するため"],"a":0,"e":"サンドボックスは本番から隔離された環境で、本番に影響を与えずに危険な行動を検証できる。実行履歴を毎回破棄するためのものではなく、本番のツール権限を引き上げたり、本番の処理速度を高めたりする目的でもない。", "qEn": "Why provide a sandbox?", "oEn": ["To verify dangerous actions without affecting production","To discard execution history every time without saving it","To raise production tool permissions to the maximum unconditionally","To directly speed up processing in the production environment"], "eEn": "A sandbox is an environment isolated from production, where dangerous actions can be verified without affecting production. It is not for discarding the execution history every time, and it is not meant to raise tool permissions in production or speed up production processing."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"段階的自律化とは何か。","o":["最初から一切の承認なしで完全自律にすること","自律度を上げずに常に同一の権限レベルで運用し続けること","承認付き→半自律→完全自律と段階的に権限を広げる","どの段階でも必ず人間の承認を必須にすること"],"a":2,"e":"段階的自律化は、承認付きから半自律、完全自律へと、信頼を確認しながら権限を広げていく進め方。最初から承認なしで完全自律にしたり、権限を固定したままにしたり、どの段階でも承認を必須にしたりするのは違う。", "qEn": "What is gradual autonomy?", "oEn": ["Making it fully autonomous from the start with no approvals at all","Continuing to operate at the same permission level at all times without raising autonomy","Widening permissions in stages: approval, semi-autonomy, then full autonomy","Making human approval mandatory at every stage"], "eEn": "Gradual autonomy is an approach that expands permissions from approval-required to semi-autonomous to fully autonomous while confirming trust. It differs from making it fully autonomous without approvals from the start, leaving permissions fixed, or requiring approval at every stage."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"失敗モード分析が改善に効く理由はどれか。","o":["頻出の失敗パターンを特定し集中対処できる","トークン課金を自動的に削減できるから","処理が必ず高速化されるようになるから","すべての失敗を事前に完全に防止できるから"],"a":0,"e":"失敗モード分析は、頻繁に起きる失敗のパターンを特定するので、影響の大きい原因に集中して対処できる。課金の自動削減や処理の高速化は保証されず、すべての失敗を事前に完全に防ぐこともできない。", "qEn": "Why does failure mode analysis help improvement?", "oEn": ["It identifies frequent failure patterns for focused handling","Because it can automatically reduce token billing","Because it makes processing always faster","Because it can completely prevent every single failure in advance"], "eEn": "Failure mode analysis identifies patterns of frequently occurring failures, so you can focus on the high-impact causes. Automatic billing reduction and faster processing are not guaranteed, and not all failures can be completely prevented in advance."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"トークン予算管理が必要な理由はどれか。","o":["トークン量が画面のUI表示を直接左右するから","累積したコンテキストが多いほどモデルの精度が必ず一貫して上がるから","反復で累積するコンテキストがコストと制限を圧迫するから","予算設定がモデルの再訓練に直接使われるから"],"a":2,"e":"エージェントは反復ごとに履歴が積み上がり、コンテキスト長の上限と課金トークンを圧迫するため、予算管理で膨張を抑える必要があるから。", "qEn": "Why is token budget management needed?", "oEn": ["Because the token amount directly affects the UI display on screen","Because the more accumulated context there is, the more the model's accuracy always rises consistently","Because context accumulated through iterations strains cost and limits","Because the budget setting is used directly for retraining the model"], "eEn": "An agent's history builds up with each iteration and strains the context length limit and billed tokens, so budget management is needed to keep the growth in check."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"並列ワーカー結果の統合で生じる課題はどれか。","o":["各ワーカーの出力が完全に同一になること","並列化により中間の実行ステップ数が必ず一定になること","矛盾・重複の解消と一貫した最終出力の生成","トークン課金が自動的に減ってしまうこと"],"a":2,"e":"並列ワーカーの結果を統合するときは、ワーカー間の矛盾や重複を解消し、一貫した最終出力にまとめる必要がある。出力が完全に同一になることはなく、中間の実行ステップ数が一定になることも、課金が自動で減ることもない。", "qEn": "What is a challenge in integrating results from parallel workers?", "oEn": ["Each worker's output being completely identical","The number of intermediate execution steps always being constant due to parallelization","Resolving contradictions and duplicates and producing a consistent final output","Token billing automatically decreasing"], "eEn": "When integrating the results of parallel workers, you need to resolve contradictions and duplicates between workers and compile a consistent final output. Outputs do not become completely identical, the number of intermediate execution steps does not become constant, and billing does not decrease automatically."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"最小実行可能版から始める利点はどれか。","o":["設計変更を一切不要にできるという利点","最初から本番規模でスケールを保証できるという利点","初期から全機能を完全実装できる利点","早期に課題を発見し過剰設計を避けられる"],"a":3,"e":"最小実行可能版から始めると、早い段階で課題を見つけられ、必要以上に作り込む過剰設計を避けられる。設計変更が不要になる、最初から本番規模の拡張性を保証する、全機能を完全に実装するといった利点はない。", "qEn": "What is the benefit of starting with a minimum viable version?", "oEn": ["The benefit that design changes become completely unnecessary","The benefit of guaranteeing production-scale scalability from the very start","The benefit of fully implementing all features from the beginning","Problems are found early and over-engineering is avoided"], "eEn": "Starting with a minimum viable version lets you find problems early and avoid over-engineering, building more than necessary. There are no benefits such as eliminating design changes, guaranteeing production-scale scalability from the start, or fully implementing all features."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"結果キャッシュが有効な場面はどれか。","o":["会話履歴が非常に長くなっている場合","同一入力に対する繰り返し処理がある場合","入力が毎回変化し結果も常に異なると分かっている場合","利用するツールの数が非常に多い場合"],"a":1,"e":"結果キャッシュは、同じ入力に対する処理が繰り返されるときに、計算結果を再利用して効率を上げる。入力が毎回変わり結果も異なる場合は再利用できず、会話履歴の長さやツールの数は関係がない。", "qEn": "In which situation is result caching effective?", "oEn": ["When the conversation history has become very long","When there is repeated processing for the same input","When it is known that the input changes every time and the results always differ","When the number of tools used is very large"], "eEn": "Result caching improves efficiency by reusing computed results when processing is repeated for the same input. When the input changes every time and results differ, they cannot be reused, and the length of the conversation history and the number of tools are irrelevant."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"単一責任設計が保守性を高める理由はどれか。","o":["トークン課金が自動的に削減されるから","一つの部品が多くの責務を兼ねるほど再利用しやすくなるから","全機能を一つのモジュールに集約できるから","各コンポーネントの役割が明確で変更が局所化する"],"a":3,"e":"単一責任の設計では、各コンポーネントの役割が明確になり、変更が局所化されるため保守しやすい。一つの部品が多くの責務を兼ねるほど再利用しにくくなり、全機能を一つのモジュールに集約する設計は逆効果。", "qEn": "Why does single-responsibility design improve maintainability?", "oEn": ["Because token billing is automatically reduced","Because the more responsibilities one component takes on, the easier it is to reuse","Because all functions can be consolidated into one module","Each component has a clear role and changes are localized"], "eEn": "In a single-responsibility design, each component's role is clear and changes are localized, so it is easy to maintain. The more responsibilities one component takes on, the harder it is to reuse, and a design that consolidates all functions into one module is counterproductive."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ツールの「名前」を明確にする理由はどれか。","o":["名前の文字数に応じてトークン課金を最適化するため","画面上のUI表示を整えるようにするため","モデルが用途を即座に把握できるようにするため","トークン課金を自動的に減らすようにするため"],"a":2,"e":"ツールの名前は、モデルが用途を一目で把握するための手がかりになる。名前の文字数に応じたトークン課金の最適化や画面上のUI表示の整形が目的ではなく、課金を自動で減らす効果もない。", "qEn": "Why make tool names clear?", "oEn": ["To optimize token billing according to the number of characters in the name","To tidy up the UI display on screen","So the model can grasp the purpose immediately","To automatically reduce token billing"], "eEn": "A tool's name is a clue that lets the model grasp its purpose at a glance. The purpose is not to optimize token billing by name length or to tidy the on-screen UI, and there is no effect of automatically reducing billing."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"入力スキーマにJSON Schemaを使う利点はどれか。","o":["トークン課金を自動で算出できるという点","引数の型・必須・制約を機械的に定義できる","画面のUIを自動生成できるようになる点","スキーマの記述量に比例して応答速度が必ず向上する点"],"a":1,"e":"入力スキーマにJSON Schemaを使うと、引数の型、必須項目、制約を機械的に定義でき、不正な呼び出しを検出しやすい。トークン課金の算出やUIの自動生成のためではなく、記述量に比例して速くなることもない。", "qEn": "What is the benefit of using JSON Schema for the input schema?", "oEn": ["The point that token billing can be calculated automatically","Argument types, required fields, and constraints can be defined mechanically","The UI screen can be generated automatically","Response speed always improves in proportion to the amount of schema description"], "eEn": "Using JSON Schema for the input schema lets you define argument types, required fields, and constraints mechanically, making invalid calls easier to detect. It is not for calculating token billing or auto-generating a UI, and it does not get faster in proportion to the amount written."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ツールパラメータに説明を付ける理由はどれか。","o":["画面上のUI表示を装飾するため","各引数の意味と期待値をモデルに伝えるため","トークン課金を自動的に減らすため","モデルの応答速度だけを引き上げるため"],"a":1,"e":"パラメータに説明を付けるのは、各引数の意味と期待される値をモデルに伝え、正しい値を渡させるため。画面上のUI表示の装飾や課金の自動削減、応答速度だけの向上が目的ではない。", "qEn": "Why add descriptions to tool parameters?", "oEn": ["To decorate what is displayed in the UI","To convey each argument's meaning and expected value","To automatically reduce token billing","To raise only the model's response speed"], "eEn": "Descriptions are added to parameters to tell the model the meaning and expected value of each argument so that it passes correct values. The purpose is not to decorate the on-screen UI, automatically reduce billing, or improve only response speed."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"MCP（Model Context Protocol）サーバーの役割はどれか。","o":["モデル本体を継続的に再訓練する役割","クライアントの代わりにモデルへの推論要求を実行する役割","APIの利用量に応じて課金を集計する役割","ツール・リソース・プロンプトを外部に公開する"],"a":3,"e":"MCPサーバーは、ツール、リソース、プロンプトを外部のクライアントに公開する役割を持つ。モデル本体の再訓練や、クライアントに代わるモデルへの推論要求の実行、APIの利用量の課金集計は担当しない。", "qEn": "What is the role of an MCP server?", "oEn": ["The role of continuously retraining the model itself","The role of executing inference requests to the model on behalf of the client","The role of aggregating billing according to API usage","Exposes tools, resources, and prompts externally"], "eEn": "An MCP server has the role of exposing tools, resources, and prompts to external clients. It is not responsible for retraining the model itself, executing inference requests to the model on behalf of the client, or aggregating billing for API usage."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"MCP（Model Context Protocol）クライアントの役割はどれか。","o":["自身の機能を外部へ公開して提供する","MCPサーバーへ接続し機能を利用する","接続してきた複数のサーバーを一元的に統括する","利用量に応じて課金を自動で集計する"],"a":1,"e":"MCPクライアントはMCPサーバーへ接続して、そのサーバーが公開する機能を利用する側。Claude Codeやデスクトップアプリが該当する。自身の機能を外部へ公開して提供するのはサーバーの役割である。", "qEn": "What is the role of an MCP (Model Context Protocol) client?", "oEn": ["Exposes its own capabilities to external parties","Connects to MCP servers and uses their capabilities","Centrally oversees the multiple servers that connect to it","Automatically tallies charges based on usage"], "eEn": "An MCP client connects to MCP servers and uses the capabilities they expose; Claude Code and the desktop app are examples. Exposing its own capabilities to the outside and offering them is the role of a server, not a client."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"MCP（Model Context Protocol）の「リソース」とは何か。","o":["接続時に交換する認証情報を表す単位","モデルが参照できる読み取り中心のデータ公開単位","モデルが呼び出して外部状態を変更するための操作単位","定型のプロンプトテンプレートを表す単位"],"a":1,"e":"MCPのリソースは、モデルが参照できる読み取り中心のデータを公開する単位。外部状態を変更する操作の単位はツール、定型のプロンプトテンプレートの単位はプロンプトで、認証情報を表す単位ではない。", "qEn": "What is a \"resource\" in MCP (Model Context Protocol)?", "oEn": ["A unit representing credentials exchanged at connection time","A read-oriented unit for exposing data the model can reference","A unit the model invokes to change external state","A unit representing a predefined prompt template"], "eEn": "An MCP resource is a unit that exposes mainly read-oriented data the model can reference. The unit for operations that change external state is a tool, and the unit for predefined prompt templates is a prompt; neither is a unit representing credentials."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"MCP（Model Context Protocol）の「プロンプト」要素とは何か。","o":["サーバー側で実行され外部システムを操作する再利用可能な関数","接続時に交換される暗号鍵などの秘密の認証情報","サーバーが提供する再利用可能なプロンプトテンプレート","モデルが参照する読み取り専用の参照データ"],"a":2,"e":"MCPのプロンプトは、サーバーが提供する再利用可能なプロンプトテンプレート。サーバー側で実行されて外部システムを操作する関数はツール、読み取り専用の参照データはリソースで、認証情報などの秘密を交換する要素ではない。", "qEn": "What is the \"prompt\" element in MCP (Model Context Protocol)?", "oEn": ["A reusable function executed on the server side that operates external systems","Secret credentials such as encryption keys exchanged at connection time","A reusable prompt template provided by the server","Read-only reference data the model consults"], "eEn": "An MCP prompt is a reusable prompt template provided by the server. A function that runs on the server side and operates external systems is a tool, and read-only reference data is a resource; it is not an element for exchanging secrets such as credentials."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"MCP（Model Context Protocol）の能力ネゴシエーションとは何か。","o":["UIのレイアウトを動的に調整する仕組み","接続時に互いの対応機能を確認し合意する仕組み","通信の応答速度を継続的に測定する仕組み","利用料金を接続時に交渉する仕組み"],"a":1,"e":"MCPでは接続確立時にクライアントとサーバーが互いの対応機能を交換・合意し、双方が使える範囲だけを利用するため互換性を保てるから。", "qEn": "What is capability negotiation in MCP (Model Context Protocol)?", "oEn": ["A mechanism that dynamically adjusts the UI layout","A mechanism to agree on supported features at connection","A mechanism that continuously measures communication response speed","A mechanism for negotiating usage fees at connection time"], "eEn": "In MCP, when a connection is established, the client and server exchange and agree on the features each supports and use only the range both can use, which preserves compatibility."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ツールのエラーメッセージを具体的にする理由はどれか。","o":["トークン課金を自動的に削減できるから","詳細なエラー文でモデルの精度が必ず向上するから","モデルが何を直せばよいか判断できるから","画面のエラー表示を赤色にできるから"],"a":2,"e":"エラーメッセージを具体的にすると、モデルが何をどう直せばよいかを判断でき、再試行で修正しやすい。トークン課金の削減や、精度が必ず向上すること、画面のエラー表示の色を赤くすることが理由ではない。", "qEn": "Why should tool error messages be made specific?", "oEn": ["Because it automatically reduces token charges","Because detailed error text always improves model accuracy","Because the model can determine what needs to be fixed","Because the on-screen error display can be made red"], "eEn": "Specific error messages let the model determine what to fix and how, making it easier to correct the problem on retry. The reasons are not reducing token charges, always improving accuracy, or turning the on-screen error display red."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"並列ツール呼び出しが有効な条件はどれか。","o":["各ツールが前段の結果に強く依存している","会話の履歴が十分に長くなっている","複数ツールの実行が互いに独立している","利用するツールの種類が非常に多い"],"a":2,"e":"並列ツール呼び出しは、複数のツールの実行が互いに独立しているときに有効。各ツールが前段の結果に強く依存していると順番に実行するしかなく、履歴の長さやツールの種類の多さは条件にならない。", "qEn": "Under what condition is parallel tool calling effective?", "oEn": ["Each tool depends strongly on the result of the previous step","The conversation history has become long enough","Multiple tool executions are independent of each other","A very large number of tool types are in use"], "eEn": "Parallel tool calling is effective when the executions of multiple tools are independent of each other. If each tool depends strongly on the result of the previous step, they can only run in sequence, and the length of the history or the number of tool types is not a condition."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ツールの戻り値を構造化する利点はどれか。","o":["処理が必ず高速化されるという利点","画面のUI表示が自動で整うという利点","トークン課金が自動的に減るという利点","モデルが結果を正確に解釈・抽出しやすくなる"],"a":3,"e":"戻り値を構造化すると、モデルが結果の項目を正確に解釈し、必要な値を抽出できる。処理が必ず速くなる、UI表示が自動で整う、トークン課金が自動で減るといった効果はない。", "qEn": "What is the benefit of structuring tool return values?", "oEn": ["Processing is always faster","The on-screen UI display is automatically tidied up","Token charges are automatically reduced","The model can accurately parse the results"], "eEn": "Structuring return values lets the model accurately interpret the fields of a result and extract the values it needs. There is no effect such as processing always becoming faster, the UI display being automatically tidied, or token charges being automatically reduced."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ツールの副作用を明示する理由はどれか。","o":["実行ログを残さず毎回破棄するようにするため","トークン課金を自動で最適化するようにするため","モデルの応答速度を高速化するようにするため","破壊的操作をモデルと利用者が認識するため"],"a":3,"e":"副作用を明示すると、削除や更新などの破壊的操作をモデルと利用者が事前に認識でき、意図しない実行を避けられるから。", "qEn": "Why should a tool's side effects be stated explicitly?", "oEn": ["So that execution logs are discarded every time rather than kept","So that token charges are automatically optimized","So that the model's response speed is increased","So that the model and the user are aware of destructive operations"], "eEn": "Stating side effects explicitly lets the model and the user recognize destructive operations such as deletion or updates in advance, so unintended execution can be avoided."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ツールの結果サイズ管理が必要な理由はどれか。","o":["画面のUI表示を整えることができるから","応答速度だけを一定に保てるようになるから","巨大な結果がコンテキストを急速に消費するから","結果が大きいほどモデルの解釈精度が必ず一貫して上がるから"],"a":2,"e":"巨大な結果は、コンテキストを急速に消費して、後続の処理に使える余地を奪うため、サイズの管理が必要になる。UI表示の整形や応答速度だけの維持が理由ではなく、結果が大きいほど解釈精度が一貫して上がることもない。", "qEn": "Why is it necessary to manage the size of tool results?", "oEn": ["Because it lets you tidy the on-screen UI display","Because it keeps only the response speed constant","Because huge results consume the context rapidly","Because the larger the result, the more consistently the model's interpretation accuracy always rises"], "eEn": "Huge results consume the context rapidly and take away room for subsequent processing, so their size needs to be managed. The reason is not tidying the UI display or merely keeping response speed steady, and a larger result does not make interpretation accuracy rise consistently."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"組み込みのEditツールの特徴はどれか。","o":["パターンでパス名を一致させる","ディレクトリ内を内容検索する","一意に定まるテキストで部分修正する","ファイル全体を常に書き換える"],"a":2,"e":"Editツールは、ファイル内で一意に一致するテキストを指定して部分的に書き換える。一致が一意でなければ使えず、その場合はReadとWriteで代替する。ファイル全体を常に書き換えるのはWriteの動きで、パターンでパス名を一致させるのはGlobの役割である。", "qEn": "What is a characteristic of the built-in Edit tool?", "oEn": ["Matches path names by pattern","Searches the contents of files within a directory","Makes partial edits using unique text","Always rewrites the entire file"], "eEn": "The Edit tool replaces a piece of text that matches uniquely in the file. If the match is not unique it cannot be used, and Read plus Write is the fallback. Rewriting the whole file every time is what Write does, and matching path names by pattern is the job of Glob."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ツールの引数検証をサーバー側で行う理由はどれか。","o":["検証を挟むことでモデルの推論精度を高めるため","画面上のUI入力欄を描画するため","モデルの誤った入力を実行前に弾くため","モデルの応答速度を引き上げるため"],"a":2,"e":"引数の検証をサーバー側で行えば、モデルが誤った入力を渡しても、実行前に弾いて被害を防げる。推論精度を高めたり、UIの入力欄を描画したり、応答速度を上げたりするための処理ではない。", "qEn": "Why should tool argument validation be done on the server side?", "oEn": ["To raise the model's reasoning accuracy by inserting validation","To render the input fields of the on-screen UI","To reject the model's incorrect input before execution","To raise the model's response speed"], "eEn": "If argument validation is done on the server side, even when the model passes incorrect input, it can be rejected before execution to prevent damage. It is not processing meant to raise reasoning accuracy, render UI input fields, or increase response speed."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ツール設計で単一責任を守る利点はどれか。","o":["処理速度が必ず高速化されるようになる","一つのツールが多くの機能を兼ねられて便利になる","役割が明確になりテストと保守が容易になる","トークン課金が自動的に削減されていく"],"a":2,"e":"ツールの責務を一つに絞ると、役割が明確になり、テストと保守が容易になる。一つのツールが多くの機能を兼ねると、モデルが選びにくくなり、処理が必ず速くなる、課金が減るといった効果もない。", "qEn": "What is the benefit of keeping to a single responsibility in tool design?", "oEn": ["Processing speed always becomes faster","One tool can serve many functions at once, which is convenient","Roles become clear, making testing and maintenance easier","Token charges are automatically reduced over time"], "eEn": "Narrowing a tool's responsibility to one makes its role clear and makes testing and maintenance easier. If one tool doubles as many functions, it becomes harder for the model to choose, and there is no effect such as processing always becoming faster or charges decreasing."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ツール名の衝突をどう避けるか。","o":["重複したら実行時に自動で片方を無効化する仕組みに任せる","ツール名をランダムな文字列で命名する","名前を使わず連番の番号のみで管理する","一意で説明的な名前と必要なら名前空間を用いる"],"a":3,"e":"一意で説明的な名前を付け、必要に応じて名前空間で修飾することで、同名ツールの取り違えや呼び出し衝突を防げるから。", "qEn": "How do you avoid tool name collisions?", "oEn": ["Leave it to a mechanism that automatically disables one of them at runtime when duplicated","Name tools with random strings","Manage them with sequential numbers only, without using names","Use unique, descriptive names, and namespaces if necessary"], "eEn": "Giving tools unique, descriptive names and qualifying them with namespaces as needed prevents mix-ups and call collisions between tools of the same name."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"MCP（Model Context Protocol）のN×M問題の解消の意味はどれか。","o":["利用するモデルの総数を削減すること","各クライアントと各ツールの個別連携をなくす","各クライアントのUIを一つに統一すること","接続ごとに専用の変換アダプタを個別実装して対応すること"],"a":1,"e":"N×M問題の解消とは、N個のクライアントとM個のツールの間で、組み合わせごとの個別連携を実装する必要をなくすこと。利用するモデルの総数やクライアントのUIを減らす話ではなく、専用の変換アダプタの個別実装はむしろ問題の原因。", "qEn": "What does resolving the N×M problem mean in MCP (Model Context Protocol)?", "oEn": ["Reducing the total number of models in use","Eliminating individual integrations between each client and each tool","Unifying the UI of every client into one","Handling each connection by implementing a dedicated conversion adapter individually"], "eEn": "Resolving the N×M problem means removing the need to implement a separate integration for every combination of N clients and M tools. It is not about reducing the total number of models or the clients' UIs, and implementing dedicated conversion adapters individually is in fact a cause of the problem."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ツールの戻り値に成功・失敗フラグを含める利点はどれか。","o":["画面のUI表示が自動で整うという利点","モデルの応答速度が必ず上がるという利点","トークン課金が自動的に減るという利点","モデルが結果の成否を確実に判別できる"],"a":3,"e":"戻り値に成功か失敗かのフラグを含めると、モデルが結果の成否を確実に判別でき、失敗時の再試行や別手段に切り替えられる。UI表示の自動整形や応答速度の向上、課金の削減とは関係がない。", "qEn": "What is the benefit of including a success/failure flag in a tool's return value?", "oEn": ["The on-screen UI display is automatically tidied up","The model's response speed always rises","Token charges are automatically reduced","The model can reliably tell success from failure"], "eEn": "Including a success or failure flag in the return value lets the model reliably tell whether the result succeeded or failed, so it can retry or switch to another approach on failure. It has nothing to do with automatic UI formatting, faster response, or reduced charges."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ツールの依存関係を設計で考慮する理由はどれか。","o":["応答速度だけを引き上げられるから","トークン課金を自動的に削減できるから","画面のUI表示を整えられるから","順序を誤ると失敗するツール連鎖があるから"],"a":3,"e":"ツールには、順序を間違えると失敗する連鎖があるため、依存関係を設計で考慮する必要がある。応答速度だけの向上や、課金の自動削減、画面表示の整形のためではない。", "qEn": "Why should tool dependencies be considered in the design?", "oEn": ["Because it can raise only the response speed","Because it can automatically reduce token charges","Because it makes it possible to tidy the on-screen UI display","Because some tool chains fail if the order is wrong"], "eEn": "Some tool chains fail if the order is wrong, so dependencies must be considered in the design. It is not for raising only response speed, automatically reducing charges, or tidying the on-screen display."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"MCP（Model Context Protocol）サーバーのログ記録が運用に効く理由はどれか。","o":["トークン課金を自動的に減らせるから","呼び出しと結果を追跡し障害を診断できる","画面のUI表示を装飾できるようになるから","モデルの応答速度を高速化できるから"],"a":1,"e":"ログに呼び出し内容と結果を記録すると、障害発生時に原因を追跡・診断でき、運用上の観測可能性を確保できるから。", "qEn": "Why does logging on an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server help operations?", "oEn": ["Because it can automatically reduce token charges","Calls and results can be traced and failures diagnosed","Because it makes it possible to decorate the on-screen UI display","Because it can speed up the model's response"], "eEn": "Recording the content and results of calls in logs makes it possible to trace and diagnose the cause when a failure occurs, which secures observability in operations."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"過剰なエラー抑制が招く問題はどれか。","o":["トークン課金が自動的に減ってしまうこと","失敗が隠れモデルが誤った前提で進む","処理が必ず高速化されてしまうこと","画面のUI表示が崩れてしまうこと"],"a":1,"e":"エラーを過剰に抑え込むと、失敗が隠れて、モデルが誤った前提のまま処理を進めてしまう。課金が減ることも、処理が必ず速くなることも、画面表示が崩れることも、この問題の本質ではない。", "qEn": "What problem does excessive error suppression cause?", "oEn": ["Token charges end up being reduced automatically","Failures are masked and the model works from false premises","Processing always becomes faster","The on-screen UI display breaks"], "eEn": "If errors are suppressed excessively, failures are hidden and the model keeps processing on a wrong assumption. Reduced charges, processing always being faster, or a broken on-screen display are not the essence of this problem."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ツールの入力サニタイズを行う理由はどれか。","o":["不正・危険な入力による被害を防ぐため","画面のUI表示を整えるようにするため","トークン課金を自動で減らすため","モデルの応答速度を高速化するため"],"a":0,"e":"入力を検証し無害化することで、インジェクションなど不正・危険な入力による被害を未然に防げるから。", "qEn": "Why should tool inputs be sanitized?", "oEn": ["To prevent damage from malicious or dangerous input","To tidy the on-screen UI display","To automatically reduce token charges","To speed up the model's response"], "eEn": "Validating and neutralizing input prevents damage from malicious or dangerous input such as injection before it happens."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"動的ツール発見が役立つ場面はどれか。","o":["エージェントの応答速度を最優先したい場合","ツールの実行結果を毎回キャッシュする場合","利用可能なツールが実行時に変わる場合","ツールの総数を減らして固定化したい場合"],"a":2,"e":"動的ツール発見は、利用可能なツールが実行時に変わる場合に役立ち、そのときの一覧を取得して使える。応答速度の最優先や結果の毎回のキャッシュ、ツール総数を減らして固定化する場面では必要ない。", "qEn": "When is dynamic tool discovery useful?", "oEn": ["When you want to prioritize agent response speed above all","When you cache tool execution results every time","When the available tools change at runtime","When you want to reduce the total number of tools and fix them"], "eEn": "Dynamic tool discovery is useful when the available tools change at runtime, since the current list can be retrieved and used. It is not needed when response speed is the top priority, when results are cached every time, or when the total number of tools is reduced and fixed."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"MCP（Model Context Protocol）の相互運用性が重要な理由はどれか。","o":["サーバー間の全通信を暗号化して安全性を常に保証できるから","モデルの推論速度を自動的に最適化できるから","異なるクライアントとサーバーを自由に組み合わせられる","各ベンダー専用の独自形式にツールを統一できるから"],"a":2,"e":"MCPの相互運用性があれば、異なるクライアントとサーバーを自由に組み合わせて使える。全通信の暗号化による安全性の保証や、推論速度の最適化、ベンダー専用の独自形式への統一を保証するものではない。", "qEn": "Why is interoperability in MCP (Model Context Protocol) important?", "oEn": ["Because all communication between servers can be encrypted, always guaranteeing safety","Because it can automatically optimize the model's inference speed","Different clients and servers can be freely combined","Because it can unify tools into a proprietary format specific to each vendor"], "eEn": "With MCP's interoperability, different clients and servers can be freely combined and used. It does not guarantee safety through encryption of all communication, optimization of inference speed, or unification into a vendor-specific proprietary format."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"Claude Codeとは何か。","o":["チームのタスク進捗を可視化するプロジェクト管理ツール","ソースコードの静的解析に特化したセキュリティ検査サービス","ブラウザ上で動作しノーコードで業務アプリを構築するプラットフォーム","ターミナルやエディタからコーディングを委譲できるエージェント型ツール"],"a":3,"e":"Claude Codeは、ターミナルやエディタからコーディング作業を委譲できるエージェント型ツールで、ファイル編集・コマンド実行・テストを自律的に行う。チームのタスク進捗を可視化するプロジェクト管理ツールや、ノーコードのアプリ構築基盤ではない。", "qEn": "What is Claude Code?", "oEn": ["A project management tool that visualizes a team's task progress","A security scanning service specialized in static analysis of source code","A browser-based platform for building business apps without code","An agentic tool for delegating coding from a terminal or editor"], "eEn": "Claude Code is an agentic tool to which you can delegate coding from the terminal or an editor, and it edits files, runs commands and runs tests on its own. It is not a project management tool for visualizing team progress or a no-code app-building platform."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"CLAUDE.mdをプロジェクトルートに置く意義はどれか。","o":["依存パッケージを自動的にインストールする","リポジトリ全体に共通する文脈を一元提供する","各ファイルの文字コードを自動判定して統一する","実行時にモデルの重みを動的に切り替える"],"a":1,"e":"CLAUDE.mdをプロジェクトのルートに置くと、そのリポジトリ全体に共通する規約や手順といった文脈を一元的に提供できる。依存パッケージの自動インストールや文字コードの判定、モデルの重みの切り替えはしない。", "qEn": "What is the significance of placing CLAUDE.md in the project root?", "oEn": ["It automatically installs dependency packages","It provides context common to the whole repository in one place","It automatically detects and unifies the character encoding of each file","It dynamically switches the model weights at runtime"], "eEn": "Placing CLAUDE.md in the project root provides context common to the whole repository, such as conventions and procedures, in one place. It does not automatically install dependency packages, detect character encodings, or switch model weights."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"フックの代表的なユースケースはどれか。","o":["編集後の自動フォーマットやテストの自動実行","モデルの学習率を動的に調整する処理","実行前に外部依存を解決して全体をビルドする処理","会話履歴を要約してトークンを削減する処理"],"a":0,"e":"フックの代表例は、ファイルの編集後に自動でフォーマットやテストを実行すること。モデルの学習率の調整、実行前の外部依存の解決とビルド、会話履歴の要約によるトークン削減は、フックの用途ではない。", "qEn": "What is a typical use case for hooks?", "oEn": ["Automatic formatting and automatic test runs after edits","Processing that dynamically adjusts the model's learning rate","Processing that resolves external dependencies and builds everything before execution","Processing that summarizes conversation history to reduce tokens"], "eEn": "Typical examples of hooks are automatically running formatting or tests after a file is edited. Adjusting the model's learning rate, resolving external dependencies and building before execution, and summarizing conversation history to reduce tokens are not uses of hooks."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"プラン モードの目的はどれか。","o":["変更を加える前に計画だけを提示させる","計画を飛ばして即座に変更を適用させる","変更を並列に複数試して比較させる","実行結果を自動でコミットまでさせる"],"a":0,"e":"プランモードは、ファイルを変更する前に調査して計画だけを提示させ、人が確認してから実行に進めるためのモード。計画を飛ばして即適用するのは逆で、並列に複数案を試して比較することや、コミットまでの自動実行が目的ではない。", "qEn": "What is the purpose of plan mode?", "oEn": ["To have it present only a plan before making changes","To have it skip the plan and apply changes immediately","To have it try multiple changes in parallel and compare them","To have it automatically go through to committing the results"], "eEn": "Plan mode is a mode in which Claude investigates and presents only a plan before changing any files, and a person reviews it before moving on to execution. Skipping the plan and applying changes immediately is the opposite, and trying multiple options in parallel to compare them or automatically executing through to commit is not its purpose."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"権限を事前許可する場合の注意点はどれか。","o":["繰り返し承認を省ける反面、誤操作リスクが上がる","許可した範囲外の操作も自動で実行される","承認のたびに処理が停止し全体が遅くなる","権限設定がセッション終了ごとに必ず初期状態へ戻される"],"a":0,"e":"権限を事前に許可すると、繰り返しの承認を省ける反面、誤った操作がそのまま実行されるリスクが上がる。許可していない範囲外の操作までは自動実行されず、承認のたびに停止するのは事前許可がない場合の動き。", "qEn": "What should you be careful about when pre-approving permissions?", "oEn": ["It saves repeated approvals but raises the risk of mistaken operations","Operations outside the permitted scope are also run automatically","Processing stops at every approval, slowing down everything","The permission settings are always reset to their initial state at the end of each session"], "eEn": "Pre-approving permissions saves repeated approvals but raises the risk that mistaken operations are run as they are. Operations outside the permitted scope are not run automatically, and stopping at every approval is what happens without pre-approval."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"CLAUDE.mdに書くべきでない情報はどれか。","o":["プロジェクトのビルド手順","コーディング規約とスタイル方針","頻繁に変わる一時的情報や機密","テスト実行時の共通の注意点"],"a":2,"e":"CLAUDE.mdには、ビルド手順、規約、テストの注意点のような恒常的な情報を書く。頻繁に変わる一時的な情報や機密は、内容が古くなったり漏えいしたりするため書くべきでない。", "qEn": "Which information should NOT be written in CLAUDE.md?", "oEn": ["The project's build procedure","Coding conventions and style policy","Frequently changing temporary info and secrets","Common points of caution to note when running tests"], "eEn": "CLAUDE.md should contain lasting information such as build procedures, conventions, and testing cautions. Frequently changing temporary information and secrets should not be written there, because the content becomes outdated or may leak."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"ヘッドレスモードとは何か。","o":["複数モデルを同時に比較実行するモード","画面表示を最優先する対話中心のモード","常に人手の確認を挟んで進めるモード","対話なしで非対話的に実行するモード"],"a":3,"e":"ヘッドレスモードは、画面での対話なしで非対話的に実行する方式で、スクリプトやCIから呼び出せる。複数モデルを同時に比較するモードや、画面表示を優先する対話中心のモード、常に人手の確認を挟むモードではない。", "qEn": "What is headless mode?", "oEn": ["A mode that runs multiple models side by side for comparison","An interactive mode that prioritizes on-screen display","A mode that always proceeds with human confirmation","A mode that runs non-interactively without any dialogue"], "eEn": "Headless mode is a way of running non-interactively, without on-screen dialogue, and can be called from scripts or CI. It is not a mode that compares multiple models at once, an interactive mode that prioritizes on-screen display, or a mode that always involves human confirmation."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"/clear（コンテキストクリア）の目的はどれか。","o":["直近の応答だけを残し古い履歴を要約する","セッションの全出力をファイルへ保存し終了する","現在のモデルをより上位のモデルへ切り替える","蓄積した文脈をリセットし無関係情報の干渉を防ぐ"],"a":3,"e":"/clearは蓄積した文脈をリセットし、無関係な情報が後の判断に干渉するのを防ぐ。長い履歴による精度低下とコスト増も抑えられる。古い履歴を要約して文脈を空けるのは/compactの動きで、/clearは空の文脈で新しく始める。", "qEn": "What is the purpose of /clear (clearing context)?", "oEn": ["To keep only the latest response and summarize the older history","To save the entire output of the session to a file and then exit","To switch the current model to a higher-tier model","To reset the accumulated context and prevent irrelevant interference"], "eEn": "/clear resets the accumulated context so that unrelated information does not interfere with later decisions, which also limits accuracy loss and cost from a long history. Summarizing the earlier history to free up space is what /compact does; /clear starts over with an empty context."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"設定の優先順位はどう決まるか。","o":["より局所的・近い階層の設定が上位を上書きする","常にグローバル設定が最優先で適用される","設定ファイルの記述された行数が多い方が優先される","先に読み込まれた設定が後の設定を上書きする"],"a":0,"e":"設定は、より局所的で作業場所に近い階層のものが上位の設定を上書きする。たとえばサブディレクトリの設定はルートの設定を上書きする。常にグローバル設定が最優先で適用されるわけではなく、記述行数の多さも優先度とは無関係。", "qEn": "How is the priority of settings determined?", "oEn": ["The more local, closer setting overrides the higher one","The global setting is always applied with the highest priority","The setting file with more lines written takes priority","A setting loaded earlier overrides ones loaded later"], "eEn": "The more local setting, the one closer to where you work, overrides the setting above it; for example a subdirectory setting overrides the root one. The global setting is not always applied with top priority, and the number of lines written has nothing to do with precedence."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"許可リスト方式の利点はどれか。","o":["明示的に許可した操作のみ自動実行され安全","危険な操作を含め全操作を一括で禁止できる","全ての操作を無条件で自動実行できる","実行のたびに毎回手動で確認を求められる"],"a":0,"e":"許可リスト方式は、明示的に許可した操作だけを自動で実行させるため、想定外の操作を通さず安全。危険な操作を含め全操作を一括で禁止したり、全操作を無条件で自動実行したりするものではなく、毎回確認を求める方式でもない。", "qEn": "What is the benefit of the allowlist approach?", "oEn": ["Only explicitly permitted operations run automatically, which is safe","All operations, including dangerous ones, can be prohibited at once","All operations can be run automatically without conditions","Manual confirmation is requested every time before execution"], "eEn": "The allowlist approach automatically runs only explicitly permitted operations, so it blocks unexpected operations and is safe. It does not prohibit all operations at once including dangerous ones, or run all operations unconditionally, and it is not an approach that asks for confirmation every time."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"フックで秘密情報の混入を防ぐ方法はどれか。","o":["コミット前検査フックで機密パターンを検出する","出力トークンの上限を小さめに設定しておく","コミットごとに履歴をすべて自動で削除しておく","環境変数を平文でリポジトリに保存しておく"],"a":0,"e":"コミット前の検査フックで機密パターンを自動検出すれば、人手のレビューでは見落としがちな秘密情報の混入を機械的に防げるから。", "qEn": "How can hooks prevent secrets from slipping in?", "oEn": ["Detect sensitive patterns with a pre-commit check hook","Set the output token limit on the low side","Automatically delete the entire history on every commit","Store environment variables in plain text in the repository"], "eEn": "A pre-commit check hook that automatically detects sensitive patterns mechanically prevents secrets from slipping in, which human review tends to miss."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【知識】settings.json でフック・権限・環境を管理する利点はどれか。","o":["スラッシュコマンドの本文をまとめて一つのファイルに書ける","共有設定と個人設定をファイルで分離・管理できる","実行環境のCPUやメモリを動的に増減できる","モデルの内部パラメータを直接編集できる"],"a":1,"e":"settings.jsonは権限・フック・環境を管理し、プロジェクト単位と個人単位で共有/個人設定を分離できる。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is the benefit of managing hooks, permissions, and environment in settings.json?", "oEn": ["The bodies of slash commands can be written together in a single file","Shared settings and personal settings can be separated and managed in files","The CPU and memory of the execution environment can be increased or decreased dynamically","The model's internal parameters can be edited directly"], "eEn": "settings.json manages permissions, hooks, and environment, and can separate shared and personal settings at the project level and the individual level."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"破壊的操作の二段階確認を設ける利点はどれか。","o":["あらゆる操作を自動で承認できる","処理を必ず高速に完了できる","重大な誤操作を二重に防げる","確認の手間を完全になくせる"],"a":2,"e":"破壊的操作に二段階の確認を設けると、重大な誤操作を二重に防げる。あらゆる操作を自動で承認することは目的と逆で、処理が必ず速くなるわけでも、確認の手間が完全になくなるわけでもない。", "qEn": "What is the benefit of requiring two-step confirmation for destructive operations?", "oEn": ["Every operation can be approved automatically","Processing is always completed quickly","Serious mistaken operations are prevented twice over","The effort of confirmation can be eliminated"], "eEn": "Requiring two-step confirmation for destructive operations prevents serious mistaken operations twice over. Approving every operation automatically is the opposite of the purpose, and it does not make processing always faster or eliminate the effort of confirmation entirely."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"機能追加とリファクタリングを分ける理由はどれか。","o":["処理速度を自動的に最適化できるから","テストを書く手間を大幅に省けるから","変更の意図を明確にしレビューを容易にする","コミット数を減らして履歴を単純化できるから"],"a":2,"e":"機能追加とリファクタリングを別の変更に分けると、それぞれの変更意図が明確になり、レビューしやすい。処理速度の自動最適化やテストを書く手間の大幅な省略、コミット数の削減は理由にならない。", "qEn": "Why separate feature additions from refactoring?", "oEn": ["Because processing speed can be optimized automatically","Because it greatly saves the effort of writing tests","It clarifies the intent of each change and makes review easier","Because it reduces commits and simplifies history"], "eEn": "Splitting feature additions and refactoring into separate changes makes the intent of each change clear and easier to review. Automatic optimization of processing speed, greatly saving the effort of writing tests, and reducing the number of commits are not reasons."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"対話セッションが長引いたときの対処はどれか。","o":["会話を続けたまま関連しない話題も投入し続ける","要約して新セッションを開始するかコンテキストをクリアする","利用するツールの数をできるだけ増やして処理能力を底上げする","出力の温度パラメータを上げて多様性を高める"],"a":1,"e":"セッションが長引いたら、要約して新しいセッションを始めるか、コンテキストをクリアして余計な情報を捨てる。関連しない話題を投入し続けたり、ツールを増やしたり、温度を上げたりしても、長いコンテキストの問題は解決しない。", "qEn": "What should you do when an interactive session drags on?", "oEn": ["Keep the conversation going and keep adding unrelated topics","Summarize and start a new session, or clear the context","Increase the number of tools in use as much as possible to boost processing capacity","Raise the output temperature parameter to increase diversity"], "eEn": "When a session drags on, summarize and start a new session, or clear the context to discard extra information. Continuing to add unrelated topics, adding more tools, or raising the temperature does not solve the problem of a long context."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"リモート実行が役立つ場面はどれか。","o":["モバイルや外出先からタスクを委譲したい場合","ローカルのGPUを直接使い切りたい場合","ネットワーク接続が全く無い環境で作業したい場合","外部への通信を完全に遮断したい場合"],"a":0,"e":"リモート実行は、モバイルや外出先からタスクを委譲して、手元のマシンを使わずに進めたい場合に役立つ。ローカルGPUを直接使い切りたい場合や、ネット接続が全くない環境、外部通信を完全に遮断したい場合には向かない。", "qEn": "When is remote execution useful?", "oEn": ["When you want to delegate tasks from mobile or while away from your desk","When you want to use up the local GPU directly","When you want to work in an environment with no network connection","When you want to block external communication completely"], "eEn": "Remote execution is useful when you want to delegate tasks from mobile or while out and have them proceed without using your local machine. It is not suited to cases where you want to use up the local GPU directly, an environment with no network connection at all, or completely blocking external communication."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"フォーマット強制（フック）の利点はどれか。","o":["実行速度が自動的に大幅に向上する","コードの実行結果まで自動的に検証してくれる","スタイルの一貫性を人手なしで保証できる","レビュー担当者を完全に不要にできる"],"a":2,"e":"フックでフォーマットを強制すれば、人手を介さずにコードのスタイルを一貫して保証できる。実行速度は向上せず、コードの実行結果の検証まではせず、レビュー担当者を完全に不要にもしない。", "qEn": "What is the benefit of enforcing formatting (with hooks)?", "oEn": ["Execution speed automatically improves greatly","Even the execution results of the code are verified automatically","Style consistency can be guaranteed without human effort","Reviewers can be made completely unnecessary"], "eEn": "Enforcing formatting with hooks guarantees consistent code style without human effort. It does not improve execution speed, does not verify the code's execution results, and does not make reviewers completely unnecessary."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"外部依存の固定を促す理由はどれか。","o":["依存関係を自動更新し続けるため","常に最新版を自動取得するため","再現性を保ち予期せぬ破壊を防ぐため","パッケージの容量を小さくするため"],"a":2,"e":"外部依存のバージョンを固定すると、同じ環境を再現でき、更新による予期せぬ破壊を防げる。依存関係を自動更新し続けたり、常に最新版を自動取得したりすると挙動が変わりうるので、固定の目的とは逆。", "qEn": "Why encourage pinning external dependencies?", "oEn": ["To keep updating dependencies automatically and continuously","To always fetch the latest version automatically","To maintain reproducibility and prevent unexpected breaks","To make the package size smaller"], "eEn": "Pinning the versions of external dependencies lets you reproduce the same environment and prevents unexpected breakage from updates. Continuously updating dependencies automatically or always fetching the latest version can change behavior, so that is the opposite of the purpose of pinning."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"ゼロショットとフューショットの使い分けはどれか。","o":["複雑な場合こそゼロショットが常に適する","単純はゼロショット、複雑・形式厳密なら例示","出力形式が厳密なときほど例示は避ける","タスクの難易度に関わらず例示数を最大化する"],"a":1,"e":"単純なタスクはゼロショットで足り、複雑なタスクや出力形式が厳密なタスクでは例を示すのが有効。複雑だからゼロショットが常に適するわけではなく、形式が厳密なときこそ例示が必要で、例示数を最大化する必要もない。", "qEn": "How do you choose between zero-shot and few-shot?", "oEn": ["When the task is complex, zero-shot is always the right fit","Zero-shot for simple tasks; examples for complex or strictly formatted ones","The stricter the output format, the more you should avoid examples","Maximize the number of examples regardless of task difficulty"], "eEn": "Simple tasks are fine with zero-shot, while giving examples is effective for complex tasks or tasks with strict output formats. Zero-shot is not always right just because a task is complex; examples are needed precisely when the format is strict, and there is no need to maximize the number of examples."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"プロンプトに文脈を与える効果はどれか。","o":["モデルの推論速度を確実に向上させる","背景情報を無視して常に汎用的な応答へ寄せる","タスクの背景に沿った適切な応答を引き出す","出力トークン数を自動的に削減できる"],"a":2,"e":"プロンプトに背景となる文脈を与えると、モデルはタスクの事情に沿った適切な応答を返しやすくなる。推論速度が確実に上がるわけでも、トークン数が自動で減るわけでもなく、背景を無視して汎用的に答えるのは文脈不足の結果。", "qEn": "What is the effect of giving context in a prompt?", "oEn": ["It reliably improves the model's inference speed","It ignores background information and always pushes toward generic responses","It elicits an appropriate response that fits the task's background","It can automatically reduce the number of output tokens"], "eEn": "When you give background context in a prompt, the model is more likely to return an appropriate response that fits the circumstances of the task. Inference speed is not reliably improved and the token count is not automatically reduced, and answering generically while ignoring the background is the result of a lack of context."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"段階的指示が有効な理由はどれか。","o":["全工程を一つの指示にまとめて渡せるから","複雑タスクを分解し各段階を確実にこなさせる","出力の長さを正確に制御できるようになるから","推論に必要なトークン数を削減できるから"],"a":1,"e":"複雑なタスクを段階的な指示に分けると、各段階を確実にこなさせられる。全工程を一つの指示にまとめると抜けやすく、出力の長さを正確に制御したり、推論のトークン数を削減したりするための手法ではない。", "qEn": "Why are step-by-step instructions effective?", "oEn": ["Because the whole process can be passed as a single instruction","They break a complex task down so each step is carried out reliably","Because the length of the output can be controlled precisely","Because the number of tokens needed for reasoning can be reduced"], "eEn": "Splitting a complex task into step-by-step instructions makes sure each step is carried out reliably. Putting the whole process into a single instruction makes it easy to miss things, and it is not a technique for precisely controlling output length or reducing the tokens used for reasoning."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"制約条件を明示する利点はどれか。","o":["推論の温度を自動調整できる","出力の範囲・長さ・形式を制御できる","モデルの応答速度を確実に上げられる","入力トークンの上限を自動で拡張できる"],"a":1,"e":"制約条件を明示すると出力の範囲・長さ・形式をモデルに指定でき、要件に沿った結果を安定して得られるから。", "qEn": "What is the benefit of stating constraints explicitly?", "oEn": ["The reasoning temperature can be adjusted automatically","Output scope, length, and format can be controlled","The model's response speed can be reliably increased","The input token limit can be extended automatically"], "eEn": "Stating constraints explicitly lets you specify the scope, length, and format of the output to the model, so you can consistently get results that meet the requirements."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"曖昧語を避けるべき理由はどれか。","o":["入力トークンが無駄に増えるから","処理速度が必ず低下してしまうから","解釈がばらつき結果が安定しないから","モデルが指示を必ず拒否してしまうから"],"a":2,"e":"曖昧な語は読み手によって解釈が分かれ、結果が安定しない。入力トークンが増えるから避けるのではなく、処理速度が必ず落ちるわけでも、モデルが指示を必ず拒否するわけでもない。", "qEn": "Why should ambiguous words be avoided?", "oEn": ["Because input tokens increase needlessly","Because processing speed always drops","Because interpretations vary and results are unstable","Because the model always ends up refusing the instruction"], "eEn": "Ambiguous words are interpreted differently by different readers, so results are not stable. They are not avoided because they increase input tokens, and processing speed does not always drop, nor does the model always refuse the instruction."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"対象読者を指定する理由はどれか。","o":["出力の生成速度を確実に高めるため","推論に使うトークン数を減らすため","語彙レベルや説明深度を適切に調整するため","読者に関わらず常に同じ表現で統一するため"],"a":2,"e":"対象読者を指定すると、語彙のレベルや説明の深さが読者に合わせて調整される。生成速度やトークン数を変えるためではなく、読者に関わらず同じ表現に統一するのは指定の目的と逆。", "qEn": "Why specify the target audience?", "oEn": ["To reliably increase the output generation speed","To reduce the number of tokens used for reasoning","To adjust the vocabulary level and depth of explanation appropriately","To unify the expression so it is always the same regardless of the reader"], "eEn": "Specifying the target audience adjusts the vocabulary level and depth of explanation to suit the reader. It is not meant to change generation speed or token counts, and unifying the expression regardless of the reader is the opposite of the purpose of specifying."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"自己検証ステップを加える利点はどれか。","o":["推論に必要なトークン数を確実に減らせる","出力前にモデル自身に整合性を確認させられる","外部ツールを使わずに事実誤認を完全に排除できる","応答の生成速度を確実に向上させられる"],"a":1,"e":"自己検証のステップを加えると、モデルが出力前に自分の回答の整合性を確認でき、誤りを減らせる。ただし外部ツールなしで事実誤認を完全に排除することはできず、トークン数の削減や生成速度の向上も保証されない。", "qEn": "What is the benefit of adding a self-verification step?", "oEn": ["It can reliably reduce the number of tokens needed for reasoning","It lets the model itself check consistency before output","It can completely eliminate factual errors without using external tools","It can reliably improve the response generation speed"], "eEn": "Adding a self-verification step lets the model check the consistency of its own answer before output, which reduces errors. However, factual errors cannot be completely eliminated without external tools, and neither reduced token counts nor faster generation is guaranteed."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"長さ制御が難しい理由はどれか。","o":["トークンと文字が常に一対一で対応するから","出力形式を指定する手段が存在しないから","文字数はプロンプトで一切指定できないから","モデルは正確なトークン数の制御が苦手だから"],"a":3,"e":"モデルは正確なトークン数を数えて出力を止めることが苦手なので、長さの制御は難しい。トークンと文字は常に一対一ではなく、出力形式やおおよその長さをプロンプトで指定する手段は存在する。", "qEn": "Why is length control difficult?", "oEn": ["Because tokens and characters always correspond one to one","Because there is no way to specify the output format","Because the number of characters cannot be specified in a prompt","Because models are not good at controlling the exact number of tokens"], "eEn": "Models are not good at counting exact tokens and stopping the output, so controlling length is difficult. Tokens and characters do not always correspond one to one, and there are ways to specify the output format and the approximate length in a prompt."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"指示の競合を避ける理由はどれか。","o":["競合する指示は自動で統合されるから","矛盾した指示はモデルを混乱させるから","入力トークンが無駄に消費されるから","指示が多いほど出力は必ず速くなるから"],"a":1,"e":"矛盾する指示を与えるとモデルがどちらに従うか判断できず出力が不安定になるため、指示間の整合を保つ必要があるから。", "qEn": "Why avoid conflicting instructions?", "oEn": ["Because conflicting instructions are merged automatically","Because contradictory instructions confuse the model","Because input tokens are consumed needlessly","Because the more instructions there are, the faster the output always becomes"], "eEn": "If you give contradictory instructions, the model cannot decide which to follow and its output becomes unstable, so consistency among instructions must be maintained."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"区切り文字を使う利点はどれか。","o":["応答の生成速度が確実に上がる","出力の温度を自動調整できる","複数項目を確実に分離・抽出できる","トークン消費量を自動で削減できる"],"a":2,"e":"区切り文字を使うと、複数の項目の境目がはっきりし、確実に分離して抽出できる。生成速度が上がったり、温度が自動調整されたり、トークン消費が自動で減ったりする効果はない。", "qEn": "What is the benefit of using delimiters?", "oEn": ["The response generation speed reliably increases","The output temperature can be adjusted automatically","Multiple items can be reliably separated and extracted","Token consumption can be reduced automatically"], "eEn": "Using delimiters makes the boundaries between multiple items clear so they can be reliably separated and extracted. They do not increase generation speed, adjust the temperature automatically, or reduce token consumption automatically."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"列挙型（enum）を使う利点はどれか。","o":["許可された値のみに出力を制限できる","出力トークン数を自動で削減できる","自由記述の文章を無制限に生成できる","推論の速度を確実に向上させられる"],"a":0,"e":"列挙型（enum）を使うと、出力できる値が許可されたものだけに制限され、表記ゆれや想定外の値を防げる。自由記述を無制限に生成させるのは逆で、トークン削減や推論速度の向上を保証するものではない。", "qEn": "What is the benefit of using an enumerated type (enum)?", "oEn": ["Output can be restricted to permitted values only","The number of output tokens can be reduced automatically","Free-form text can be generated without limit","Inference speed can be reliably improved"], "eEn": "Using an enum restricts the values that can be output to the permitted ones only, preventing inconsistent notation and unexpected values. Generating free-form text without limit is the opposite, and an enum does not guarantee reduced tokens or faster inference."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"指示の優先順位を明示する利点はどれか。","o":["競合時にどれを優先するかが明確になる","指示の数を実質的に減らせるようになる","推論トークンを自動で節約できるようになる","応答の生成速度が確実に向上する"],"a":0,"e":"優先順位を明示すると、指示が競合したときにどれを優先すべきかが明確になり、モデルの判断が一貫するから。", "qEn": "What is the benefit of stating the priority of instructions explicitly?", "oEn": ["It is clear which takes priority in a conflict","The number of instructions can be effectively reduced","Reasoning tokens can be saved automatically","The response generation speed reliably improves"], "eEn": "Stating priorities explicitly makes clear which instruction should take precedence when instructions conflict, so the model's judgment stays consistent."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"出力の根拠提示を求める利点はどれか。","o":["応答速度が確実に上がる","トークン消費を大きく減らせる","出力の温度を自動調整できる","検証可能性と信頼性が高まる"],"a":3,"e":"出力に根拠の提示を求めると、内容を確認でき、検証可能性と信頼性が高まる。応答速度が確実に上がることや、トークン消費の大幅な削減、温度の自動調整は、根拠提示の利点ではない。", "qEn": "What is the benefit of asking for the basis of an output?", "oEn": ["Response speed reliably increases","Token consumption can be greatly reduced","The output temperature is adjusted automatically","Verifiability and reliability increase"], "eEn": "Asking for the basis of an output lets you check its content and raises verifiability and reliability. A reliable increase in response speed, a large reduction in token consumption, and automatic temperature adjustment are not benefits of asking for the basis."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"文脈注入とファインチューニングの違いはどれか。","o":["どちらも実行時に一時的な文脈を渡すだけの手法","前者は実行時に文脈を与え、後者は重みを更新する","前者は重みを更新し、後者は実行時に文脈を与える","どちらもモデルの重みを実行時に書き換える手法"],"a":1,"e":"文脈注入は実行時にプロンプトで情報を与えるだけで即時かつ柔軟だが、ファインチューニングはモデルの重み自体を更新する点で異なるから。", "qEn": "What is the difference between context injection and fine-tuning?", "oEn": ["Both are methods that only pass temporary context at runtime","The former provides context at runtime, and the latter updates the weights","The former updates the weights, and the latter provides context at runtime","Both are methods that rewrite the model's weights at runtime"], "eEn": "Context injection only gives information in the prompt at runtime, so it is immediate and flexible, whereas fine-tuning differs in that it updates the model's weights themselves."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"評価セット維持が長期的に効く理由はどれか。","o":["変更のたびに回帰検証でき品質を守れる","推論コストを自動で削減できるから","テストを毎回書き直す必要がなくなるから","応答の生成速度が確実に速くなるから"],"a":0,"e":"評価セットを維持すると、プロンプトやモデルを変えるたびに回帰検証ができ、品質の低下に気づける。推論コストの自動削減や応答の高速化が目的ではなく、テストの書き直しが不要になるわけでもない。", "qEn": "Why does maintaining an evaluation set pay off in the long term?", "oEn": ["Regression checks on every change protect quality","Because inference cost can be reduced automatically","Because tests no longer need to be rewritten every time","Because the response generation speed reliably becomes faster"], "eEn": "Maintaining an evaluation set allows regression checks each time the prompt or model is changed, so you notice quality degradation. The goal is not automatic inference cost reduction or faster responses, and tests do not become free of rewriting."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"システムプロンプトとユーザーメッセージの役割分担はどれか。","o":["どちらも一回限りの一時的な指示として扱われる","システムは恒常的方針、ユーザーは個別の要求","システムは個別要求、ユーザーは恒常的方針を担う","両者は完全に同じ役割で常に交換可能である"],"a":1,"e":"システムプロンプトは役割や制約といった恒常的な方針を担い、ユーザーメッセージは個別の要求を伝える。両者は一回限りの指示でも、同じ役割で交換可能でもなく、役割を逆にするのも誤り。", "qEn": "How are roles divided between the system prompt and the user message?", "oEn": ["Both are treated as one-time, temporary instructions","The system prompt holds standing policy; the user message, individual requests","The system prompt holds individual requests; the user message holds standing policy","The two have exactly the same role and are always interchangeable"], "eEn": "The system prompt carries standing policy such as role and constraints, and the user message conveys individual requests. They are neither one-time instructions nor interchangeable with the same role, and swapping their roles is also wrong."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"トークン予算（Token Budget）とは何か。","o":["サーバーに割り当てられるCPU時間全体の上限値","画面に表示できる最大の文字幅の設定値","1か月あたりに支払う利用料金の総額","タスクで許容する入出力トークンの上限配分"],"a":3,"e":"トークン予算は、タスクで許容する入出力トークンの上限配分のこと。コストとコンテキスト超過の両方を抑える。サーバーのCPU時間の上限や、1か月あたりに支払う利用料金の総額とは別の概念で、トークン数で管理する。", "qEn": "What is a token budget?", "oEn": ["The upper limit of the total CPU time allocated to a server","A setting for the maximum character width that can be shown on screen","The total usage fees paid per month","The allotted limit of input and output tokens for a task"], "eEn": "A token budget is the cap on input and output tokens allowed for a task, and it helps limit both cost and context overflow. It is not a limit on server CPU time or the total amount paid per month; it is managed in tokens."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"コンテキスト圧縮のリスクはどれか。","o":["出力の温度が自動で上がること","トークン消費が逆に増大してしまうこと","要約過程で重要情報が失われる可能性","処理速度が必ず低下してしまうこと"],"a":2,"e":"コンテキストを圧縮すると、要約の過程で重要な情報が失われる可能性がある。圧縮によって温度が上がることはなく、トークン消費は減る方向で、処理速度が必ず落ちるわけでもない。", "qEn": "What is a risk of context compression?", "oEn": ["The output temperature rises","Token consumption ends up increasing","Key information may be lost in summarizing","Processing speed always drops"], "eEn": "Compressing context may cause important information to be lost in the summarization process. Compression does not raise the temperature, token consumption goes down rather than up, and processing speed does not always drop."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"ストリーミング出力の利点はどれか。","o":["生成される出力の正確さが確実に高まる","消費トークン総量を自動的に削減できる","総処理時間そのものが必ず短縮される","完了を待たず逐次表示でき体感速度が上がる"],"a":3,"e":"ストリーミングは、生成の完了を待たずに出力を逐次表示できるため、体感の待ち時間が短くなる。出力の正確さは変わらず、トークン総量も減らず、総処理時間そのものが必ず短縮されるわけでもない。", "qEn": "What is the benefit of streaming output?", "oEn": ["The accuracy of the generated output reliably increases","The tokens consumed can be reduced automatically","The total processing time itself is always shortened","Output can be shown incrementally, so perceived speed improves"], "eEn": "Streaming can display output incrementally without waiting for generation to finish, so the perceived waiting time is shorter. The accuracy of the output does not change, the total number of tokens does not decrease, and the total processing time itself is not always shortened."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"スループットとレイテンシの違いはどれか。","o":["レイテンシは単位時間の処理量、スループットは1件の応答時間","スループットは単位時間の処理量、レイテンシは1件あたりの応答時間","どちらも1秒あたりに処理できるリクエスト件数を表す","どちらもモデルの応答にかかる合計時間を指す同義語"],"a":1,"e":"スループットは単位時間あたりに処理できる量で、レイテンシは1件の応答にかかる時間。両者は別の指標で、要件に応じてどちらを最適化するか決める。レイテンシは単位時間の処理量だとする説明は定義が逆で、同義語とする説明も誤り。", "qEn": "What is the difference between throughput and latency?", "oEn": ["Latency is the amount processed per unit time; throughput is the response time of one request","Throughput is the amount processed per unit time; latency is the response time of a single request","Both represent the number of requests that can be processed per second","Both are synonyms for the total time taken by the model's response"], "eEn": "Throughput is how much can be processed per unit of time, and latency is how long a single response takes. They are different metrics, and you choose which to optimize based on requirements. Saying latency is the processing volume per unit time reverses the definitions, and calling them synonyms is also wrong."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"キャッシュヒット率を高める設計はどれか。","o":["リクエストごとに接頭辞をランダム化する","可変部分を先頭に置き固定部分を後方へ置く","固定部分を先頭に置き可変部分を後方に配置する","毎回プロンプト全体を動的に組み替える"],"a":2,"e":"固定部分を先頭に、可変部分を後方に置くと共通の接頭辞が再利用され、プロンプトキャッシュのヒット率が高まるから。", "qEn": "Which design raises the cache hit rate?", "oEn": ["Randomize the prefix for each request","Put the variable part first and the fixed part after it","Put the fixed part first and the variable part at the end","Dynamically reassemble the entire prompt every time"], "eEn": "Putting the fixed part first and the variable part after it lets the common prefix be reused, which raises the prompt cache hit rate."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【知識】部分障害時に全体を止めず縮退運転する設計思想を何と呼ぶか。","o":["ハードフェイル（障害時に即時全面停止）","コールドスタンバイ（障害時に待機系へ手動で切替）","フェイルオーバー（冗長系への自動切替）","グレースフル デグラデーション（優雅な劣化）"],"a":3,"e":"一部障害時も機能を縮退させつつ動作を続け、可用性を保つ設計思想がグレースフル デグラデーション。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is the design philosophy of running in a degraded mode without stopping everything during a partial failure called?", "oEn": ["Hard fail (immediate full shutdown on failure)","Cold standby (manual switch to the standby system on failure)","Failover (automatic switch to a redundant system)","Graceful degradation"], "eEn": "Graceful degradation is the design philosophy of keeping the system running with reduced functionality during a partial failure, preserving availability."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"グレースフル シャットダウンとは何か。","o":["処理中タスクを保存せず接続を強制切断する","処理中タスクを破棄して即座に停止する","新規リクエストの受付を止めず全処理を継続する","処理中タスクを安全に完了・保存してから停止する"],"a":3,"e":"グレースフルシャットダウンは、処理中のタスクを安全に完了・保存してから停止することで、データ損失や中途半端な状態を避ける仕組みだから。", "qEn": "What is a graceful shutdown?", "oEn": ["Forcibly disconnecting without saving in-progress tasks","Discarding in-progress tasks and stopping immediately","Continuing all processing without stopping the acceptance of new requests","Safely completing and saving in-progress tasks before stopping"], "eEn": "A graceful shutdown stops only after safely completing and saving in-progress tasks, which avoids data loss and half-finished states."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"長文処理でチャンキングを行う理由はどれか。","o":["全体の推論速度を一定に保つため","窓に収まる単位に分けて処理するため","課金トークン数を増やすため","出力の見栄えを整えて可読性を高めるため"],"a":1,"e":"長文はコンテキスト窓に収まらないため、窓に収まる単位に分割して処理し、結果を統合する必要があるから。", "qEn": "Why chunk text when processing long documents?", "oEn": ["To keep overall inference speed constant","To process it in units that fit in the window","To increase the number of billed tokens","To tidy up the appearance of the output and improve readability"], "eEn": "A long document does not fit in the context window, so it must be split into units that fit in the window, processed, and the results combined."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"RAG（Retrieval-Augmented Generation）の検索精度が全体品質を左右する理由はどれか。","o":["検索UIの応答速度と体感を高めるため","無関係な文書を取得すると生成も誤るから","APIの推論コストを削減するため","生成テキストの多様性を高めるため"],"a":1,"e":"RAGでは、検索で無関係な文書を取り込むと、生成もそれに引きずられて誤るため、検索精度が全体の品質を左右する。検索UIの体感速度や推論コストの削減、生成テキストの多様性が理由ではない。", "qEn": "Why does the retrieval accuracy of RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) determine overall quality?", "oEn": ["To improve the response speed and perceived feel of the search UI","Irrelevant retrieved documents make the generation wrong too","To reduce the API's inference cost","To increase the diversity of the generated text"], "eEn": "In RAG, if retrieval pulls in irrelevant documents, the generation is dragged along and goes wrong too, so retrieval accuracy determines overall quality. The perceived speed of the search UI, reduced inference cost, and diversity of generated text are not the reasons."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"アラート設計が重要な理由はどれか。","o":["全体の生成速度を一定に保つため","劣化を早期に通知し迅速対処を促すため","APIの推論コストを削減するため","検索インデックスの再構築を毎晩実行するため"],"a":1,"e":"アラートがあれば、品質や性能の劣化を早期に通知でき、迅速に対処できる。生成速度を一定に保つことや、推論コストの削減、検索インデックスの毎晩の再構築は、アラート設計の目的ではない。", "qEn": "Why is alert design important?", "oEn": ["To keep overall generation speed constant","To warn of degradation early for quick response","To reduce the API's inference cost","To rebuild the search index every night"], "eEn": "With alerts, degradation in quality or performance can be notified early and handled quickly. Keeping generation speed constant, reducing inference cost, and rebuilding the search index every night are not the purposes of alert design."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"フェイルセーフ既定値とは何か。","o":["障害時に必ず全体を停止する挙動","障害時に安全側へ倒れる既定の挙動","障害時に処理を強制続行する挙動","障害時にシステムを再起動する挙動"],"a":1,"e":"フェイルセーフ既定値は、障害や不確実な状況で自動的に安全側へ倒れる挙動を既定とし、被害の拡大を防ぐ設計だから。", "qEn": "What is a fail-safe default?", "oEn": ["Behavior that always shuts down everything on failure","Default behavior that falls to the safe side on failure","Behavior that forcibly continues processing on failure","Behavior that restarts the system on failure"], "eEn": "A fail-safe default is a design whose default behavior automatically falls to the safe side during failures or uncertain situations, preventing damage from spreading."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"観測可能性が改善の前提となる理由はどれか。","o":["生成の応答速度を高める前提になるから","何が起きたか分からなければ改善できないから","UIの見栄えや操作性を良くする前提になるから","推論コストを一定に保つ前提になるから"],"a":1,"e":"何が起きたかが見えなければ原因を特定できず、改善できないため、観測可能性が改善の前提になる。応答速度やUIの見栄え、推論コストを一定に保つことが前提になるわけではない。", "qEn": "Why is observability a prerequisite for improvement?", "oEn": ["Because it is a prerequisite for raising generation response speed","Because you cannot improve what you cannot tell happened","Because it is a prerequisite for improving the UI's appearance and usability","Because it is a prerequisite for keeping inference cost constant"], "eEn": "If you cannot see what happened, you cannot identify the cause and cannot improve, so observability is a prerequisite for improvement. Response speed, UI appearance, and keeping inference cost constant are not what it is a prerequisite for."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"圧縮と検索の併用が有効な理由はどれか。","o":["常に全ての履歴を圧縮せずそのまま保持できる","直近は圧縮し過去詳細は検索で再取得できる","常に全履歴を毎回まとめて削除できる","全ツールの呼び出しを毎回記録できる"],"a":1,"e":"直近の会話は圧縮し、過去の詳細は必要なときに検索で再取得すれば、容量を抑えつつ情報を失わない。全履歴を圧縮せずに保持したり、毎回まとめて削除したり、ツール呼び出しを全記録したりする方法とは異なる。", "qEn": "Why is combining compression and retrieval effective?", "oEn": ["All history can always be kept as is, with no compression","Compress recent history, and re-retrieve past details by search","All history can always be deleted in one go every time","Every tool call can be recorded every time"], "eEn": "By compressing recent conversation and retrieving past details by search when needed, you keep capacity down without losing information. This differs from keeping all history uncompressed, deleting it in one go every time, or recording every tool call."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"ヘルスチェックの役割はどれか。","o":["依存先の稼働状況を継続確認する","利用トークン数に応じ課金する","推論の応答速度を高速化する","UI画面のレイアウトを描画する"],"a":0,"e":"ヘルスチェックは依存先サービスの稼働状況を継続的に確認し、異常を早期に検知して可用性を維持するための仕組みだから。", "qEn": "What is the role of a health check?", "oEn": ["Continuously checking the operating status of dependencies","Billing according to the number of tokens used","Speeding up the response of inference","Rendering the layout of the UI screen"], "eEn": "A health check is a mechanism that continuously checks the operating status of dependent services, detects abnormalities early, and maintains availability."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"段階的ロールアウトの意義はどれか。","o":["処理速度を必ず高速化する","利用トークンの課金を削減する","モデルの推論精度そのものを引き上げる","本番障害の影響範囲を限定する"],"a":3,"e":"段階的ロールアウトは、少数のユーザーから順に展開して、本番障害が起きたときの影響範囲を限定する。処理速度の高速化や課金の削減、モデルの推論精度そのものの向上を目的とするものではない。", "qEn": "What is the significance of a staged rollout?", "oEn": ["It always speeds up processing","It reduces token usage charges","It raises the model's inference accuracy","It limits the blast radius of a production failure"], "eEn": "A staged rollout deploys to a small number of users first and expands gradually, limiting the blast radius when a production failure occurs. Its purpose is not faster processing, reduced charges, or raising the model's inference accuracy itself."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"依存先の分離が役立つ理由はどれか。","o":["推論の課金額を削減するため","生成の応答速度を高めるため","UIの応答速度と体感を大きく高めるため","一つの障害が全体に波及するのを防ぐ"],"a":3,"e":"依存先を分離しておけば、一つの依存先の障害が全体に波及するのを防げる。推論の課金額の削減や生成の応答速度の向上、UIの体感速度の改善が理由ではない。", "qEn": "Why is isolating dependencies useful?", "oEn": ["To reduce the inference billing amount","To raise the generation response speed","To greatly improve the UI's response speed and perceived feel","A single failure cannot spread to the whole system"], "eEn": "If dependencies are isolated, a failure in one dependency can be kept from spreading to the whole system. Reducing the inference billing amount, raising generation response speed, and improving the UI's perceived speed are not the reasons."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"べき等な再試行が必須な理由はどれか。","o":["UIの表示崩れを防ぐようにするため","再試行が重複副作用を生まないようにするため","再試行時にシステム全体の応答速度を高めるため","推論の課金額を削減するようにするため"],"a":1,"e":"ネットワーク不確実性の下で再試行は避けられず、べき等でないと重複した副作用が生じるため、べき等設計が前提となるから。", "qEn": "Why are idempotent retries essential?", "oEn": ["To prevent the UI display from breaking","So that retries do not produce duplicate side effects","To raise the response speed of the whole system during retries","To reduce the inference billing amount"], "eEn": "Under network uncertainty, retries are unavoidable, and without idempotency they cause duplicate side effects, so an idempotent design is a prerequisite."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】問い合わせを返金・技術サポート・営業の3部門へ自動振り分けしたい。最適なワークフローは。","o":["オーケストレーター・ワーカー","ルーティング ワークフロー","評価者・最適化者ワークフロー","並列化（セクショニング）"],"a":1,"e":"問い合わせを返金・技術サポート・営業のどれかに分類し、専用の処理へ振り分ける構成がルーティング ワークフロー。オーケストレーター・ワーカーは作業を動的に分解して割り振る構成で、固定の部門への振り分けとは用途が違う。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want to automatically route inquiries to three departments: refunds, technical support, and sales. What is the best workflow?", "oEn": ["Orchestrator-workers","Routing workflow","Evaluator-optimizer workflow","Parallelization (sectioning)"], "eEn": "Classifying each inquiry as refund, technical support or sales and sending it to a dedicated path is the routing workflow. Orchestrator-workers breaks a task down dynamically and delegates the pieces, which is a different purpose from sorting into fixed departments."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】1つの問いに複数の独立した情報源を同時に調べ統合したい。最適な構成は。","o":["プロンプトチェイニング","オーケストレーター・ワーカー","ルーティングによる振り分け","並列化（セクショニング）"],"a":3,"e":"複数の独立した情報源を同時に調べて統合するには、並列化のセクショニングが最適。プロンプトチェイニングは直列のため同時に調べられず、ルーティングは振り分け、オーケストレーター・ワーカーは分解が動的に変わる場合向き。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want to investigate multiple independent information sources for a single question at the same time and combine the results. What is the best configuration?", "oEn": ["Prompt chaining","Orchestrator-workers","Routing","Parallelization (sectioning)"], "eEn": "To investigate multiple independent information sources at the same time and combine them, parallelization with sectioning is best. Prompt chaining is sequential and cannot investigate them at the same time, routing is for dispatching, and orchestrator-workers suits cases where the decomposition changes dynamically."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】契約書ドラフトを生成し専門基準で評価して反復改善したい。最適なパターンは。","o":["プロンプトチェイニング","評価者・最適化者","並列化（投票）","ルーティング"],"a":1,"e":"ドラフトを生成し、専門基準で評価して反復改善するなら、評価者・最適化者パターンが最適。プロンプトチェイニングは固定手順、並列化（投票）は同一タスクの多数決、ルーティングは入力の振り分けで、反復改善の仕組みを持たない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want to generate a contract draft, evaluate it against professional standards, and improve it iteratively. What is the best pattern?", "oEn": ["Prompt chaining","Evaluator-optimizer","Parallelization (voting)","Routing"], "eEn": "To generate a draft, evaluate it against professional standards, and improve it iteratively, the evaluator-optimizer pattern is best. Prompt chaining is a fixed procedure, parallelization (voting) is a majority vote on the same task, and routing dispatches inputs; none has a mechanism for iterative improvement."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】入力ごとにサブタスク数が変わる複雑な分析を自動化したい。何を選ぶべきか。","o":["評価者・最適化者ワークフロー","ルーティングによる振り分け","並列化（セクショニング）","オーケストレーター・ワーカー型"],"a":3,"e":"入力ごとにサブタスクの数が変わる複雑な分析には、オーケストレーター・ワーカーが適する。中心役が動的にタスクを分解して配る。評価者・最適化者は反復改善、ルーティングは振り分け、並列化（セクショニング）は分け方が事前に決まっている場合向き。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want to automate a complex analysis in which the number of subtasks varies with each input. What should you choose?", "oEn": ["Evaluator-optimizer workflow","Routing","Parallelization (sectioning)","Orchestrator-workers"], "eEn": "For a complex analysis in which the number of subtasks varies with each input, orchestrator-workers is suitable: the central role decomposes the task dynamically and distributes it. Evaluator-optimizer is for iterative improvement, routing is for dispatching, and parallelization (sectioning) suits cases where the split is decided in advance."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】解けないタスクで延々とループしコストが急増した。最初に追加すべきは。","o":["フューショット例の追加による誘導","停止条件（最大反復回数・トークン上限）","役割プロンプトの追加による誘導","各ツールの説明文と入力名称のさらなる改善"],"a":1,"e":"ループが止まらないなら、まず停止条件を入れる。最大反復回数やトークン上限、タイムアウトで確実に止められ、コストの急増を防げる。フューショット例の追加や役割プロンプトで誘導しても、停止そのものは保証されない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] An agent looped endlessly on a task it could not solve and costs spiked. What should be added first?", "oEn": ["Guidance by adding few-shot examples","Stopping conditions (maximum iterations and token limit)","Guidance by adding a role prompt","Further improvement of each tool's description and input names"], "eEn": "If the agent loops endlessly, first add stop conditions. A maximum iteration count, a token cap or a timeout reliably stops it and prevents cost spikes. Guiding it with added few-shot examples or a role prompt does not guarantee that it stops."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】ファイル削除を無断実行し障害を起こした。再発防止に最も有効なのは。","o":["temperature低下による出力安定化","利用可能なツールの数を大幅に増やす対応","ヒューマン・イン・ザ・ループ（承認ステップ）","ループ反復回数の上限を撤廃する対応"],"a":2,"e":"ファイルの無断削除を防ぐには、実行前に人間の承認を挟むヒューマン・イン・ザ・ループが最も有効。温度を下げても誤った操作は防げず、ツールを増やすとリスクが増え、反復回数の上限を撤廃すると暴走しやすくなる。", "qEn": "[Scenario] An agent ran a file deletion without permission and caused an outage. What is most effective for preventing recurrence?", "oEn": ["Stabilizing output by lowering the temperature","Greatly increasing the number of available tools","Human-in-the-loop (an approval step)","Removing the cap on loop iterations"], "eEn": "To prevent unauthorized file deletion, human-in-the-loop, which inserts human approval before execution, is most effective. Lowering the temperature does not prevent mistaken operations, adding tools increases risk, and removing the iteration cap makes runaway behavior more likely."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【シナリオ】複数のツールが似た機能を持ち選択を誤る。改善策は。","o":["ツールの統合と説明・名称の明確化","temperatureを上げて多様化する","会話履歴をさらに長く保持する","利用ツールをさらに細かく分割する"],"a":0,"e":"似た機能のツールは統合し、説明と名称を明確にすると選択精度が上がる。ツール数が減り、各ツールの違いがモデルに伝わるからだ。さらに細かく分割すると似たツールが増えて迷いが増し、temperatureを上げても選択の正確さは上がらない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] Several tools have similar functions and the wrong one gets selected. What is the fix?", "oEn": ["Merge the tools and clarify descriptions and names","Raise the temperature to make the output more diverse","Keep the conversation history even longer","Split the tools used into even finer pieces"], "eEn": "Merging overlapping tools and making their descriptions and names clear improves selection accuracy, because there are fewer tools and each difference is communicated to the model. Splitting tools into finer pieces adds more look-alikes, and raising temperature does not make the choice more accurate."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】長い対話で当初の目標を見失う。対処は。","o":["temperatureを上げて出力を多様化する","目標と計画のコンテキストへの再提示","利用ツールを削除して選択肢を減らす","会話履歴を増やして情報を補う"],"a":1,"e":"目標と計画をコンテキストへ再提示すると、各ステップで整合を点検でき、長い対話でも当初の目標に戻れる。会話履歴を増やして情報を補っても重要指示は埋もれたままで、ツールを削除して選択肢を減らしても目標のずれは直らない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] In a long conversation, the agent loses sight of the original goal. What is the remedy?", "oEn": ["Raise the temperature to diversify the output","Re-present the goal and plan in the context","Remove tools to reduce the options","Increase the conversation history to supplement the information"], "eEn": "Re-presenting the goal and plan in the context lets the agent check alignment at each step and return to the original objective in a long dialogue. Adding more conversation history leaves the key instruction buried, and removing tools to reduce options does not fix goal drift."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【シナリオ】編集後に毎回フォーマットとテストを確実に走らせたい。何を使うか。","o":["プランモード（事前計画）","CLAUDE.md（常時指示の記載）","スラッシュコマンド（手動起動）","フック（編集後の自動実行）"],"a":3,"e":"フックは編集後などのタイミングで自動実行されるので、フォーマットとテストを毎回確実に走らせられる。CLAUDE.mdへの記載は依頼にすぎず強制力がなく、スラッシュコマンドは手動で起動する必要があるため漏れが出る。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want to run formatting and tests reliably after every edit. What should you use?", "oEn": ["Plan mode (planning in advance)","CLAUDE.md (standing instructions)","Slash commands (manual invocation)","Hooks (automatic execution after edits)"], "eEn": "A hook runs automatically at points such as after an edit, so formatting and tests run every time without fail. Writing the rule in CLAUDE.md is only a request with no enforcement, and a slash command must be started manually, so runs can be missed."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【シナリオ】CIでプルリクエストの自動レビューを行いたい。何を使うか。","o":["プランモード（事前計画の提示）","ヘッドレス（非対話）モード","スラッシュコマンド（手動起動）","対話モード（逐次確認しながら）"],"a":1,"e":"CIには対話できる人がいないため、非対話のヘッドレスモードで実行し、プルリクエストの自動レビューを継続的に回せる。対話モードは逐次確認しながら進める前提で、プランモードは事前に計画を提示して承認を待つので、CIの自動実行には向かない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want to run automated pull request reviews in CI. What should you use?", "oEn": ["Plan mode (presenting a plan in advance)","Headless (non-interactive) mode","Slash commands (manual invocation)","Interactive mode (with step-by-step confirmation)"], "eEn": "CI has no person to interact with, so running in non-interactive headless mode lets pull request reviews run automatically and continuously. Interactive mode assumes step-by-step confirmation, and plan mode presents a plan and waits for approval, so neither suits automated CI runs."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【シナリオ】同一の長い社内規約を毎回先頭に付けて数千件処理する。コスト削減に最適なのは。","o":["会話履歴の全削除","利用ツールの追加","temperatureの低下","プロンプト キャッシュ"],"a":3,"e":"固定の長い社内規約は毎回同じ接頭辞なので、プロンプトキャッシュで再利用できる。再処理のコストが大幅に下がる。会話履歴の全削除やtemperatureの低下は入力トークンの再処理量を減らさず、ツールの追加はむしろ入力を増やす。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You process thousands of items, each with the same long set of internal rules prepended. What is best for reducing cost?", "oEn": ["Deleting the entire conversation history","Adding tools","Lowering the temperature","Prompt caching"], "eEn": "The long, fixed policy text is the same prefix every time, so prompt caching can reuse it and cut reprocessing cost sharply. Deleting the whole conversation history or lowering temperature does not reduce reprocessed input tokens, and adding tools only increases the input."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【シナリオ】頻繁に更新される製品情報に基づき回答させたい。最適な手法は。","o":["temperatureの調整","会話履歴の全削除","検索拡張生成（RAG）","ファインチューニング"],"a":2,"e":"頻繁に更新される製品情報は、検索拡張生成（RAG）で最新の文書を取得して回答に使うのが適している。再訓練が不要で更新に即応でき、出典も示せる。ファインチューニングは更新のたびに再学習が必要になり、変化の速い情報には向かない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want answers based on frequently updated product information. What is the best approach?", "oEn": ["Adjusting the temperature","Deleting the entire conversation history","Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG)","Fine-tuning"], "eEn": "For frequently updated product information, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) fetches the latest documents and uses them in the answer. It needs no retraining, reflects updates right away and can cite sources. Fine-tuning needs retraining for each update, so it suits fast-changing information poorly."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【シナリオ】数日にわたるタスクでセッションをまたいで状態を保持する必要がある。何を使うか。","o":["利用可能なツールの数を増やす対応","temperatureの低下による安定化","メモリツール（外部ストアへの永続化）","会話履歴を毎回まとめて消去する運用"],"a":2,"e":"数日にわたるタスクで状態を保つには、外部ストアに保存するメモリツールを使う。ツールの数を増やしても状態は残らず、温度を下げても記憶は保持されず、会話履歴を毎回まとめて消去する運用では状態が失われる。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A task spanning several days needs to keep state across sessions. What should you use?", "oEn": ["Increasing the number of available tools","Stabilizing by lowering the temperature","A memory tool (external-store persistence)","Clearing the conversation history all at once every time"], "eEn": "To keep state across a task spanning several days, use a memory tool that saves to an external store. Adding more tools does not retain state, lowering the temperature does not preserve memory, and clearing the conversation history every time loses the state."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【シナリオ】API連携が時々一時的に失敗する。最も適切な信頼性対策は。","o":["temperatureを最大化する","最初の失敗で即座に処理を諦める","上限のない即時リトライの継続","指数バックオフ付きリトライ（上限あり）"],"a":3,"e":"一時的な失敗には、待ち時間を指数的に延ばす指数バックオフ付きで、上限ありのリトライが適する。恒久的な障害での無限再試行を防げる。上限のない即時リトライの継続は障害時に負荷をかけ続け、最初の失敗で諦めると一時的な失敗から回復できない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] An API integration sometimes fails temporarily. What is the most appropriate reliability measure?", "oEn": ["Maximizing the temperature","Giving up immediately on the first failure","Continuing immediate retries with no upper limit","Exponential backoff retries (capped)"], "eEn": "For occasional transient failures, retry with exponential backoff and a cap is appropriate, and the cap stops endless retries against a permanent outage. Continuing immediate retries with no limit keeps hammering a failing service, and giving up at the first failure never recovers from a transient error."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【シナリオ】依存先の連続障害時も呼び出しを繰り返し全体が遅延する。対処は。","o":["利用ツールの追加","利用履歴の全保持","サーキット ブレーカー","リトライのみを継続する"],"a":2,"e":"依存先が連続して失敗するのに呼び出しを繰り返して遅延する場合は、サーキットブレーカーで呼び出しを遮断する。リトライのみの継続は遅延を悪化させ、ツールの追加や利用履歴の全保持は原因に対処しない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] Even when a dependency fails repeatedly, calls keep being repeated and everything slows down. What is the fix?", "oEn": ["Adding tools","Keeping the entire usage history","A circuit breaker","Continuing with retries only"], "eEn": "When a dependency fails repeatedly yet calls keep being repeated and cause delays, cut off the calls with a circuit breaker. Continuing with retries only makes the delay worse, and adding tools or keeping the entire usage history does not address the cause."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【シナリオ】出力がJSON形式から逸脱し前置き文が混入する。確実に形式を守らせる手段は。","o":["モデルの自由な生成にすべてそのまま任せる","ツール定義（入力スキーマ）またはプレフィルの利用","temperatureの調整のみですべて対応する","会話履歴を毎回削除して文脈を整理する"],"a":1,"e":"JSON形式を確実に守らせるには、ツール定義の入力スキーマで構造を強制するか、プレフィルで応答の冒頭を固定する。自由な生成に任せたり、温度の調整だけに頼ったり、会話履歴を削除したりしても、前置き文の混入は防げない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] The output deviates from JSON format and a preamble creeps in. What is the way to reliably enforce the format?", "oEn": ["Leave everything to the model's free generation as is","Use a tool definition (input schema) or prefill","Handle everything by adjusting the temperature alone","Delete the conversation history every time to tidy the context"], "eEn": "To reliably enforce JSON format, either force the structure with the input schema of a tool definition, or fix the start of the response with prefill. Leaving it to free generation, relying only on temperature adjustment, or deleting the conversation history does not prevent a preamble from creeping in."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】複数のサブエージェントで並行調査するが互いの文脈が混ざる。対処は。","o":["各エージェントの会話履歴を増やす","全サブエージェントで文脈を共有する","temperatureを上げて多様化する","サブエージェントごとのコンテキスト分離"],"a":3,"e":"並行して調査するサブエージェントの文脈が混ざるなら、サブエージェントごとにコンテキストを分離する。文脈を全員で共有すれば混ざりが悪化し、会話履歴を増やしても、温度を上げて多様化しても、混ざりは解消されない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] Several subagents investigate in parallel, but their contexts get mixed. What is the fix?", "oEn": ["Increase each agent's conversation history","Share context across all subagents","Raise the temperature to diversify","Isolate the context for each subagent"], "eEn": "If the contexts of subagents investigating in parallel get mixed, isolate the context for each subagent. Sharing context among all of them makes the mixing worse, and neither increasing conversation history nor raising the temperature to diversify resolves it."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【シナリオ】RAG（Retrieval-Augmented Generation）が無関係な文書を取得し回答が誤る。最初に改善すべき箇所は。","o":["利用可能なツールの総数","生成temperatureの設定","生成応答の最大トークン数の上限値","検索（リトリーバル）精度"],"a":3,"e":"無関係な文書が取得されるなら、原因は検索の段階にある。チャンクサイズや検索手法を改善して検索（リトリーバル）精度を上げるのが最初の手だ。生成時のtemperatureや応答の最大トークン数を変えても、取得される文書は変わらない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) retrieves irrelevant documents and answers are wrong. Where should you improve first?", "oEn": ["The total number of available tools","The generation temperature setting","The upper limit of the maximum tokens of the generated response","Retrieval accuracy"], "eEn": "If irrelevant documents are retrieved, the cause is in the search step, so the first fix is to improve retrieval accuracy through chunk size and search method. Changing the generation temperature or the maximum response length does not change which documents are retrieved."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【シナリオ】ローカルの社内DBにClaude Codeから接続したい。最適なMCP（Model Context Protocol）トランスポートは。","o":["stdio（標準入出力）","FTPによるファイル転送","WebSocketのみでの接続","HTTP/SSE（サーバー送信）"],"a":0,"e":"ローカルの社内DBへ同じマシン上から接続するなら、MCPのstdio（標準入出力）が単純で速い。サーバーを子プロセスとして起動し、ネットワークを介さずにやり取りできる。HTTP/SSEはリモートサーバー向けで、FTPによるファイル転送はMCPの接続方式ではない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want to connect to a local internal DB from Claude Code. What is the best MCP (Model Context Protocol) transport?", "oEn": ["stdio (standard input/output)","File transfer via FTP","A connection over WebSocket only","HTTP/SSE (server-sent events)"], "eEn": "To reach a local internal database from the same machine, MCP's stdio transport is simple and fast. The server runs as a child process and communicates over standard input and output without the network. HTTP/SSE is aimed at remote servers, and FTP file transfer is not an MCP connection method."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【シナリオ】本番エージェントの劣化に気づくのが遅い。継続的な品質担保に必要なものは。","o":["会話履歴を長く保持する運用","利用ツールの数を増やす対応","自動評価と監視指標・アラート","temperatureの調整"],"a":2,"e":"本番エージェントの劣化に早く気づくには、自動評価と監視指標、アラートが必要。会話履歴を長く保持しても、ツールを増やしても、温度を調整しても、劣化の検知にはつながらない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You notice degradation of a production agent too late. What is needed to maintain quality continuously?", "oEn": ["Keeping conversation history for a long time","Increasing the number of tools used","Automated evaluation, monitoring metrics, and alerts","Adjusting the temperature"], "eEn": "To notice degradation of a production agent early, you need automated evaluation, monitoring metrics, and alerts. Keeping conversation history longer, adding tools, or adjusting the temperature does not lead to detecting degradation."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】入力種別ごとに処理が分かれ、各種別の件数が事前に確定している業務がある。ボーティングでもオーケストレーターでもなく最適なのはどれか。","o":["ルーティング＋並列化（セクショニング）の組み合わせ","単一エージェントの自律ループによる処理","評価者・最適化者による段階的な反復改善","オーケストレーター・ワーカーによる動的なタスク分解"],"a":0,"e":"種別が確定＝動的分割不要なのでオーケストレーターは過剰。分類（ルーティング）後に独立処理を並列実行する固定構成が最適。サブタスク数が可変ならオーケストレーターを選ぶ。", "qEn": "[Advanced] A task splits by input type, and the count for each type is fixed in advance. Neither voting nor an orchestrator is the best fit. Which one is?", "oEn": ["A combination of routing and parallelization (sectioning)","Processing by a single agent's autonomous loop","Stepwise iterative improvement by an evaluator-optimizer","Dynamic task decomposition by orchestrator-workers"], "eEn": "Fixed types mean no dynamic splitting is needed, so an orchestrator is overkill. A fixed configuration that classifies (routing) and then runs independent processing in parallel is best. If the number of subtasks is variable, choose an orchestrator."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】サブエージェントに調査を委譲したが、親が「結論だけ欲しいのに大量の生ログが返り親の窓を圧迫」した。設計上の誤りはどれか。","o":["サブエージェントに要約して返す責務を持たせていない","サブエージェントの数が少なすぎる構成にしている","親のツール数が多すぎて選択を誤っている","temperatureが低すぎて出力が硬直している"],"a":0,"e":"コンテキスト分離の利点は『親が要約のみ受け取る』こと。生ログをそのまま返すと分離の意味が薄れる。サブエージェント側で要約・抽出してから返す設計が必要。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Research was delegated to a subagent, but although the parent wanted only the conclusion, a large amount of raw logs came back and squeezed the parent's window. What is the design error?", "oEn": ["The subagent was not given the responsibility to summarize before returning","The configuration has too few subagents","The parent has too many tools and selects wrongly","The temperature is too low and the output is rigid"], "eEn": "The advantage of context isolation is that the parent receives only a summary. Returning raw logs as they are undermines the point of isolation. The design needs the subagent to summarize and extract before returning."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】停止条件を『タスク完了の自己申告』のみにしたところ、未完了でも完了と報告し処理が止まった。最も適切な補強はどれか。","o":["temperatureを上げて出力の多様性を高める","利用可能なツールを増やして選択肢を広げる","最大反復回数の上限だけを新たに設定して制御する","客観的な成功基準による検証ステップ（評価者）を追加する"],"a":3,"e":"自己申告は楽観的に倒れやすい。反復上限は『止める』だけで『正しく完了したか』は保証しない。生成と評価を分離し客観基準で確認する評価者ステップが本質的解決。", "qEn": "[Advanced] When the stopping condition was only a \"self-report of task completion\", the agent reported completion even though the task was unfinished, and processing stopped. What is the most appropriate reinforcement?", "oEn": ["Raise the temperature to increase the diversity of the output","Add available tools to broaden the options","Newly set only a maximum iteration limit to control it","Add a verification step (evaluator) with objective success criteria"], "eEn": "Self-reports tend to lean optimistic. An iteration limit only \"stops\" it and does not guarantee it \"finished correctly\". An evaluator step that separates generation from evaluation and checks against objective criteria is the essential fix."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】次のうち『マルチエージェントにすべきでない』兆候として最も強いものはどれか。","o":["サブタスク間に強い逐次依存があり、前の結果が次の入力を決める","親の文脈を汚さず並行して処理を進めたい状況である","複数の調査方向が互いに独立していて同時並行で進められる状況である","各サブタスクが個別の専門知識を要し分業が有効である"],"a":0,"e":"逐次依存が強いと並列化の利点が消え、調整オーバーヘッドだけが残る。独立・並列分解可能・専門分化・文脈分離はいずれもマルチ採用の根拠になる。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Which of the following is the strongest sign that you should NOT use a multi-agent setup?", "oEn": ["Subtasks are strongly sequential, with each result determining the next input","You want to proceed in parallel without polluting the parent's context","Multiple research directions are independent of each other and can proceed at the same time","Each subtask needs separate specialized knowledge, so division of labor is effective"], "eEn": "Strong sequential dependency removes the benefit of parallelization and leaves only coordination overhead. Independence, parallel decomposability, specialization, and context isolation are all grounds for adopting multi-agent."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】コストが想定の3倍に膨らんだエージェントを調査した。ターン数は想定通りだったが入力トークンだけ激増していた。最も疑うべき原因はどれか。","o":["毎ターン履歴全体を再送しており、キャッシュも圧縮もしていない","出力トークンが毎ターン長すぎて全体を圧迫している","temperatureが高すぎて出力が毎回不安定になっている","各ツールの戻り値が構造化されておらず肥大化している"],"a":0,"e":"ターン数が正常なのに入力だけ増えるのは履歴累積の再送が主因。プロンプトキャッシュや要約で固定部分・過去履歴の再処理を抑えるのが対処。出力長やtemperatureは入力トークン累積の主因ではない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] You investigated an agent whose cost ballooned to three times what was expected. The number of turns was as expected, but only input tokens had surged. What cause should you suspect most?", "oEn": ["The entire history is resent every turn, with neither caching nor compression","Output tokens are too long every turn and are straining the total","The temperature is too high and the output is unstable every time","Each tool's return value is unstructured and has bloated"], "eEn": "When the turn count is normal but only input grows, the main cause is resending the accumulated history. The remedy is to use prompt caching or summarization to reduce reprocessing of the fixed part and past history. Output length and temperature are not the main cause of accumulating input tokens."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】ヒューマン・イン・ザ・ループと権限最小化はどう使い分けるのが正しいか。","o":["どちらか一方だけで十分なので権限は制限せず承認だけで対応すればよい","権限最小化とはすべての読み取り操作を例外なく全面的に禁止しエージェントを無力化することを指す","承認は低リスクの操作にこそ最も重点的に挟むのが本来の正しい運用である","権限最小化で危険な操作を構造的に制限し、それでも必要な高リスク操作には承認を挟む（併用）"],"a":3,"e":"両者は排他でなく層を成す。まず権限で行動空間を絞り、残る不可避な高リスク操作に承認を重ねる。安全設計は単層でなく多層で考える。", "qEn": "[Advanced] What is the correct way to use human-in-the-loop and least privilege together?", "oEn": ["Either one alone is enough, so permissions need not be restricted at all and approval alone will do","Least privilege means banning every read operation without exception and thereby disabling the agent entirely","Approval is properly placed most heavily on low-risk operations","Use both: least privilege to restrict dangerous operations, and approval for high-risk ones still needed"], "eEn": "The two are not exclusive but form layers. First narrow the action space with permissions, then add approval for the unavoidable high-risk operations that remain. Think of safety design in multiple layers, not a single layer."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】ツールを18個から5個に統合したら選択精度が上がったが、ある複合操作だけ失敗が増えた。最も妥当な解釈はどれか。","o":["すべてをMCPに移行すれば失敗はすべて解決する","統合で粒度が粗くなりすぎ、その操作に必要な細かい制御が失われた","ツールは常に少ないほど良いのでこの操作の失敗は単なる偶然にすぎない","temperatureを下げれば失敗はすべて解決する"],"a":1,"e":"ツール削減は選択精度を上げるが、過度な統合は粒度を粗くし柔軟性を奪う。少数化と適切な粒度は別軸。失敗した操作だけ粒度を見直すのが筋。", "qEn": "[Advanced] After consolidating tools from 18 to 5, selection accuracy improved, but failures increased for one particular compound operation. What is the most reasonable interpretation?", "oEn": ["Moving everything to MCP will resolve all failures","Consolidation made granularity too coarse, losing the fine control that operation needs","Fewer tools are always better, so the failures of this particular operation are mere coincidence","Lowering the temperature will resolve all failures"], "eEn": "Reducing tools raises selection accuracy, but over-consolidation makes granularity coarse and removes flexibility. Having fewer tools and having the right granularity are separate axes. The sound approach is to revisit the granularity for just the operation that failed."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】MCP（Model Context Protocol）ツールがタイムアウトを返した。errorCategoryと再試行方針の組み合わせとして正しいのはどれか。","o":["permanent と判定し、即座に恒久的失敗として処理を打ち切る","validation と判定し、引数を修正して再試行する","transient と判定し、指数バックオフ付きで再試行する","permission と判定し、直ちに管理者へエスカレーションする"],"a":2,"e":"タイムアウトは一時的障害＝transient。同じ引数のまま待機を挟んで再試行するのが適切。validationは引数誤り、permissionは権限不足で、いずれもタイムアウトには当てはまらない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] An MCP (Model Context Protocol) tool returned a timeout. Which combination of errorCategory and retry policy is correct?", "oEn": ["Classify as permanent and immediately abort as a permanent failure","Classify as validation and retry after fixing the arguments","Classify as transient and retry with exponential backoff","Classify as permission and escalate to an administrator immediately"], "eEn": "A timeout is a temporary failure, i.e. transient. It is appropriate to wait and retry with the same arguments. Validation means incorrect arguments and permission means insufficient authorization; neither applies to a timeout."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】ツールが『空の結果』と『アクセス失敗』を同じ空配列で返している。生じる最大の問題はどれか。","o":["tool_choiceの強制が効かなくなる","失敗を成功と誤認し、再試行すべき場面で再試行されない","結果が常に大きくなりすぎてコンテキスト全体を圧迫する","認証フローが二重に走り無駄な処理が重複する"],"a":1,"e":"『無かった（空）』と『取れなかった（失敗）』の混同はアンチパターン。失敗を空成功に偽装すると、本来必要な再試行やエスカレーションが発火しない。両者は構造化エラーで区別する。", "qEn": "[Advanced] A tool returns the same empty array for both \"empty result\" and \"access failure\". What is the biggest problem this causes?", "oEn": ["Forcing with tool_choice stops working","A failure is mistaken for success, and no retry occurs where one is needed","Results always become too large and strain the whole context","The authentication flow runs twice and wasteful processing is duplicated"], "eEn": "Confusing \"there was nothing (empty)\" with \"could not retrieve (failure)\" is an anti-pattern. If a failure is disguised as an empty success, the retry or escalation that is actually needed never fires. Distinguish the two with structured errors."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】tool_choiceを『auto』にしているが、構造化データを必ずJSONで得たい。最も確実な変更はどれか。","o":["temperatureを0に固定して再現性を高める","過去の会話履歴を全て消去してから改めて依頼する","特定ツールを名指しで強制し、その入力スキーマで形式を縛る","プロンプトで『JSONで出して』と強めに頼む"],"a":2,"e":"autoはテキストも返しうるため確実でない。特定ツールを強制（forced）すれば必ずそのスキーマ準拠の構造化出力が得られる。プロンプト依頼やtemperature調整は強制力が弱い。", "qEn": "[Advanced] tool_choice is set to \"auto\", but you want structured data to always come back as JSON. What is the most reliable change?", "oEn": ["Fix the temperature at 0 to improve output reproducibility","Erase the entire past conversation history and then make the same request again","Force a specific tool by name, and bind the format with its input schema","Ask firmly in the prompt, \"Output in JSON\""], "eEn": "auto may also return text, so it is not reliable. Forcing a specific tool (forced) always yields structured output that conforms to its schema. Asking in the prompt or adjusting the temperature has weak enforcement power."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】顧客サポート エージェントが、返金処理の途中でツール呼び出しがタイムアウトし、同じ返金を2回実行してしまった。今後この種の事故を構造的に防ぐ設計として最も的確なのはどれか。","o":["タイムアウトの上限時間を大幅に延ばし、処理が毎回最後まで完了する確率を高めて再発を防ぐ","返金ツールのtemperatureを0に固定して毎回の出力を安定させる","返金ツールに冪等キー（idempotency key）を持たせ、同一キーの再実行を無効化する","返金の実行前に必ずCoT（思考の連鎖）で手順を段階的に推論させてから処理する"],"a":2,"e":"二重実行はリトライと副作用の組み合わせで起きる。冪等キーで「同じ操作は何度呼んでも一度しか効かない」ことを保証するのが根本対策。タイムアウト延長は確率を下げるだけ、temperatureやCoTは副作用の重複とは無関係。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A customer support agent's tool call timed out midway through a refund and the same refund was executed twice. Which design most precisely prevents this kind of incident structurally from now on?", "oEn": ["Greatly extend the timeout limit to raise the probability that processing completes every time and prevent a recurrence","Fix the temperature of the refund tool at 0 to stabilize the output each time","Give the refund tool an idempotency key and make re-execution with the same key a no-op","Always have it reason through the steps with CoT (chain of thought) before processing a refund"], "eEn": "Double execution arises from the combination of retries and side effects. The root fix is to guarantee with an idempotency key that \"the same operation takes effect only once no matter how many times it is called\". Extending the timeout only lowers the probability, and temperature and CoT have nothing to do with duplicated side effects."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】10件の独立した競合製品を同時に調査し、最後に比較表へ統合したい。各調査は重い検索を伴い、件数は常に10で固定。最も適切な構成はどれか。","o":["オーケストレーター・ワーカー構成を用いて各調査を動的に分割し必要に応じて順次実行する","並列化（セクショニング）で10件を分担実行し、統合ステップで比較表を生成する","評価者・最適化者ループで各調査結果を反復的に評価し改善する","プロンプト チェイニングで10件を1件ずつ順番に直列処理する"],"a":1,"e":"件数が固定＝動的分割は不要なのでオーケストレーターは過剰。独立タスクを同時実行するセクショニングが最適で、統合は別ステップが担う。チェイニングは直列で遅く、評価者・最適化者は反復改善用途。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want to investigate 10 independent competing products at the same time and finally combine them into a comparison table. Each investigation involves heavy searching, and the count is always fixed at 10. What is the most appropriate configuration?", "oEn": ["Use an orchestrator-workers configuration to split each investigation dynamically and run them sequentially as needed","Use parallelization (sectioning) to run the 10 in parallel, then build the table in an integration step","Use an evaluator-optimizer loop to evaluate and improve each result iteratively","Use prompt chaining to process the 10 one at a time in series"], "eEn": "A fixed count means dynamic splitting is unnecessary, so an orchestrator is overkill. Sectioning, which runs independent tasks at the same time, is best, and a separate step handles the integration. Chaining is serial and slow, and evaluator-optimizer is for iterative improvement."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】長時間タスクで、エージェントが20ターン目あたりから当初要件と無関係な作業を始めた。観測ログでは各ツール呼び出し自体は成功している。最初に講じるべき対策はどれか。","o":["定期的に目標と制約を再注入し、各ステップで計画との整合を検証する","会話履歴を全て削除してからタスクを最初から再開する","利用できるツールをいくつか追加して行動の選択肢を大きく広げてみる","temperatureを上げて出力に多様性を持たせる"],"a":0,"e":"ツールが成功しているのに脱線するのは目標漂流（goal drift）。目標・計画の再注入と整合チェックが要。ツール追加やtemperature上昇はむしろ悪化させ、履歴全削除は文脈ごと失う。", "qEn": "[Scenario] In a long-running task, the agent started doing work unrelated to the original requirements around turn 20. In the observability logs, each tool call itself succeeded. What measure should be taken first?", "oEn": ["Periodically re-inject the goal and constraints, and verify consistency with the plan at each step","Delete the entire conversation history and restart the task from the beginning","Add a few available tools to greatly expand the agent's action options","Raise the temperature to give the output diversity"], "eEn": "Going off track while tools succeed is goal drift. Re-injecting the goal and plan and checking consistency are key. Adding tools or raising the temperature would make it worse, and deleting the whole history loses the context altogether."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】サブエージェントへ調査を委譲する設計で、親のコンテキスト消費を最小化するために最も効くのはどれか。","o":["サブエージェントの数を増やして調査の並列度を上げる","サブエージェント側で要約・抽出を済ませ、親へは結論と根拠のみを返す","親がサブエージェントの生ログを全件保持して後で参照する","親エージェントのtemperatureを下げて出力の再現性を高める"],"a":1,"e":"コンテキスト分離の価値は『親が要約だけ受け取る』点にある。生ログを親に渡すと分離の意味が消える。サブ数やtemperatureは親の消費量の本質的要因ではない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] In a design that delegates research to subagents, what is most effective for minimizing the parent's context consumption?", "oEn": ["Increase the number of subagents to raise the parallelism of research","Have each subagent finish summarizing and extracting, and return only the conclusion and its basis to the parent","Have the parent keep all raw logs from the subagents to consult later","Lower the parent agent's temperature to improve output reproducibility"], "eEn": "The value of context isolation is that \"the parent receives only a summary\". Handing raw logs to the parent erases the point of isolation. The number of subagents and the temperature are not essential factors in the parent's consumption."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】自律エージェントに「完了したら停止」とだけ指示したところ、未完了でも『完了した』と報告して止まった。停止判定を信頼できるものにする最善策はどれか。","o":["モデルの自己申告した確信度が十分に高い場合にのみ停止させる","停止条件をプロンプト内でより強く明確な表現に繰り返し言い換える","最大反復回数の上限だけを設定してその回数に達した時点で強制的に処理を打ち切らせる","客観的な成功基準を定義し、独立した検証ステップで合否を判定してから停止させる"],"a":3,"e":"自己申告は楽観に倒れやすく、反復上限は『止める』だけで『正しく終わったか』を保証しない。生成と評価を分離し客観基準で検証するのが本質。言い換えは強制力を持たない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] An autonomous agent was told only \"stop when done\", and it reported \"done\" and stopped even though the task was unfinished. What is the best measure for making the stop decision trustworthy?", "oEn": ["Stop only when the model's self-reported confidence is high enough","Repeatedly rephrase the stopping condition in the prompt using stronger, clearer wording","Set only a maximum iteration cap, and forcibly abort processing once that count is reached","Define objective success criteria and verify with an independent step before stopping"], "eEn": "Self-reports tend to lean optimistic, and an iteration cap only \"stops\" the agent without guaranteeing it \"finished correctly\". The essential fix is to separate generation from evaluation and verify against objective criteria. Rewording has no enforcing power."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】あるエージェントのコストが想定の3倍に膨らんだ。ターン数は想定通りだが、ターンごとの入力トークンが線形に増加していた。最も妥当な原因と対策の組み合わせはどれか。","o":["temperatureが高すぎるのが原因。0に下げて出力を安定させる","履歴の累積再送が原因。プロンプトキャッシュや要約で固定部分・過去履歴の再処理を抑える","出力トークンが長すぎるのが原因。max_tokensを下げて1件あたりの生成量を抑える","ツール定義の数が多いのが原因。不要なツールを削減して定義量を減らす"],"a":1,"e":"ターン数一定で入力だけ線形増加は、毎ターン履歴全体を再送している兆候。キャッシュや要約が対策。出力長・ツール数・temperatureは入力トークンの線形累積の主因ではない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] An agent's cost ballooned to three times what was expected. The number of turns is as expected, but input tokens per turn were increasing linearly. Which combination of most plausible cause and remedy is correct?", "oEn": ["The cause is a temperature that is too high. Lower it to 0 to stabilize the output","The cause is cumulative resending of history. Cut reprocessing with prompt caching or summarization","The cause is output tokens that are too long. Lower max_tokens to limit the amount of output generated per request","The cause is a large number of tool definitions. Remove unnecessary tools to reduce the definition size"], "eEn": "A constant number of turns with only input growing linearly is a sign that the entire history is resent every turn. Caching or summarization is the remedy. Output length, the number of tools, and temperature are not the main cause of linear accumulation of input tokens."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】次のうち、単一エージェントではなくマルチエージェント構成を採用する根拠として最も弱いものはどれか。","o":["親エージェントの文脈を各専門調査の細かな詳細情報で汚したくない","調査すべき方向が複数あり互いに独立している","各領域が高度な専門知識を要し分業の効果が大きい","各サブタスクが前段の結果に強く依存し、順序を変えられない"],"a":3,"e":"強い逐次依存は並列性の利点を消し、調整コストだけが残るためマルチの根拠として最も弱い。独立性・専門分業・文脈分離はいずれもマルチ採用を後押しする要因。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Which of the following is the weakest ground for adopting a multi-agent configuration rather than a single agent?", "oEn": ["You do not want to pollute the parent agent's context with the fine details of each specialized investigation","There are multiple directions to investigate and they are independent of each other","Each area requires advanced specialized knowledge, so division of labor is highly effective","Each subtask depends strongly on the result of the previous stage, and the order cannot be changed"], "eEn": "Strong sequential dependency removes the advantage of parallelism and leaves only coordination cost, so it is the weakest ground for multi-agent. Independence, specialized division of labor, and context isolation are all factors that favor adopting multi-agent."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】ヒューマン・イン・ザ・ループ（HITL）と権限最小化を併用する設計思想として正しいのはどれか。","o":["権限最小化とは読み取りを含む全ての操作を一律に禁止することを指す","どちらか一方で十分なので権限は広く開けたまま全ての操作をHITLのみで確認する","権限で危険な行動空間を構造的に絞り、それでも残る不可避な高リスク操作にHITLを重ねる","HITLは高リスク操作よりむしろ低リスク操作にこそ優先して適用する"],"a":2,"e":"両者は排他でなく多層防御の層を成す。まず権限で行動空間を狭め、残る不可避な高リスク操作に承認を重ねる。HITLは高リスク操作向けで、権限最小化は読み取り禁止のことではない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Which is the correct design philosophy for using human-in-the-loop (HITL) together with least privilege?", "oEn": ["Least privilege means uniformly prohibiting all operations, including reads","Either one is enough, so leave permissions wide open and operate by confirming every operation with HITL alone","Narrow the dangerous action space via permissions, then layer HITL on the unavoidable high-risk operations","Apply HITL with priority to low-risk operations rather than to high-risk ones"], "eEn": "The two are not exclusive; they form layers of defense in depth. First narrow the action space with permissions, then add approval for the unavoidable high-risk operations that remain. HITL is for high-risk operations, and least privilege does not mean banning reads."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】評価で『全体97%正解』だが、本番では特定タイプの入力でだけ事故が頻発する。評価設計の改善として最も的確なのはどれか。","o":["temperatureを下げてから全体を再評価する","入力タイプ別に層化抽出して評価し、タイプごとの正答率を個別に測る","評価データの件数を倍に増やして全体で再度評価する","評価全体の合格基準を97%から99%へとさらに一段大きく引き上げる"],"a":1,"e":"全体精度は特定タイプの低精度を覆い隠す（集計精度の罠）。層化抽出でタイプ別に測れば弱点が露見する。件数増や基準引き上げ、temperature変更では型別の偏りは見えない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] Evaluation shows \"97% correct overall\", but in production incidents occur frequently only for a certain type of input. Which improvement to the evaluation design is most precise?", "oEn": ["Lower the temperature and then re-evaluate everything","Use stratified sampling by input type and measure each type's accuracy separately","Double the number of evaluation items and evaluate everything again","Raise the overall pass threshold of the whole evaluation yet another notch from 97% to 99%"], "eEn": "Overall accuracy masks low accuracy for a specific type (the aggregate-accuracy trap). Measuring by type with stratified sampling exposes the weak spots. Increasing the count, raising the threshold, or changing the temperature will not reveal per-type bias."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【シナリオ】MCP（Model Context Protocol）ツールが断続的にタイムアウトを返す。errorCategoryの分類と対処の組み合わせとして正しいのはどれか。","o":["permissionと分類し、権限不足として即座に管理者へエスカレーションする","transientと分類し、指数バックオフ付きで上限回数まで再試行する","validationと分類し、引数を修正して再試行する","permanentと分類し、恒久的失敗として即座に処理を打ち切る"],"a":1,"e":"タイムアウトは一時的障害＝transientで、同じ引数のまま待機して再試行するのが定石。validationは引数誤り、permissionは権限不足の分類で、いずれもタイムアウトには該当しない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] An MCP (Model Context Protocol) tool intermittently returns timeouts. Which combination of errorCategory classification and handling is correct?", "oEn": ["Classify as permission and escalate to an administrator immediately as insufficient authorization","Classify as transient and retry with exponential backoff up to a maximum number of attempts","Classify as validation and retry after fixing the arguments","Classify as permanent and abort immediately as a permanent failure"], "eEn": "A timeout is a temporary failure, i.e. transient, and the standard approach is to wait and retry with the same arguments. Validation is a classification for incorrect arguments and permission for insufficient authorization; neither applies to a timeout."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】18個あったツールを5個に統合したら全体の選択精度は上がったが、ある複合操作だけ失敗が増えた。最も妥当な解釈はどれか。","o":["temperatureを下げれば複合操作の失敗も解決する","MCP（Model Context Protocol）に移行すれば自動的に解決する","ツールは少ないほど常に良いので今回の失敗は偶然である","過度な統合で粒度が粗くなり、その操作に必要な細かい制御が失われた"],"a":3,"e":"ツール削減は選択精度を上げるが、統合しすぎると粒度が粗くなり柔軟性を失う。少数化と適切な粒度は別の軸であり、失敗した操作だけ粒度を見直すのが筋。temperatureやMCP移行は本質と無関係。", "qEn": "[Advanced] After consolidating 18 tools into 5, overall selection accuracy improved, but failures increased for one particular compound operation. What is the most reasonable interpretation?", "oEn": ["Lowering the temperature will also resolve the failures of that one compound operation","Migrating to MCP (Model Context Protocol) will resolve it automatically","Fewer tools are always better, so this failure must just be a coincidence","Over-consolidation made granularity too coarse and lost needed fine-grained control"], "eEn": "Reducing tools raises selection accuracy, but consolidating too much makes granularity coarse and loses flexibility. Having fewer tools and having the right granularity are separate axes, and the sound approach is to revisit the granularity for just the operation that failed. Temperature and migrating to MCP are unrelated to the essence."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【シナリオ】あるツールが『該当データなし』と『アクセス失敗』をどちらも空配列で返している。本番で起きうる最も深刻な問題はどれか。","o":["調査結果が常に大きくなりすぎてコンテキスト全体を大きく圧迫してしまう","tool_choiceによるツール強制が効かなくなる","認証フローが二重に走ってしまい無駄な処理が重複する","失敗を成功と誤認し、本来必要な再試行やエスカレーションが発火しない"],"a":3,"e":"『無かった（空）』と『取れなかった（失敗）』の混同はアンチパターン。失敗を空成功に偽装すると回復処理が起動しない。両者は構造化エラー（isError等）で明確に区別する。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A tool returns an empty array for both \"no matching data\" and \"access failure\". What is the most serious problem that can occur in production?", "oEn": ["Investigation results always become too large and put heavy pressure on the whole context","Forcing a tool with tool_choice stops working","The authentication flow runs twice and wasteful processing is duplicated","A failure is mistaken for success, so the needed retry or escalation never fires"], "eEn": "Confusing \"there was nothing (empty)\" with \"could not retrieve (failure)\" is an anti-pattern. If a failure is disguised as an empty success, recovery processing never starts. Distinguish the two clearly with structured errors (such as isError)."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】社内DBへローカル接続するMCP（Model Context Protocol）サーバーで、認証情報の扱いとして本番運用に最も適切なのはどれか。","o":["データベース接続の設定ファイルに認証情報を平文で書き、アクセス権限だけで保護する","認証情報をコードに直書きし、.gitignoreで対象ファイルを除外する","データベース接続用の認証トークンをツールの説明文に直接記載して参照させる","環境変数展開（${DB_TOKEN}等）で注入し、設定ファイルやコードに秘密を埋め込まない"],"a":3,"e":"秘密はコード・設定・説明文のいずれにも埋め込まず、環境変数で注入するのが原則。平文や直書きは漏えいリスクが高く、説明文への記載はプロンプトに露出するため論外。", "qEn": "[Advanced] For an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that connects locally to an internal DB, what is the most appropriate handling of credentials for production?", "oEn": ["Write the credentials in plain text in the database connection config file and protect them only with file access permissions","Hardcode the credentials in the code and exclude the file with .gitignore","Write the database authentication token directly in the tool description and have it referenced","Inject them through environment variable expansion (such as ${DB_TOKEN}) and do not embed secrets in config files or code"], "eEn": "As a rule, secrets are not embedded in code, config, or descriptions but injected through environment variables. Plain text and hardcoding carry a high risk of leakage, and writing them in a description is out of the question because it exposes them in the prompt."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】tool_choiceがautoのまま、構造化JSONを必ず得たい。最も確実な変更はどれか。","o":["temperatureを0に固定しばらつきを抑え形式を安定させる","モデルの出力の冒頭をプレフィルで{の文字から始めさせる","特定ツールを名指しで強制（forced）し、その入力スキーマで形式を縛る","プロンプトで『JSONのみで出力すること』と強く依頼する"],"a":2,"e":"autoはテキストも返しうるため不確実。ツール強制ならスキーマ準拠の構造化出力が保証される。プレフィルは出だしの制御に留まり、プロンプト依頼やtemperatureは強制力が弱い。", "qEn": "[Advanced] With tool_choice still set to auto, you want to always get structured JSON. What is the most reliable change?", "oEn": ["Fix the temperature at 0 to reduce variation in the output and stabilize the format","Have the model's output start with the character { by using prefill","Force a specific tool by name (forced) and bind the format to its input schema","Ask strongly in the prompt, \"Output only JSON\""], "eEn": "auto may also return text, so it is not certain. Forcing a tool guarantees structured output that conforms to the schema. Prefill only controls the beginning, and asking in the prompt or adjusting the temperature has weak enforcement power."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】ツールの戻り値が巨大で、数回の呼び出しでコンテキストが逼迫した。設計上の最善策はどれか。","o":["ツールの戻り値をそのまま全て返し、後段の処理で無視する","temperatureを下げてツールの出力を短くする","ツール側で要約・ページング・フィールド選択を行い、必要最小限だけ返す","さらに大きなコンテキスト窓を持つ上位モデルに置き換えるだけで対応する"],"a":2,"e":"巨大な戻り値はツール側で要約・ページング・射影して投入量を制御するのが本質。窓の拡大は一時しのぎ、全件返却は無駄、temperatureは戻り値サイズに無関係。", "qEn": "[Advanced] A tool's return value is huge, and the context became tight after a few calls. What is the best design measure?", "oEn": ["Return the tool's whole return value as is and ignore it in later processing","Lower the temperature to make the tool's output shorter","Summarize, paginate, and select fields on the tool side, and return only the necessary minimum","Handle it merely by switching to a higher-tier model with a larger context window"], "eEn": "For a huge return value, the essential approach is to control the amount injected by summarizing, paginating, and projecting on the tool side. Enlarging the window is a stopgap, returning everything is wasteful, and temperature has nothing to do with return value size."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】複数のMCP（Model Context Protocol）ツールを並列呼び出ししたところ、結果が不整合になった。最も疑うべき原因はどれか。","o":["temperatureが高く出力が不安定","ツール間に実行順序の依存があり、並列化で前提が崩れた","呼び出したツールの数が多すぎるのが原因である","各ツールの説明文が長すぎるのが原因である"],"a":1,"e":"並列呼び出しが安全なのは各実行が互いに独立な場合に限る。依存関係があると順序前提が崩れ不整合が出る。依存を明示し、依存があるものは直列化する。", "qEn": "[Advanced] When multiple MCP (Model Context Protocol) tools were called in parallel, the results were inconsistent. What cause should you suspect most?", "oEn": ["The temperature is high and the output is unstable","Order dependency between tools was broken by parallelization","The cause is that too many tools were called","The description of each tool is far too long"], "eEn": "Parallel calls are safe only when the executions are independent of each other. With dependencies, the order assumption breaks and inconsistencies appear. State dependencies explicitly and serialize the ones that have them."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】ツール定義の品質がエージェントの精度を左右する。最も効果が大きい改善はどれか。","o":["名前・説明・入力スキーマ・例・境界条件を明確化し、用途と誤用を判別可能にする","組織内の全てのツールの実装プログラミング言語を1つに統一して開発環境を揃える","各ツールの実装ファイルを全て1つのファイルにまとめて管理する","各ツールにバージョン番号を付けて世代を管理できるようにする"],"a":0,"e":"モデルにとってツール定義は実質プロンプト。名前・説明・スキーマ・例・境界の明確さが選択精度を決める。実装言語やファイル構成、版番号は精度の主因ではない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] The quality of tool definitions determines an agent's accuracy. Which improvement has the greatest effect?", "oEn": ["Clarify the name, description, input schema, examples, and boundary conditions so that intended use and misuse can be distinguished","Unify the implementation programming language of all tools in the organization into one to align the development environment","Combine the implementation files of all tools into a single file for management","Attach a version number to each tool so that generations can be managed"], "eEn": "To the model, a tool definition is effectively a prompt. The clarity of the name, description, schema, examples, and boundaries determines selection accuracy. The implementation language, file layout, and version numbers are not the main factors in accuracy."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【シナリオ】エラーを握りつぶして常に成功扱いにしていたら、モデルが誤った前提で処理を進め事故になった。設計原則として正しいのはどれか。","o":["発生した例外を全て内部で握りつぶし、後段の自動リトライ機構に処理を任せる","失敗は構造化エラーとして透過的に返し、モデルが自己修正・再試行できるようにする","エラーが発生した時点で必ずエージェント全体の処理を即停止する","エラーはUI上にだけ表示し、モデルには一切返さないようにする"],"a":1,"e":"過剰なエラー抑制は失敗を隠し誤った前提を生む。構造化エラーを返せばモデルは原因を理解し自己修正できる。握りつぶしや即停止、モデル非通知はいずれも回復力を奪う。", "qEn": "[Scenario] Errors were swallowed and always treated as success, so the model proceeded on a wrong assumption and caused an incident. Which design principle is correct?", "oEn": ["Swallow all exceptions internally and leave everything to a downstream automatic retry mechanism","Return failures transparently as structured errors so the model can self-correct and retry","Always stop the entire agent immediately the moment an error occurs","Show errors only in the UI and never return them to the model"], "eEn": "Excessive error suppression hides failures and creates wrong assumptions. If you return structured errors, the model can understand the cause and self-correct. Swallowing, stopping immediately, and not notifying the model all take away resilience."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【シナリオ】チーム共有のコード規約をAIに常時守らせたいが、個人の実験的設定はチームに影響させたくない。最適な設定配置はどれか。","o":["共有規約も個人設定も全てユーザー設定に書き、プロジェクト側には何も置かない運用にする","共有規約はプロジェクトのCLAUDE.md、個人設定はユーザー設定に置き、局所が上位を上書きする階層を使う","共有規約も個人の実験的設定も全てプロジェクトのCLAUDE.mdに書き、ユーザー設定は一切使わない運用にする","共有規約は設定ファイルには置かず、必要になった時にプロンプトで毎回貼り付けて渡す"],"a":1,"e":"プロジェクト設定はチーム共有、ユーザー設定は個人専用で、より局所的な階層が上書きする。これにより共有と個人を分離できる。全部同一階層に置くと分離できず、毎回貼り付けは非効率で漏れる。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want the AI to always follow the team's shared coding conventions, but you do not want an individual's experimental settings to affect the team. Which configuration placement is best?", "oEn": ["Write both shared conventions and personal settings in user settings, and put nothing on the project side","Shared conventions in the project's CLAUDE.md, personal settings in user settings; the more local level overrides","Write both shared conventions and personal experimental settings in the project's CLAUDE.md and never use user settings at all","Do not put shared conventions in a config file; paste them into the prompt each time they are needed"], "eEn": "Project settings are shared with the team, user settings are for an individual only, and the more local level overrides. This separates shared from personal. Putting everything at the same level cannot separate them, and pasting every time is inefficient and prone to omissions."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【シナリオ】編集のたびにフォーマットとテストを『確実に』実行させたい。プロンプトで依頼しても時々スキップされる。最も確実な手段はどれか。","o":["PostToolUse等のフックでイベント駆動の決定的強制として自動実行する","CLAUDE.mdに『編集後は必ず実行せよ』と明記して指示する","プラン モードに切り替えてから毎回の編集完了ごとに実行させる","利用者が専用のスラッシュコマンドを用意しておき、編集のたびに都度手動で実行する"],"a":0,"e":"フックはイベント駆動で確実に走るため、必須処理の決定的強制に向く。スラッシュコマンドは手動、CLAUDE.mdの記述は依頼に留まり強制力がない。プラン モードは変更前設計用。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want formatting and tests to be run \"reliably\" on every edit. Even when asked in the prompt, they are sometimes skipped. What is the most reliable means?", "oEn": ["Auto-run them from a hook such as PostToolUse, as deterministic event-driven enforcement","Instruct it by stating \"always run after editing\" in CLAUDE.md","Switch to plan mode and have it run at the completion of each edit","Have the user prepare a dedicated slash command and run it manually, case by case, after each edit"], "eEn": "Hooks run reliably because they are event-driven, which suits deterministic enforcement of mandatory steps. Slash commands are manual, and a statement in CLAUDE.md remains a request with no enforcing power. Plan mode is for design before making changes."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】破壊的操作（本番削除・送金）の自動許可方針として、リスクの非対称性に最も整合するのはどれか。","o":["読み取りも書き込みも破壊的な操作も、全ての操作を一律に自動で許可する","読み取りは広く自動許可、書き込みは対象を絞り、破壊的操作は承認必須とする","操作の種別や危険度に関わらずランダムに許可の可否を決める","読み取りを含む全ての操作を例外なく一律に承認必須として扱う"],"a":1,"e":"調査（読み取り）は安全だが変更・破壊は事故を生むという非対称性に応じて配分するのが原則。一律自動許可は危険、一律承認必須は非効率、ランダム許可は論外。", "qEn": "[Advanced] As an auto-approval policy for destructive operations (production deletion, money transfers), which best matches the asymmetry of risk?", "oEn": ["Automatically allow all operations uniformly, whether they are reads, writes, or destructive operations","Auto-allow reads broadly, narrow the scope of writes, require approval for destructive operations","Decide whether to allow an operation at random regardless of its type or risk","Treat all operations, including reads, uniformly as requiring approval without exception"], "eEn": "The principle is to allocate according to the asymmetry that investigation (reads) is safe while changes and destruction cause incidents. Uniform auto-approval is dangerous, uniform required approval is inefficient, and random approval is out of the question."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】長い対話セッションで精度が落ちコストも増えてきた。最も適切な対処はどれか。","o":["現在利用可能なツールをさらに複数追加してエージェント自身の能力を補強してみる","要約して新セッションを開始するか、/clearで無関係な文脈をリセットする","CLAUDE.mdを削除して読み込む文脈量そのものを減らす","temperatureを上げて発想の幅を広げ多様な出力を得る"],"a":1,"e":"履歴肥大は精度低下とコスト増を招く。要約しての再開や/clearでの文脈リセットが対処。ツール追加やtemperature変更は無関係で、CLAUDE.md削除は規約まで失う。", "qEn": "[Advanced] In a long interactive session, accuracy has dropped and cost has increased. What is the most appropriate action?", "oEn": ["Add several more of the currently available tools to reinforce the agent's own capabilities","Summarize and start a new session, or reset irrelevant context with /clear","Delete CLAUDE.md to reduce the amount of context loaded","Raise the temperature to widen the range of ideas and get more diverse output"], "eEn": "A bloated history causes lower accuracy and higher cost. The remedy is to summarize and restart, or reset the context with /clear. Adding tools or changing the temperature is unrelated, and deleting CLAUDE.md loses the conventions too."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】CIでプルリクエストの自動レビューを無人実行したい。最適なClaude Codeの使い方はどれか。","o":["通常の対話モードで起動し、各ステップの操作内容を人が都度画面で確認し承認して進める","プラン モードで起動し、実際の実行はせず計画だけを出力させる","対話画面で専用のスラッシュコマンドを人が手動で叩いて実行する","ヘッドレス（非対話）モードでコマンドとして起動し、構造化出力をパイプラインに渡す"],"a":3,"e":"ヘッドレスは人の介在なしにコマンド実行でき、JSON等の構造化出力でCIに統合できる。対話・手動コマンドは無人化に反し、プラン モードは実行を伴わない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] You want to run automated pull request reviews unattended in CI. What is the best way to use Claude Code?", "oEn": ["Start it in normal interactive mode and have a person check and approve each step's operations on screen as it goes","Start it in plan mode and have it output only a plan without actually executing","Have a person manually type a dedicated slash command on the interactive screen to run it","Start it as a command in headless (non-interactive) mode and pass its structured output to the pipeline"], "eEn": "Headless mode can run as a command without human involvement and integrates with CI through structured output such as JSON. Interactive and manual commands defeat unattended operation, and plan mode does not involve execution."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】SKILL.mdに context: fork と allowed-tools を設定する意図として正しいのはどれか。","o":["隔離サブ文脈で実行して親を汚さず、使用可能ツールを制限して安全性を高める","これまでの会話履歴を全て消去し、生成される出力を固定する","使用するモデルを複製し、それぞれの温度パラメータを変える","課金アカウントを実行ごとに分岐させ、表示するUI全体を複数の画面に分割する"],"a":0,"e":"context: forkは隔離サブ文脈での実行を、allowed-toolsはツール制限を意味し、親文脈の汚染防止と最小権限を両立する。課金分岐・モデル複製・履歴消去のいずれでもない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] What is the correct intent of setting context: fork and allowed-tools in SKILL.md?", "oEn": ["Run in an isolated sub-context to keep the parent clean, and limit usable tools for safety","Erase the entire conversation history so far and fix the generated output","Duplicate the model in use and vary the temperature parameter of each copy","Branch the billing account for each run and split the entire UI into multiple separate screens"], "eEn": "context: fork means running in an isolated sub-context and allowed-tools means restricting tools, together achieving both prevention of parent-context pollution and least privilege. It is none of billing branching, model duplication, or history erasure."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】CLAUDE.mdに書くべきでない情報はどれか。","o":["ビルドとテストの実行手順や日常的な開発コマンド","頻繁に変わる一時的な値やAPIキー等の機密","既知の落とし穴やハマりやすい注意点","プロジェクトのコーディング規約と命名規則"],"a":1,"e":"CLAUDE.mdは常時読み込まれる普遍的な規約・手順を書く場所。頻繁に変わる値や機密は別の安全な手段（環境変数等）で扱う。手順・規約・注意点は適切な記載対象。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Which information should NOT be written in CLAUDE.md?", "oEn": ["Procedures for building and testing, and everyday development commands","Frequently changing temporary values and secrets such as API keys","Known pitfalls and cautions where people tend to get stuck","The project's coding conventions and naming rules"], "eEn": "CLAUDE.md is the place for universal conventions and procedures that are always loaded. Frequently changing values and secrets should be handled by other safe means (such as environment variables). Procedures, conventions, and cautions are appropriate to include."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【シナリオ】サブディレクトリの設定がリポジトリルートの設定と矛盾した。どちらが優先されるか。","o":["階層に関わらず常にユーザー個人の設定が優先される","より局所的・近い階層（サブディレクトリ）の設定が上位を上書きする","設定の階層に関わらず常にリポジトリルート側の設定が優先して適用される","設定ファイルのサイズがより大きい方が常に優先される"],"a":1,"e":"設定はより局所的・近い階層が上位を上書きする。サブディレクトリ設定がルートを上書きするため、局所的な例外を表現できる。ユーザー優先やサイズ基準ではない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A subdirectory's settings conflict with the repository root's settings. Which takes precedence?", "oEn": ["The user's personal settings always take precedence regardless of hierarchy","The setting at the more local, closer level (the subdirectory) overrides the one above it","The repository root's settings are always applied with priority regardless of the settings hierarchy","The settings file with the larger size always takes precedence"], "eEn": "The more local, closer level overrides the one above. Because subdirectory settings override the root, local exceptions can be expressed. It is not user priority or file size."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】機能追加とリファクタリングを同一コミットに混ぜないことが推奨される主な理由はどれか。","o":["モデルのtemperatureが安定して生成される出力がぶれなくなる","変更の意図が明確になりレビューと原因切り分けが容易になる","変更が一括されるためビルドの処理が速くなる","全体のコミット数が減って履歴がすっきりする"],"a":1,"e":"目的別にコミットを分けると、レビュー時に意図が読み取りやすく、不具合時の原因切り分けも容易。コミット数やビルド速度、temperatureとは無関係。", "qEn": "[Advanced] What is the main reason it is recommended not to mix a feature addition and refactoring in the same commit?", "oEn": ["The model's temperature becomes stable and the generated output no longer fluctuates","Each change's intent is clear, so review and root-cause isolation are easier","Changes are bundled, so the build runs faster","The total number of commits decreases and the history becomes cleaner"], "eEn": "Splitting commits by purpose makes the intent easier to read during review and makes it easier to isolate the cause when a defect appears. It has nothing to do with the number of commits, build speed, or the temperature."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【シナリオ】出力が時々JSONから逸脱し前置き文が混入する。確実に形式を守らせる手段として最も強いのはどれか。","o":["出力をプレフィルで{の文字から始めさせて形式を誘導する","プロンプトで『JSONのみで出力せよ』と強く依頼する","ツール定義（入力スキーマ）で形式を強制し、構文エラーを排除する","temperatureを0まで下げて出力のばらつきを最小限に抑える"],"a":2,"e":"スキーマによる形式強制が最も確実で構文エラーを排除できる。プレフィルは出だしの制御、プロンプト依頼やtemperature低下は逸脱を減らすが保証はしない。強制力の順を理解しているかが問われる。", "qEn": "[Scenario] The output sometimes deviates from JSON and a preamble creeps in. Which is the strongest means of reliably enforcing the format?", "oEn": ["Steer the format toward JSON by making the output begin with the character { via prefill","Strongly request \"output JSON only\" in the prompt","Enforce the format with a tool definition (input schema), eliminating syntax errors","Lower the temperature to 0 to minimize output variation"], "eEn": "Format enforcement through a schema is the most reliable and eliminates syntax errors. Prefill controls only the beginning, and asking in the prompt or lowering the temperature reduces deviations but does not guarantee them. This tests whether you understand the order of enforcement strength."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】『保守的に判断せよ』という指示が精度向上に効かない理由として最も的確なのはどれか。","o":["指示文が長くなり全体の可読性が下がってしまうから","生成される出力に構文エラーを誘発しやすくなるから","余分なトークン消費が増えて全体の実行コストが上がってしまうから","『保守的』が測定不能な曖昧語で、モデルの解釈がばらつくから"],"a":3,"e":"曖昧語は解釈を分散させ結果を不安定にする。『確信度0.8未満は人間へ』のような測定可能な基準に置き換えるのが正解。長さ・コスト・構文は本質ではない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Which best explains why an instruction like \"judge conservatively\" does not improve accuracy?", "oEn": ["Because the instruction gets longer and overall readability drops","Because it tends to induce syntax errors in the generated output","Because extra token consumption increases and the overall execution cost ends up rising","Because \"conservative\" is a vague, unmeasurable word, so interpretations vary"], "eEn": "Vague words scatter interpretation and make results unstable. The right answer is to replace it with a measurable criterion such as \"escalate to a human if confidence is below 0.8\". Length, cost, and syntax are not the essence."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】スキーマ検証（型・必須・enum）で防げない誤りはどれか。","o":["スキーマで定義した型と実際に返る値の型の不一致","計算値と申告値の不一致など、形式は正しいが意味が矛盾する誤り","スキーマで必須と定義されたフィールドの値がそもそも欠落している","enumで許可された候補以外の想定外の値の混入"],"a":1,"e":"スキーマは構文・型・必須・列挙を強制できるが、意味的な整合（calculated vs stated等）は別途の検証層が要る。残り3つはスキーマで防げるため、防げないのは意味エラー。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Which error cannot be prevented by schema validation (type, required, enum)?", "oEn": ["A mismatch between the type defined in the schema and the type of the value that is actually returned","A well-formed but semantically contradictory error, e.g. calculated vs stated values","The value of a field defined as required in the schema is missing altogether","An unexpected value that is not among the candidates permitted by the enum"], "eEn": "A schema can enforce syntax, types, required fields, and enumerations, but semantic consistency (such as calculated vs stated) needs a separate validation layer. The other three can be prevented by a schema, so what cannot be prevented is the semantic error."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】値が存在しない場合の捏造（幻覚）を防ぐスキーマ設計はどれか。","o":["該当フィールドをnullable（null許容）にし、無い場合はnullを返させる","スキーマの全フィールドを必須（required）として定義する","スキーマの全てのフィールドを一律にstring型として定義する","出力スキーマに定義するフィールドの数を必要以上にできる限り多く増やして冗長にしておく"],"a":0,"e":"全必須にすると、値が無くてもモデルが無理に埋めて捏造する。nullableなら『無い』をnullで表現でき捏造を防げる。string化やフィールド増は捏造対策にならない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Which schema design prevents fabrication (hallucination) when a value does not exist?", "oEn": ["Make the field nullable, and have it return null when there is none","Define all fields in the schema as required","Define all fields in the schema uniformly as the string type","Increase the number of fields in the output schema as much as possible beyond what is necessary, making it redundant"], "eEn": "If everything is required, the model forces itself to fill in values even when there are none, and fabricates. If the field is nullable, \"none\" can be expressed as null, which prevents fabrication. Turning fields into strings or adding fields does not prevent fabrication."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】拡張可能な分類を実現しつつ未知パターンも取りこぼさないenum設計はどれか。","o":["出力のenumのみを使い、未知のパターンは全て強制的に最も近い既存の値へ丸める","出力のenumによる分類を一切使わず、全ての値を制約のない自由記述のテキストで受け取る","enumに加えて『other』値とdetailフィールドを併設し、未知は other+説明で受ける","出力の文字列ラベルを一切使わず、数値コードのみで全ての分類を表現して管理する"],"a":2,"e":"許可値で縛りつつotherとdetailで未知に対応するのが定石。自由文化は下流処理が不安定、最近傍丸めは誤分類、数値のみは可読性と拡張性を欠く。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Which enum design allows extensible classification while not missing unknown patterns?", "oEn": ["Use only the output enum, and forcibly round every unknown pattern to the nearest existing value","Do not use enum classification at all, and accept every value as unconstrained free-form text","Add \"other\" and a detail field to the enum; unknowns go in as other plus a description","Do not use string labels at all, and manage all classifications with numeric codes only"], "eEn": "The standard approach is to constrain with permitted values and handle unknowns with other and detail. Free-form text makes downstream processing unstable, rounding to the nearest value causes misclassification, and numbers alone lack readability and extensibility."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】独立レビュー インスタンスが自己レビューより優れる主因はどれか。","o":["レビュー結果を表示する画面のUIが見やすくなる","追加のAPIコストがゼロになり無償で実行できる","生成時の推論文脈を持たないため、微妙な問題を客観的に検出できる","レビュー全体の処理速度が必ず速くなり全体の待ち時間が大きく減る"],"a":2,"e":"生成者は自分の判断を疑いにくいというバイアスがある。独立インスタンスは生成文脈を持たず客観的に検証できる。速度・コスト・UIは本質ではない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] What is the main reason an independent review instance is better than self-review?", "oEn": ["The UI of the screen showing the review results becomes easier to read","The additional API cost becomes zero and it can run free of charge","Having no reasoning context from generation, it can detect subtle problems objectively","The overall review processing speed always becomes faster and total waiting time drops greatly"], "eEn": "A generator has a bias that makes it hard to doubt its own judgments. An independent instance has no generation context and can verify objectively. Speed, cost, and UI are not the essence."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】思考の連鎖（CoT）を常用すべきでない場面はどれか。","o":["多段の論理推論を要するタスク","複数制約を満たす計画立案","複雑な数式の計算","即答できる単純なタスク"],"a":3,"e":"CoTは複雑な推論・計算・計画で精度を上げるが、即答できる単純タスクではトークンとレイテンシを無駄に増やす。常用ではなく複雑タスクに限定するのが正しい。", "qEn": "[Advanced] In which situation should chain-of-thought (CoT) NOT be used routinely?", "oEn": ["Tasks requiring multi-step logical reasoning","Planning with multiple constraints","Calculating complex formulas","Simple tasks that can be answered immediately"], "eEn": "CoT raises accuracy on complex reasoning, calculation, and planning, but on simple tasks that can be answered immediately it wastes tokens and latency. The right approach is to limit it to complex tasks rather than use it routinely."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】夜間バッチで数千件のレポートを生成する。即時性は不要。最もコスト効率が良いのはどれか。","o":["各レポートの生成ごとにプロンプト全体を毎回一から新しく作り直して送信する","各リクエストのtemperatureを下げて出力を短くしトークンを節約する","Message Batches APIを使う（最大約50%節約・最大24時間・SLAなし）","通常の同期APIを使い、数千件のレポートを1件ずつ順番にリアルタイムで逐次的に即時処理する"],"a":2,"e":"待てる大量処理はBatches APIが最適で、約50%節約・最大24時間・SLAなしという特性が用途に合う。同期は割高、temperatureやプロンプト作り直しはコスト構造に効かない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] You generate thousands of reports in a nightly batch. Immediacy is not needed. Which is the most cost-efficient?", "oEn": ["Rebuild the entire prompt from scratch and send it anew for every report generation","Lower each request's temperature to shorten the output and save tokens","Use the Message Batches API (up to about 50% savings, up to 24 hours, no SLA)","Use the regular synchronous API and process thousands of reports one at a time, in order, in real time"], "eEn": "For bulk processing that can wait, the Batches API is best, and its characteristics of about 50% savings, up to 24 hours, and no SLA fit the use case. Synchronous calls are more expensive, and temperature or rebuilding prompts does not affect the cost structure."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【シナリオ】同一の長い社内規約（数千トークン）を毎リクエストの先頭に付けて1万件処理する。コスト削減に最も効くのはどれか。","o":["各リクエストのtemperatureを下げて出力を安定させる","プロンプトキャッシュを使い、固定接頭辞を先頭に、可変部分を後方に配置する","利用できるツールをいくつか追加してエージェントの能力を補う","各リクエストのたびにこれまでの会話履歴を毎回全て削除してから最初から送り直す"],"a":1,"e":"固定の長い接頭辞を繰り返し送る状況はプロンプトキャッシュが最も効く。固定→可変の順にするとヒット率が最大化する。履歴削除やtemperature、ツール追加は再処理コストに無関係。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You process 10,000 items, each request prefixed with the same long set of internal rules (thousands of tokens). What is most effective for reducing cost?", "oEn": ["Lower each request's temperature to stabilize the output","Use prompt caching, placing the fixed prefix first and the variable part after it","Add several available tools to supplement the agent's capabilities","With every request, delete the entire conversation history so far and resend from the beginning"], "eEn": "Prompt caching is most effective when a fixed long prefix is sent repeatedly. Putting the fixed part before the variable part maximizes the hit rate. Deleting history, temperature, and adding tools are unrelated to reprocessing cost."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【シナリオ】頻繁に更新される製品カタログに基づき正確に回答させたい。出典提示も必要。最適手法はどれか。","o":["長いコンテキスト窓に製品カタログ全体を毎回そのまま丸ごと投入して回答させる","RAG（検索拡張生成）で実行時に最新情報を取得し、出典付きで回答させる","ファインチューニングで最新の知識をモデルの重みに焼き込む","各回答時にtemperatureを細かく調整して精度を上げる"],"a":1,"e":"頻繁更新かつ出典が要る用途はRAGが最適で、再訓練不要・即時更新・出典提示が可能。ファインチューニングは更新に弱く、全件投入はコスト過大、temperatureは無関係。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want accurate answers based on a frequently updated product catalog, and citing sources is also required. What is the best approach?", "oEn": ["Feed the entire product catalog as is into a long context window every time and have the model answer from it","RAG (retrieval-augmented generation): fetch the latest information at runtime and cite sources","Bake the latest knowledge into the model's weights with fine-tuning","Finely tune the temperature for each answer to raise accuracy"], "eEn": "For frequently updated content that needs citations, RAG is best: it needs no retraining, updates immediately, and can present sources. Fine-tuning is weak at updates, feeding in everything is excessively costly, and temperature is unrelated."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【シナリオ】依存先APIが連続して落ち始め、リトライを繰り返した結果システム全体が遅延・連鎖障害を起こした。最も的確なパターンはどれか。","o":["全ての依存呼び出しを非同期化してブロッキングを避け並列度を高める","リトライ回数と間隔を増やして失敗した呼び出しを粘り強く再試行する","タイムアウト値を延長し依存先の応答をより長く待機する設定に変更する","サーキット ブレーカーで連続失敗時に呼び出しを一時遮断し、回復を待つ"],"a":3,"e":"連続失敗時はサーキット ブレーカーで呼び出しを遮断し、負荷集中と連鎖障害を防ぐ。リトライ増加やタイムアウト延長は悪化させ、temperatureは信頼性と無関係。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A dependency API began to fail continuously, and repeated retries caused delays and a cascading failure across the whole system. Which pattern is most fitting?", "oEn": ["Make all dependency calls asynchronous to avoid blocking and maximize the degree of parallelism","Increase the retry count and interval and persistently retry the failed calls","Extend the timeout value and change the setting to wait longer for the dependency's response","Use a circuit breaker to cut off calls during continuous failures and wait for recovery"], "eEn": "During continuous failures, a circuit breaker cuts off calls and prevents load concentration and cascading failures. Increasing retries or extending the timeout makes things worse, and temperature is unrelated to reliability."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】長文の中間に置いた重要指示がしばしば無視される。最も的確な対策はどれか。","o":["文脈全体を要約して短く圧縮し指示が相対的に埋没しないよう調整する","重要情報を冒頭または末尾に配置する（lost in the middle対策）","重要な指示を複数回に分けて長文全体へ均等に分散配置し何度も繰り返し確実に想起させる","重要な指示を箇条書き化して本文の中央付近にまとめ枠線で強調する"],"a":1,"e":"モデルは長文中間の情報を参照しにくい（lost in the middle）。重要情報は両端に置くのが定石。表示上の装飾やtemperature、履歴量は参照率に効かない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Important instructions placed in the middle of a long text are often ignored. What is the most fitting countermeasure?", "oEn": ["Summarize and compress the whole context to make it short so the instruction is not relatively buried","Place the important information at the beginning or the end (a countermeasure for lost in the middle)","Split the important instruction into multiple parts and spread them evenly across the whole text, repeating them many times to make sure they are recalled","Turn the important instruction into a bulleted list, gather it near the center of the body, and emphasize it with a border"], "eEn": "Models have difficulty referencing information in the middle of a long text (lost in the middle). The standard approach is to place important information at both ends. Visual decoration, temperature, and the amount of history do not affect the reference rate."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】数日にわたるタスクで、セッションをまたいで状態を保持する必要がある。最適な手段はどれか。","o":["会話履歴をすべてコンテキスト窓に保持し続けて状態を維持する","セッションごとに状態をゼロから再構築して毎回作り直す","メモリツール（外部ストアへの永続化）で窓を超えて保存し再参照する","temperatureを下げてモデルの忘却を防ぎ状態を保つ"],"a":2,"e":"短期メモリ（窓内）は揮発的なので、長期保持には外部ストアへ永続化するメモリツールが要る。全履歴保持は窓を超えて破綻し、毎回再構築は非効率。temperatureは記憶に無関係。", "qEn": "[Advanced] A task spanning several days needs to keep state across sessions. What is the best means?", "oEn": ["Maintain the state by continuing to hold the entire conversation history in the context window","Rebuild the state from scratch in every session","Use a memory tool (external-store persistence) to save beyond the window and refer back","Lower the temperature to prevent the model from forgetting and keep the state"], "eEn": "Short-term memory (within the window) is volatile, so long-term retention requires a memory tool that persists to an external store. Holding the whole history breaks down once it exceeds the window, and rebuilding every time is inefficient. Temperature is unrelated to memory."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】複数情報源を統合して回答する際、出典間で統計値が矛盾していた。正しい扱いはどれか。","o":["矛盾する2つの値の平均を計算して代表値として一つだけ提示する","claim-sourceの対応を統合まで保持し、出典付きで両論併記する","最も新しい出典の統計値だけを採用して古い情報源は破棄し単一の値に統一する","信頼度の高い方の出典を選び矛盾する情報源は結果から除外する"],"a":1,"e":"矛盾は claim-source マッピングを保ったまま出典付きで両論併記するのが誠実。安易な採用・平均・削除は情報の歪曲や根拠の喪失を招く。", "qEn": "[Advanced] When combining multiple information sources into an answer, the statistics contradicted each other across sources. What is the correct handling?", "oEn": ["Calculate the average of the two contradicting values and present it as the single representative value","Keep the claim-source mapping through to the combination, and present both views with citations","Adopt only the statistic from the newest source, discard the older source, and unify to a single value","Pick the more reliable source and exclude the contradicting source from the result"], "eEn": "The honest approach is to present both views with citations while keeping the claim-source mapping. Casually adopting one, averaging, or deleting leads to distorted information and a loss of evidence."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】非決定的なエージェント出力を本番に反映する前に、信頼性を担保する最善策はどれか。","o":["temperatureを0にすれば出力が決定的になり検証は不要になる","モデル自身に出力を自己検証させれば別途の検証層は要らない","決定的な検証層（ルールベース等）で出力を検査し、不合格は反映しない","出力をそのまま本番に反映し問題があればログから事後追跡する"],"a":2,"e":"非決定性はコードによる決定的検証層で囲むのが本質。temperature 0でも非決定性は残り、自己検証はバイアスを含む。検証なしの反映はログがあっても事故を防げない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] What is the best way to ensure reliability before reflecting non-deterministic agent output in production?", "oEn": ["Setting the temperature to 0 makes the output fully deterministic, so no verification is needed at all","If the model verifies its own output, no separate verification layer is needed","Check output with a deterministic verification layer (e.g. rule-based); reject failures","Reflect the output in production as is and trace problems after the fact from the logs"], "eEn": "The essence is to wrap non-determinism in a deterministic verification layer built in code. Even at temperature 0 non-determinism remains, and self-verification contains bias. Reflecting without verification cannot prevent incidents even with logs."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】エスカレーションを発火させる契機として適切なのはどれか。","o":["人間の明示的要求・適用すべきポリシーの欠如・進展不能の検知","モデルが自己申告した確信度スコアが所定の閾値を下回ったときのみ","生成された出力テキストの長さが規定の上限を超えたとき","ユーザーの感情表現の強さが一定水準を超えたとき"],"a":0,"e":"エスカレーションは『人の要求・ポリシー欠如・進展不能』で発火させるのが妥当。自己申告確信度や感情の強さは校正が不正確な代理指標で、出力長は無関係。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Which is an appropriate trigger for firing escalation?", "oEn": ["A human's explicit request, a missing applicable policy, or inability to make progress","Only when the model's self-reported confidence score falls below a predetermined threshold value","When the length of the generated output text exceeds a set limit","When the intensity of the user's emotional expression exceeds a certain level"], "eEn": "It is reasonable to fire escalation on \"a human's request, lack of policy, or inability to progress\". Self-reported confidence and emotional intensity are proxy indicators with inaccurate calibration, and output length is irrelevant."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】エージェントループの終了判定を実装している。ループを継続すべきか終了すべきかを最も確実に判断する方法はどれか。","o":["生成された応答の総文字数が事前に設定した閾値を超えたら終了と判断する","あらかじめ定めた固定の最大反復回数に達したか否かだけを基準に判断する","stop_reasonが\"tool_use\"なら継続、\"end_turn\"なら終了とする","アシスタントの応答テキストに「完了しました」等の終了を示す語句が含まれるかを走査して判定する"],"a":2,"e":"ループ制御はstop_reasonで判定するのが正攻法。自然言語の解析・テキスト内容での完了判定・反復上限のみの依存はいずれもアンチパターンで、誤判定や早期終了を招く。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You are implementing the termination check for an agent loop. What is the most reliable way to decide whether the loop should continue or end?", "oEn": ["Judge that it should end when the total number of characters in the generated response exceeds a preset threshold","Judge solely by whether a predetermined fixed maximum iteration count has been reached","Continue if stop_reason is \"tool_use\", and end if it is \"end_turn\"","Scan the assistant's response text for phrases indicating completion, such as \"Completed\", and decide on that basis"], "eEn": "The orthodox way to control the loop is to decide by stop_reason. Parsing natural language, deciding completion from text content, and relying only on an iteration cap are all anti-patterns that cause misjudgments and early termination."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】ツール実行後、次の反復でモデルが新情報を踏まえて推論できるようにするには何が必要か。","o":["temperatureを上げてモデルに多様な解釈を促してから続行する","ツール結果を会話履歴（tool_result）に追加してから次のリクエストを送る","ツール結果を短く要約してsystemプロンプトに書き換えたうえで次のリクエストを送る","ツール結果を破棄して元の質問文だけをもう一度そのまま再送する"],"a":1,"e":"ツール結果を会話コンテキストに追加することで、モデルは新情報を取り込んで次の行動を決められる。破棄や差し替えは情報を失い、temperatureは無関係。", "qEn": "[Scenario] After a tool runs, what is needed so the model can reason with the new information in the next iteration?", "oEn": ["Raise the temperature to encourage the model to take diverse interpretations before continuing","Add the tool result to the conversation history (tool_result) before sending the next request","Summarize the tool result briefly, rewrite it into the system prompt, and then send the next request","Discard the tool result and resend only the original question as is"], "eEn": "Adding the tool result to the conversation context lets the model take in the new information and decide its next action. Discarding or replacing it loses information, and temperature is unrelated."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】モデル駆動の意思決定と、事前構成された決定木（固定ツール列）の違いとして正しいのはどれか。","o":["前者は文脈に基づきClaudeが次のツールを推論する／後者は経路が固定","両者とも経路が事前に固定されており実行時の分岐は生じない","前者は経路があらかじめ固定され後者は文脈に応じて動的に決まる","両者とも実行時にモデルが文脈から次に呼び出すツールを推論して決定していく"],"a":0,"e":"モデル駆動はClaudeが文脈から次の行動を選ぶ非決定的な方式。決定木・固定ツール列は経路が事前に定まる。柔軟性と予測可能性のトレードオフを理解しているか問う。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Which correctly states the difference between model-driven decision-making and a preconfigured decision tree (a fixed sequence of tools)?", "oEn": ["The former has Claude infer the next tool from context; the latter has a fixed path","Both have paths fixed in advance, and no branching occurs at runtime","The former has a path fixed in advance, and the latter is determined dynamically according to context","In both, the model infers and decides at runtime, from context, the next tool to call"], "eEn": "Model-driven is a non-deterministic approach in which Claude chooses the next action from context. A decision tree or fixed tool sequence has a path set in advance. This tests whether you understand the trade-off between flexibility and predictability."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】解けないタスクでループが延々と続きコストが急増した。停止機構として最も適切なのはどれか。","o":["アシスタントの応答テキストを詳細に解析して停止すべきかどうかを判断する","反復回数の上限だけを唯一の主要な停止機構として運用時に設定する","完了条件に加え、反復上限とトークン予算を補助的な安全装置として設ける","temperatureを0にして生成を完全に決定的にし停止させる"],"a":2,"e":"主たる停止はstop_reasonベースの完了判定。反復上限・トークン予算は暴走を防ぐ補助的安全装置として併用する。上限のみを主機構にするのはアンチパターン。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A loop continued endlessly on an unsolvable task and costs spiked. Which stopping mechanism is most appropriate?", "oEn": ["Analyze the assistant's response text in detail to judge whether or not it should stop","Set only an iteration cap as the sole primary stopping mechanism in operation","Completion condition plus an iteration cap and token budget as auxiliary safeguards","Set the temperature to 0 to make generation fully deterministic and make it stop"], "eEn": "The primary stop is a completion decision based on stop_reason. An iteration cap and token budget are used alongside it as auxiliary safeguards against runaway behavior. Making a cap alone the primary mechanism is an anti-pattern."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】コーディネーターが調査トピックを3つのサブタスクに分解したが、最終レポートが一部領域しかカバーしていない。最も可能性の高い根本原因はどれか。","o":["文書分析エージェントが厳しすぎる関連性基準でフィルタしている","統合エージェントにギャップ検出の指示が与えられていないため","コーディネーターの分解が狭すぎ、関連領域を網羅しないサブタスク割当になっている","Web検索を担当するサブエージェントのクエリが不十分で関連情報を取りこぼしている"],"a":2,"e":"各サブエージェントが割り当て範囲内で正しく動作している場合、網羅性の欠落は分解の狭さが原因。下流エージェントを責めるのは誤り。コーディネーターのログが分解内容を示している。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A coordinator decomposed a research topic into three subtasks, but the final report covers only part of the area. What is the most likely root cause?", "oEn": ["The document analysis agent is filtering with overly strict relevance criteria","Because the synthesis agent was not given instructions to detect gaps","The coordinator's decomposition is too narrow, assigning subtasks that miss relevant areas","The queries of the subagent in charge of web search are insufficient and miss relevant information"], "eEn": "When each subagent works correctly within its assigned scope, a lack of coverage is caused by a narrow decomposition. Blaming the downstream agents is wrong. The coordinator's logs show what the decomposition was."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【知識】ハブ＆スポーク型のマルチエージェント構成でコーディネーターが担う役割として正しいのはどれか。","o":["ツール定義の生成のみを担当し実行は各自に任せる","各サブエージェントを互いに直接通信させ連携判断を各自に委ねる","サブエージェント間の全通信・エラー処理・情報ルーティングを仲介する","サブエージェントに親の全会話履歴を自動で継承させる"],"a":2,"e":"ハブ＆スポークではコーディネーターが全通信を仲介し、観測可能性・一貫したエラー処理・制御された情報フローを担保する。直接通信や自動継承は前提に反する。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] In a hub-and-spoke multi-agent configuration, which correctly describes the role of the coordinator?", "oEn": ["It handles only generating tool definitions and leaves execution to each agent","It has the subagents communicate directly with one another and leaves overall coordination decisions to each","It mediates all communication, error handling, and information routing among subagents","It makes subagents automatically inherit the parent's entire conversation history"], "eEn": "In hub-and-spoke, the coordinator mediates all communication, ensuring observability, consistent error handling, and controlled information flow. Direct communication and automatic inheritance contradict the premise."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【知識】サブエージェントのコンテキストに関する正しい記述はどれか。","o":["親の会話履歴をそのまま自動継承するため文脈を明示的に渡す必要はない","呼び出しの間でも内部メモリを共有し続けて状態を持ち越せる","systemプロンプトを親と必ず共有する仕様になっている","親の会話履歴を自動継承せず、必要な文脈はプロンプトで明示的に渡す必要がある"],"a":3,"e":"サブエージェントは隔離コンテキストで動作し、親履歴を自動継承しない。前段の調査結果などは明示的にプロンプトへ含める必要がある。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which statement about a subagent's context is correct?", "oEn": ["It always automatically inherits the parent's conversation history, so there is no need to explicitly pass any context","It continues to share internal memory across calls and can carry state over","It is specified to always share the system prompt with the parent","It does not inherit the parent's history automatically; needed context must be passed explicitly in the prompt"], "eEn": "A subagent runs in an isolated context and does not automatically inherit the parent's history. Earlier research results and the like must be included explicitly in the prompt."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】コーディネーターが常に全パイプライン（検索→分析→統合→生成）を経由するため、単純な質問でも遅く高コストになる。改善策はどれか。","o":["サブエージェントの総数を増やして役割分担をより細かくする","temperatureを下げて処理を高速化し安定させる","クエリ要件を分析し、必要なサブエージェントのみ動的に選択して呼び出す","単純な質問でも常に全サブエージェントを並列で一斉に起動して速度を稼ぐ"],"a":2,"e":"コーディネーターはクエリの複雑さを評価し、必要なサブエージェントだけ動的に選ぶべき。固定の全経路通過は無駄を生む。", "qEn": "[Scenario] Because the coordinator always runs the whole pipeline (search, analysis, synthesis, generation), even simple questions are slow and costly. What is the fix?", "oEn": ["Increase the total number of subagents to divide roles more finely","Lower the temperature to speed up and stabilize processing","Analyze the query requirements and dynamically select and invoke only the necessary subagents","Even for simple questions, always launch all subagents at once in parallel to gain speed"], "eEn": "The coordinator should assess the complexity of the query and dynamically select only the subagents it needs. Always passing through a fixed full path is wasteful."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】複数サブエージェントで広範な調査を行うと、担当範囲が重複して同じ情報を重ねて取得してしまう。最善の設計はどれか。","o":["全てのエージェントに全く同一の広範な指示を与えてそれぞれ同時並行で走らせる","各エージェントに異なるサブトピックや情報源タイプを割り当て、範囲を分割する","サブエージェントを1つに統合して全体を逐次的に調査させる","temperatureを上げて出力を多様化し重複を避ける"],"a":1,"e":"重複を最小化するには、サブトピックや情報源タイプを明示的に分割して割り当てる。同一指示は重複を、統合は並列性の喪失を招く。", "qEn": "[Scenario] When several subagents conduct broad research, their assigned scopes overlap and they retrieve the same information repeatedly. What is the best design?", "oEn": ["Give all agents exactly the same broad instructions and run them all concurrently","Assign each agent a different subtopic or source type to split the scope","Merge the subagents into one and have it investigate everything sequentially","Raise the temperature to diversify the output and avoid duplication"], "eEn": "To minimize duplication, explicitly divide and assign subtopics or information source types. Identical instructions cause duplication, and merging loses parallelism."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】統合結果にカバレッジのギャップがあるとき、コーディネーターが取るべき反復的精緻化の流れはどれか。","o":["全工程を毎回最初から完全にやり直し調査計画そのものを白紙から組み直して進める","一度の統合で必ず結果を確定させ、それ以降は追加の再委譲や再統合をいかなる場合も一切行わない方針をとる","統合出力のギャップを評価し、対象を絞ったクエリで検索・分析へ再委譲し、十分になるまで統合を再実行する","検出したカバレッジのギャップは無視してそのまま最終出力として利用者に提示する"],"a":2,"e":"反復的精緻化ループでは、コーディネーターがギャップを検出し、的を絞って再委譲し、カバレッジが十分になるまで統合を繰り返す。", "qEn": "[Advanced] When there are coverage gaps in the synthesized result, what iterative refinement flow should the coordinator follow?", "oEn": ["Redo the entire process from scratch every time, rebuilding the research plan itself from a blank slate","Finalize the result in a single synthesis and adopt a policy of never re-delegating or re-synthesizing afterward under any circumstance at all","Assess the gaps in the output, re-delegate targeted queries to search and analysis, and re-synthesize until coverage suffices","Ignore the detected coverage gaps and present the output to the user as the final result as is"], "eEn": "In an iterative refinement loop, the coordinator detects gaps, re-delegates in a targeted way, and repeats synthesis until coverage is sufficient."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【知識】コーディネーターがサブエージェントを生成（spawn）するための仕組みと前提として正しいのはどれか。","o":["設定内容に関係なく自動的に無条件でサブエージェントが生成される仕組み","Bashツールを使って子プロセスとして生成しシェルスクリプト経由で個別に起動する必要がある","GrepツールとGlobツールの両方が生成の必須の前提条件となる","Taskツールで生成し、allowedToolsに\"Task\"が含まれている必要がある"],"a":3,"e":"サブエージェント生成はTaskツールが担い、コーディネーターのallowedToolsに\"Task\"が含まれていなければ呼び出せない。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which is the correct mechanism and prerequisite for a coordinator to spawn subagents?", "oEn": ["A mechanism by which subagents are generated automatically and unconditionally regardless of configuration","They must be created as child processes using the Bash tool and launched individually via shell scripts","Both the Grep tool and the Glob tool are required prerequisites for spawning","They are spawned with the Task tool, and \"Task\" must be included in allowedTools"], "eEn": "Spawning subagents is handled by the Task tool, and it cannot be called unless the coordinator's allowedTools includes \"Task\"."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】統合サブエージェントに、前段のWeb検索結果と文書分析結果を渡したい。正しい方法はどれか。","o":["サブエージェントが親から自動継承するので特に何も渡さずそのまま起動する","temperatureを上げてサブエージェントに内容を推測させる","前段の結果をsystemプロンプトに恒久的に焼き込んで渡す","前段エージェントの完全な所見をサブエージェントのプロンプトに直接含める"],"a":3,"e":"サブエージェントは文脈を自動継承しないため、前段の所見を明示的にプロンプトへ含める。自動継承を前提にすると情報が欠落する。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want to pass the earlier web search results and document analysis results to a synthesis subagent. What is the correct method?", "oEn": ["The subagent automatically inherits from the parent, so launch it as is without passing anything","Raise the temperature to make the subagent guess the content","Permanently bake the earlier results into the system prompt and pass them that way","Include the preceding agents' complete findings directly in the subagent's prompt"], "eEn": "A subagent does not automatically inherit context, so include the preceding findings explicitly in the prompt. Assuming automatic inheritance leaves information missing."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】エージェント間で文脈を渡す際、出典（URL・文書名・ページ番号）を保持するための最善策はどれか。","o":["出典情報を数値コードだけに置き換えて渡す","内容とメタデータを分離する構造化フォーマットで受け渡す","メタデータは省略して本文の内容だけをそのまま渡す","全ての情報を区切りのない1つの自由文にまとめて一括で渡す"],"a":1,"e":"構造化フォーマットで内容とメタデータ（出典）を分離すれば、下流での帰属（attribution）が保持される。自由文化や省略は出典喪失を招く。", "qEn": "[Advanced] What is the best way to keep sources (URL, document name, page number) when passing context between agents?", "oEn": ["Replace the source information with numeric codes only and pass those","Pass it in a structured format that separates content from metadata","Omit the metadata and pass only the body content as is","Combine all information into a single unbroken free-form text and pass it all at once"], "eEn": "If content and metadata (sources) are separated in a structured format, attribution is preserved downstream. Turning it into free text or omitting it causes loss of sources."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】独立した複数のサブエージェントを同時に走らせたい。最も適切な起動方法はどれか。","o":["ターンを複数に分けてサブエージェントを1つずつ逐次順番に起動していく","temperatureを上げて全体の並行実行性を高める","1つのコーディネーター応答内で複数のTaskツール呼び出しを発行する","各サブエージェントを直列にチェイニングして順に繋いでいく"],"a":2,"e":"並列起動は単一応答内で複数のTask呼び出しを発行して行う。ターンを分けると直列になり並列性の利点を失う。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want to run several independent subagents at the same time. What is the most appropriate way to launch them?", "oEn": ["Split across multiple turns and launch the subagents one at a time in sequence","Raise the temperature to increase overall concurrency","Issue multiple Task tool calls within a single coordinator response","Chain the subagents in series and connect them one after another"], "eEn": "Parallel launch is done by issuing multiple Task calls within a single response. Splitting across turns makes it sequential and loses the benefit of parallelism."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】サブエージェントの適応性を高めるコーディネータープロンプトの書き方はどれか。","o":["手順を逐一指示せず、調査目標と品質基準を示してサブエージェントに委ねる","各ステップの手続きを細部まで固定し実行手順を逐一細かく具体的に指示する","生成する出力の文字数と体裁だけを厳密に細かく指定する","ツールの呼び出し順序を全て事前に細かく指定しておく"],"a":0,"e":"目標と品質基準を示す方が、サブエージェントが状況に適応できる。手続きを細部まで固定すると柔軟性を損なう。", "qEn": "[Advanced] How should a coordinator prompt be written to increase the subagent's adaptability?", "oEn": ["Do not specify each procedure; give the research goal and quality criteria and leave the rest to the subagent","Fix the procedure of each step in detail and instruct the execution steps one by one","Strictly specify only the character count and layout of the output to be generated","Specify the order of all tool calls in detail in advance"], "eEn": "Giving goals and quality criteria lets the subagent adapt to the situation. Fixing procedures in detail impairs flexibility."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】返金処理の前に必ず本人確認（get_customer）を完了させたい。プロンプトで指示しても12%のケースで順序が守られない。最も確実な対策はどれか。","o":["systemプロンプトの冒頭で本人確認を必須の手順として繰り返し強調し、正しい呼び出し順序を必ず守るよう毎回明示的に指示して運用で徹底させる方針をとる","リクエストの種別ごとに使用可能なツールを動的に出し分けるルーティング分類器を導入し、経路単位でツール呼び出しの可否を制御する仕組みにする","本人確認を先に呼び出すfew-shot例を複数追加してモデルに望ましい呼び出し順序のパターンを学習させ、実行時にその再現を促す構成を整える","get_customerが検証済み顧客IDを返すまでlookup_orderとprocess_refundをプログラム的に遮断する前提ゲートを設ける"],"a":3,"e":"金銭的影響のある重要な順序制御は、前提ゲート（プログラム的強制）で決定的に保証する。プロンプトやfew-shotは確率的で非ゼロの失敗率が残る。ルーティングはツールの可用性の問題で、順序の問題には対処しない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want identity verification (get_customer) to be completed before any refund is processed. Even when instructed in the prompt, the order is not followed in 12% of cases. What is the most reliable countermeasure?", "oEn": ["Repeatedly emphasize identity verification as a mandatory step at the top of the system prompt, explicitly instruct it to follow the correct call order every time, and ensure compliance through operations","Introduce a routing classifier that dynamically provides different tools per request type, controlling whether a tool call is allowed on a per-route basis","Add several few-shot examples that call identity verification first, so the model learns the desired call order pattern and is encouraged to reproduce it at runtime","Add a prerequisite gate that programmatically blocks lookup_order and process_refund until get_customer returns a verified customer ID"], "eEn": "For important ordering with financial impact, guarantee it deterministically with a prerequisite gate (programmatic enforcement). Prompts and few-shot examples are probabilistic and leave a nonzero failure rate. Routing is a matter of tool availability and does not address ordering."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【知識】ワークフロー順序の保証における、プログラム的強制とプロンプトベース誘導の違いとして正しいのはどれか。","o":["前者は確率的で一定割合で失敗し得る／後者は決定的に順序を常に保証する","前者はフックや前提ゲートで決定的に保証／後者は確率的で失敗率が非ゼロ","両者とも決定的に順序を保証し失敗率は完全にゼロになる","両者とも本質的に確率的なため厳密な順序保証はできない"],"a":1,"e":"フック・前提ゲートは決定的なコンプライアンスを保証する。プロンプト指示は確率的で、本人確認→金銭処理のような重要順序には不十分。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which correctly describes the difference between programmatic enforcement and prompt-based guidance in guaranteeing workflow order?", "oEn": ["The former is probabilistic and can fail at a certain rate; the latter deterministically guarantees the order every time","The former is deterministic via hooks or prerequisite gates; the latter is probabilistic, with a nonzero failure rate","Both guarantee the order deterministically, with a failure rate of exactly zero","Both are inherently probabilistic, so a strict order guarantee is impossible"], "eEn": "Hooks and prerequisite gates guarantee deterministic compliance. Prompt instructions are probabilistic and insufficient for critical ordering such as identity verification followed by financial processing."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】人間エージェントへエスカレーションするが、相手は会話の文字起こしを参照できない。引き継ぎとして最適なのはどれか。","o":["顧客ID・根本原因・返金額・推奨アクションを含む構造化サマリーを編集して渡す","会話の生のログ全体を編集も要約も一切せずそのまま人間の担当者に転送して読ませる","顧客IDのみを渡し残りの経緯や詳細は全て相手に調べさせる","「対応してください」とだけ短く伝えて後の判断は相手に委ねる"],"a":0,"e":"文字起こしにアクセスできない人間向けには、顧客ID・根本原因・推奨アクション等を含む構造化された引き継ぎサマリーが必要。生ログ全体や断片的情報は不十分。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You are escalating to a human agent, but they cannot see the conversation transcript. What is the best handoff?", "oEn": ["Pass a compiled structured summary with the customer ID, root cause, refund amount, and recommended action","Forward the entire raw conversation log to the human agent as is, without editing or summarizing it, for them to read","Pass only the customer ID and have them investigate all the rest of the background and details","Say only \"Please handle this\" briefly and leave all later judgment to them"], "eEn": "For a human who cannot access the transcript, a structured handoff summary containing the customer ID, root cause, recommended action, and so on is needed. The entire raw log or fragmentary information is insufficient."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】返金額が閾値（例：$500）を超える操作だけを確実にブロックして人間へ回したい。最適な実装はどれか。","o":["few-shot例で大きな返金を丁寧に断る様子を複数見せてモデルに学習させる","送出ツール呼び出しを傍受するフックで閾値超過を検出し、エスカレーションへリダイレクトする","systemプロンプトで「$500を超える返金は必ず人間の承認を取れ」と明記して指示する","temperatureを下げて出力を安定させ閾値を超える処理を防ぐ"],"a":1,"e":"金額閾値のような業務ルールの確実な強制は、ツール呼び出し傍受フックで決定的に行う。プロンプトやfew-shotは確率的で保証できない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want to reliably block only operations where the refund amount exceeds a threshold (for example, $500) and route them to a human. What is the best implementation?", "oEn": ["Show the model several examples of politely declining large refunds with few-shot prompting so it learns","Use a hook that intercepts outgoing tool calls to detect threshold violations and redirect them to escalation","State in the system prompt, \"Always obtain human approval for refunds over $500\"","Lower the temperature to stabilize output and prevent processing that exceeds the threshold"], "eEn": "Reliably enforcing a business rule such as an amount threshold is done deterministically with a hook that intercepts tool calls. Prompts and few-shot examples are probabilistic and cannot guarantee it."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】複数のMCP（Model Context Protocol）ツールがUnixタイムスタンプ・ISO 8601・数値ステータスコードなど異なる形式で結果を返し、モデルが混乱する。最適な対処はどれか。","o":["モデルに毎回プロンプト内で形式変換を依頼してその都度手動で整形させる","PostToolUseフックでツール結果をモデル処理前に正規化する","temperatureを下げてモデルの形式解釈を安定させる","使用するツールの数自体を減らして返却形式の種類を絞る"],"a":1,"e":"PostToolUseフックはツール結果をモデルが処理する前に変換・正規化できる。異種フォーマットの統一はフックで決定的に行うのが堅牢。", "qEn": "[Scenario] Several MCP (Model Context Protocol) tools return results in different formats, such as Unix timestamps, ISO 8601, and numeric status codes, and the model gets confused. What is the best remedy?", "oEn": ["Ask the model in the prompt every time to convert the format, having it tidy up manually each time","Normalize tool results before the model processes them with a PostToolUse hook","Lower the temperature to stabilize the model's interpretation of formats","Reduce the number of tools used to narrow the variety of return formats"], "eEn": "A PostToolUse hook can transform and normalize tool results before the model processes them. Unifying heterogeneous formats deterministically with a hook is robust."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【知識】業務ルールが「保証されたコンプライアンス」を要求する場合、フックとプロンプトベース強制のどちらを選ぶべきか。","o":["temperatureの調整","プロンプトベースの指示（柔軟だから）","フック（決定的保証が必要なため）","状況に応じてどちらでもよい"],"a":2,"e":"保証が必要な業務ルールにはフックを選ぶ。プロンプトベースは確率的で、保証要件を満たせない。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] When a business rule requires \"guaranteed compliance\", should you choose hooks or prompt-based enforcement?", "oEn": ["Adjusting the temperature","Prompt-based instructions (for flexibility)","Hooks (because a deterministic guarantee is needed)","Either, depending on the situation"], "eEn": "For business rules that need a guarantee, choose hooks. Prompt-based enforcement is probabilistic and cannot meet a guarantee requirement."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】予測可能な多側面レビュー（各ファイルを個別分析→クロスファイル統合）に適した分解パターンはどれか。","o":["単一プロンプトで全体を一括処理する方式","複数実行の多数決によるボーティング方式","実行時に構成を動的に変える適応的なタスク分解パターン","プロンプトチェイニング（固定の直列パイプライン）"],"a":3,"e":"予測可能で段階が定まったレビューは固定直列のプロンプトチェイニングが適する。動的分解は探索的・開放的タスク向け。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Which decomposition pattern suits a predictable multi-aspect review (analyze each file individually, then cross-file integration)?", "oEn": ["A method that processes everything at once with a single prompt","A voting method using a majority vote over multiple runs","An adaptive task decomposition pattern that changes its structure dynamically at runtime","Prompt chaining (a fixed sequential pipeline)"], "eEn": "For a predictable review with fixed stages, a fixed sequential prompt chain is suitable. Dynamic decomposition is for exploratory, open-ended tasks."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】「レガシーコードベースに包括的なテストを追加する」ような開放的タスクに適した分解はどれか。","o":["まず構造を把握し高インパクト領域を特定し、依存発見に応じて適応する動的分解","複数回の独立実行の結果をボーティングで多数決して決定する","一つの単一プロンプトで全体をまとめて一括ですべて依頼する","あらかじめ定めた固定の直列パイプラインで全体を段階的に順を追って確実に処理する"],"a":0,"e":"開放的・探索的タスクは中間発見に基づく動的適応分解が適する。何が必要かが事前に定まらないため固定パイプラインは不向き。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Which decomposition suits an open-ended task such as \"add comprehensive tests to a legacy codebase\"?", "oEn": ["Dynamic decomposition: grasp the structure, identify high-impact areas, adapt as dependencies emerge","Deciding by majority vote over the results of multiple independent runs","Requesting everything at once in a single prompt","Processing the whole task reliably, step by step and in order, with a fixed sequential pipeline defined in advance"], "eEn": "Open-ended, exploratory tasks suit a dynamic, adaptive decomposition based on intermediate discoveries. A fixed pipeline is unsuitable because what is needed is not determined in advance."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】大規模なコードレビューを単一パスで行うと、注意が分散し一部ファイルが浅くなる。最善の再構成はどれか。","o":["ファイルごとの局所分析パス＋別途クロスファイル統合パスに分割する","3回独立に実行して2回以上出た指摘だけを採用する","開発者にPRをより小さな単位に分割させて対応する","より大きな文脈窓を持つモデルに置き換えて全体を一度に1パスで処理する"],"a":0,"e":"注意の希薄化が根本原因なので、ファイル単位の局所パスとクロスファイル統合パスに分割する。文脈窓拡大は注意の質を解決せず、多数決は断続的にしか検出されない実バグを抑制する。", "qEn": "[Scenario] When a large code review is done in a single pass, attention is dispersed and some files are reviewed shallowly. What is the best restructuring?", "oEn": ["Split into per-file local analysis passes plus a separate cross-file integration pass","Run it independently three times and adopt only the findings that appear at least twice","Have developers split the PR into smaller units","Replace the model with one that has a larger context window and process everything in one pass"], "eEn": "The root cause is diluted attention, so split into per-file local passes and a cross-file integration pass. Enlarging the context window does not fix the quality of attention, and majority voting suppresses real bugs that are only detected intermittently."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【知識】--resume <session-name> の用途として正しいのはどれか。","o":["名前付きの特定の過去会話を継続する","過去の会話履歴を全て消去する","現在のセッションを分岐して複製する","常に新規セッションを開始する"],"a":0,"e":"--resume <session-name>は名前付きの特定セッションを継続するために使う。分岐はfork_session、消去は別機能。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is the correct use of --resume <session-name>?", "oEn": ["Continue a specific named past conversation","Erase all past conversation history","Branch and duplicate the current session","Always start a new session"], "eEn": "--resume <session-name> is used to continue a specific named session. Branching is fork_session, and erasing is a different feature."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】共有のコードベース分析を基点に、2つの異なるリファクタリング方針を並行検討したい。最適な手段はどれか。","o":["fork_sessionで共有ベースラインから独立ブランチを作る","temperatureを上げて多様な案を出させる","毎回まっさらな新規セッションを開始して個別に検討する","--resumeで同一のセッションをそのまま続けて両案を検討する"],"a":0,"e":"fork_sessionは共有ベースラインから独立ブランチを作り、発散的アプローチの並行探索に向く。--resumeは単一線形の継続。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Starting from a shared codebase analysis, you want to explore two different refactoring approaches in parallel. What is the best means?", "oEn": ["Create independent branches from the shared baseline with fork_session","Raise the temperature to get diverse proposals","Start a fresh new session each time and consider them separately","Continue the same session as is with --resume and consider both approaches"], "eEn": "fork_session creates independent branches from a shared baseline and suits parallel exploration of divergent approaches. --resume is a single linear continuation."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】コード修正後にセッションを再開する。以前の解析結果（ツール結果）が古くなっている可能性が高い。最も信頼できる方法はどれか。","o":["過去の会話履歴を増やしてから再開する","temperatureを下げてそのまま再開する","構造化サマリーを注入して新規セッションを開始する","古いツール結果を残したまま--resumeで再開する"],"a":2,"e":"以前のツール結果が陳腐化している場合、古い結果で再開するより、構造化サマリーを注入した新規セッションの方が信頼できる。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You resume a session after fixing code. The earlier analysis results (tool results) are likely stale. What is the most reliable method?", "oEn": ["Increase the past conversation history and then resume","Lower the temperature and resume as is","Start a new session with a structured summary injected","Resume with --resume while leaving the old tool results in place"], "eEn": "When earlier tool results have become stale, a new session with a structured summary injected is more reliable than resuming with the old results."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】セッション再開時、前回から特定ファイルだけが変更された。効率的な進め方はどれか。","o":["全ファイルを対象に最初からもう一度すべて探索し直させる","どのファイルが変更されたかを伝えずにそのまま解析を進める","変更されたファイルを再開セッションに伝え、対象を絞って再解析させる","既存のセッションを完全に破棄して毎回新規セッションの作成のみを行う"],"a":2,"e":"再開時は変更ファイルを伝えて的を絞った再解析を促すのが効率的。全再探索は無駄、変更を伝えないと古い前提で誤る。", "qEn": "[Scenario] When resuming a session, only certain files have changed since last time. What is an efficient way to proceed?", "oEn": ["Have it explore all files again from the beginning","Proceed with the analysis without telling it which files changed","Tell the resumed session which files changed and have it reanalyze with a narrowed scope","Discard the existing session entirely and only create a new session every time"], "eEn": "When resuming, it is efficient to tell it the changed files and prompt a targeted reanalysis. Re-exploring everything is wasteful, and without being told about the changes it will err on outdated assumptions."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】次のうち「マルチエージェント化すべきでない」最も強いシグナルはどれか。","o":["各領域がそれぞれ異なる専門知識を必要とする","親エージェントの文脈を余計な情報で汚染したくないと考える","各サブタスクが前段の結果に強く依存し順序を変えられない","調査の方向が複数あり互いに完全に独立している"],"a":2,"e":"強い逐次依存は並列性の利点を消し調整コストだけが残る。独立性・専門分業・文脈分離はマルチ化の根拠になる。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Which of the following is the strongest signal that you should NOT go multi-agent?", "oEn": ["Each area requires different specialized knowledge","You want to avoid polluting the parent agent's context with unnecessary information","Each subtask depends strongly on the previous result and the order cannot change","There are multiple research directions that are completely independent of one another"], "eEn": "Strong sequential dependency removes the benefit of parallelism and leaves only coordination cost. Independence, specialized division of labor, and context isolation are grounds for going multi-agent."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】サブエージェントに調査を委譲したが、親に大量の生ログが返り親の文脈を圧迫した。設計上の誤りはどれか。","o":["サブエージェントに、返却前の要約・抽出の責務を与えていない","親エージェントが保持するツールの数が多すぎる","temperatureの設定値が全体的に低すぎることが原因である","調査を分担するサブエージェントの数がそもそも少なすぎる"],"a":0,"e":"隔離の利点は親が要約だけ受け取る点にある。生ログ返却はそれを台無しにする。サブエージェントは返却前に要約・抽出すべき。", "qEn": "[Scenario] Research was delegated to a subagent, but a large amount of raw logs came back to the parent and squeezed the parent's context. What is the design error?", "oEn": ["The subagent was not told to summarize or extract before returning","The parent agent holds too many tools","The cause is that the temperature setting is too low overall","The number of subagents sharing the research is too small to begin with"], "eEn": "The advantage of isolation is that the parent receives only a summary. Returning raw logs ruins that. A subagent should summarize and extract before returning."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】複数の懸念を含む顧客リクエスト（返金＋アカウント問題＋請求疑義）を効率よく解決したい。最適なアプローチはどれか。","o":["全ての懸念を1つの曖昧な指示にまとめて一括で処理する","最初に挙がった一つの懸念だけに対応してそこで処理を終了する","個別項目に分解し、共有文脈で各々を並行調査してから統一的な解決に統合する","懸念ごとにそれぞれ別々のセッションを個別に立てて共有文脈を完全に分断する"],"a":2,"e":"複数懸念は個別に分解し、共有文脈で並行調査してから統一解決へ統合する。単一処理や文脈分断は取りこぼしや非効率を生む。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want to efficiently resolve a customer request containing multiple concerns (a refund, an account problem, and a billing dispute). What is the best approach?", "oEn": ["Bundle all the concerns into one vague instruction and process them all at once","Handle only the first concern raised and end processing there","Decompose into separate items, investigate each in parallel with shared context, then integrate into a unified resolution","Set up a separate session for each concern and completely sever the shared context"], "eEn": "For multiple concerns, decompose them individually, investigate in parallel with shared context, and then integrate into a unified resolution. Single-pass handling or severing context causes omissions and inefficiency."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】返金処理ツールの二重実行による事故を構造的に防ぐ設計はどれか。","o":["処理のタイムアウト値を長めに延ばす","処理の実行前にCoTで段階的にじっくり推論させる","冪等キーを持たせ、同一キーの再実行を無効化する","生成のtemperatureを0に設定する"],"a":2,"e":"リトライ×副作用で二重実行が起きる。冪等キーで「同じ操作は一度しか効かない」ことを保証するのが根本対策。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Which design structurally prevents incidents caused by double execution of a refund tool?", "oEn": ["Lengthen the processing timeout value","Have it reason step by step with CoT before carrying out the processing","Add an idempotency key and void re-execution with the same key","Set the generation temperature to 0"], "eEn": "Retries combined with side effects cause double execution. The root fix is to guarantee with an idempotency key that \"the same operation takes effect only once\"."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【知識】PostToolUseフックの主目的として正しいのはどれか。","o":["モデルのツール呼び出し自体を生成する","ツール結果をモデルが処理する前に傍受・変換する","現在の会話全体をその場で終了させる","利用者向けの画面のUIを描画して画面に表示する"],"a":1,"e":"PostToolUseフックはツール結果を傍受し、モデル処理前に変換・正規化するために使う。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is the main purpose of a PostToolUse hook?", "oEn": ["Generate the model's tool call itself","Intercept and transform tool results before the model processes them","End the entire current conversation on the spot","Render the UI screen for the user and display it"], "eEn": "A PostToolUse hook is used to intercept tool results and transform or normalize them before the model processes them."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】ライブラリ移行（45ファイル以上に影響、複数の有効なアプローチあり）に着手する。最適な進め方はどれか。","o":["プランモードで探索・設計してから実装に移る","事前に包括的な指示を与えて直接実行する","直接実行で逐次変更しながら自然に境界を見つける","直接実行で始め複雑化したらプランモードに切り替える"],"a":0,"e":"大規模・多アプローチ・アーキ判断を伴うタスクはプランモードで設計してから実装する。直接実行は手戻りリスクが高い。複雑さは要件に既に明示されている。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You are starting a library migration (affecting 45+ files, with multiple valid approaches). What is the best way to proceed?", "oEn": ["Explore and design in plan mode, then move on to implementation","Give comprehensive instructions up front and execute directly","Execute directly, changing things incrementally and finding the boundaries naturally","Start with direct execution and switch to plan mode if it becomes complicated"], "eEn": "Tasks that are large, have multiple approaches, and involve architectural decisions should be designed in plan mode before implementing. Direct execution carries a high risk of rework. The complexity is already explicit in the requirements."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】単一の検証チェックを1関数に追加するような、明確でスコープの狭い変更に適すのはどれか。","o":["並列化","ボーティング","プランモード","直接実行"],"a":3,"e":"スコープが明確で単純な変更は直接実行が適切。プランモードは大規模・複雑なタスク向けで、ここでは過剰。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Which suits a clear, narrowly scoped change such as adding a single validation check to one function?", "oEn": ["Parallelization workflow","Voting","Plan mode","Direct execution"], "eEn": "A change with clear scope and simplicity suits direct execution. Plan mode is for large, complex tasks and would be overkill here."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】エージェントが返金を無断実行し、不可逆な事故を起こした。再発防止に最も有効なのはどれか。","o":["反復回数の上限を撤廃して完了まで実行を続けさせる","temperatureを下げてモデル出力の一貫性と再現性を高める","不可逆操作の前にヒューマン・イン・ザ・ループの承認ステップを挟む","利用可能なツールの種類を増やして対応範囲を広げる"],"a":2,"e":"不可逆・高リスク操作の前には人間承認を挟むのが最も有効。temperatureやツール追加は事故防止に寄与しない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] An agent executed a refund without permission and caused an irreversible incident. What is most effective for preventing recurrence?", "oEn": ["Remove the iteration cap and let it keep running until completion","Lower the temperature to improve the consistency and reproducibility of the model's output","Insert a human-in-the-loop approval step before irreversible operations","Increase the types of available tools to broaden the range it can handle"], "eEn": "Inserting human approval before irreversible, high-risk operations is the most effective. Temperature and adding tools do not help prevent incidents."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【知識】AgentDefinition設定に含まれる要素として正しいのはどれか。","o":["課金プランと各APIキーごとの月次利用上限とアラート設定","UIテーマと表示言語およびログ出力フォーマットの指定","各サブエージェントに割り当てるGPUメモリ量とモデルの重みの初期値","説明・systemプロンプト・各サブエージェント型ごとのツール制限"],"a":3,"e":"AgentDefinitionは説明・systemプロンプト・ツール制限などサブエージェントの定義を担う。重みや課金は無関係。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which is an element included in an AgentDefinition configuration?", "oEn": ["Billing plan, monthly usage limits per API key, and alert settings","UI theme, display language, and log output format settings","GPU memory allocated to each subagent and initial model weights","Description, system prompt, and tool restrictions for each subagent type"], "eEn": "An AgentDefinition defines a subagent through its description, system prompt, tool restrictions, and so on. Weights and billing are unrelated."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】共有の分析ベースラインから発散的アプローチを探索するセッション管理方式はどれか。","o":["fork-based セッション管理（fork_session）","temperatureを調整して出力の多様性を確保する方式","--resumeフラグを用いた直近セッションからの線形的な継続実行","会話履歴を全て削除して新しいセッションを毎回作り直す"],"a":0,"e":"フォークベースのセッション管理は共有ベースラインから独立に分岐し、発散的探索を可能にする。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Which session management approach explores divergent approaches from a shared analysis baseline?", "oEn": ["Fork-based session management (fork_session)","Adjusting the temperature to secure diversity of output","Linear continuation from the most recent session using the --resume flag","Deleting all conversation history and recreating a new session every time"], "eEn": "Fork-based session management branches independently from a shared baseline, enabling divergent exploration."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】コードレビューを「各ファイル個別分析→クロスファイル統合パス」に分ける主目的はどれか。","o":["注意の希薄化（attention dilution）を避け、一貫した深さと整合性を保つ","各ファイルのレビュー処理を完全に並列実行して全体のレイテンシを大幅に短縮し高速化するため","出力フォーマットを統一してレビュー結果全体の可読性と体裁を整えるため","トークン消費を抑えてAPI課金コストを削減することを主目的とするため"],"a":0,"e":"多ファイル一括は注意が分散し浅い指摘や矛盾を生む。個別パス＋統合パスで注意の希薄化を防ぐ。", "qEn": "[Scenario] What is the main purpose of splitting a code review into \"individual per-file analysis, then a cross-file integration pass\"?", "oEn": ["To avoid attention dilution and maintain consistent depth and coherence","To run each file's review fully in parallel and greatly shorten overall latency","To unify the output format and tidy the readability and appearance of the whole review","To reduce token consumption and cut API billing cost as the main goal"], "eEn": "Reviewing many files at once disperses attention and produces shallow findings and contradictions. Individual passes plus an integration pass prevent attention dilution."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】コーディネーターが研究トピックを過度に細かく分解し、広いトピックのカバレッジが不完全になるリスクがある。これを避ける設計はどれか。","o":["分解の網羅性を確保し、統合段でギャップを評価して再委譲する","トピックを分解せず単一のエージェントに全て任せる","temperatureを上げて各サブトピックの探索を多様化する","常に最小単位まで細かく分解して各タスクを個別に処理する"],"a":0,"e":"過度に狭い分解は網羅性を損なう。網羅的な分解とギャップ評価・再委譲の反復ループで補う。", "qEn": "[Scenario] There is a risk that the coordinator decomposes a research topic too finely, leaving coverage of a broad topic incomplete. Which design avoids this?", "oEn": ["Make the decomposition comprehensive, and evaluate gaps at synthesis and re-delegate","Do not decompose the topic and leave everything to a single agent","Raise the temperature in order to diversify the exploration of each of the subtopics","Always decompose down to the smallest possible units and process each task individually"], "eEn": "An overly narrow decomposition undermines coverage. Compensate with a comprehensive decomposition and an iterative loop of gap evaluation and re-delegation."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】コーディネーターが全サブエージェント通信を仲介する設計の利点として正しいのはどれか。","o":["サブエージェント間の通信が常に高速化し全体のレイテンシが大きく下がる","観測可能性・一貫したエラー処理・制御された情報フローを実現する","各エージェントが使うツールの総数を自動的に削減できる","収集した対話データからモデルを追加訓練して精度を上げられる"],"a":1,"e":"全通信をコーディネーター経由にすることで、観測可能性・統一エラー処理・情報フロー制御が得られる。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Which is a correct benefit of a design in which the coordinator mediates all subagent communication?", "oEn": ["Communication between subagents always becomes faster and overall latency drops greatly","It gives observability, consistent error handling, and controlled information flow","The total number of tools each agent uses can be reduced automatically","The model can be further trained on the collected dialogue data to raise accuracy"], "eEn": "Routing all communication through the coordinator provides observability, unified error handling, and control of information flow."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】サブエージェントが一時的失敗（タイムアウト）に遭遇した。多エージェント系での適切な扱いはどれか。","o":["サブエージェント内で局所的に回復を試み、解決不能なエラーのみ部分結果とともにコーディネーターへ伝播する","失敗したタスクを空の成功レスポンスに静かに置き換えてコーディネーターへ何事もなく正常完了したかのように返す","エラーを検知した時点でただちにワークフロー全体を強制的に終了し全処理を停止する","発生した一時的な失敗は無視してサブエージェントをそのまま次のタスクへ進ませる"],"a":0,"e":"一時的失敗はサブエージェント内で局所回復し、解決不能なものだけ部分結果と試行内容を添えて伝播する。全終了や隠蔽はアンチパターン。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A subagent encountered a transient failure (a timeout). What is the appropriate handling in a multi-agent system?", "oEn": ["Recover locally inside the subagent, and propagate to the coordinator only unresolvable errors, with partial results","Quietly replace the failed task with an empty success response and return it to the coordinator as if it had completed normally","Immediately terminate the entire workflow and halt all processing the moment an error is detected","Ignore the transient failure and let the subagent move on to the next task as is"], "eEn": "Recover from transient failures locally within the subagent, and propagate only unresolvable ones along with partial results and what was attempted. Terminating everything or concealing the failure are anti-patterns."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【知識】Taskツールでサブエージェントを並列起動する正しい方法はどれか。","o":["Taskを一度だけ発行してサブエージェント内部で繰り返しループさせる","各Taskを別々のターンに分けて一つずつ順番に発行する","Bashコマンドから複数のプロセスを並列に起動する","単一のコーディネーター応答で複数のTask呼び出しを発行する"],"a":3,"e":"並列起動は単一応答内で複数Task呼び出しを発行する。別ターンに分けると直列になる。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is the correct way to launch subagents in parallel with the Task tool?", "oEn": ["Issue Task only once and have it loop repeatedly inside the subagent","Split each Task into separate turns and issue them one at a time in order","Launch multiple processes in parallel from a Bash command","Issue multiple Task calls in a single coordinator response"], "eEn": "Parallel launch is done by issuing multiple Task calls in a single response. Splitting them across turns makes it sequential."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】顧客が「人間につないでほしい」と明示的に要求した。エージェントの最適な対応はどれか。","o":["対応の確信度を計算してから引き継ぐか判断する","まず自律的に問題解決を試みてから対応方針を判断する","調査を試みず、ただちに人間へエスカレーションする","感情分析の結果に基づいて対応方針を決定する"],"a":2,"e":"顧客が人間への引き継ぎを明示的に求めたら、調査を挟まず直ちにエスカレーションする。要求の尊重が優先で、まず自律的に問題解決を試みてから判断する対応は顧客の求めを後回しにする。確信度の計算や感情分析で方針を決めるのも同じ理由で不適切。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A customer explicitly asked to be connected to a human. What is the agent's best response?", "oEn": ["Calculate the confidence of handling it and then decide whether to hand over","First try to solve the problem autonomously and then decide on a response policy","Escalate to a human immediately, without attempting an investigation","Decide the response policy based on the result of sentiment analysis"], "eEn": "When a customer explicitly asks for a human, escalate immediately without investigating first. Respecting the request comes first, and trying to resolve the problem autonomously before deciding puts the customer's request on hold. Computing confidence or running sentiment analysis to decide is inappropriate for the same reason."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】顧客が苛立っているが、問題自体はエージェントの能力内で解決可能。最適な対応はどれか。","o":["自己申告した確信度が低いことを理由に解決を諦めて顧客対応を打ち切る","苛立ちを受け止めつつ解決を提案し、顧客が人間対応を再度求めた場合のみエスカレーションする","顧客の感情スコアが一定の閾値を超えた場合に自動でエスカレーションする","顧客の苛立ちを少しでも検知した時点でただちに調査を打ち切って人間の担当者へエスカレーションする"],"a":1,"e":"解決可能なら苛立ちを認めつつ解決を提案し、顧客が改めて人間を求めた場合に限りエスカレーションする。感情ベースの自動判定は不適切。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A customer is frustrated, but the problem itself can be resolved within the agent's capabilities. What is the best response?", "oEn": ["Give up resolving and end the customer interaction because the self-reported confidence is low","Acknowledge the frustration and offer a resolution; escalate only if the customer asks for a human again","Escalate automatically when the customer's sentiment score exceeds a set threshold","Cut off the investigation immediately and escalate to a human agent the moment any frustration at all is detected"], "eEn": "If it is resolvable, acknowledge the frustration while offering a resolution, and escalate only if the customer asks for a human again. Automatic sentiment-based decisions are inappropriate."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】自社サイトの価格調整しかポリシーに記載がなく、顧客が競合価格マッチを求めた。最適な対応はどれか。","o":["エージェント自身の判断で競合他社の価格へのマッチを承認する","自己申告の確信度スコアに基づいて対応を判断する","方針にないため一律に要求を拒否して対応を終える","ポリシーが沈黙・曖昧な事項なのでエスカレーションする"],"a":3,"e":"ポリシーが特定要求について沈黙・曖昧な場合はエスカレーションが妥当。独断の承認・拒否はリスク。", "qEn": "[Scenario] The policy mentions only price adjustments on the company's own site, and a customer asks for a competitor price match. What is the best response?", "oEn": ["Approve matching the competitor's price on the agent's own judgment","Decide the response based on a self-reported confidence score","Reject the request across the board because it is not in the policy, and end the interaction","Escalate, because the policy is silent or ambiguous on the matter"], "eEn": "When the policy is silent or ambiguous about a specific request, escalation is appropriate. Approving or rejecting on one's own is risky."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【知識】感情ベースのエスカレーションや自己申告の確信度スコアが、案件の複雑さの代理指標として不適切な理由はどれか。","o":["スコア計算が余分なトークンを大量に消費してしまうから","その指標をユーザーインターフェースに表示できないから","処理は常に高速だがその分だけ計算コストが非常に高くついてしまうから","感情や自己申告確信度は実際の複雑さと相関せず校正も不正確だから"],"a":3,"e":"感情の強さは複雑さと相関せず、自己申告確信度は校正が不正確。明示基準＋few-shotで判断境界を定義すべき。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Why are sentiment-based escalation and self-reported confidence scores inappropriate proxies for case complexity?", "oEn": ["Because computing the score consumes a large number of extra tokens","Because the metric cannot be displayed in the user interface","Because processing is always fast, but the computational cost ends up being correspondingly very high as a result","Because sentiment and self-reported confidence do not correlate with complexity and are miscalibrated"], "eEn": "The intensity of emotion does not correlate with complexity, and self-reported confidence is poorly calibrated. The decision boundary should be defined with explicit criteria plus few-shot examples."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】ツール結果が複数の顧客にマッチした。エージェントの正しい振る舞いはどれか。","o":["ヒューリスティクスで1件を選ぶ","追加の識別子を求めて明確化する","最初にマッチした1件を採用する","処理を中断してエラーで停止する"],"a":1,"e":"複数マッチ時は追加識別子を求めて明確化する。ヒューリスティック選択は誤認アカウントのリスク。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A tool result matched multiple customers. What is the agent's correct behavior?", "oEn": ["Pick one using a heuristic","Ask for an extra identifier to disambiguate","Adopt the first match","Interrupt the processing and halt with an error"], "eEn": "When there are multiple matches, ask for an additional identifier to disambiguate. Choosing by heuristic risks misidentifying the account."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】返金額が方針上限を超える業務エラーをエージェントが顧客へ適切に伝えられるようにするには、ツールは何を返すべきか。","o":["エラーの詳細や原因情報を一切含まない汎用的な「処理に失敗しました」というメッセージ","何のデータ要素も含まない空の配列をそのまま呼び出し元へと返す","発生した例外を内部で握りつぶして正常に完了したかのように返す","retriable: false と顧客向けの分かりやすい説明を含む構造化エラー"],"a":3,"e":"業務ルール違反はretriable:falseと顧客向け説明を含む構造化エラーで返し、エージェントが適切に伝達できるようにする。", "qEn": "[Advanced] For the agent to properly communicate to the customer a business error where the refund amount exceeds the policy limit, what should the tool return?", "oEn": ["A generic \"Processing failed\" message that contains no error details or cause","An empty array containing no data elements, returned to the caller as is","The caught exception swallowed internally and returned as if it had completed normally","A structured error containing retriable: false and a clear explanation for the customer"], "eEn": "A business rule violation is returned as a structured error containing retriable: false and an explanation for the customer, so the agent can communicate it properly."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】コーディネーターが各サブエージェントの状態を失うクラッシュに備えたい。最適な設計はどれか。","o":["temperatureを下げて各エージェントの出力の揺らぎを最小限に抑える","すべてのエージェントの全対話履歴を常にそのままコンテキスト窓の中に保持し続ける","各エージェントの内部状態は一切保持せずクラッシュが発生するたびに毎回最初からすべての処理をやり直す","各エージェントが既知の場所へ状態をエクスポートし、再開時にコーディネーターがマニフェストを読み込む"],"a":3,"e":"クラッシュ復旧は各エージェントの構造化状態エクスポート（マニフェスト）を用い、再開時に読み込んでプロンプトへ注入する。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want to prepare for a crash in which the coordinator loses each subagent's state. What is the best design?", "oEn": ["Lower the temperature to minimize fluctuation in each agent's output","Keep the full conversation history of all agents as is in the context window at all times","Keep no internal state for any agent at all and redo all of the processing from the beginning every time a crash occurs","Have each agent export its state to a known location, and have the coordinator load the manifest on resume"], "eEn": "Crash recovery uses each agent's structured state export (a manifest), loaded on resume and injected into the prompt."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】長い探索セッションでモデルが「典型的なパターン」を参照し始め、以前発見した具体的クラスを忘れる現象への対処はどれか。","o":["反復処理の上限回数を引き上げて探索を長く続けさせる","temperatureを下げてモデル出力のばらつきを抑え安定させる","スクラッチパッドファイルに主要所見を記録し、後続の問いで参照させる","利用できるツールの種類を増やして探索の範囲を広げる"],"a":2,"e":"文脈劣化にはスクラッチパッドで主要所見を永続化し参照させるのが有効。temperatureやツール追加では解決しない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] In a long exploration session, the model starts referring to \"typical patterns\" and forgets the specific classes it discovered earlier. What is the remedy?", "oEn": ["Raise the iteration cap to let the exploration continue longer","Lower the temperature to reduce variation in the model's output and make it more stable","Record the key findings in a scratchpad file and have later questions refer to it","Increase the types of available tools to widen the exploration"], "eEn": "For context degradation, persisting the key findings in a scratchpad and having them referenced is effective. Temperature or adding tools does not solve it."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】探索フェーズの冗長な出力で主会話の文脈が枯渇しそうだ。最適な手段はどれか。","o":["探索フェーズで生成された冗長な全出力をそのまますべて主会話の文脈の中に残しておく","Exploreサブエージェントで冗長な発見出力を隔離し、要約だけ主会話へ返す","temperatureを上げて探索の出力の多様性をさらに高める","コンテキスト窓に残しておく対話履歴の量をさらに増やして対応する"],"a":1,"e":"Exploreサブエージェントは冗長な探索出力を隔離し、要約を返して主会話の文脈を守る。", "qEn": "[Scenario] Verbose output from the exploration phase is about to exhaust the main conversation's context. What is the best means?", "oEn": ["Leave all of the verbose output generated in the exploration phase sitting in the main conversation's context as is","Isolate the verbose findings in an Explore subagent and return only a summary to the main conversation","Raise the temperature to further increase the diversity of exploration output","Handle it by further increasing the amount of conversation history left in the context window"], "eEn": "An Explore subagent isolates verbose exploration output and returns a summary, protecting the main conversation's context."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】プランモードと直接実行を組み合わせる典型的なパターンはどれか。","o":["直接実行で先に調査と設計を済ませてからプランモードで実装する","プランモードで調査・設計し、計画に沿って直接実行で実装する","調査から実装まですべての工程をプランモードで行う","調査から実装まですべての工程を直接実行で行う"],"a":1,"e":"調査・設計はプランモード、実装は直接実行という組み合わせが典型。例：ライブラリ移行を計画してから実行。", "qEn": "[Advanced] What is the typical pattern for combining plan mode and direct execution?", "oEn": ["Finish investigation and design first with direct execution, and only then implement in plan mode","Investigate and design in plan mode, then implement by direct execution per the plan","Do every step from investigation to implementation in plan mode","Do every step from investigation to implementation with direct execution"], "eEn": "The typical combination is plan mode for investigation and design and direct execution for implementation. Example: plan a library migration, then execute it."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【知識】エージェントの観測可能性（observability）が重要な理由はどれか。","o":["エージェントの出力生成そのものを高速化し全体のレイテンシを短縮するため","非決定的な経路を事後に追跡し、失敗原因を診断できるようにするため","ユーザーインターフェースを描画して見た目を整えるため","APIの課金コストを抑えて全体の費用を削減するため"],"a":1,"e":"各ステップのツール呼び出しと推論をログ化することで、非決定的な失敗の原因を診断できる。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Why is agent observability important?", "oEn": ["To speed up the generation of the agent's output itself and shorten the overall latency","To trace non-deterministic paths afterward and diagnose failure causes","To render the user interface and tidy its appearance","To keep API billing costs down and reduce overall expense"], "eEn": "Logging each step's tool calls and reasoning makes it possible to diagnose the causes of non-deterministic failures."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】長時間タスクで20ターン目あたりから当初要件と無関係な作業を始めた。ツール呼び出し自体は成功している。最初の対策はどれか。","o":["会話履歴を全て削除してコンテキストを初期状態に戻す","temperatureを上げて出力の多様性をさらに高める","目標と制約を定期的に再注入し、各ステップで計画との整合を検証する","エージェントが利用できるツールの種類をさらに増やして対応力を高める"],"a":2,"e":"ツール成功下での脱線は目標漂流。目標・計画の再注入と整合チェックが要。ツール追加やtemperature上昇は悪化させる。", "qEn": "[Scenario] In a long-running task, the agent started doing work unrelated to the original requirements around turn 20. The tool calls themselves succeeded. What is the first measure?", "oEn": ["Delete the entire conversation history and return the context to its initial state","Raise the temperature to further increase output diversity","Re-inject the goal and constraints periodically, and verify plan consistency at each step","Further increase the types of tools available to the agent in order to raise its capability to respond"], "eEn": "Going off track while tools succeed is goal drift. Re-injecting the goal and plan and checking consistency are key. Adding tools or raising the temperature makes it worse."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】10件の独立した競合を同時調査し最後に比較表へ統合したい。件数は常に10で固定。最適な構成はどれか。","o":["評価者・最適化者で出力を反復的に改善していく","プロンプトチェイニングで各調査を直列に処理する","並列化（セクショニング）で分担実行し、統合ステップで比較表を生成","オーケストレーター・ワーカー構成で調査タスクを動的に分割し統合する"],"a":2,"e":"件数固定＝動的分割不要なのでオーケストレーターは過剰。独立タスクの同時実行＝セクショニングが最適。", "qEn": "[Advanced] You want to investigate 10 independent competitors at the same time and combine them into a comparison table at the end. The count is always fixed at 10. What is the best configuration?", "oEn": ["Iteratively improve the output with an evaluator-optimizer","Process each investigation in series with prompt chaining","Split the work by parallelization (sectioning) and build the comparison table in an integration step","Dynamically split up the investigation tasks and then integrate them with an orchestrator-workers configuration"], "eEn": "A fixed count means dynamic splitting is unnecessary, so an orchestrator is overkill. Running independent tasks at the same time, i.e. sectioning, is best."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】契約書ドラフトを生成し専門基準で評価して反復改善したい。最適なパターンはどれか。","o":["ルーティング","単一プロンプト","評価者・最適化者","並列化ワークフロー"],"a":2,"e":"契約書ドラフトを生成し、専門基準で評価して反復改善する流れは、生成と評価を分けて繰り返す評価者・最適化者パターンに合う。単一プロンプトは1回の生成で終わり、ルーティングは入力を分類して振り分けるだけで、反復改善の仕組みを持たない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] You want to generate a contract draft, evaluate it against professional standards, and improve it iteratively. What is the best pattern?", "oEn": ["Routing","A single prompt","Evaluator-optimizer","A parallelization workflow"], "eEn": "Generating a contract draft, scoring it against professional criteria and refining it repeatedly fits the evaluator-optimizer pattern, which separates generation from evaluation. A single prompt ends after one generation, and routing only classifies and dispatches, so neither has an iterative improvement loop."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】問い合わせを返金・技術サポート・営業へ自動振り分けしたい。最適なワークフローはどれか。","o":["単一プロンプトで処理","並列化（セクショニング）","評価者・最適化者ワークフロー","ルーティング ワークフロー"],"a":3,"e":"入力を分類して専用処理パスへ振り分けるのはルーティング。種別ごとの処理に適する。", "qEn": "[Advanced] You want to automatically route inquiries to refunds, technical support, and sales. What is the best workflow?", "oEn": ["Process with a single prompt","Parallelization (sectioning)","Evaluator-optimizer workflow","Routing workflow"], "eEn": "Classifying the input and dispatching it to a dedicated processing path is routing. It suits handling that differs by type."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】停止条件を『タスク完了の自己申告』のみにしたら、未完了でも完了と報告して止まった。最適な補強はどれか。","o":["客観的な成功基準を持つ独立した検証ステップ（評価者）を加える","反復処理の上限回数だけをあらかじめ厳密に設定して停止を制御する","利用できるツールの種類を増やして対応力を高める","temperatureを上げて出力の多様性を高める"],"a":0,"e":"自己申告は楽観に偏る。生成と評価を分離し客観基準で検証するのが本質的な補強。反復上限は止めるだけで正しさを保証しない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] When the stopping condition was only a \"self-report of task completion\", the agent reported completion and stopped even though the task was unfinished. What is the best reinforcement?", "oEn": ["Add an independent verification step (evaluator) with objective success criteria","Strictly set only a maximum iteration count in advance and rely on it to control stopping","Increase the types of tools available to raise its capability to respond","Raise the temperature to increase output diversity"], "eEn": "Self-reports lean optimistic. The essential reinforcement is to separate generation from evaluation and verify against objective criteria. An iteration cap only stops the agent and does not guarantee correctness."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】コストが3倍に膨らんだ。ターン数は想定通りだが入力トークンだけ激増。最も疑うべき原因はどれか。","o":["ツールの実行結果が構造化されていないから","毎ターン履歴全体を再送しており、キャッシュや要約がない","temperatureの設定値が高すぎるから","モデルが毎回生成する出力トークンが一回ごとに長すぎるから"],"a":1,"e":"ターン一定で入力だけ増加は履歴の累積再送が原因。プロンプトキャッシュや要約で対処する。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Cost ballooned threefold. The number of turns is as expected, but only input tokens surged. What cause should you suspect most?", "oEn": ["Because tool execution results are not structured","The entire history is resent every turn, with no caching or summarization","Because the temperature setting is too high","Because the output tokens the model generates each time are too long per request"], "eEn": "When the turn count is constant and only input increases, the cause is cumulative resending of history. Address it with prompt caching or summarization."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【知識】ヒューマン・イン・ザ・ループと権限最小化を併用する正しい考え方はどれか。","o":["権限で危険な行動空間を構造的に絞り、残る不可避な高リスク操作に承認を重ねる（多層防御）","権限最小化とはエージェントの読み取り操作を全面的に禁止することを指す","権限の最小化と人間による承認のどちらか一方だけを導入しておけば安全性は十分に確保できる","人間による承認はむしろ低リスクな操作にこそ重点的に適用すべきである"],"a":0,"e":"権限最小化は、権限で危険な行動空間を構造的に絞る。そのうえで残る不可避の高リスク操作にだけ人間の承認を重ねる、という多層防御の考え方だ。権限の最小化と承認のどちらか一方だけで安全性が十分とは言えず、承認を低リスクな操作に集中させるのも逆である。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is the correct way of thinking about using human-in-the-loop and least privilege together?", "oEn": ["Structurally narrow the dangerous action space with permissions, and layer approval on the unavoidable high-risk operations that remain (defense in depth)","Least privilege means banning all of the agent's read operations","Introducing either least privilege or human approval alone is enough to secure safety","Human approval should be applied most heavily to low-risk operations"], "eEn": "Least privilege structurally narrows the space of dangerous actions through permissions, and human approval is then layered on the unavoidable high-risk operations that remain. This is defense in depth. Having only one of the two is not enough, and focusing approval on low-risk operations gets it backwards."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】複数サブエージェントで並行調査するが互いの文脈が混ざる。最適な対処はどれか。","o":["サブエージェントごとにコンテキストを隔離し、親へは要約のみ返す","temperatureを上げて各エージェントの出力を多様化する","各エージェントが保持する対話履歴の量をさらに増やす","すべてのサブエージェント間で全文脈をそのまま共有させる"],"a":0,"e":"サブエージェントごとにコンテキストを隔離し、親には要約だけ返すと、互いの文脈が混ざらない。すべてのサブエージェント間で全文脈を共有させると混在がむしろ悪化し、対話履歴の量を増やしても隔離にはならない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] Several subagents investigate in parallel, but their contexts get mixed. What is the best remedy?", "oEn": ["Isolate the context for each subagent and return only a summary to the parent","Raise the temperature to diversify each agent's output","Further increase the amount of conversation history each agent holds","Have all subagents share the full context as is"], "eEn": "Isolating the context of each subagent and returning only a summary to the parent keeps their contexts from mixing. Having all subagents share the full context makes the mixing worse, and giving each agent more conversation history does not create isolation."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】サブゴール分解の利点として正しいのはどれか。","o":["小さく検証可能なマイルストーンにより完遂率が上がる","タスク全体の処理速度が常に高速になり実行時間が短縮される","ユーザーインターフェースの見た目が良くなる","APIの課金コストが常に確実に下がっていく"],"a":0,"e":"大きな目標を小さく検証可能なマイルストーンに分けると、各段の成否を確認しながら進められ、完遂率が上がる。処理速度が常に速くなるわけではなく、課金コストが必ず下がるとも言えない。手順が増えれば、かえって時間や費用が増える場合もある。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Which correctly states the benefit of subgoal decomposition?", "oEn": ["Small, verifiable milestones raise the completion rate","The processing speed of the whole task always becomes faster and execution time is shortened","The appearance of the user interface improves","API billing cost always goes down reliably"], "eEn": "Splitting a large goal into small, verifiable milestones lets you confirm each stage as you go, which raises the completion rate. Overall processing speed is not always faster and API cost does not always fall; more steps can even add time and cost."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】中間チェックポイントを設ける利点はどれか。","o":["タスク全体の処理速度が常に高速になり最初から最後まで実行時間が確実に短縮される","ユーザーインターフェースの見た目が良くなり操作性が向上する","長いタスクで途中状態を保存・再開・検証でき、失敗時にゼロからやり直さずに済む","APIの課金コストが常に下がって全体の運用費用が削減される"],"a":2,"e":"チェックポイントにより途中状態を保存・再開・検証でき、失敗時の手戻りを減らせる。", "qEn": "[Advanced] What is the benefit of setting intermediate checkpoints?", "oEn": ["The processing speed of the whole task always becomes faster, and execution time is reliably shortened from start to finish","The appearance of the user interface improves and usability increases","In a long task, intermediate state can be saved, resumed, and verified, so a failure does not mean starting over","API billing cost always goes down and overall operating expense is reduced"], "eEn": "Checkpoints let you save, resume, and verify intermediate state, which reduces rework on failure."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【知識】冪等性（idempotency）が重要な理由はどれか。","o":["処理全体を高速化してレイテンシを短縮するため","APIの課金コストを抑えて費用を削減するため","ユーザーインターフェースを整えて見やすくするため","リトライ時の重複実行による副作用を防ぐため"],"a":3,"e":"冪等な設計では、同じ操作を繰り返しても結果が変わらない。そのため再試行で重複実行されても副作用が出ず、リトライを安全にできる。処理全体を高速化してレイテンシを短縮する効果はなく、課金コストの削減や画面の見やすさとも関係がない。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Why is idempotency important?", "oEn": ["To speed up the whole process and shorten latency","To hold down API billing cost and reduce expense","To tidy up the user interface and make it easier to read","To prevent side effects from duplicate runs on retry"], "eEn": "With an idempotent design, repeating the same operation does not change the result, so a retry that runs twice causes no extra side effects and retries are safe. It does not speed up the whole process or reduce latency, and it has nothing to do with billing cost or how the screen looks."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】保守的デフォルト設計とは何か。","o":["不確実時に必ず破壊的な操作を選ぶ方針","不確実時に安全な行動を選ぶ既定方針","不確実時に常に処理を停止する方針","不確実時にランダムに行動を選ぶ方針"],"a":1,"e":"保守的デフォルトは、不確実なときに安全な行動を選ぶ既定の方針で、リスクの非対称性に備える。必ず破壊的な操作を選ぶ方針は被害を広げ、常に処理を停止する方針は何も進まず、ランダムに行動を選ぶ方針は結果が予測できない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] What is a conservative default design?", "oEn": ["A policy of always choosing a destructive operation when uncertain","A default policy of choosing a safe action when uncertain","A policy of always stopping processing when uncertain","A policy of choosing an action at random when uncertain"], "eEn": "A conservative default is a standing policy of choosing the safe action when unsure, which guards against the asymmetry of risk. Always choosing a destructive action widens the damage, always stopping makes no progress, and choosing at random gives unpredictable results."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】結果の信頼度スコアを返す利点はどれか。","o":["APIの課金コストが確実に下がる","画面の見た目が良くなり操作しやすい","処理全体が常に高速になり短縮される","下流が信頼度に応じて処理を選べる"],"a":3,"e":"信頼度スコアにより、低スコアは追加検証、高スコアは直接利用と下流処理を分岐できる。", "qEn": "[Advanced] What is the benefit of returning a confidence score with a result?", "oEn": ["API billing cost reliably goes down","The appearance of the screen improves and it becomes easier to use","The whole process always becomes faster and shorter","Downstream steps can pick processing by confidence level"], "eEn": "With a confidence score, downstream processing can branch: additional verification for low scores and direct use for high scores."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】段階的自律化（staged autonomy）とは何か。","o":["権限のレベルをランダムに変え続ける方式","最初から全自律で全ての権限を一度にまとめて与える","承認付き→半自律→全自律と権限を段階的に広げる","常に人間の承認を必須とし権限を広げない"],"a":2,"e":"検証しながら自律度を段階的に上げるのが段階的自律化。リスクを抑えつつ能力を拡張する。", "qEn": "[Advanced] What is staged autonomy?", "oEn": ["A method of continually changing permission levels at random","Granting all permissions together at once with full autonomy right from the start","Raising permissions in stages: supervised, semi-autonomous, fully autonomous","Always requiring human approval and never widening permissions"], "eEn": "Staged autonomy raises the degree of autonomy step by step while verifying. It extends capability while keeping risk down."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】サンドボックスを用意する理由はどれか。","o":["危険な操作を本番に影響させず検証できる","ユーザーインターフェースを描画するため","対話履歴を長く保持しておくため","APIの課金コストを削減するため"],"a":0,"e":"サンドボックスは隔離された環境なので、危険な操作を本番に影響させずに試して検証できる。安全に反復開発する土台になる。対話履歴の保持や画面の描画、課金コストの削減は、サンドボックスを用意する理由ではない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Why prepare a sandbox?", "oEn": ["Dangerous operations can be verified without affecting production","To render the user interface","To keep conversation history for a long time","To reduce API billing cost"], "eEn": "A sandbox is an isolated environment, so risky operations can be tried and verified without affecting production, which makes safe iterative development possible. Keeping conversation history, rendering a UI or reducing API cost are not reasons to set one up."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】動的サブタスク生成のリスクはどれか。","o":["処理全体が常に高速になり短縮される","無制限な分解でステップ数が爆発する","APIの課金コストが確実に下がる","画面の表示が崩れて見づらくなる"],"a":1,"e":"動的生成は柔軟だが、分解の深さ・数に上限を設けないとステップが爆発しコストが膨らむ。", "qEn": "[Advanced] What is a risk of dynamic subtask generation?", "oEn": ["The whole process always becomes faster and takes less time","Unbounded decomposition makes the step count explode","API billing cost reliably goes down","The screen display breaks and becomes hard to read"], "eEn": "Dynamic generation is flexible, but without a cap on the depth and number of decompositions, steps explode and costs balloon."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】並列ワーカーの結果統合で生じる主な課題はどれか。","o":["競合・重複を解消して一貫した出力にまとめること","APIの課金コストが確実に下がっていくこと","処理全体が常に高速化し全体の実行時間が短縮されること","画面の表示が崩れて見づらくなること"],"a":0,"e":"並列ワーカーの結果を統合するときの課題は、競合や重複を解消して一貫した出力にまとめることだ。統合ロジックが矛盾を裁定する必要がある。並列化しても処理全体が常に高速化するとは限らず、課金コストが確実に下がるとも言えない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] What is the main challenge in combining the results of parallel workers?", "oEn": ["Resolving conflicts and duplicates to produce consistent output","API billing cost steadily going down","The whole process always speeding up and total execution time being shortened","The screen display breaking and becoming hard to read"], "eEn": "The main challenge in merging parallel workers' results is resolving conflicts and duplicates so the output is consistent, with the merge logic arbitrating contradictions. Parallelism does not always speed up the whole process, and API cost does not reliably fall."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】最小実行可能版から始める利点はどれか。","o":["ユーザーインターフェースが改善される","早期に問題を発見し過剰設計を避けられる","APIの課金コストが確実に下がる","処理全体が常に高速化し実行時間が短縮される"],"a":1,"e":"最小実行可能版から始めると、小さく作って検証しながら広げられるので、問題を早期に発見でき、過剰設計も避けられる。ユーザーインターフェースの改善や課金コストの低下、処理の常時高速化を保証するものではない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] What is the benefit of starting from a minimum viable version?", "oEn": ["The user interface is improved","Problems are found early and over-engineering is avoided","API billing cost reliably goes down","The whole process always speeds up and execution time is shortened"], "eEn": "Starting from a minimum viable version lets you build small, verify and expand, so problems surface early and over-engineering is avoided. It does not guarantee a better user interface, lower API cost or faster processing."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】失敗モード分析が改善に効く理由はどれか。","o":["APIの課金コストが着実に下がる","頻出する失敗パターンを特定し対処できる","画面の見た目が改善され使いやすくなる","処理速度が常に高速化し実行時間が短縮される"],"a":1,"e":"失敗モード分析は、評価ログから頻出する失敗パターンを抽出し、原因ごとに対処できるので、改善が的を射る。画面の見た目が良くなるわけでも、課金コストや処理速度が着実に改善するわけでもない。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Why does failure mode analysis help improvement?", "oEn": ["API billing cost steadily goes down","Frequent failure patterns can be identified and addressed","The appearance of the screen improves and it becomes easier to use","Processing speed always rises and execution time is shortened"], "eEn": "Failure mode analysis extracts the most frequent failure patterns from evaluation logs so each cause can be addressed, which makes improvements well targeted. It does not make the screen look better, and it does not steadily cut cost or processing time."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【知識】単一障害点（SPOF）を避ける設計はどれか。","o":["重要経路に冗長性とフォールバックを導入する","temperatureを最大値まで引き上げる","利用するツールをすべて削除して減らす","対話履歴の量をさらに増やして保持する"],"a":0,"e":"単一障害点は、重要経路に冗長性とフォールバックを入れて、1つが止まっても別手段で続けられるようにして避ける。temperatureを最大値まで引き上げても障害点は減らず、ツールをすべて削除すると機能そのものを失う。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which design avoids a single point of failure (SPOF)?", "oEn": ["Introduce redundancy and fallbacks on critical paths","Raise the temperature to its maximum value","Delete and reduce all the tools in use","Increase the amount of conversation history kept even further"], "eEn": "A single point of failure is avoided by adding redundancy and fallbacks on critical paths so work continues through another route if one fails. Raising temperature to its maximum does not remove failure points, and deleting all the tools would remove the functionality itself."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】探索（explore）と活用（exploit）の調整とは何か。","o":["並列実行と直列実行のどちらを選ぶかを決めること","モデルの温度パラメータを高低に切り替えて出力の多様性を制御すること","利用可能なツールの総数を状況に応じて増減させること","新手段を試すことと既知の有効手段を使うことの配分を調整する"],"a":3,"e":"探索vs活用はタスク段階に応じて配分を変える調整。新規探索と既知活用のバランス。", "qEn": "[Advanced] What is balancing exploration and exploitation?", "oEn": ["Deciding whether to choose parallel or serial execution","Controlling output diversity by switching the model's temperature parameter between high and low","Increasing or decreasing the total number of available tools depending on the situation","Adjusting the allocation between trying new approaches and using known effective ones"], "eEn": "Exploration versus exploitation is the adjustment of changing the allocation according to the stage of the task: the balance between new exploration and using what is known."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】ホットパス最適化とは何か。","o":["呼び出し回数が最少の経路だけを集中的に最適化する","利用頻度の低い経路を優先的に改善する","全ての実行経路を均等に最適化して平均遅延を下げる","最頻出の経路を優先して高速化・低コスト化する"],"a":3,"e":"ホットパス最適化は、最も頻繁に通る経路を優先して高速化・低コスト化する。頻出経路の改善が全体に最も効くからだ。利用頻度の低い経路や呼び出しが最少の経路を優先すると効果が小さく、全経路を均等に最適化する方法も効率が悪い。", "qEn": "[Advanced] What is hot path optimization?", "oEn": ["Intensively optimizing only the path with the fewest calls","Preferentially improving rarely used paths","Optimizing all execution paths equally to lower the average latency","Prioritizing the most frequent paths for speed and cost"], "eEn": "Hot-path optimization prioritizes speeding up and cheapening the most frequently used path, since improving it helps the whole system most. Prioritizing rarely used or least-called paths has little effect, and optimizing every path evenly is inefficient."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】エージェントをステートレスに保つ利点はどれか。","o":["各インスタンスがローカルにセッション状態を蓄積でき文脈参照のオーバーヘッドが確実に減る","インスタンス固有のキャッシュに依存でき課金と計算量を確実に削減できる","外部状態により任意のインスタンスが処理を引き継げ、水平スケールと障害復旧が容易","リクエストごとに全ての処理が必ず高速化され応答遅延が一定に保たれる"],"a":2,"e":"ステートレスなエージェントは状態を外部に持つので、任意のインスタンスが処理を引き継げる。水平スケールと障害復旧が容易になる理由だ。ローカルのセッション状態やインスタンス固有のキャッシュに頼ると、そのインスタンスが落ちたときに状態を失う。", "qEn": "[Advanced] What is the benefit of keeping an agent stateless?", "oEn": ["Each instance can accumulate session state locally, reliably reducing the overhead of referencing context","It can rely on instance-specific caches, reliably cutting billing and computation","With external state, any instance can take over, making horizontal scaling and failure recovery easy","Every process is always faster for each request, and response latency stays constant"], "eEn": "A stateless agent keeps its state externally, so any instance can take over, which is why horizontal scaling and failure recovery become easy. Relying on local session state or an instance-specific cache means the state is lost when that instance goes down."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【知識】単一責任設計が保守性を高める理由はどれか。","o":["常に実行速度が向上し応答遅延が確実に短縮される","役割が明確になり変更が局所化されテストが容易になる","実行時の課金額が下がりインフラコストが最小化される","コンポーネント間の結合が増え再利用性が高まる"],"a":1,"e":"責任を分離するとコンポーネント単位で変更が局所化され、テスト・修正が容易になる。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Why does a single-responsibility design improve maintainability?", "oEn": ["Execution speed always improves and response latency is reliably shortened","Roles become clear, changes are localized, and testing becomes easy","Billing at runtime goes down and infrastructure cost is minimized","Coupling between components increases and reusability rises"], "eEn": "Separating responsibilities localizes changes to the component, making testing and fixes easy."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】入力種別ごとに処理が分かれ、各種別の件数が事前に確定している業務がある。最適なのはどれか。","o":["単一エージェントの自律ループに一任する","ルーティング＋並列化（セクショニング）の組み合わせ","オーケストレーター・ワーカー方式で実行時に動的にサブタスクを分解する","評価者・最適化者ループで反復的に品質改善する"],"a":1,"e":"種別固定なら動的分割不要でオーケストレーターは過剰。分類（ルーティング）後に独立処理を並列実行する。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A task splits by input type, and the count for each type is fixed in advance. What is best?", "oEn": ["Leave it all to a single agent's autonomous loop","A combination of routing and parallelization (sectioning)","Decompose subtasks dynamically at runtime with orchestrator-workers","Iteratively improve quality with an evaluator-optimizer loop"], "eEn": "With fixed types, dynamic splitting is unnecessary and an orchestrator is overkill. After classification (routing), run independent processing in parallel."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】サブエージェントが返却前に要約しないことの最大の問題はどれか。","o":["サブエージェントの実行速度が常に低下してしまう","親の文脈が生ログで圧迫され、隔離の利点が失われる","並列サブエージェント間で出力フォーマットが自動的に統一される","親エージェントの課金額が予測できなくなる"],"a":1,"e":"隔離の利点は親が要約だけ受け取ること。生ログ返却はその利点を消し文脈を圧迫する。", "qEn": "[Advanced] What is the biggest problem with a subagent not summarizing before returning?", "oEn": ["The subagent's execution speed always drops","Raw logs squeeze the parent's context, and isolation's benefit is lost","The output format is automatically unified across all of the parallel subagents","The parent agent's billing amount becomes unpredictable"], "eEn": "The benefit of isolation is that the parent receives only a summary. Returning raw logs erases that benefit and strains the context."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】反復的精緻化ループでコーディネーターが「再委譲」を行う契機はどれか。","o":["利用可能なツールの数が多いと判明したとき","モデルのtemperatureが高く設定されているとき","反復回数があらかじめ定めた上限に達したとき","統合出力にカバレッジのギャップを検出したとき"],"a":3,"e":"統合段でギャップを検出したら、対象を絞ったクエリで検索・分析へ再委譲し再統合する。", "qEn": "[Advanced] In an iterative refinement loop, what triggers the coordinator to re-delegate?", "oEn": ["When it turns out that the number of available tools is large","When the model's temperature is set high","When the iteration count reaches a predetermined cap","When it detects a coverage gap in the synthesized output"], "eEn": "When a gap is detected at the synthesis stage, re-delegate to search and analysis with targeted queries and synthesize again."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【知識】サブエージェントへ前段の所見を渡す際、メタデータ（出典URL・文書名・ページ）を構造化フォーマットで分離する目的はどれか。","o":["帰属（attribution）を統合まで保持するため","後続処理全体の実行速度を確実に高速化するため","サブエージェント間の出力形式を強制的に一致させるため","トークン課金を段階的に削減して予算内に収めるため"],"a":0,"e":"出典URL・文書名・ページなどのメタデータを内容と分けて構造化して渡すと、出典の帰属が統合の段階まで保たれる。後続処理の高速化や、サブエージェント間の出力形式を強制的に一致させることが目的ではなく、トークン課金の削減でもない。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] When passing earlier findings to a subagent, what is the purpose of separating metadata (source URL, document name, page) in a structured format?", "oEn": ["To preserve attribution through to synthesis","To reliably speed up the execution of all downstream processing","To force the output formats among subagents to match","To reduce token billing step by step and stay within budget"], "eEn": "Passing source URLs, document names and pages as structured metadata separate from the content keeps attribution intact until synthesis. The goal is not to speed up later steps, to force subagent outputs into the same format, or to cut token charges."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】開放的タスクの動的分解で最初に行うべきことはどれか。","o":["詳細を検討せず全実装に即着手する","構造を把握し高インパクト領域を特定する","複数出力を生成し多数決で選ぶ","モデルのtemperatureを上げて多様性を確保する"],"a":1,"e":"動的分解はまず構造把握→高インパクト領域特定→優先順位付き計画、と進め依存発見に応じて適応する。", "qEn": "[Advanced] What should be done first in the dynamic decomposition of an open-ended task?", "oEn": ["Start full implementation immediately without examining the details","Understand the structure and identify high-impact areas","Generate multiple outputs and choose by majority vote","Raise the model's temperature to secure diversity"], "eEn": "Dynamic decomposition proceeds by first understanding the structure, then identifying high-impact areas, then making a prioritized plan, and adapting as dependencies are discovered."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】顧客サポートで80%以上の初回解決率を目標とするが、簡単な案件までエスカレーションしている。最適な改善はどれか。","o":["過去の解決済みチケット群を教師データとして分類モデルを新たに訓練する","エージェントの自己申告する確信度スコアに基づいて案件を自動的にルーティングし振り分ける","顧客メッセージの感情分析結果に応じて自動でエスカレーションする","明示的なエスカレーション基準とfew-shot例をsystemプロンプトに追加する"],"a":3,"e":"根本原因は判断境界の不明確さ。明示基準＋few-shotが比例的な第一対応。自己申告確信度は校正が悪く、分類器は過剰、感情は複雑さと無相関。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A customer support team targets a first-contact resolution rate of 80% or more, but it escalates even simple cases. What is the best improvement?", "oEn": ["Train a new classification model using a set of past resolved tickets as training data","Automatically route and sort cases based on the agent's self-reported confidence score","Escalate automatically according to the sentiment analysis result of the customer's message","Add explicit escalation criteria and few-shot examples to the system prompt"], "eEn": "The root cause is an unclear decision boundary. Explicit criteria plus few-shot examples are the proportionate first response. Self-reported confidence is poorly calibrated, a classifier is excessive, and sentiment is uncorrelated with complexity."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】55%の初回解決率で目標を大きく下回り、複雑案件を無理に自律処理している。最も効果的な改善はどれか。","o":["案件ごとに確信度スコアを算出し設定した閾値を超えたものだけを自律処理にルーティングする","顧客の感情を検出して閾値を超過した時に自動でエスカレーションする","別個の分類器モデルを新規に訓練して案件の種別を自動判定させる","いつ解決しいつエスカレーションするかの明示基準とfew-shot例を追加する"],"a":3,"e":"明示的なエスカレーション基準とfew-shotが根本原因（判断境界の曖昧さ）に直接効く。インフラ追加は前段の最適化後。", "qEn": "[Scenario] The first-contact resolution rate is 55%, well below the target, and complex cases are being forced through autonomous handling. What is the most effective improvement?", "oEn": ["Calculate a confidence score for each case and route only those above a set threshold to autonomous handling","Detect customer sentiment and escalate automatically when it exceeds a threshold","Newly train a separate classifier model to determine case types automatically","Add explicit criteria for when to resolve and when to escalate, along with few-shot examples"], "eEn": "Explicit escalation criteria and few-shot examples directly address the root cause (the vague decision boundary). Adding infrastructure comes after optimizing the earlier stage."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【シナリオ】get_customer と lookup_order の説明が共に最小限（「顧客情報を取得」「注文詳細を取得」）で、注文番号付きの質問でも誤ってget_customerを呼ぶ。最も効果的な第一歩はどれか。","o":["両ツールを単一のlookup_entityツールに統合してしまう","正しい選択を示すfew-shot例を5〜8個ほどsystemプロンプトへ追加していく","各ツールの説明に入力形式・例クエリ・エッジケース・使い分け境界を加えて拡充する","ユーザー入力を解析してツールを事前選択するルーティング層を実装する"],"a":2,"e":"ツール説明はLLMの選択の主機構。最小説明が根本原因なので、説明拡充が低労力・高レバレッジの第一歩。few-shotはトークン増だけ、ルーティングは過剰、統合は第一歩としては労力過大。", "qEn": "[Scenario] The descriptions of get_customer and lookup_order are both minimal (\"Retrieve customer information\" and \"Retrieve order details\"), and even for a question that includes an order number it wrongly calls get_customer. What is the most effective first step?", "oEn": ["Merge both tools into a single lookup_entity tool","Go on adding about 5 to 8 few-shot examples showing the correct choice to the system prompt","Expand descriptions with input formats, example queries, edge cases, and boundaries","Implement a routing layer that parses user input and preselects the tool"], "eEn": "A tool description is the main mechanism of an LLM's selection. Minimal descriptions are the root cause, so expanding them is a low-effort, high-leverage first step. Few-shot examples only add tokens, routing is overkill, and merging is too much effort as a first step."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【知識】LLM（Large Language Model）がツールを選択する際に最も依存する情報はどれか。","o":["ツールの説明（description）","ツールの実装プログラミング言語","ツールのバージョン番号と直近のリリース日時","ツールの内部実装コードの行数"],"a":0,"e":"LLMはツールの説明（description）を主な手がかりにして、どのツールを使うかを選ぶ。説明が最小限だと似たツールを見分けられず誤選択につながる。ツールの実装プログラミング言語や内部実装コードの行数、バージョン番号は選択に使われない。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What information does an LLM (Large Language Model) rely on most when selecting a tool?", "oEn": ["The tool's description","The programming language the tool is implemented in","The tool's version number and latest release date and time","The number of lines of the tool's internal implementation code"], "eEn": "An LLM mainly relies on a tool's description to decide which tool to call. With a minimal description it cannot tell similar tools apart and picks the wrong one. The implementation language, the length of the internal code and the version number are not what it uses."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】analyze_content と analyze_document がほぼ同一説明で誤ルーティングが起きる。最善の是正はどれか。","o":["analyze_content を extract_web_results に改名しWeb特化の説明に更新する","重複を避けるため両方のツールを一旦削除して一つの汎用的な統合ツールにまとめて置き換える","両ツールのモデル呼び出し時のtemperatureを下げつつ最大トークン数も制限して出力の一貫性と再現性を高める","両方のツールの説明文をより短く簡潔な文章にまとめ直して冗長な記述を全て慎重に取り除く"],"a":0,"e":"機能重複は改名＋説明更新で解消する。例：analyze_contentをextract_web_resultsに改名してWeb特化に。", "qEn": "[Advanced] analyze_content and analyze_document have nearly identical descriptions, causing misrouting. What is the best fix?", "oEn": ["Rename analyze_content to extract_web_results and update its description to be web-specific","To avoid overlap, delete both tools for now and replace them with a single general-purpose merged tool","Lower the temperature when calling both tools and also limit the maximum tokens to improve output consistency and reproducibility","Rewrite both tools' descriptions into shorter, more concise text and carefully remove all redundant wording"], "eEn": "Overlapping functionality is resolved by renaming plus updating the description. Example: rename analyze_content to extract_web_results and make it web-specific."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】汎用的な analyze_document が誤用される。推奨される設計はどれか。","o":["extract_data_points・summarize_content・verify_claim_against_source 等、目的別ツールに分割する","文書処理を全て単一の汎用ツールに集約したうえで、入力パラメータの種類を増やすことでより多様なタスクに柔軟かつ確実に対応させる","analyze_document の説明文により多くのキーワードと利用例を追記して、単一ツールのままモデルが正しく使い分けられるようにする","モデルのtemperatureとmax_tokensパラメータを細かく調整して、analyze_document の呼び出しごとに出力の粒度と応答の長さを動的に最適化する"],"a":0,"e":"汎用ツールは入出力契約が定義された目的別ツールへ分割すると選択精度と保守性が上がる。", "qEn": "[Advanced] A generic analyze_document is being misused. What design is recommended?", "oEn": ["Split it into purpose-specific tools such as extract_data_points, summarize_content, and verify_claim_against_source","Consolidate all document processing into a single general-purpose tool, and handle more varied tasks flexibly and reliably by increasing the kinds of input parameters","Add more keywords and usage examples to analyze_document's description so the model can use it correctly while it remains a single tool","Finely adjust the model's temperature and max_tokens parameters to dynamically optimize output granularity and response length for each analyze_document call"], "eEn": "Splitting a general-purpose tool into purpose-specific tools with defined input and output contracts improves selection accuracy and maintainability."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【知識】systemプロンプトの文言がツール選択に与える影響として正しいのはどれか。","o":["systemプロンプトの文言はUIの表示にのみ影響し内部のツール選択には全く及ばない","systemプロンプトは常にツールの説明より優先して解釈される","systemプロンプトの文言はツール選択に一切影響を与えない","キーワードに敏感な指示が意図しないツール連想を作り、良い説明を上書きしうる"],"a":3,"e":"systemプロンプトのキーワード敏感な指示は、適切に書かれたツール説明を上書きしてしまうことがある。レビューが必要。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which correctly describes the effect of system prompt wording on tool selection?", "oEn": ["System prompt wording affects only the UI display and has no influence at all on internal tool selection","The system prompt is always interpreted with priority over tool descriptions","System prompt wording has no effect at all on tool selection","Keyword-sensitive wording can create unintended tool associations that override good descriptions"], "eEn": "Keyword-sensitive instructions in the system prompt can override well-written tool descriptions. A review is needed."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【知識】MCP（Model Context Protocol）ツールの失敗をエージェントに伝える仕組みはどれか。","o":["空の文字列を返して示す","例外のスタックトレース全文","isError フラグパターン","HTTPステータスコードのみで通知"],"a":2,"e":"MCPはisErrorフラグでツール失敗をエージェントに伝える。構造化メタデータで回復判断を支援する。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which mechanism tells an agent that an MCP (Model Context Protocol) tool failed?", "oEn": ["Returning an empty string to indicate it","The full text of the exception's stack trace","The isError flag pattern","Notifying with an HTTP status code only"], "eEn": "MCP conveys tool failures to the agent with the isError flag. Structured metadata supports recovery decisions."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【知識】エラー分類として正しい区分の組み合わせはどれか。","o":["success（成功）・failure（失敗）・pending（保留中）・timeout（時間切れ）の四つの区分のみで扱う","transient（一時的）・validation（検証）・business（業務）・permission（権限）","retryable（再試行可）・fatal（致命的）・unknown（原因不明）の3分類","high（高）・medium（中）・low（低）という深刻度の3段階のみに分類して扱う"],"a":1,"e":"エラーは一時的（transient）・検証（validation）・業務（business）・権限（permission）に分けると、再試行するか入力を直すか、権限不足として止めるかなど、適切な回復判断ができる。成功・失敗・保留の区分や深刻度の3段階だけでは、回復方法を決められない。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which combination of categories is the correct error classification?", "oEn": ["Handle with only four categories: success, failure, pending, and timeout","transient, validation, business, permission","Three categories: retryable, fatal, and unknown","Classify only into three severity levels: high, medium, and low"], "eEn": "Classifying errors as transient, validation, business and permission lets the agent decide whether to retry, fix the input or stop for lack of permission. Success/failure/pending states or three severity levels alone cannot tell it how to recover."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【シナリオ】全ツールが汎用の「Operation failed」だけを返す。生じる問題はどれか。","o":["ログの出力量が減り監視ダッシュボードの表示が簡潔になる","全てのツール呼び出しが常に高速化され、システム全体の応答時間が確実に安定する","エージェントが適切な回復判断（再試行・代替・エスカレーション）をできない","トークン課金額が下がりコスト全体の予測がより容易になる"],"a":2,"e":"全ツールが汎用の「Operation failed」だけを返すと、失敗の種類や文脈が隠れ、エージェントが再試行・代替・エスカレーションの適切な回復判断をできない。構造化メタデータを返す必要がある。ログの出力量や監視ダッシュボードの表示、応答速度は、この設計が生む問題の中身ではない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] All tools return only a generic \"Operation failed\". What problem arises?", "oEn": ["The log output volume decreases and the monitoring dashboard display becomes simpler","All tool calls always become faster and the response time of the whole system is reliably stable","The agent cannot make appropriate recovery decisions (retry, alternative, escalation)","Token billing goes down and forecasting overall cost becomes easier"], "eEn": "If every tool returns only a generic Operation failed message, the type and context of the failure are hidden and the agent cannot decide whether to retry, use an alternative or escalate. Structured metadata is needed. Log volume, the look of the monitoring dashboard and response speed are not the problem this design causes."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】無駄なリトライを防ぐために構造化エラーに含めるべき情報はどれか。","o":["ツールのバージョン番号とビルド識別子と直近のコミットハッシュ値および実行日時","呼び出しにかかった課金額と累積したトークンの消費量","errorCategory・isRetryable・人間可読の説明","UIに表示する色コードとアイコンと画面レイアウト情報"],"a":2,"e":"errorCategory（transient/validation/permission）・isRetryable・説明を返せば、再試行可否を機械的に判断でき無駄を防げる。", "qEn": "[Advanced] What information should a structured error include to prevent useless retries?", "oEn": ["The tool's version number, build identifier, latest commit hash, and execution date and time","The billing amount for the call and the accumulated token consumption","errorCategory, isRetryable, and a human-readable explanation","Color codes, icons, and screen layout information shown in the UI"], "eEn": "If you return errorCategory (transient/validation/permission), isRetryable, and an explanation, whether to retry can be decided mechanically, preventing waste."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【シナリオ】MCP（Model Context Protocol）ツールがタイムアウトを返した。errorCategoryと再試行方針の正しい組み合わせはどれか。","o":["permissionと分類して即座にエスカレーションする","恒久的な失敗と分類してその場で処理を諦める","validationと分類し引数を修正してから再試行する","transientと分類し指数バックオフ付きで再試行する"],"a":3,"e":"タイムアウトはtransient。同じ引数で待機して再試行する。validationは引数誤り、permissionは権限不足。", "qEn": "[Scenario] An MCP (Model Context Protocol) tool returned a timeout. Which is the correct combination of errorCategory and retry policy?", "oEn": ["Classify as permission and escalate immediately","Classify as a permanent failure and give up on the spot","Classify as validation and retry after fixing the arguments","Classify as transient and retry with exponential backoff"], "eEn": "A timeout is transient. Wait and retry with the same arguments. Validation means incorrect arguments and permission means insufficient authorization."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【シナリオ】業務ルール違反（方針上限超の返金）を返すツール。エージェントが顧客へ適切に説明できるようにするには何を含めるか。","o":["空の配列と処理成功を示すステータスコードを返す","retriable: true と汎用的な内部エラーコードを返す","retriable: false と顧客向けの分かりやすい説明","汎用的な失敗を示す文字列のみを返して処理を終える"],"a":2,"e":"業務エラーはretriable:falseと顧客向け説明を含め、エージェントが正しく伝達できるようにする。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A tool returns a business rule violation (a refund over the policy limit). What should it include so the agent can explain it properly to the customer?", "oEn": ["Return an empty array and a status code indicating the process succeeded","Return retriable: true and a generic internal error code","retriable: false and a clear explanation for the customer","Return only a string indicating a generic failure and end the process"], "eEn": "A business error includes retriable: false and an explanation for the customer, so the agent can communicate it correctly."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【シナリオ】サブエージェントが一時的失敗に遭遇。多エージェント系での最適なエラー処理はどれか。","o":["失敗を空の成功結果として扱い、コーディネーターには一切報告せず隠蔽する","エラーを完全に無視してそのまま次のステップの処理へと一気に進み続けてしまう","局所的に回復を試み、解決不能なエラーのみ部分結果と試行内容を添えてコーディネーターへ伝播する","何らかのエラーを検知した時点で多エージェント系の全体を即座に停止し、実行中の処理をすべて終了する"],"a":2,"e":"一時的な失敗は、サブエージェントが局所的に回復を試みる。解決できないエラーだけ、部分結果と試行内容を添えてコーディネーターへ伝える。失敗を空の成功として隠すと誤った結果が混ざり、全体を即座に停止すると回復できる失敗でも成果を失う。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A subagent encountered a transient failure. What is the best error handling in a multi-agent system?", "oEn": ["Treat the failure as an empty success result and conceal it without reporting anything to the coordinator","Ignore the error completely and keep rushing ahead to the next step's processing as is","Recover locally, and propagate only unresolvable errors to the coordinator, with partial results and what was tried","Immediately stop the whole multi-agent system the moment any error whatsoever is detected, and end all running processing"], "eEn": "For a transient failure, the subagent tries to recover locally and escalates to the coordinator only errors it cannot resolve, with partial results and what it tried. Hiding a failure as an empty success mixes in wrong results, and halting everything at once throws away work even when recovery was possible."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【知識】ツールが『アクセス失敗』と『有効な空結果』を区別すべき理由はどれか。","o":["どちらも同一の失敗として扱ってしまえば、エラー処理の分岐が単純になるから","前者は再試行判断が必要／後者はマッチなしの成功であり扱いが異なるから","両者を区別すると条件分岐が増えて応答速度が遅くなるから","監視画面の表示を分かりやすくするためだけに必要だから"],"a":1,"e":"アクセス失敗（取れなかった）と空結果（無かった）は意味が異なる。混同すると必要な再試行が発火しない。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Why should a tool distinguish an \"access failure\" from a \"valid empty result\"?", "oEn": ["Because treating both as one and the same failure would simplify the branching of error handling","Because the former calls for a retry decision, while the latter is a no-match success","Because distinguishing them adds conditional branches and slows response speed","Because it is needed only to make the monitoring screen easier to understand"], "eEn": "An access failure (could not retrieve) and an empty result (there was nothing) mean different things. If they are confused, the retry that is needed never fires."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【知識】エージェントに与えるツール数に関する原則として正しいのはどれか。","o":["ツールの数はエージェントの選択信頼性とは全く無関係だと言える","ツールは常に1つに絞り込むことが最も高い選択信頼性をもたらす","ツールが多すぎる（例：4-5でなく18）と判断複雑さが増し選択信頼性が低下する","ツールは多ければ多いほど常に選択の精度と網羅性が高まり判断の質も確実に向上する"],"a":2,"e":"過多なツールは決定の複雑さを増し選択信頼性を下げる。役割に必要なツールに絞るべき。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which is the correct principle about the number of tools given to an agent?", "oEn": ["The number of tools can be said to have nothing to do with the agent's selection reliability","Narrowing to just one tool always yields the highest selection reliability","Too many tools (for example, 18 instead of 4 to 5) increase decision complexity and lower selection reliability","The more tools there are, the more the accuracy and coverage of selection always improve and the quality of judgment reliably rises"], "eEn": "Too many tools increase decision complexity and lower selection reliability. Narrow them down to the tools the role needs."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【知識】専門外のツールを持つエージェントに起きがちな問題はどれか。","o":["全てのタスクの実行速度が常に向上し、システム全体の応答が確実に安定する","監視用ダッシュボードの表示が崩れて全体が読みにくくなる","トークン課金が下がり運用コストが確実に予測しやすくなる","専門外ツールを誤用する（例：統合エージェントがWeb検索を試みる）"],"a":3,"e":"専門外ツールを持つと誤用しやすい。各エージェントは役割に必要なツールに限定する。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What problem tends to occur with an agent that has tools outside its specialty?", "oEn": ["The execution speed of all tasks always improves and the whole system's responses are reliably stable","The monitoring dashboard display breaks and becomes hard to read overall","Token billing goes down and operating cost becomes reliably easier to predict","It misuses the out-of-specialty tools (for example, a synthesis agent attempting a web search)"], "eEn": "Agents with out-of-specialty tools are prone to misusing them. Limit each agent to the tools its role needs."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】スコープ付きツールアクセスの考え方として正しいのはどれか。","o":["どのエージェントに対してもツールを一切与えないまま運用を続ける","全てのエージェントに利用可能な全てのツールを役割を問わず一律にまとめて付与しておく","各エージェントに対して毎回ランダムにツールを割り当てて運用する","役割に必要なツールのみ与え、高頻度の特定ニーズには限定的なクロスロールツールを足す"],"a":3,"e":"役割別にツールを絞りつつ、高頻度の特定ニーズには限定的なクロスロールツールを提供する。", "qEn": "[Advanced] Which correctly describes the idea of scoped tool access?", "oEn": ["Keep operating without giving any agent any tools at all","Grant all available tools uniformly to every single agent regardless of its role","Assign tools to each agent at random every time","Give only role-needed tools, plus a limited cross-role tool for frequent specific needs"], "eEn": "Narrow tools by role, while providing a limited cross-role tool for specific high-frequency needs."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【知識】tool_choice の設定オプションの正しい組み合わせはどれか。","o":["\"auto\"・\"any\"・強制（{\"type\":\"tool\",\"name\":...}）","\"on\"・\"off\"・\"default\" の3つのモードから指定する","\"high\"・\"medium\"・\"low\" の3段階でツール呼び出しの優先度を細かく指定する","\"sync\"・\"async\" の2つの実行方式のいずれかから選択する"],"a":0,"e":"tool_choiceはauto（委ねる）・any（必ずツール）・強制（特定ツール名指し）の3種。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which is the correct set of tool_choice options?", "oEn": ["\"auto\", \"any\", and forced ({\"type\":\"tool\",\"name\":...})","Specified from three modes: \"on\", \"off\", and \"default\"","Specify the priority of tool calls in three levels: \"high\", \"medium\", and \"low\"","Choose either of two execution methods: \"sync\" or \"async\""], "eEn": "tool_choice has three kinds: auto (leave it to the model), any (must use a tool), and forced (name a specific tool)."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】fetch_url が任意URLを取得して誤用される。制約を加える是正はどれか。","o":["fetch_url ツールを完全に削除して呼べなくする","モデルのtemperatureを下げて任意URLの誤用を減らそうとする","fetch_url の説明文を短く簡潔にまとめ直す","文書URLを検証する load_document に置き換える"],"a":3,"e":"汎用のfetch_urlを、入力を検証する制約付きのload_documentに置き換えると誤用を防げる。", "qEn": "[Advanced] fetch_url fetches arbitrary URLs and is misused. Which fix adds constraints?", "oEn": ["Delete the fetch_url tool completely so it cannot be called","Lower the model's temperature to try to reduce misuse on arbitrary URLs","Rewrite fetch_url's description to be shorter and more concise","Replace it with load_document, which validates document URLs"], "eEn": "Replacing the general-purpose fetch_url with a constrained load_document that validates its input prevents misuse."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【シナリオ】統合エージェントが頻繁に簡単な事実確認（日付・名前・統計）を要し、毎回コーディネーター経由で40%遅延する。85%は単純、15%は深い調査。最適策はどれか。","o":["Web検索エージェントが事前に周辺の余分な文脈まで先読みしてまとめてキャッシュしておく","全ての事実確認ニーズを処理の末尾までバッチとしてまとめておき、最後にコーディネーター経由で一括して返す方式へと変更する","統合エージェントに全てのWeb検索ツールをそのまま付与して制限なく自由に呼び出させる","統合エージェントに範囲限定の verify_fact ツールを与え、複雑な検証のみコーディネーター経由を維持する"],"a":3,"e":"最小権限の原則。85%の単純ケースに範囲限定のverify_factを与え、複雑ケースは既存の調整パターンを維持する。全ツール付与は責務分離違反、バッチはブロッキング依存、投機的キャッシュは予測不能。", "qEn": "[Scenario] The synthesis agent frequently needs simple fact checks (dates, names, statistics), and each one goes through the coordinator, causing a 40% delay. 85% are simple and 15% need deep research. What is the best measure?", "oEn": ["Have the web search agent read ahead and cache extra surrounding context in advance","Batch up all fact-check needs until the end of processing and change to return them all at once through the coordinator at the very end","Give the synthesis agent all of the web search tools as is and let it call them freely without restriction","Give the synthesis agent a scope-limited verify_fact tool, and keep complex verification going through the coordinator"], "eEn": "This is the principle of least privilege. Give the 85% simple cases a scope-limited verify_fact, and keep the existing coordination pattern for the complex cases. Giving all tools violates separation of responsibilities, batching creates a blocking dependency, and speculative caching is unpredictable."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】特定の抽出ツールを必ず最初に呼ばせ、その後の工程は後続ターンで処理したい。最適な設定はどれか。","o":["モデルのtemperatureを0に設定して呼び出しの順序を固定しようとする","tool_choice 強制（forced）で extract_metadata を先に呼ばせる","systemプロンプトで extract_metadata を最初に呼ぶよう指示する","tool_choice を auto に設定して、どのツールをどの順で呼ぶかを全てモデルの判断に任せる"],"a":1,"e":"特定ツールを先に確実に呼ばせるには強制選択を使う。autoやプロンプト依頼は確実でない。", "qEn": "[Applied] You want a specific extraction tool to always be called first, with the remaining steps handled in later turns. Which configuration is best?", "oEn": ["Set the model's temperature to 0 to try to fix the order of calls","Use forced tool_choice to make the model call extract_metadata first","Instruct in the system prompt to call extract_metadata first","Set tool_choice to auto and leave every decision about which tools to call, and in what order, to the model"], "eEn": "Use forced tool selection to reliably make a specific tool run first. auto and prompt requests are not reliable."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】モデルが会話テキストを返さず必ずツールを呼ぶことを保証したい。最適な設定はどれか。","o":["temperatureを0に固定する","tool_choice: \"auto\" に設定する","tool_choice: \"any\"","プロンプトで強く必ず呼ぶよう頼む"],"a":2,"e":"anyはモデルに必ずツールを呼ばせる（どれを呼ぶかは選べる）。autoはテキストを返しうる。", "qEn": "[Applied] You want to guarantee that the model always calls a tool instead of returning conversational text. Which configuration is best?", "oEn": ["Fix temperature at 0","Set tool_choice: \"auto\"","tool_choice: \"any\"","Strongly ask in the prompt to always call a tool"], "eEn": "any makes the model always call a tool (it can choose which one). auto may return text."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【知識】MCP（Model Context Protocol）サーバーのスコープに関する正しい記述はどれか。","o":["全てのMCPサーバー設定は例外なく常にユーザースコープの下で一元的に管理され全体で確実に共有される","プロジェクト用は .mcp.json（チーム共有）、個人/実験用は ~/.claude.json","全てのMCPサーバー設定は例外なくプロジェクトスコープへと常に固定される","MCPサーバーの設定にはスコープを分けるという概念自体がそもそも存在しない"],"a":1,"e":"共有ツールはプロジェクトの.mcp.json、個人/実験用はユーザーの~/.claude.jsonに置く。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which statement about MCP (Model Context Protocol) server scopes is correct?", "oEn": ["All MCP server configuration is, without exception, always managed centrally under user scope and reliably shared everywhere","Project servers go in .mcp.json (shared with the team); personal/experimental ones go in ~/.claude.json","All MCP server configuration is, without exception, always fixed to project scope","The concept of separating scopes does not exist at all for MCP server configuration"], "eEn": "Shared tools go in the project's .mcp.json; personal/experimental ones go in the user's ~/.claude.json."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】.mcp.json で認証トークンをコミットせず扱う方法はどれか。","o":["トークンを平文のまま設定ファイルに直接書き込んで保存する","アプリケーションのソースコードに直接埋め込む","環境変数展開（例：${GITHUB_TOKEN}）を使う","各ツールの説明文の中にそのまま記載しておく"],"a":2,"e":"環境変数展開で秘密をコミットせず注入する。平文・直書き・説明文記載は漏洩リスク。", "qEn": "[Applied] How can you handle authentication tokens in .mcp.json without committing them?", "oEn": ["Write the token directly in the config file in plain text and save it","Embed it directly in the application source code","Use environment variable expansion (e.g., ${GITHUB_TOKEN})","Write it as-is in each tool's description"], "eEn": "Environment variable expansion injects secrets without committing them. Plain text, hardcoding, and putting them in descriptions all risk leaks."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【知識】複数のMCP（Model Context Protocol）サーバーを設定したときのツールの可用性はどれか。","o":["接続時に全サーバーのツールが発見され同時に利用可能になる","接続のたびにランダムに1つのサーバーが選ばれる","最後に設定したサーバーのツールだけが有効になる","一度に1つのサーバーのツールしか順番にしか呼び出して使えない"],"a":0,"e":"設定済み全MCPサーバーのツールは接続時に発見され、エージェントから同時利用できる。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] When multiple MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers are configured, how is tool availability handled?", "oEn": ["All servers' tools are discovered on connection and available at once","One server is chosen at random on each connection","Only the tools of the last configured server are enabled","Only one server's tools can be called and used at a time, strictly one after another"], "eEn": "Tools from all configured MCP servers are discovered on connection and can be used by the agent simultaneously."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】探索的なツール呼び出しを減らすため、課題サマリーや文書階層・DBスキーマをエージェントに見せたい。最適なMCP（Model Context Protocol）要素はどれか。","o":["環境変数（起動時の設定値の注入）","systemプロンプト（役割や指示内容の記述）","MCPツール（外部への操作実行）","MCPリソース（コンテンツカタログの公開）"],"a":3,"e":"MCPリソースはコンテンツカタログを公開し、探索的ツール呼び出しを減らす読み取り中心の手段。", "qEn": "[Applied] To reduce exploratory tool calls, you want to show the agent an issue summary, document hierarchy, and database schema. Which MCP (Model Context Protocol) element is best?", "oEn": ["Environment variables (injecting values at startup)","System prompt (describing roles and instructions)","MCP tools (performing operations on external systems)","MCP resources (exposing a content catalog)"], "eEn": "MCP resources expose a content catalog and are a read-oriented way to reduce exploratory tool calls."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【シナリオ】エージェントが高機能なMCP（Model Context Protocol）ツールより組み込みのGrepを好んでしまう。是正策はどれか。","o":["MCPツールの説明を強化し能力と出力を詳細に説明する","MCPサーバーの数を増やして選択肢を広げる","組み込みのGrepツールを完全に削除して使えなくする","モデルのtemperatureを下げて選択を安定させる"],"a":0,"e":"MCPツール説明を詳細化し能力・出力を明示すれば、組み込みツールより適切に選ばれる。", "qEn": "[Scenario] The agent prefers the built-in Grep over a more capable MCP (Model Context Protocol) tool. What is the fix?", "oEn": ["Detail the MCP tool's capabilities and outputs in its description","Increase the number of MCP servers to widen the choices","Remove the built-in Grep tool completely so that it can no longer be used","Lower the model's temperature to stabilize selection"], "eEn": "Detailing the MCP tool description and stating its capabilities and outputs makes it get chosen appropriately over built-in tools."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】標準的な統合（例：Jira）でMCP（Model Context Protocol）サーバーをどう選ぶべきか。","o":["既存のコミュニティMCPサーバーを優先し、カスタムはチーム固有ワークフローに限る","既存のサーバーは全て避け、全ての統合を独自の実装で置き換える","統合の種類を問わず全て常に自前でカスタムのMCPサーバーを毎回一から実装していく","MCPサーバーを一切使わずに直接APIを毎回呼び出して連携する"],"a":0,"e":"標準統合は既存コミュニティサーバーを優先し、カスタムはチーム固有用途に予約するのが効率的。", "qEn": "[Applied] How should you choose an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server for a standard integration (e.g., Jira)?", "oEn": ["Prefer an existing community MCP server, and limit custom ones to team-specific workflows","Avoid all existing servers and replace every integration with your own implementation","Always build a custom MCP server from scratch every time, regardless of the type of integration","Use no MCP servers at all and call the API directly each time to integrate"], "eEn": "For standard integrations, prefer existing community servers and reserve custom ones for team-specific uses; this is the efficient approach."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【知識】Grep と Glob の使い分けとして正しいのはどれか。","o":["GrepもGlobもどちらもファイルの内容を対象に全文検索する仕組みである","GrepもGlobもどちらもパスパターンの一致だけを対象に処理する仕組みである","Grepは内容検索（関数名・エラー文字列等）、Globはパスパターン一致（ファイル名・拡張子）","Grepはパスパターン一致（ファイル名・拡張子）を担い、Globは内容検索（関数名・エラー文字列）を担う"],"a":2,"e":"Grepはファイルの内容を検索し、関数名やエラー文字列を探すのに使う。Globはパスのパターンに一致するファイルを探し、ファイル名・拡張子で絞る。両方を内容検索、または両方をパス一致とする説明や、役割を逆にした説明は誤り。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which is correct about when to use Grep versus Glob?", "oEn": ["Both Grep and Glob perform full-text search over file contents","Both Grep and Glob only process path-pattern matches","Grep searches contents (function names, error strings, etc.); Glob matches path patterns (file names, extensions)","Grep handles path-pattern matching (file names, extensions), and Glob handles content search (function names, error strings)"], "eEn": "Grep searches file contents, for things like function names or error strings, while Glob matches path patterns such as file names and extensions. Saying both search contents, both match paths, or that their roles are swapped is wrong."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【シナリオ】Editが一意なテキストを見つけられず失敗した。信頼できる代替はどれか。","o":["Grepを使って該当箇所を探し出して修正する","Globを使って対象ファイルを一覧から選び直す","Bashコマンドからsedを使って対象を強制的に置換してしまう","Read + Write で全体を読み込んで書き換える"],"a":3,"e":"Editが一意マッチを得られない場合、Read+Writeが信頼できるフォールバック。", "qEn": "[Scenario] Edit failed because it could not find a unique piece of text. What is a reliable alternative?", "oEn": ["Use Grep to locate the relevant spot and fix it","Use Glob to reselect the target file from a list","Forcibly replace the target with sed from a Bash command","Read the whole file and rewrite it with Read + Write"], "eEn": "When Edit cannot get a unique match, Read + Write is a reliable fallback."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】コードベースを効率よく理解する進め方はどれか。","o":["Globでファイル名のパターン一致だけを見て全体の構造を推測しながら進める","Grepで入口を見つけ、Readでimportを辿り流れを追う（全ファイル一括読みしない）","先に全ファイルを一括で読み込んで全体像を頭に入れ、それから該当する箇所を特定して作業を進める","Bashコマンドで全ファイルの内容を連結出力し上から順に目視で読み進める"],"a":1,"e":"段階的にGrepで入口特定→Readで追跡が効率的。全ファイル一括読みは文脈を浪費する。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is an efficient way to understand a codebase?", "oEn": ["Proceed by inferring the overall structure from only Glob's file-name pattern matches","Find entry points with Grep, then follow the flow by tracing imports with Read (do not read all files at once)","First read all files at once to take in the big picture in your head, then pinpoint the relevant parts and proceed with the work","Concatenate and print all file contents with a Bash command and read through them visually from the top"], "eEn": "Incrementally identifying entry points with Grep and tracing with Read is efficient. Reading all files at once wastes context."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】ラッパーモジュール越しに関数の使用箇所を追う方法はどれか。","o":["対象の1ファイルだけを読んで使用箇所を把握する","Bashのgrepで全文検索し、ヒット行だけをそのまま結果とする","まず全エクスポート名を特定し、各名をコードベース全体で検索する","Globでファイル名の一致だけを見て使用箇所を判断する"],"a":2,"e":"エクスポート名を特定してから各名を全体検索することで、ラッパー越しの使用箇所を追える。", "qEn": "[Applied] How do you trace where a function is used through a wrapper module?", "oEn": ["Read only the one target file to understand its usages","Run a full-text search with Bash grep and take only the hit lines","First identify all exported names, then search the whole codebase for each name","Judge usages by looking only at Glob file-name matches"], "eEn": "Identifying the exported names first and then searching the whole codebase for each one lets you trace usages through a wrapper."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】ツールの戻り値が巨大でコンテキストを圧迫した。設計上の最善策はどれか。","o":["ツール側で要約・ページング・フィールド選択し必要最小限を返す","生成のtemperatureを下げて出力量を安定させる","より大きなコンテキスト窓を持つモデルに切り替えて全件をそのまま渡す","全件をそのまま返し後段の処理で不要分を無視させる"],"a":0,"e":"巨大な戻り値はツール側で要約・ページング・射影して投入量を制御する。窓拡大は一時しのぎ。", "qEn": "[Applied] A tool's return value was huge and strained the context. What is the best design fix?", "oEn": ["Have the tool summarize, paginate, and select fields, returning only what is needed","Lower the generation temperature to stabilize the output volume","Switch to a model with a larger context window and pass all results through","Return everything as is and have downstream processing ignore the unneeded parts"], "eEn": "Control input volume by summarizing, paginating, or projecting large return values on the tool side. Enlarging the window is only a stopgap."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】ツールの戻り値に成功・失敗フラグを含める利点はどれか。","o":["画面のUI表示が見やすく改善される","API課金コストが確実に下がる","ツールの応答時間が常に一定に短縮される","モデルが成功/失敗を確実に判断できる"],"a":3,"e":"ツールの戻り値に成功・失敗フラグを含めると、モデルが結果を文章から推測せず、成功か失敗かを確実に判断できる。判断の信頼性が上がる。画面のUI表示や応答時間、API課金コストの改善とは関係がない。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the benefit of including a success/failure flag in tool return values?", "oEn": ["The on-screen UI display is improved and easier to read","API billing costs are certain to go down","Tool response time is always reduced to a constant short value","The model can reliably determine success or failure"], "eEn": "Including a success or failure flag in a tool's return value lets the model judge the outcome reliably instead of guessing from prose. It has nothing to do with how the UI looks, how fast the tool responds, or API cost."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】ツールの副作用を明示する理由はどれか。","o":["API課金の内訳をより明確に集計するため","実行速度を最適化して全体の処理時間を大きく短縮するため","モデルとユーザーが破壊的操作を認識できるようにするため","画面のUI表示をユーザーに分かりやすく整えるため"],"a":2,"e":"ツールの副作用を明示すると、モデルとユーザーが書き込みや削除などの破壊的操作を事前に認識でき、意図しない実行を防げる。API課金の内訳の集計や実行速度の最適化、UIの見た目を整えることが目的ではない。", "qEn": "[Applied] Why should tool side effects be stated explicitly?", "oEn": ["To tally the breakdown of API billing more clearly","To optimize execution speed and greatly shorten overall processing time","So that the model and the user can recognize destructive operations","To arrange the on-screen UI display so users can understand it easily"], "eEn": "Stating a tool's side effects lets the model and the user recognize destructive operations such as writes or deletes beforehand, which prevents unintended execution. The purpose is not to itemize API charges, tune speed or tidy the UI."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【知識】MCP（Model Context Protocol）のN×M問題の解消が意味するのはどれか。","o":["クライアントごと・ツールごとの個別統合を不要にする","複数サービスの課金体系を単一の共通窓口へ統一できる","利用するモデルの総数を大幅に削減できる","クライアント側のUI表現を全て統一できる"],"a":0,"e":"N×M問題は、N個のクライアントとM個のツールを個別に結ぶ統合が必要になる問題。MCPの共通標準を使えば、その個別統合の実装が不要になる。複数サービスの課金体系の統一やモデル数の削減、UI表現の統一を意味する言葉ではない。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What does resolving the N×M problem in MCP (Model Context Protocol) mean?", "oEn": ["It removes the need for separate integrations for each client and each tool","It lets the billing systems of multiple services be unified under a single common point of contact","It greatly reduces the total number of models in use","It lets all client-side UI expression be unified"], "eEn": "The N-by-M problem is that N clients and M tools would each need their own custom integration. A common standard like MCP removes the need for those individual integrations. It does not mean unifying billing systems, reducing the number of models, or standardizing UI."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】ツールの引数検証をサーバー側で行う理由はどれか。","o":["API課金額を確実に抑えるため","全体の実行速度をより高速化するため","モデルの誤入力を実行前に弾けるから","画面のUI応答を良くするため"],"a":2,"e":"サーバー側で引数を検証すると、モデルが誤った入力を渡しても実行前に拒否でき、安全性が高まる。API課金額の抑制や実行速度の向上、UIの応答性を上げるための仕組みではない。", "qEn": "[Applied] Why should tool argument validation be done on the server side?", "oEn": ["To reliably keep the amount of API billing charges down","To make overall execution faster","To reject the model's wrong inputs before execution","To improve UI responsiveness on screen"], "eEn": "Validating arguments on the server rejects wrong inputs from the model before execution, which improves safety. It is not a mechanism for reducing API cost, speeding up execution or making the UI more responsive."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】18個のツールを5個に統合したら選択精度は上がったが、ある複合操作だけ失敗が増えた。最も妥当な解釈はどれか。","o":["MCPへ移行すれば統合の副作用は自然に解消される","過度な統合で粒度が粗くなり、その操作に必要な細かい制御が失われた","生成のtemperatureを調整すれば失敗は解消できる","ツールは少ないほど良いという原則から、失敗の増加は誤差の範囲にすぎない"],"a":1,"e":"統合しすぎると粒度が粗くなり柔軟性を失う。少数化と適切な粒度は別軸で、その操作だけ粒度を見直す。", "qEn": "[Applied] After consolidating 18 tools into 5, selection accuracy improved, but failures increased for one particular compound operation. What is the most reasonable interpretation?", "oEn": ["Moving to MCP will naturally resolve the side effects of consolidation","Over-consolidation made the granularity coarse, and the fine-grained control that operation needs was lost","Adjusting the generation temperature can resolve the failures","Under the principle that fewer tools are better, the increase in failures is merely within the margin of error"], "eEn": "Over-consolidation coarsens granularity and loses flexibility. Reducing the tool count and having appropriate granularity are separate axes; revisit the granularity for just that operation."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【知識】MCP（Model Context Protocol）の3要素（ツール・リソース・プロンプト）の役割として正しいのはどれか。","o":["ツールは操作、リソースは参照データ、プロンプトは定型指示テンプレート","ツール・リソース・プロンプトはいずれも操作を実行する要素である","三つの要素はいずれも参照用の読み取りデータを表している","ツールもリソースもプロンプトも全て定型の指示を出すテンプレートである"],"a":0,"e":"ツール=操作（副作用あり）、リソース=参照データ（読み取り中心）、プロンプト=再利用可能な指示テンプレート。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which correctly describes the roles of the three elements of MCP (Model Context Protocol) (tools, resources, prompts)?", "oEn": ["Tools are operations, resources are reference data, and prompts are templates for standard instructions","Tools, resources, and prompts are all elements that perform operations","All three elements represent read-only data for reference","Tools, resources, and prompts are all templates that issue standard instructions"], "eEn": "Tools = operations (with side effects), resources = reference data (read-oriented), prompts = reusable instruction templates."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【知識】MCP（Model Context Protocol）の能力ネゴシエーションとは何か。","o":["画面のUI設定を調整する","接続時に対応機能を確認し合意する","接続後に通信速度を測定して評価する","接続時に課金条件を交渉する"],"a":1,"e":"能力ネゴシエーションは接続時に双方の対応機能を確認・合意し、互換性の基盤になる。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is MCP (Model Context Protocol) capability negotiation?", "oEn": ["Adjusting the on-screen UI settings","Confirming and agreeing on supported features at connection time","Measuring and evaluating communication speed after the connection is made","Negotiating billing terms at connection time"], "eEn": "Capability negotiation confirms and agrees on both sides' supported features at connection time, forming the basis for compatibility."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】並列ツール呼び出しが安全に行える条件はどれか。","o":["会話履歴が十分に長いこと","各ツール実行が互いに独立している","生成のtemperatureが高いこと","呼び出すツールの総数が多いこと"],"a":1,"e":"並列でツールを呼べるのは、各ツールの実行が互いに独立しているときだ。結果が前の出力に依存すると、実行順序の前提が崩れて誤動作する。会話履歴の長さやtemperatureの高さ、ツールの総数の多さは、並列実行の安全性とは関係がない。", "qEn": "[Applied] Under what condition is it safe to make parallel tool calls?", "oEn": ["The conversation history is long enough","Tool executions are independent of each other","The generation temperature is high","The number of tools being called is large"], "eEn": "Tools can be called in parallel safely when each execution is independent of the others. If one depends on another's output, the ordering assumption breaks. The length of the history, a high temperature or a large number of tools has no bearing on parallel safety."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【シナリオ】ツールが『空結果』と『アクセス失敗』を同じ空配列で返す。生じる最大の問題はどれか。","o":["認証処理が二重に実行されてしまい呼び出し全体が重複する","失敗を成功と誤認し、再試行すべき場面で再試行されない","戻り値のサイズが大きすぎてコンテキストを圧迫する","tool_choiceの指定が正しく効かなくなる"],"a":1,"e":"失敗を空成功に偽装すると必要な再試行・エスカレーションが発火しない。構造化エラーで区別する。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A tool returns the same empty array for both an \"empty result\" and an \"access failure\". What is the biggest problem this causes?", "oEn": ["Authentication is executed twice, so the whole call gets duplicated","Failure is taken as success, so a needed retry is skipped","The return value is too large and strains the context","The tool_choice setting stops taking effect correctly"], "eEn": "Disguising a failure as an empty success means the necessary retries and escalation never fire. Distinguish them with structured errors."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】ツール名の衝突を避ける方法はどれか。","o":["一意で説明的な名前を使い、必要なら名前空間を導入する","ツール名をランダムな文字列で自動生成する","すべてのツールに同じ共通の名前を割り当てる","各ツールを通し番号のみで識別して説明的な名前を省略する"],"a":0,"e":"ツール名は一意で説明的にし、必要なら名前空間を導入すると衝突を避けられる。ランダムな文字列や通し番号だけの名前は、モデルが用途を判断できず、すべてに同じ名前を付ければ衝突そのものが起きる。", "qEn": "[Applied] How do you avoid tool name collisions?", "oEn": ["Use unique, descriptive names, and introduce namespaces if needed","Auto-generate tool names as random strings","Assign the same common name to all tools","Identify each tool by serial number alone and omit descriptive names"], "eEn": "Using unique, descriptive tool names, with namespaces where needed, avoids collisions. Random strings or bare serial numbers give the model no clue about purpose, and giving every tool the same name would cause the very collisions you want to avoid."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】MCP（Model Context Protocol）サーバーのログ記録が運用に効く理由はどれか。","o":["画面のUI表示を見やすく改善できるから","API課金額を抑えられるから","全体の処理速度を高速化できるから","呼び出しと結果を追跡し失敗を診断できる"],"a":3,"e":"MCPサーバーのログがあれば、呼び出しと結果を追跡でき、失敗の原因を診断できる。観測可能性が確保される。ログを取っても、画面表示が見やすくなったり、API課金額や処理速度が改善したりはしない。", "qEn": "[Applied] Why does logging on an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server help operations?", "oEn": ["Because it can improve how the on-screen UI looks","Because it can reduce API billing","Because it can speed up overall processing","It traces calls and results so failures can be diagnosed"], "eEn": "Logs from an MCP server let you trace calls and their results and diagnose why something failed, which gives observability. Logging does not make the display easier to read, and it does not reduce API cost or speed up processing."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】tool_choice を auto のまま構造化JSONを必ず得たい。最も確実な変更はどれか。","o":["プロンプトで形式を強く指示して依頼する","生成のtemperatureを0に固定する","特定ツールを強制し、その入力スキーマで形式を縛る","直近の会話履歴を全て消去して文脈を一度リセットする"],"a":2,"e":"autoはテキストも返しうる。特定ツール強制ならスキーマ準拠の構造化出力が保証される。", "qEn": "[Applied] With tool_choice left at auto, you want to always get structured JSON. What is the most reliable change?", "oEn": ["Strongly instruct the format in the prompt","Fix the generation temperature at 0","Force a specific tool and constrain the format with its schema","Erase all of the recent conversation history and reset the context once"], "eEn": "auto may also return text. Forcing a specific tool guarantees schema-conformant structured output."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】複数の抽出スキーマがあり文書型が不明なとき、構造化出力を保証する設定はどれか。","o":["プロンプトで出力形式を強く指示して頼む","tool_choice: \"auto\" に設定する","tool_choice: \"any\" にする","生成のtemperatureを下げて安定させる"],"a":2,"e":"anyは必ずいずれかのツールを呼ばせるため、文書型不明でも構造化出力を保証できる。", "qEn": "[Applied] When there are multiple extraction schemas and the document type is unknown, which setting guarantees structured output?", "oEn": ["Strongly instruct the output format in the prompt","Set tool_choice: \"auto\"","Set tool_choice: \"any\"","Lower the generation temperature to stabilize"], "eEn": "any always makes the model call one of the tools, so structured output is guaranteed even when the document type is unknown."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【知識】stdio と HTTP（MCP（Model Context Protocol）トランスポート）の違いとして正しいのはどれか。","o":["stdioはリモート通信向けであり、HTTPはローカルの標準入出力のみを用いて通信する方式","stdioもHTTPも同じくローカル通信専用で認証は不要である","stdioもHTTPもどちらもリモート接続専用で認証が必須になる","stdioはローカル・標準入出力で攻撃面が狭い／HTTPはリモートで認証/認可が重要"],"a":3,"e":"stdioはローカル接続用で攻撃面が狭い。HTTPはリモート用で認証・認可が重要（旧来のSSEは非推奨。2026年11月時点）。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which correctly describes the difference between the stdio and HTTP MCP (Model Context Protocol) transports?", "oEn": ["stdio is the method for remote communication, and HTTP is the method that communicates using only local standard input/output","Both stdio and HTTP are local-only communication and require no authentication","Both stdio and HTTP are remote-only connections and require authentication","stdio is local standard I/O with a narrow attack surface / HTTP is remote, where authentication/authorization matters"], "eEn": "stdio is for local connections and has a narrow attack surface. HTTP/SSE is for remote use, where authentication and authorization are important."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【知識】MCP（Model Context Protocol）の「リソース」の性質として正しいのはどれか。","o":["モデルが参照できる読み取り中心のデータ単位","副作用を伴う実行操作を表す単位である","接続に用いる認証情報を格納する単位である","定型の指示を持つプロンプトテンプレートである"],"a":0,"e":"MCPのリソースは、モデルが参照できる読み取り中心のデータ単位。副作用を伴う実行操作はツールの役割で、リソースではない。認証情報を格納する単位でも、定型の指示を持つプロンプトテンプレートでもない。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which correctly describes the nature of MCP (Model Context Protocol) \"resources\"?", "oEn": ["Read-oriented units of data the model can reference","Units representing executable operations with side effects","Units that store the credentials used for connections","Prompt templates holding standard instructions"], "eEn": "An MCP resource is a unit of data the model can reference, mainly for reading. Actions with side effects are the role of tools, not resources. A resource is also not a store for credentials or a prompt template holding fixed instructions."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】ツールの結果サイズ管理が必要な理由はどれか。","o":["画面のUI表示を見やすく整えられるから","巨大な結果が急速にコンテキストを消費するから","API利用の課金コストを確実に抑えられるから","実行全体の処理速度を高速化できるから"],"a":1,"e":"ツールの巨大な結果は急速にコンテキストを消費し、後の判断に使える余地を奪う。要約やページングで投入量を制御する必要がある。画面のUI表示を整えることや、課金の確実な削減、処理速度の向上が理由ではない。", "qEn": "[Applied] Why is managing the size of tool results necessary?", "oEn": ["Because it tidies up the on-screen UI display","Because huge results consume context rapidly","Because it reliably reduces API usage billing costs","Because it speeds up overall execution"], "eEn": "A very large tool result quickly consumes context and leaves less room for later reasoning, so the amount passed in must be controlled with summaries or paging. The reason is not to tidy the UI, guarantee lower cost or speed up execution."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】過剰なエラー抑制が招く問題はどれか。","o":["画面のUI表示が全体的に改善され見やすくなる","失敗が隠れ、モデルが誤った前提で処理を進める","処理が常に高速に完了するようになる","API利用時の課金額が確実に下がる"],"a":1,"e":"エラー抑制は失敗を隠し誤った前提を生む。透過的な構造化エラーが自己修正を可能にする。", "qEn": "[Applied] What problem does excessive error suppression cause?", "oEn": ["The on-screen UI display improves and becomes easier to read","Failures are hidden, and the model proceeds on incorrect assumptions","Processing always completes quickly","API billing is certain to go down"], "eEn": "Error suppression hides failures and creates incorrect assumptions. Transparent structured errors enable self-correction."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】ツール定義の品質改善で最も効果が大きいのはどれか。","o":["各ツールの実装言語をチーム全体で一つに統一して揃える","全てのツール定義を一つの共通ファイルにまとめて集約し一元的に管理していく","各ツールに版番号を付与して変更履歴を細かく記録し続ける","名前・説明・スキーマ・例・境界条件を明確化し用途と誤用を判別可能にする"],"a":3,"e":"ツール定義は実質プロンプト。名前・説明・スキーマ・例・境界の明確さが選択精度を決める。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is most effective for improving tool definition quality?", "oEn": ["Unify the implementation language of each tool across the whole team","Gather and consolidate all tool definitions into one common file and keep managing them in a unified way","Assign a version number to each tool and keep a detailed change history","Make name, description, schema, examples, and boundaries clear so use and misuse can be told apart"], "eEn": "A tool definition is effectively a prompt. The clarity of the name, description, schema, examples, and boundaries determines selection accuracy."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】MCP（Model Context Protocol）サーバーをプロジェクトで共有しつつ認証を安全に保つ設定はどれか。","o":["平文の認証トークンを直接.mcp.jsonに書き込む","各開発者が起動のたびにトークンを毎回手入力する","認証トークンの仕組みを廃止し誰でも自由に接続できる設定にする",".mcp.json に環境変数展開で認証トークンを記述する"],"a":3,"e":"共有MCPサーバーはプロジェクトスコープの.mcp.jsonに環境変数展開で設定し、秘密をコミットしない。", "qEn": "[Applied] What setting shares an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server across a project while keeping authentication secure?", "oEn": ["Write a plaintext authentication token directly in .mcp.json","Have each developer manually type the token every time they start up","Abolish the authentication token mechanism and make it so anyone can connect freely","Write the authentication token in .mcp.json using environment variable expansion"], "eEn": "Configure a shared MCP server in the project-scope .mcp.json with environment variable expansion, and do not commit secrets."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【シナリオ】チームの標準レビューを実行する /review スラッシュコマンドを、リポジトリをclone/pullした全開発者が使えるようにしたい。どこに作るか。","o":["プロジェクトルートに置く CLAUDE.md ファイル",".claude/config.json の commands 配列に登録する","プロジェクトの .claude/commands/ ディレクトリ","各開発者のホームにある ~/.claude/commands/ ディレクトリ"],"a":2,"e":"プロジェクトスコープのスラッシュコマンドは.claude/commands/に置き、バージョン管理で全員に共有される。~/.claude/commands/は個人用、CLAUDE.mdは指示用、config.jsonのcommands配列は存在しない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want every developer who clones/pulls the repository to be able to use a /review slash command that runs the team's standard review. Where do you create it?", "oEn": ["A CLAUDE.md file at the project root","Register it in the commands array of .claude/config.json","The project's .claude/commands/ directory","The ~/.claude/commands/ directory in each developer's home"], "eEn": "Project-scope slash commands go in .claude/commands/ and are shared with everyone through version control. ~/.claude/commands/ is personal, CLAUDE.md is for instructions, and a commands array in config.json does not exist."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【シナリオ】モノリスをマイクロサービスへ再構成する（多数ファイルに影響、サービス境界の判断が必要）。最適な進め方はどれか。","o":["直接実行モードで逐次的に変更を加えサービス境界を自然に発見していく","構造を全て事前指定した包括的な指示で最初から直接実行する","プランモードでコードベースを探索し依存を理解し、変更前に実装方針を設計する","まず直接実行で始め、予期せぬ複雑さに直面した時点でプランモードへ切り替える"],"a":2,"e":"大規模・多アプローチ・アーキ判断を伴うタスクはプランモードが設計目的。直接実行は手戻りリスク、事前包括指示は探索なしの前提、複雑さは要件に既に明示されている。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You are restructuring a monolith into microservices (affecting many files and requiring judgments about service boundaries). What is the best approach?", "oEn": ["Use direct execution mode to make changes sequentially and discover service boundaries naturally","Run directly from the start with a comprehensive instruction that specifies the whole structure up front","Use plan mode to explore the codebase, understand dependencies, and design the implementation approach before making changes","Start with direct execution, and switch to plan mode when you hit unexpected complexity"], "eEn": "Large tasks with multiple approaches and architectural decisions are what plan mode is designed for. Direct execution risks rework, a comprehensive upfront instruction assumes things without exploration, and the complexity is already evident in the requirements."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【シナリオ】コードベースに領域別の異なる規約があり、テストファイルは各コードの隣に散在する。場所に依らず全テストに同じ規約を自動適用したい。最も保守的な方法はどれか。","o":["コードの種別ごとに適用すべき規約を記述したSKILL.mdを個別に用意し、それぞれをスキルとして呼び出す","テストが存在する各サブディレクトリにそれぞれ個別のCLAUDE.mdを配置し、そこに規約を記述する",".claude/rules/ にYAMLフロントマターのglobパターン（例：**/*.test.tsx）で条件適用するルールを作る","プロジェクトルートのCLAUDE.mdに領域別の見出しを設けて全ての規約を一箇所にまとめ、実際の適用の判断はすべてモデル側の推論に委ねる"],"a":2,"e":"散在するテストにはglobパターンのパス別ルールが最適で、場所に依らず自動適用される。CLAUDE.mdは推論依存・ディレクトリ束縛、スキルは手動呼び出しで自動適用にならない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] The codebase has different conventions per area, and test files are scattered next to each piece of code. You want to automatically apply the same conventions to all tests regardless of location. What is the most maintainable approach?", "oEn": ["Prepare separate SKILL.md files describing the conventions to apply for each type of code, and invoke each as a skill","Place an individual CLAUDE.md in each subdirectory containing tests and write the conventions there","Create a rule in .claude/rules/ with YAML frontmatter that applies conditionally by glob pattern (e.g., **/*.test.tsx)","Put all the conventions in one place in the project-root CLAUDE.md under per-area headings, and leave all decisions about actual application to the model's inference"], "eEn": "Path-specific rules with glob patterns are best for scattered tests and apply automatically regardless of location. CLAUDE.md depends on inference and is bound to directories, and skills are invoked manually and do not apply automatically."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【知識】CLAUDE.md の設定階層として正しいのはどれか。","o":["設定はユーザー（~/.claude/CLAUDE.md）の一階層のみで、プロジェクトやサブディレクトリのCLAUDE.mdは読み込まれず無視される","プロジェクト（.claude/CLAUDE.md か ルートCLAUDE.md）の一階層のみが有効で、ユーザーやディレクトリ単位の設定は存在しない","ユーザー（~/.claude/CLAUDE.md）・プロジェクト（.claude/CLAUDE.md か ルートCLAUDE.md）・ディレクトリ（サブディレクトリのCLAUDE.md）","CLAUDE.mdに設定の階層や優先順位という概念は存在せず、ユーザー・プロジェクト・ディレクトリのどのファイルも常に同じ優先度で一括して読み込まれ、互いの上書きは一切起きず全て対等に扱われる"],"a":2,"e":"CLAUDE.mdには、ユーザー（~/.claude/CLAUDE.md）、プロジェクト、サブディレクトリの3階層がある。ユーザー階層やプロジェクト階層の一階層のみで足りるとする説明は誤りで、階層という概念がないとする説明も誤り。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which correctly describes the CLAUDE.md configuration hierarchy?", "oEn": ["There is only one level, user (~/.claude/CLAUDE.md); project and subdirectory CLAUDE.md files are not loaded and are ignored","Only one level, project (.claude/CLAUDE.md or root CLAUDE.md), is in effect; user- and directory-level settings do not exist","User (~/.claude/CLAUDE.md), project (.claude/CLAUDE.md or root CLAUDE.md), and directory (subdirectory CLAUDE.md)","CLAUDE.md has no concept of configuration hierarchy or precedence; files at the user, project, and directory levels are always loaded together at the same priority, never override one another, and are all treated as equals"], "eEn": "CLAUDE.md has three levels: user (under the home .claude folder), project, and subdirectory. Saying only a single level exists, whether user or project, is wrong, and so is saying the concept of levels does not exist."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【シナリオ】新メンバーがチームの指示を受け取れない。原因として最も疑うべきは何か。","o":["会話の履歴が長くなりすぎて、セッション初期に与えた指示が文脈の外へ完全に押し出されて失われている","指示がプロジェクトレベルでなくユーザーレベル（~/.claude/CLAUDE.md）にある","登録済みのツールの数が多すぎて、肝心の指示の処理に全く追いついていない","生成のtemperature設定が低すぎて指示がうまく読み込まれていない"],"a":1,"e":"ユーザーレベルの設定はその個人にしか適用されず、バージョン管理で共有されない。チーム共有はプロジェクトレベルに置く。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A new team member is not receiving the team's instructions. What should you suspect as the most likely cause?", "oEn": ["The conversation history has grown too long, and the instructions given early in the session have been completely pushed out of context and lost","The instructions are at the user level (~/.claude/CLAUDE.md) rather than the project level","The number of registered tools is too large, and processing of the key instructions is not keeping up at all","The generation temperature setting is too low, so the instructions are not being loaded properly"], "eEn": "User-level settings apply only to that individual and are not shared via version control. Put team-shared instructions at the project level."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】CLAUDE.md をモジュール化し、各パッケージに関連する標準ファイルだけ取り込む方法はどれか。","o":["全ての内容を一つのCLAUDE.mdファイルに書き込む","@import 構文で外部ファイルを参照する","内容をsystemプロンプト側へ全て移す","CLAUDE.mdを削除しファイル自体をなくす"],"a":1,"e":"@import構文で外部ファイルを参照すれば、CLAUDE.mdをモジュール化し、パッケージに関連する標準だけを取り込める。全ての内容を一つのCLAUDE.mdファイルに書き込むと常に全部が読み込まれ、systemプロンプトへ移しても、削除しても、モジュール化にはならない。", "qEn": "[Applied] How do you modularize CLAUDE.md so that each package pulls in only the relevant standards files?", "oEn": ["Write all the content into one CLAUDE.md file","Reference external files with the @import syntax","Move all the content to the system prompt","Delete CLAUDE.md and get rid of the file itself"], "eEn": "Referencing external files with the @import syntax modularizes CLAUDE.md so each package pulls in only its relevant standards. Writing everything into one CLAUDE.md file loads it all every time, and moving it to the system prompt or deleting the file does not modularize anything."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】巨大なCLAUDE.mdを整理したい。推奨される方法はどれか。","o":[".claude/rules/ にトピック別ファイル（testing.md, api-conventions.md, deployment.md）として分割する","CLAUDE.mdファイルそのもの自体を削除してリポジトリから完全に取り除き、必要な規約はその都度各開発者が個別に記憶して口頭で共有しながら運用していくようにする","コード内のコメントとして区切り線や見出しを挿入し、既存のCLAUDE.mdの中を視覚的に見やすく整理して一つのまま保つ","分割はせず、全ての規約を引き続き一つのCLAUDE.mdファイルの中に章立ての大きな見出しで区切りながらまとめて書き続ける"],"a":0,"e":"モノリシックなCLAUDE.mdは.claude/rules/のトピック別ファイルへ分割すると保守しやすい。", "qEn": "[Applied] You want to clean up a huge CLAUDE.md. What is the recommended method?", "oEn": ["Split it into topic-specific files in .claude/rules/ (testing.md, api-conventions.md, deployment.md)","Delete the CLAUDE.md file itself and remove it from the repository entirely, and operate by having each developer memorize the needed conventions individually and share them verbally as needed","Insert divider lines and headings as comments in the code to visually organize the existing CLAUDE.md and keep it as a single file","Do not split it, and keep writing all conventions in the single CLAUDE.md file, separated by large chapter headings"], "eEn": "A monolithic CLAUDE.md is easier to maintain when split into topic-specific files in .claude/rules/."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】どのメモリファイルが読み込まれているか確認し、セッション間の不整合を診断するコマンドはどれか。","o":["/resume","/memory","/compact","/clear"],"a":1,"e":"/memoryは、読み込まれているメモリファイルを確認するコマンドで、セッション間の挙動の不整合を診断できる。/resumeは過去のセッションを再開し、/compactは履歴を要約し、/clearは文脈を消すもので、メモリファイルの確認用ではない。", "qEn": "[Applied] Which command checks which memory files are loaded and diagnoses inconsistencies between sessions?", "oEn": ["/resume","/memory (view)","/compact","/clear"], "eEn": "/memory shows which memory files are loaded, so it can be used to diagnose inconsistent behavior between sessions. /resume resumes a past session, /compact summarizes the history and /clear wipes the context, and none of them is for checking memory files."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【知識】プロジェクトスコープとユーザースコープのスラッシュコマンドの違いはどれか。","o":["前者は個人用として ~/.claude/commands/ に置かれ、後者はチームで共有する .claude/commands/ に置かれる","どちらも ~/.claude/commands/ に置かれる個人専用の設定で、他の開発者とは共有されない","どちらも .claude/commands/ に置かれ、チーム全体でVCSを介して共有される点で全く同じ扱いになる","前者は .claude/commands/（VCSで共有）／後者は ~/.claude/commands/（個人）"],"a":3,"e":"プロジェクトの.claude/commands/はVCS共有、ユーザーの~/.claude/commands/は個人用。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is the difference between project-scope and user-scope slash commands?", "oEn": ["The former is personal and placed in ~/.claude/commands/, and the latter is shared with the team and placed in .claude/commands/","Both are personal-only settings placed in ~/.claude/commands/ and are not shared with other developers","Both are placed in .claude/commands/ and are treated exactly the same, shared across the whole team via VCS","The former is .claude/commands/ (shared via VCS); the latter is ~/.claude/commands/ (personal)"], "eEn": "The project's .claude/commands/ is shared via VCS, and the user's ~/.claude/commands/ is personal."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【知識】SKILL.md のフロントマターでサポートされる設定はどれか。","o":["model・region・endpoint といった接続先の指定","billing・quota・rate_limit といった課金関連の設定","context: fork・allowed-tools・argument-hint","temperature・max_tokens・top_p などの生成パラメータ全般"],"a":2,"e":"SKILL.mdフロントマターはcontext: fork・allowed-tools・argument-hint等をサポートする。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which settings are supported in SKILL.md frontmatter?", "oEn": ["Connection target specifications such as model, region, and endpoint","Billing-related settings such as billing, quota, and rate_limit","context: fork, allowed-tools, argument-hint","Generation parameters in general such as temperature, max_tokens, and top_p"], "eEn": "SKILL.md frontmatter supports context: fork, allowed-tools, argument-hint, and others."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】冗長な出力を出すスキル（コードベース解析等）を主会話の文脈から隔離したい。最適な設定はどれか。","o":["allowed-tools を空に設定して使えるツールを無くす","context: shared を指定して主会話と文脈を共有させる","argument-hint を付けて引数の入力例を明示する","context: fork で隔離サブエージェント文脈で実行する"],"a":3,"e":"context: forkは隔離サブ文脈で実行し、スキル出力が主会話を汚さないようにする。", "qEn": "[Applied] You want to isolate a skill that produces verbose output (e.g., codebase analysis) from the main conversation context. What is the best setting?", "oEn": ["Set allowed-tools to empty so no tools are available","Specify context: shared to share context with the main conversation","Add argument-hint to show example argument input","Run it in an isolated subagent context with context: fork"], "eEn": "context: fork runs in an isolated sub-context so the skill's output does not pollute the main conversation."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】スキル実行中のツールアクセスを制限し破壊的操作を防ぎたい。最適な設定はどれか。","o":["context: fork のみを設定して文脈を分離する","生成時のtemperatureを大きく下げて出力の変動を抑え込む","フロントマターの allowed-tools でツールを制限する","argument-hint のみを指定して引数の例を示す"],"a":2,"e":"allowed-toolsでスキル実行中の使用可能ツールを制限し、破壊的操作を防げる。", "qEn": "[Applied] You want to restrict tool access while a skill runs to prevent destructive operations. What is the best setting?", "oEn": ["Set only context: fork to separate the context","Greatly lower the temperature at generation to suppress output variation","Restrict the tools with allowed-tools in the frontmatter","Specify only argument-hint to show example arguments"], "eEn": "allowed-tools restricts the tools usable while the skill runs, preventing destructive operations."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】引数なしでスキルを呼んだ開発者に必要パラメータを促したい。最適な設定はどれか。","o":["allowed-tools フロントマター","temperature パラメータの指定","context: fork の設定","argument-hint フロントマター"],"a":3,"e":"argument-hintは引数未指定時に必要パラメータを促すためのフロントマター。", "qEn": "[Applied] You want to prompt a developer who invoked a skill without arguments for the required parameters. What is the best setting?", "oEn": ["allowed-tools frontmatter","Specifying the temperature parameter","The context: fork setting","argument-hint frontmatter"], "eEn": "argument-hint is the frontmatter used to prompt for required parameters when no arguments are given."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【知識】スキルとCLAUDE.mdの使い分けとして正しいのはどれか。","o":["スキルもCLAUDE.mdもどちらもオンデマンドで、必要時にのみ手動で呼び出す","スキルはオンデマンド呼び出しのタスク特化、CLAUDE.mdは常時読み込みの普遍的標準","スキルもCLAUDE.mdもどちらも常時読み込まれ、内容は自動で全て適用される","スキルは常時読み込まれる普遍的な標準で、CLAUDE.mdはオンデマンドで呼び出すタスク特化型である"],"a":1,"e":"スキルはタスク特化の知識をオンデマンドで呼び出す仕組みで、CLAUDE.mdは常時読み込まれる普遍的な標準を置く場所。両方が常時読み込まれる、両方がオンデマンドになる、あるいはスキルは常時読み込まれるとする説明は誤り。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which correctly describes when to use skills versus CLAUDE.md?", "oEn": ["Both skills and CLAUDE.md are on-demand and are invoked manually only when needed","Skills are task-specific and invoked on demand; CLAUDE.md holds universal standards that are always loaded","Both skills and CLAUDE.md are always loaded, and all of their content is applied automatically","Skills are universal standards that are always loaded, and CLAUDE.md is task-specific and on demand"], "eEn": "A skill holds task-specific knowledge that is invoked on demand, while CLAUDE.md holds universal standards that are always loaded. Saying both are always loaded, both are on demand, or that skills are the always-loaded ones is wrong."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】チームメイトに影響を与えずスキルを個人的にカスタマイズしたい。最適な方法はどれか。","o":["共有しているスキルそのものを削除して各自が毎回一から作り直させる","変更内容をルートのCLAUDE.mdに直接書き込む","~/.claude/skills/ に別名の個人バリアントを作る","プロジェクトのスキルファイルを直接書き換えてしまう"],"a":2,"e":"個人カスタマイズは~/.claude/skills/に別名で作り、チームへの影響を避ける。", "qEn": "[Applied] You want to customize a skill personally without affecting teammates. What is the best method?", "oEn": ["Delete the shared skill itself and have everyone recreate it from scratch each time","Write the changes directly into the root CLAUDE.md","Create a personal variant under a different name in ~/.claude/skills/","Directly rewrite the project's skill file"], "eEn": "Create personal customizations under a different name in ~/.claude/skills/ to avoid affecting the team."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【知識】.claude/rules/ のYAMLフロントマター paths フィールドの役割はどれか。","o":["特定のルールを完全に無効化して、どのファイルでも一切適用させない設定である","登録された全てのルールを常に無条件で読み込ませる指定である","globパターンに一致するファイル編集時にのみルールを条件付きで有効化する","画面のUI表示に関する見た目の設定を細かく指定するものである"],"a":2,"e":"pathsのglobパターンで、一致するファイル編集時にだけルールを読み込み、無関係な文脈とトークンを減らす。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is the role of the paths field in the YAML frontmatter of .claude/rules/?", "oEn": ["A setting that completely disables a specific rule so it is never applied to any file","A specification that makes all registered rules always load unconditionally","Conditionally activates the rule only when editing files that match a glob pattern","A field that specifies detailed visual settings for the on-screen UI display"], "eEn": "With glob patterns in paths, the rule is loaded only when editing matching files, reducing irrelevant context and tokens."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】複数ディレクトリにまたがる規約（散在するテストファイル等）に、ディレクトリ別CLAUDE.mdよりglobパターンルールが優れる理由はどれか。","o":["画面のUI表示がより見やすく改善されるようになるから","API利用にかかる課金コストをより安く抑えられるようになるから","実行時に常に全体の処理が高速に動作するようになるから","ディレクトリ位置に依らずファイル型単位で規約を適用できるから"],"a":3,"e":"globパターンルールは位置に依らずファイル型で適用でき、散在ファイルに有効。CLAUDE.mdはディレクトリ束縛。", "qEn": "[Applied] Why are glob-pattern rules better than per-directory CLAUDE.md files for conventions that span multiple directories (such as scattered test files)?", "oEn": ["Because the on-screen UI display becomes easier to read","Because the billing cost incurred by API usage can be kept even lower","Because overall processing always runs faster at execution time","Because conventions apply by file type, not by directory location"], "eEn": "Glob-pattern rules apply by file type regardless of location, which works for scattered files. CLAUDE.md is bound to directories."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】terraform配下のファイル編集時だけ規約を読み込ませたい。正しい設定はどれか。","o":["paths: [\"terraform/**/*\"] をYAMLフロントマターに書く","リポジトリ内の全てのファイルに対して無条件で常に適用させる","ルートのCLAUDE.mdに規約を書いてそのままプロジェクト全体へ一律に反映させる","terraform専用のスキルを新たに作成してそこに規約をまとめる"],"a":0,"e":"paths: [\"terraform/**/*\"]で、一致ファイル編集時のみルールが読み込まれる。", "qEn": "[Applied] You want conventions loaded only when editing files under terraform. What is the correct setting?", "oEn": ["Write paths: [\"terraform/**/*\"] in the YAML frontmatter","Apply them unconditionally to all files in the repository at all times","Write the conventions in the root CLAUDE.md and apply them uniformly to the whole project as is","Create a new terraform-specific skill and consolidate the conventions there"], "eEn": "With paths: [\"terraform/**/*\"], the rule is loaded only when editing matching files."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【知識】プランモードが設計されている対象タスクはどれか。","o":["既存の検証ロジックへ短いアサーションを一行追加","コメント文言の修正やインデント調整といった軽微なスタイル変更","大規模変更・複数の有効アプローチ・アーキ判断・多ファイル修正","スタックトレースが明確な単一ファイルのバグ修正"],"a":2,"e":"プランモードは大規模・多アプローチ・アーキ判断・多ファイル修正のような複雑タスク向け。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which tasks is plan mode designed for?", "oEn": ["Adding a single short assertion line to existing validation logic","Minor style changes, such as fixing a comment's wording or adjusting indentation","Large-scale changes, several valid approaches, architectural decisions, multi-file edits","A single-file bug fix with a clear stack trace"], "eEn": "Plan mode is for complex tasks such as large-scale changes, multiple approaches, architectural decisions, and multi-file changes."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【知識】直接実行が適切なのはどれか。","o":["複数の有効アプローチがあるアーキテクチャ判断","モノリスを複数サービスへ分割する構造的リファクタリング","単純でスコープが明確な変更（1関数への検証追加等）","45ファイルに及ぶ大規模なライブラリ移行"],"a":2,"e":"1関数への検証追加のように単純でスコープが明確な変更は、計画を挟まず直接実行するのが適切。複数の有効なアプローチがあるアーキテクチャ判断や、サービス分割のリファクタリング、45ファイルのライブラリ移行は規模が大きく、プランモードで計画を立てるべき。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] When is direct execution appropriate?", "oEn": ["An architectural decision with multiple valid approaches","A structural refactoring that breaks a monolith apart into several separate services","A simple change with a clear scope (e.g., adding validation to one function)","A large-scale library migration spanning 45 files"], "eEn": "A simple change with a clear scope, such as adding validation to one function, is best done by direct execution. An architecture decision with several valid approaches, a refactoring that splits a monolith, or a 45-file library migration is large and calls for plan mode."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】多段タスクで文脈窓の枯渇を防ぎつつ冗長な発見フェーズを処理したい。最適な手段はどれか。","o":["会話履歴の保持量を増やして発見結果を全て文脈に残す","モデルのtemperatureを上げて発見の網羅性を高める","発見フェーズの全出力を主会話にそのまま残して継続する","Exploreサブエージェントで発見出力を隔離し要約を返す"],"a":3,"e":"Exploreサブエージェントは冗長な発見出力を隔離し要約を返して文脈枯渇を防ぐ。", "qEn": "[Applied] In a multi-step task, you want to handle a verbose discovery phase while avoiding context window exhaustion. What is the best approach?", "oEn": ["Increase the amount of conversation history retained and keep all discovery results in context","Raise the model's temperature to make discovery more exhaustive","Continue while leaving the entire output of the discovery phase in the main conversation as is","Isolate the discovery output with an Explore subagent and have it return a summary"], "eEn": "An Explore subagent isolates verbose discovery output and returns a summary, preventing context exhaustion."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】散文での指示が一貫せず解釈がぶれる。期待する変換を最も効果的に伝える方法はどれか。","o":["利用可能なツールの種類を増やす","指示文をさらに長く詳細に書き直す","temperatureを下げて出力を安定させる","具体的な入出力例（2-3個）を示す"],"a":3,"e":"散文の指示が一貫しないときは、具体的な入出力例を2〜3個示すと、期待する変換を最も確実に伝えられる。指示文をさらに長く詳細に書き直しても解釈のぶれは残り、temperatureを下げても指示の曖昧さは解消しない。", "qEn": "[Applied] Instructions in prose are inconsistent and interpretation varies. What is the most effective way to convey the expected transformation?", "oEn": ["Increase the number of available tool types","Rewrite the instructions to be even longer and more detailed","Lower the temperature to stabilize output","Provide concrete input/output examples (2-3)"], "eEn": "When prose instructions are interpreted inconsistently, showing two or three concrete input and output examples conveys the expected transformation most reliably. Rewriting the instructions longer and in more detail still leaves room for interpretation, and lowering temperature does not remove ambiguity."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】テスト駆動の反復改善の進め方として正しいのはどれか。","o":["テストは書かず実装後に手動で動作確認だけを行う","実装を一通り進めた後で気づいた箇所へテストを後追いで追加していく","先にテストスイートを書き、テスト失敗を共有して段階的に改善する","先に実装を完成させてから網羅的なテストをまとめて書く"],"a":2,"e":"期待挙動・エッジケース・性能要件をカバーするテストを先に書き、失敗を共有して反復改善する。", "qEn": "[Applied] Which correctly describes how to run test-driven iterative improvement?", "oEn": ["Write no tests and only manually verify behavior after implementation","Proceed with the implementation first, then add tests after the fact for the spots you notice","Write the test suite first, share the test failures, and improve step by step","Finish the implementation first, then write comprehensive tests all at once"], "eEn": "Write tests first that cover expected behavior, edge cases, and performance requirements, then share the failures and improve iteratively."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】不慣れな領域で実装前に見落としを洗い出したい。最適な手法はどれか。","o":["詳細な仕様を渡さずいきなり実装に着手して後から調整する","利用可能なツールの種類を増やして事前に探索範囲を広げてから実装に着手する","temperatureを上げて多様な実装案を一度に生成させる","インタビュー パターン（Claudeに質問させて考慮点を表面化する）"],"a":3,"e":"インタビューパターンはClaudeに質問させ、開発者が想定しなかった考慮点（キャッシュ無効化戦略・失敗モード等）を引き出す。", "qEn": "[Applied] In an unfamiliar domain, you want to surface oversights before implementing. What is the best technique?", "oEn": ["Start implementing right away without giving a detailed specification and adjust later","Increase the number of available tool types to widen the exploration scope before starting implementation","Raise the temperature to generate many different implementation ideas at once","The interview pattern (have Claude ask questions to surface considerations)"], "eEn": "The interview pattern has Claude ask questions, drawing out considerations the developer had not anticipated (cache invalidation strategy, failure modes, etc.)."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】相互に影響する複数の問題を修正する場合の進め方はどれか。","o":["相互作用する問題は単一の詳細メッセージでまとめて与える","影響し合う問題は無視して独立に扱える問題のみ対応する","temperatureを上げて複数の修正案を並行生成する","常に一つずつ順番に切り分けて個別に修正していく"],"a":0,"e":"互いに影響し合う問題は、単一の詳細なメッセージにまとめて与えると、相互作用を踏まえて修正できる。常に一つずつ個別に直すと、修正どうしの衝突を見落とす。影響し合う問題を無視する進め方も不適切。独立した問題なら逐次修正でよい。", "qEn": "[Applied] How should you proceed when fixing multiple problems that interact with each other?", "oEn": ["Give interacting problems together in a single detailed message","Ignore interacting problems and handle only those that can be treated independently","Raise the temperature to generate multiple fix proposals in parallel","Always isolate and fix them one at a time in order"], "eEn": "Problems that affect each other should be given together in one detailed message so the fixes account for their interaction. Always fixing one at a time misses conflicts between fixes, and ignoring the interacting problems is also wrong. Independent problems can be fixed one by one."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【シナリオ】パイプラインで claude \"...\" を実行するとジョブが無限に待機する。対話入力待ちが原因。正しい対処はどれか。","o":["-p（--print）フラグを付けて非対話モードで実行する","標準入力を/dev/nullにリダイレクトして実行する","--batch フラグを付けて非対話の一括処理モードで実行する","環境変数CLAUDE_HEADLESS=trueを設定して起動する"],"a":0,"e":"-p（--print）は非対話実行の正式手段で、プロンプト処理→stdout出力→終了する。他は存在しない機能やUnix回避策で適切でない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] Running claude \"...\" in a pipeline makes the job wait forever. The cause is waiting for interactive input. What is the correct fix?", "oEn": ["Add the -p (--print) flag to run in non-interactive mode","Redirect standard input to /dev/null when running","Add the --batch flag to run in non-interactive batch processing mode","Set the environment variable CLAUDE_HEADLESS=true before launching"], "eEn": "-p (--print) is the official way to run non-interactively: it processes the prompt, outputs to stdout, and exits. The others are nonexistent features or Unix workarounds and are not appropriate."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】CIで機械可読な構造化所見を生成しPRにインラインコメントしたい。最適なCLIフラグはどれか。","o":["--verboseと--log-level=debugを組み合わせて指定する","-p フラグのみを付けて結果をプレーンテキストで出力する","--output-format json と --json-schema","--stream-json フラグで逐次出力しつつ標準エラーへ整形して表示する"],"a":2,"e":"--output-format jsonと--json-schemaで機械可読な構造化出力を生成し、自動投稿できる。", "qEn": "[Applied] In CI, you want to generate machine-readable structured findings and post them as inline PR comments. Which CLI flags are best?", "oEn": ["Specify --verbose combined with --log-level=debug","Add only the -p flag and output the result as plain text","--output-format json and --json-schema","Use the --stream-json flag to output incrementally while formatting and displaying to standard error"], "eEn": "--output-format json and --json-schema produce machine-readable structured output that can be posted automatically."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【知識】CI起動のClaude Codeへプロジェクト文脈（テスト標準・フィクスチャ規約・レビュー基準）を渡す仕組みはどれか。","o":["UI設定画面で指定","CLAUDE.md","コマンドライン引数のみ","環境変数だけで渡す"],"a":1,"e":"CLAUDE.mdがCI起動時のプロジェクト文脈提供の仕組み。テスト標準やレビュー基準を渡せる。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What mechanism passes project context (test standards, fixture conventions, review criteria) to Claude Code launched in CI?", "oEn": ["Specifying it in a UI settings screen","CLAUDE.md","Command-line arguments only","Passing it through environment variables alone"], "eEn": "CLAUDE.md is the mechanism for providing project context when launched in CI. It can carry test standards and review criteria."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【知識】コードを生成したのと同じセッションが自分の変更をレビューするのが不得手な理由はどれか。","o":["長い会話履歴によって出力の描画表示が乱れ結果が読みにくくなるから","同一セッションでは処理速度が常に低下してしまうから","生成時の推論文脈を保持しており、自分の判断を疑いにくいから","セッションを跨ぐとトークン課金が大幅に増えるから"],"a":2,"e":"同一セッションは生成時の推論文脈を持つため自分の判断を疑いにくい。独立レビューインスタンスが有効。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Why is the same session that generated the code poor at reviewing its own changes?", "oEn": ["Because a long conversation history garbles the rendered display of the output and makes results hard to read","Because processing speed always drops in the same session","Because it retains the reasoning context from generation, so it is hard to doubt its own judgments","Because token billing increases substantially across sessions"], "eEn": "The same session holds the reasoning context from generation, so it has difficulty questioning its own judgments. An independent review instance is effective."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】新コミット後にレビューを再実行する際、重複コメントを避けるには何をすべきか。","o":["毎回すべての指摘を最初から漏れなく再報告させる","temperatureを上げて指摘内容に多様性を持たせて報告させる","差分に関係なくファイル全体を毎回レビューし直させる","過去の所見を文脈に含め、新規または未対応の問題のみ報告させる"],"a":3,"e":"過去の所見を文脈に含め、新規または未対応の問題だけを報告させると、同じ指摘の重複コメントを避けられる。毎回すべての指摘を最初から再報告させる、またはファイル全体を毎回レビューし直させると、同じコメントが何度も投稿される。", "qEn": "[Applied] When re-running a review after a new commit, what should you do to avoid duplicate comments?", "oEn": ["Have it re-report every finding from scratch, without omission","Raise the temperature so the findings are reported with more variety","Have it re-review the entire file every time regardless of the diff","Add past findings to the context; report only new or unaddressed issues"], "eEn": "Including earlier findings in the context and asking for only new or unresolved issues avoids duplicate comments. Having it re-report every finding from scratch, or re-review the whole file each time, posts the same comments over and over."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】テスト生成で既存テストと重複させないためには何をすべきか。","o":["temperatureを下げて安定させる","利用可能なツールの数を増やす","既存テストファイルを文脈に提供する","会話履歴を消去して初期化する"],"a":2,"e":"既存のテストファイルを文脈として渡すと、既にカバーされているシナリオを把握でき、重複するテストの提案を避けられる。temperatureを下げても、ツール数を増やしても、会話履歴を消去しても、既存テストの内容はモデルに伝わらない。", "qEn": "[Applied] What should you do to avoid duplicating existing tests in test generation?", "oEn": ["Lower the temperature to stabilize","Increase the number of available tools","Provide the existing test files in context","Erase the conversation history and initialize it"], "eEn": "Providing the existing test files as context lets the model see which scenarios are already covered, so it avoids proposing duplicates. Lowering temperature, adding tools or clearing the conversation history does not tell the model what the existing tests contain."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】テスト生成の品質を上げ低価値な出力を減らすには何をCLAUDE.mdに書くべきか。","o":["課金プランの詳細と月次利用料金の内訳や上限","本番環境のデータベース接続文字列と管理者アカウントの認証情報","モデルの重みとハイパーパラメータの調整値","テスト標準・価値ある検証基準・利用可能なフィクスチャ"],"a":3,"e":"テスト標準・価値基準・フィクスチャをCLAUDE.mdに記すと、テスト生成品質が上がり低価値出力が減る。", "qEn": "[Applied] What should you write in CLAUDE.md to improve test generation quality and reduce low-value output?", "oEn": ["Billing plan details and the breakdown and limits of monthly usage charges","Production database connection strings and administrator account credentials","Model weights and hyperparameter tuning values","Test standards, criteria for valuable checks, and available fixtures"], "eEn": "Writing test standards, value criteria, and fixtures in CLAUDE.md improves test generation quality and reduces low-value output."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】権限を事前許可する場合の注意点はどれか。","o":["事前許可はトークン課金を大きく増やすため大規模な操作では基本的に避けるべき","事前許可すれば操作は常に安全になりリスクは完全に消える","反復承認を省けるが誤操作リスクが上がるため破壊的操作の自動許可は慎重に","承認を省くと処理速度が常に低下して全体が遅くなってしまう"],"a":2,"e":"事前許可は効率的だが、破壊的操作の自動許可は誤操作リスクを高めるため慎重に扱う。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is a caution when pre-approving permissions?", "oEn": ["Pre-approval greatly increases token billing, so it should be avoided for large-scale operations","Pre-approval makes operations always safe and eliminates risk entirely","It spares repeated approvals but raises misoperation risk, so auto-allow destructive operations with care","Skipping approvals always slows processing and makes everything slower"], "eEn": "Pre-approval is efficient, but auto-approving destructive operations raises the risk of mistakes, so handle it carefully."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【知識】CLAUDE.md に書くべきでない情報はどれか。","o":["頻繁に変わる一時的な値や機密（APIキー等）","プロジェクトのビルド手順とテスト実行方法","開発時に注意すべき既知の落とし穴や制約事項の一覧","チームで共有するコーディング規約"],"a":0,"e":"CLAUDE.mdは常時読み込まれる普遍的内容を書く。頻繁に変わる値や機密は環境変数等で扱う。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which information should not be written in CLAUDE.md?", "oEn": ["Frequently changing temporary values and secrets (API keys, etc.)","The project's build steps and how to run tests","A list of known pitfalls and constraints to be aware of during development","Coding conventions shared by the team"], "eEn": "CLAUDE.md holds universal content that is always loaded. Handle frequently changing values and secrets with environment variables and the like."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】許可リスト（allowlist）方式の利点はどれか。","o":["明示的に許可された操作のみ自動実行され安全","操作ごとにランダムで許可し柔軟性を確保する","あらゆる操作を一律に禁止して実行を止める","すべての操作を無条件に自動許可して手間を省ける"],"a":0,"e":"許可リスト方式は、明示的に許可された操作だけを自動実行するので、予測可能で安全。ランダムに許可する方式は挙動が読めず、すべてを無条件に自動許可すると危険な操作も通り、あらゆる操作を禁止すると実行自体が止まる。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the benefit of an allowlist approach?", "oEn": ["Only explicitly permitted operations run automatically, which is safe","Operations are permitted at random to preserve flexibility","All operations are uniformly prohibited, stopping execution","All operations are automatically permitted unconditionally, saving effort"], "eEn": "An allowlist runs automatically only the operations that are explicitly permitted, which keeps behavior predictable and safe. Random permission is unpredictable, auto-approving everything lets dangerous operations through, and forbidding every operation stops execution altogether."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】フックで秘密情報の混入を防ぐ方法はどれか。","o":["temperatureを上げて生成の多様性を高める","コミット前チェックのフックで秘密パターンを検出する","会話履歴を定期的に消去して情報を残さない","利用可能なツールの種類を追加して検査の網羅性を広げる"],"a":1,"e":"pre-commitチェックフックで秘密パターンを検出し、人的見落としを補える。", "qEn": "[Applied] How can hooks prevent secrets from slipping in?", "oEn": ["Raise the temperature to increase generation diversity","Detect secret patterns with a pre-commit check hook","Periodically clear the conversation history so no information remains","Add more tool types to widen the inspection coverage"], "eEn": "A pre-commit check hook detects secret patterns and compensates for human oversight."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【知識】settings.json の役割はどれか。","o":["スラッシュコマンドの定義と説明文をまとめて記述する","月次の課金記録と利用料金を集計する","モデルの重みとパラメータを保存する","権限・フック・環境をファイルで管理する"],"a":3,"e":"settings.jsonは権限・フック・環境を管理し、共有設定と個人設定を分離できる。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is the role of settings.json?", "oEn": ["Describes slash command definitions and descriptions together","Tallies monthly billing records and usage charges","Stores model weights and parameters","Manages permissions, hooks, and environment in a file"], "eEn": "settings.json manages permissions, hooks, and environment, and lets you separate shared settings from personal settings."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】破壊的操作の二段階確認を設ける利点はどれか。","o":["処理が常に高速化する","トークン課金が下がる","エディタのUI表示が改善する","重大な誤操作を二重に防げる"],"a":3,"e":"破壊的操作の二段階確認は、不可逆な操作の前に再度確認を挟むので、重大な誤操作を二重に防げる安全装置になる。処理が常に高速化するわけではなく、むしろ確認の分だけ遅くなる。トークン課金やエディタのUI表示を改善する仕組みでもない。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the benefit of requiring two-step confirmation for destructive operations?", "oEn": ["Processing is always faster","Token billing goes down","The display of the editor's UI is improved and looks better","Serious mistaken operations are prevented twice over"], "eEn": "A two-step confirmation for destructive operations adds a second check before an irreversible action, so serious mistakes are blocked twice over. It does not speed things up, and it actually adds a little time. It also does not improve token billing or the editor UI."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】機能追加とリファクタリングを別コミットにする理由はどれか。","o":["変更意図が明確になりレビューと原因切り分けが容易","コミットの総数が減って履歴が短くなる","生成時のtemperatureが安定して出力がぶれにくくなる","ビルド時間が短縮されて処理が速くなる"],"a":0,"e":"目的別にコミットを分けると意図が明確になり、レビューと原因切り分けが容易になる。", "qEn": "[Applied] Why put a feature addition and a refactoring in separate commits?", "oEn": ["The intent of changes becomes clear, easing review and root-cause isolation","The total number of commits decreases and the history gets shorter","The generation temperature stabilizes, making the output less prone to fluctuating","Build time is shortened and processing gets faster"], "eEn": "Splitting commits by purpose clarifies intent and makes review and root-cause isolation easier."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】対話セッションが長引いて精度低下・コスト増したときの対処はどれか。","o":["そのまま放置して同じセッションで会話を続けていく","要約して新セッション開始、または /clear で文脈リセット","利用可能なツールを追加して処理の能力を補強する","temperatureを上げて出力の多様性を高めて精度を取り戻す"],"a":1,"e":"履歴肥大は精度低下とコスト増を招く。要約しての再開や/clearでの文脈リセットが対処。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the remedy when an interactive session drags on and accuracy drops and costs rise?", "oEn": ["Leave it as is and keep conversing in the same session","Summarize and start a new session, or reset the context with /clear","Add available tools to reinforce processing capability","Raise the temperature to increase output diversity and regain accuracy"], "eEn": "A bloated history causes lower accuracy and higher cost. The remedy is to summarize and restart, or reset the context with /clear."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】外部依存の固定（pinning）を促す理由はどれか。","o":["トークン課金を抑えるため","エディタのUI表示を整えるため","処理を大きく高速化するため","再現性を保ち予期せぬ破壊を防ぐ"],"a":3,"e":"外部依存のバージョンを固定すると、いつ誰が実行しても同じ依存で動く再現性が保てる。自動更新で依存が変わって予期せず壊れるのを防げる。トークン課金を抑えたりUI表示や処理速度を良くしたりするための工夫ではない。", "qEn": "[Applied] Why is pinning of external dependencies encouraged?", "oEn": ["To reduce token billing","To tidy up the editor's UI display so it looks nicer","To greatly speed up processing","To keep it reproducible and prevent unexpected breakage"], "eEn": "Pinning external dependencies keeps runs reproducible, since anyone running at any time gets the same versions, and it prevents unexpected breakage when an automatic update changes a dependency. It is not meant to cut token costs, tidy the UI or speed things up."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【知識】設定の優先順位（どれが上書きするか）として正しいのはどれか。","o":["ユーザー設定が常に最優先されプロジェクト設定より上位に位置する","ファイルサイズが大きい設定ファイルほど自動的に優先され小さいファイルを上書きする","より局所的・近い階層（ディレクトリ）が上位（ユーザー/プロジェクト）を上書きする","適用順序は毎回ランダムに決まり実行ごとに上書き結果が変動する"],"a":2,"e":"より局所的・近い階層の設定が上位を上書きする。サブディレクトリ設定がルートを上書きする。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which correctly describes configuration precedence (which one overrides)?", "oEn": ["User settings always take top priority and rank above project settings","The larger the settings file, the more automatically it takes priority and overrides smaller files","A more local, closer level (directory) overrides the higher levels (user/project)","The order of application is decided at random each time, so override results vary from run to run"], "eEn": "Settings at a more local, closer level override the higher levels. Subdirectory settings override the root."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【知識】ヘッドレスモードとは何か。","o":["リッチなUIを描画するモード","常に対話入力を必要とするモード","対話なしで実行する非対話モード","課金計算に特化したモード"],"a":2,"e":"ヘッドレスモードは、対話入力なしで実行する非対話モードで、スクリプトやCIに組み込める。リッチなUIを描画するモードでも、常に対話入力を必要とするモードでもなく、課金計算に特化したモードでもない。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is headless mode?", "oEn": ["A mode that renders a rich UI","A mode that requires interactive input","A non-interactive mode, run without dialogue","A mode specialized for billing calculation"], "eEn": "Headless mode is a non-interactive mode that runs without conversational input, so it can be embedded in scripts and CI. It is not a mode for drawing a rich UI, it does not always require interactive input, and it is not specialized for billing calculations."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】/clear（コンテキストクリア）の目的はどれか。","o":["エディタのUIを再描画して整える","実行中の課金処理を停止して料金を止める","使用するモデルを別のものへ切り替える","蓄積した文脈をリセットして干渉を防ぐ"],"a":3,"e":"/clearは蓄積した文脈をリセットして、無関係な情報の干渉を防ぐ。長い履歴による精度低下とコスト増を抑えられる。使用するモデルを別のものへ切り替える機能ではなく、エディタのUIの再描画や課金処理の停止を行うコマンドでもない。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the purpose of /clear (clearing the context)?", "oEn": ["Redraw and tidy the editor UI","Stop billing processing in progress to halt charges","Switch the model in use to a different one","Reset the built-up context to avoid interference"], "eEn": "/clear resets the accumulated context to prevent interference from unrelated information, and it limits accuracy loss and cost growth from a long history. It does not switch to a different model, redraw the editor UI or stop billing."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】CLAUDE.md をプロジェクトルートに置く意義はどれか。","o":["プロジェクト単位で利用料金を課金できる","リポジトリ全体に共通の文脈を集中的に提供できる","エディタのUIを描画して表示を整えられる","リポジトリ内のコードでモデルを追加学習させられる"],"a":1,"e":"ルートのCLAUDE.mdはリポジトリ全体に共通文脈を提供し、チームで規約を統一できる。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the significance of placing CLAUDE.md at the project root?", "oEn": ["Usage charges can be billed per project","It provides context common to the whole repository in one place","It can render the editor UI and tidy the display","It lets the model be further trained on the code in the repository"], "eEn": "The root CLAUDE.md provides context common to the whole repository and lets the team unify conventions."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】フックの代表的なユースケースはどれか。","o":["月次の利用料金を集計して課金額を算出する","外部データを使ったモデルの追加学習","編集後の自動フォーマットやテスト自動実行","エディタのUIを描画して表示を整える"],"a":2,"e":"フックは編集後の自動フォーマットやテスト自動実行など、品質チェックの自動強制に使う。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is a typical use case for hooks?", "oEn": ["Tallying monthly usage charges to compute the billed amount","Further training the model with external data","Automatic formatting and automatic test runs after edits","Rendering the editor UI and tidying the display"], "eEn": "Hooks are used to automatically enforce quality checks, such as automatic formatting and automatic test runs after edits."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】プランモードの目的はどれか。","o":["実行にかかる利用料金を事前に計算する","変更前に計画を提示し、危険な変更を事前に防ぐ","計画を挟まず即座に変更を実行して反映する","エディタのUIを描画して変更箇所を強調表示する"],"a":1,"e":"プランモードは、変更を実行する前に計画を提示させるので、大規模改修での危険な変更を未然に防げる。計画を挟まずに即座に変更を反映するのはその逆で、料金の事前計算やUIの強調表示のための機能でもない。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the purpose of plan mode?", "oEn": ["Calculate in advance the usage charges for execution","Show a plan before changes to head off dangerous changes","Execute and apply changes immediately without a plan","Render the editor UI and highlight the changed spots on screen"], "eEn": "Plan mode has the agent present a plan before making any change, so risky changes in a large refactor are caught beforehand. Applying changes immediately without a plan is the opposite, and the mode is not for precomputing cost or highlighting changes in the UI."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】リモート実行が役立つ場面はどれか。","o":["月次の利用料金を集計して課金するとき","収集したデータでモデルを追加学習させるとき","モバイルや外出先からタスクを委譲したいとき","エディタのUIを描画して表示するとき"],"a":2,"e":"リモート実行は、モバイルや外出先からタスクを委譲し、場所を問わず作業を進めたいときに役立つ。月次の利用料金を集計して課金することや、モデルの追加学習、エディタのUIの描画は、リモート実行の用途ではない。", "qEn": "[Applied] When is remote execution useful?", "oEn": ["When tallying and billing monthly usage charges","When further training the model using the data you have collected","When you want to delegate tasks from mobile or on the go","When rendering and displaying the editor UI"], "eEn": "Remote execution helps when you want to delegate a task from a phone or while away and keep work moving wherever you are. Totaling monthly charges, further training a model on collected data, or drawing an editor UI are not what it is for."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】フォーマット強制（フック）の利点はどれか。","o":["トークン課金が下がって費用が減る","処理が常に高速化して待ち時間が減る","収集したコードでモデルを追加学習させられる","手作業なしでスタイルの一貫性を保証できる"],"a":3,"e":"フォーマット強制フックは手作業なしでスタイル一貫性を保証し、統一されたコードベースを維持する。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the benefit of enforced formatting (hooks)?", "oEn": ["Token billing goes down and costs decrease","Processing is always faster and wait times decrease","The model can be further trained on the code that was collected","Style consistency is guaranteed with no manual work"], "eEn": "Format-enforcing hooks guarantee style consistency without manual work and keep the codebase uniform."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【シナリオ】14ファイルを変更するPRを単一パスでレビューすると、ファイルにより深さがばらつき矛盾も生じる。最適な再構成はどれか。","o":["同じPRを独立に3回レビューさせ2回以上出た指摘のみを採用する","各ファイル個別の局所パス＋別途クロスファイル統合パスに分割する","PRを3〜4ファイル単位の複数のPRに分割させる","より大きな文脈窓を持つモデルで全ファイルを一括処理する"],"a":1,"e":"注意の希薄化が根本原因。個別パス＋統合パスに分割する。文脈窓拡大は注意の質を解決せず、多数決は実バグを抑制する。", "qEn": "[Scenario] When a PR changing 14 files is reviewed in a single pass, depth varies by file and contradictions arise. What is the best restructuring?", "oEn": ["Have the same PR reviewed independently three times and adopt only findings that appear two or more times","Split into per-file local passes plus a separate cross-file integration pass","Have the PR split into multiple PRs of 3-4 files each","Process all files at once with a model that has a larger context window"], "eEn": "Attention dilution is the root cause. Split into per-file passes plus an integration pass. A larger context window does not fix the quality of attention, and majority voting suppresses real bugs."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【シナリオ】単一ファイルのバグ修正で、明確なスタックトレースがある。最適な進め方はどれか。","o":["ボーティング","評価者最適化","直接実行","プランモード"],"a":2,"e":"スタックトレースが明確な単一ファイルのバグ修正は、スコープが明確なので計画を挟まず直接実行が適切。プランモードは過剰で、ボーティングは複数の出力を比べて決める構成、評価者最適化は生成と評価を繰り返す構成であり、単純な修正には重い。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A single-file bug fix with a clear stack trace. What is the best approach?", "oEn": ["Voting","Evaluator-optimizer","Direct execution","Plan mode"], "eEn": "A single-file bug fix with a clear stack trace has a well-defined scope, so direct execution is appropriate and plan mode would be overkill. Voting compares multiple outputs and evaluator-optimizer loops generation with evaluation, both too heavy for a simple fix."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【知識】.claude/rules/ がディレクトリ別CLAUDE.mdに対して持つ構造的な利点はどれか。","o":["globパターンで複数ディレクトリにまたがる規約を型単位で適用できる","エディタのUI上で規約が見やすく整理され視認性が高まり管理が楽になる","設定ファイルの読み込みが常に高速になり待ち時間が短縮される","ディレクトリごとに課金が分離され利用料金を細かく管理できる"],"a":0,"e":"globパターンルールは位置に依らず型単位で適用でき、散在ファイルへの規約適用に強い。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What structural advantage does .claude/rules/ have over per-directory CLAUDE.md?", "oEn": ["Glob patterns let you apply conventions that span multiple directories by file type","Conventions are neatly organized in the editor UI, improving visibility and making management easier","Loading of configuration files is always fast, shortening wait times","Billing is separated per directory, so usage charges can be managed finely"], "eEn": "Glob-pattern rules apply by file type regardless of location, making them strong for applying conventions to scattered files."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】API層だけに規約を適用したい。正しいフロントマター設定はどれか。","o":["全ファイルを対象にする設定を記述する","ルートのCLAUDE.mdに直接ルールを記述する","規約をスキルとして切り出して定義する","paths: [\"src/api/**/*\"]"],"a":3,"e":"paths: [\"src/api/**/*\"]で、API層のファイル編集時のみ規約が読み込まれる。", "qEn": "[Applied] You want to apply conventions only to the API layer. What is the correct frontmatter setting?", "oEn": ["Write a setting that targets all files","Write the rule directly in the root CLAUDE.md","Extract the conventions and define them as a skill","paths: [\"src/api/**/*\"]"], "eEn": "With paths: [\"src/api/**/*\"], the conventions are loaded only when editing API-layer files."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【シナリオ】スキルが verbose な探索出力で主会話を圧迫している。フロントマターでの最適な対処はどれか。","o":["context: fork で隔離実行する","allowed-tools を増やして使えるツールを拡張する","何も変更せず既定の設定のまま実行を続ける","argument-hint を付けて引数の候補を提示する"],"a":0,"e":"context: forkで隔離サブ文脈実行すれば、冗長な出力が主会話を汚さない。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A skill is straining the main conversation with verbose exploration output. What is the best fix in the frontmatter?", "oEn": ["Run it in isolation with context: fork","Add more allowed-tools to expand the available tools","Change nothing and continue running with the default settings","Add argument-hint to suggest argument candidates"], "eEn": "Running in an isolated sub-context with context: fork keeps verbose output from polluting the main conversation."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】プランモードで調査・設計した後、計画に沿って実装する段階で使うべきはどれか。","o":["ボーティング","直接実行","評価者最適化","プランモード"],"a":1,"e":"プランモードで調査と設計を終えたら、計画が確定しているので、実装は直接実行で進める。プランモードは調査・設計の段階向けで、実装には直接実行へ移る。ボーティングや評価者最適化は実装の段階を表さない。", "qEn": "[Applied] After investigating and designing in plan mode, what should you use in the stage of implementing according to the plan?", "oEn": ["Voting","Direct execution","Evaluator-optimizer","Plan mode"], "eEn": "After investigation and design in plan mode, the plan is settled, so the implementation proceeds by direct execution. Plan mode is for the research and design phase, and implementation moves to direct execution. Voting and evaluator-optimizer do not describe an implementation stage."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【知識】-p / --print フラグの効果として正しいのはどれか。","o":["複数プロンプトをまとめて逐次処理するバッチ実行を行う","リッチなUIを起動して対話的に処理結果を画面へ描画して表示する","非対話でプロンプトを処理し結果をstdoutへ出力して終了する","対話モードを必須にして入力待ちの状態で起動する"],"a":2,"e":"-p（--print）は非対話実行で、プロンプト処理→stdout出力→終了する。CIに適する。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which correctly describes the effect of the -p / --print flag?", "oEn": ["Performs batch execution that processes multiple prompts together in sequence","Launches a rich UI and renders the results interactively on the screen","Processes the prompt non-interactively, outputs the result to stdout, and exits","Makes interactive mode mandatory and starts in an input-waiting state"], "eEn": "-p (--print) runs non-interactively: it processes the prompt, outputs to stdout, and exits. Suited to CI."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】CIの自動レビュー結果をインラインPRコメントとして投稿するために必要な出力形式はどれか。","o":["--output-format json で機械可読にする","所見を画像に描画してスクリーンショット画像の形式で出力する","HTML形式でスタイル付きのページとして出力する","整形しないプレーンテキスト形式でそのまま出力する"],"a":0,"e":"--output-format jsonで機械可読な構造化所見を生成し、自動投稿できる。", "qEn": "[Applied] What output format is needed to post CI automated review results as inline PR comments?", "oEn": ["Make it machine-readable with --output-format json","Render the findings as an image and output them as a screenshot","Output as a styled page in HTML format","Output as is in unformatted plain text"], "eEn": "--output-format json produces machine-readable structured findings that can be posted automatically."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】レビュー再実行時に同じ指摘を何度も投稿しないための指示はどれか。","o":["毎回すべての指摘を最初から漏れなく報告させる","レビュー自体を止めて指摘を一切出さないようにする","過去所見を文脈に含め、新規・未対応のみ報告させる","temperatureを上げて指摘の表現に幅を持たせる"],"a":2,"e":"過去の所見を文脈に含め、新規・未対応の問題だけを報告させると、同じ指摘の重複投稿を防げる。毎回すべての指摘を最初から報告させるのは重複の原因になり、レビュー自体を止めると指摘が出なくなる。", "qEn": "[Applied] Which instruction prevents posting the same finding repeatedly when a review is re-run?", "oEn": ["Have it report every finding from scratch, without omission","Stop the review itself so that no findings are produced at all","Include past findings in context; report only new or unaddressed ones","Raise the temperature to give the wording of findings more variety"], "eEn": "Including earlier findings in the context and asking for only new or unresolved issues prevents the same comment from being posted again. Reporting every finding from scratch each time causes duplicates, and stopping the review altogether produces no findings."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】@import を使う主な目的はどれか。","o":["外部ファイルを取り込みCLAUDE.mdをモジュール化する","起動時にモデルへ与えるシステムプロンプトを差し替える","セッションごとに文脈ウィンドウのサイズを動的に拡張する","CLAUDE.mdの内容を暗号化してリポジトリ外に保存する"],"a":0,"e":"@importは外部標準ファイルを選択的に取り込み、CLAUDE.mdをモジュール化する。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the main purpose of using @import?", "oEn": ["Pull in external files to modularize CLAUDE.md","Swap out the system prompt given to the model at startup","Dynamically expand the context window size for each session","Encrypt the contents of CLAUDE.md and store them outside the repository"], "eEn": "@import selectively pulls in external standards files and modularizes CLAUDE.md."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】.claude/rules/ のYAML paths スコープが減らすものはどれか。","o":["モデル応答のレイテンシとコスト","無関係なコンテキストとトークン使用","エージェントが呼び出せるツールの総数","生成される出力トークンの最大長"],"a":1,"e":"パススコープにより、一致ファイル編集時のみルールが読み込まれ、無関係な文脈とトークンを減らす。", "qEn": "[Applied] What does the YAML paths scope in .claude/rules/ reduce?", "oEn": ["Model response latency and cost","Irrelevant context and token usage","The total number of tools the agent can call","The maximum length of generated output tokens"], "eEn": "With path scoping, a rule is loaded only when editing matching files, reducing irrelevant context and tokens."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【シナリオ】チーム全員で使う定型操作をコマンド化したい。バージョン管理で共有するには。","o":["プロジェクトの .claude/commands/ に作成する","settings.json の権限設定に定義して配布する","CLAUDE.md にコマンド手順を記述して共有する","~/.claude/commands/ に個人用として作成する"],"a":0,"e":"チーム共有のスラッシュコマンドはプロジェクトの.claude/commands/に置き、VCSで共有する。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want to turn a routine operation used by the whole team into a command. How do you share it through version control?", "oEn": ["Create it in the project's .claude/commands/","Define it in the permission settings of settings.json and distribute it","Describe the command steps in CLAUDE.md and share them","Create it as a personal command in ~/.claude/commands/"], "eEn": "Team-shared slash commands go in the project's .claude/commands/ and are shared through VCS."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【知識】/memory コマンドの用途はどれか。","o":["現在のセッションを分岐し並行タスク用の作業コピーを作成する","プロジェクト設定と個人設定の間で生じる権限競合を自動解決する","読み込まれているメモリファイルを確認し挙動の不整合を診断する","会話履歴を自動で要約し文脈ウィンドウの使用量を圧縮して削減する"],"a":2,"e":"/memoryは読み込み済みメモリファイルを確認し、セッション間の不整合を診断する。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is the /memory command used for?", "oEn": ["Branch the current session and create a working copy for parallel tasks","Automatically resolve permission conflicts between project settings and personal settings","Check the loaded memory files and diagnose inconsistent behavior","Automatically summarize the conversation history to compress and reduce context window usage"], "eEn": "/memory lets you check the loaded memory files and diagnose inconsistencies between sessions."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】テストファイルが各コードの隣に散在する状況で規約を自動適用する最善手段はどれか。","o":["ルートのCLAUDE.mdにテスト規約を集約しモデルが推論で全ファイルへ自動適用するのに任せる","スキルとして定義しテスト作成のたびに開発者が明示的に手動呼び出しする",".claude/rules/ に **/*.test.* のglobパターンルールを置く","各コードに隣接させてCLAUDE.mdを個別配置しテスト規約を記述する"],"a":2,"e":"テストがコードの隣に散在していても、.claude/rules/に**/*.test.*のglobパターンのルールを置けば、位置に関係なく該当ファイルへ自動適用される。ルートのCLAUDE.mdにまとめてモデルの推論に任せても、適用は保証されない。", "qEn": "[Applied] When test files are scattered next to each piece of code, what is the best way to apply conventions automatically?", "oEn": ["Consolidate the test conventions in the root CLAUDE.md and leave it to the model to apply them to all files automatically by inference","Define them as a skill that developers explicitly invoke manually every time they write tests","Put a glob-pattern rule for **/*.test.* in .claude/rules/","Place an individual CLAUDE.md next to each piece of code and write the test conventions there"], "eEn": "Even when tests are scattered beside the code, a glob-pattern rule for the test files placed in the .claude/rules folder applies automatically wherever they are. Collecting the conventions in the root CLAUDE.md and relying on the model's inference does not guarantee they are applied."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【知識】プランモードが手戻りを防ぐ理由はどれか。","o":["実装コードの生成速度が上がり手戻り時の全体待ち時間が短縮されるから","生成物の見た目が整い開発者にとって読みやすくなるから","使用トークンが減り実行あたりの課金コストを抑えられるから","変更前に安全に探索・設計でき、後から依存を発見する事態を避けられる"],"a":3,"e":"プランモードは変更前の探索・設計を可能にし、依存の後出し発見による高コストな手戻りを防ぐ。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Why does plan mode prevent rework?", "oEn": ["Because the generation speed of implementation code goes up and the overall wait time during rework is shortened","Because the output looks tidier and is easier for developers to read","Because tokens used decrease and the billing cost per run can be kept down","Because you can safely explore and design before changes, avoiding discovering dependencies later"], "eEn": "Plan mode enables exploration and design before changes, preventing costly rework caused by discovering dependencies late."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】テスト生成の重複を避けるために文脈へ含めるべきものはどれか。","o":["モデルの重みパラメータ","課金プランの契約情報","実行環境のCPU使用率","既存のテストファイル"],"a":3,"e":"既存のテストファイルを文脈に含めると、すでにカバーされたシナリオを把握でき、重複する提案を避けられる。モデルの重みパラメータや課金プランの契約情報、CPU使用率は、テストの重複とは関係のない情報で、含めても役に立たない。", "qEn": "[Applied] What should be included in context to avoid duplicate test generation?", "oEn": ["Model weight parameters","Billing plan contract information","CPU utilization of the execution environment","Existing test files"], "eEn": "Including the existing test files in the context shows which scenarios are already covered, so duplicate suggestions are avoided. Model weight parameters, billing plan details or CPU usage are unrelated to test duplication and would not help."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】不慣れな領域でキャッシュ無効化戦略や失敗モードを実装前に洗い出す手法はどれか。","o":["ボーティング パターン","インタビュー パターン","リフレクション ループ","プロンプトチェイニング"],"a":1,"e":"インタビューパターンはClaudeに質問させ、見落としがちな設計考慮点を表面化する。", "qEn": "[Applied] Which technique surfaces cache invalidation strategies and failure modes before implementation in an unfamiliar domain?", "oEn": ["Voting pattern","Interview pattern","Reflection loop pattern","Prompt chaining"], "eEn": "The interview pattern has Claude ask questions, surfacing design considerations that are easy to overlook."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】移行スクリプトのnull値などエッジケースの扱いを直すのに最も有効なのはどれか。","o":["具体的な入力例と期待出力のテストケースを与える","会話履歴を消去して文脈を初期状態に戻す","サンプリング温度を下げて出力の揺らぎを抑える","利用可能なツールの数を増やして対応範囲を広げる"],"a":0,"e":"具体的なテストケース（入力例＋期待出力）を与えると、エッジケースの扱いを的確に修正できる。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is most effective for fixing the handling of edge cases such as null values in a migration script?", "oEn": ["Provide test cases with concrete example inputs and expected outputs","Clear the conversation history to return the context to its initial state","Lower the sampling temperature to suppress output fluctuation","Increase the number of available tools to broaden coverage"], "eEn": "Giving concrete test cases (example input + expected output) lets you fix edge case handling precisely."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【知識】独立したレビューインスタンスが自己レビューより優れる主因はどれか。","o":["追加の課金が発生せずコストをかけずに実行できる","生成時の推論文脈を持たず客観的に問題を検出できる","処理速度が速く大量のコードを一度に短時間で走査できる","生成モデルと同一の文脈を共有し一貫性を保てる"],"a":1,"e":"独立インスタンスは生成文脈を持たないため、自己レビューでは見逃す微妙な問題を客観検出できる。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is the main reason an independent review instance outperforms self-review?", "oEn": ["No additional billing is incurred, so it can run at no cost","It has no reasoning context from generation, so it can detect problems objectively","It is fast and can scan a large amount of code all at once","It shares the same context as the generating model and can maintain consistency"], "eEn": "An independent instance has no generation context, so it can objectively detect subtle problems that self-review misses."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】大規模PRレビューの注意の希薄化を避ける構成はどれか。","o":["レビュー前に開発者にPR自体を小さく分割し直させる","全ファイルを単一のパスでまとめて一度にレビューさせる","ファイル単位の局所パスとクロスファイル統合パスに分割する","使用するモデルをより長い文脈長を持つ上位モデルへ変更する"],"a":2,"e":"大規模PRは、ファイル単位の局所パスと、クロスファイルの統合パスに分けてレビューすると、注意が薄まらず、矛盾した所見も避けられる。全ファイルを単一のパスで一度にレビューさせるのが、注意の希薄化を招く元の構成である。", "qEn": "[Applied] Which structure avoids attention dilution in large PR reviews?", "oEn": ["Have the developer re-split the PR itself into smaller ones before review","Have all files reviewed together in a single pass at once","Split into per-file local passes and a cross-file integration pass","Change the model to a higher-tier model with a longer context length"], "eEn": "Splitting a large PR review into per-file local passes plus a cross-file integration pass keeps attention from thinning and avoids contradictory findings. Reviewing every file in a single pass at once is the setup that causes the attention dilution."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【シナリオ】settings.json で共有設定と個人設定を分けたい。正しい考え方はどれか。","o":["すべての設定を個人用ファイルにまとめて各自が管理する","設定ファイルを使わず起動時に毎回手動で指定する","すべての設定を共有ファイルに集約しチーム全体で常に一元管理する","権限・フック・環境をファイルで管理し、共有分と個人分を分離する"],"a":3,"e":"settings.jsonは権限・フック・環境を管理し、共有と個人を分離できる。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want to separate shared and personal settings in settings.json. What is the correct way to think about it?", "oEn": ["Put all settings in a personal file and have each person manage them","Don't use settings files and specify everything manually at every startup","Consolidate all settings into a shared file and always manage them centrally for the whole team","Manage permissions, hooks, and environment in files, separating shared from personal"], "eEn": "settings.json manages permissions, hooks, and environment and lets you separate shared from personal."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】CI起動のClaude Codeにレビュー基準を渡すにはどこに書くか。","o":["実行時の標準入力","環境変数の設定値","コマンドライン引数","CLAUDE.md"],"a":3,"e":"CLAUDE.mdがCI起動時のプロジェクト文脈（レビュー基準等）提供の仕組み。", "qEn": "[Applied] Where do you write review criteria to pass them to Claude Code launched in CI?", "oEn": ["Standard input at runtime","Environment variable values","Command-line arguments","CLAUDE.md"], "eEn": "CLAUDE.md is the mechanism for providing project context (review criteria, etc.) when launched in CI."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】破壊的操作の自動許可で誤操作リスクを抑える方法はどれか。","o":["操作をランダムに選んで一部だけ自動実行する","すべての操作を無条件に自動許可して実行を高速化する","許可リスト方式で明示許可された操作のみ自動実行する","すべての操作を一律に禁止して手動実行のみに限定する"],"a":2,"e":"許可リストにより明示許可された操作のみ自動実行され、予測可能性と安全性が高まる。", "qEn": "[Applied] How do you reduce the risk of mistaken operations when auto-approving destructive operations?", "oEn": ["Pick operations at random and auto-run only some of them","Automatically approve every operation unconditionally to speed up execution","Use an allowlist: only explicitly permitted operations run automatically","Uniformly prohibit all operations and limit to manual execution only"], "eEn": "An allowlist runs only explicitly permitted operations automatically, improving predictability and safety."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】コミット前に秘密情報の混入を防ぐ仕組みはどれか。","o":["サンプリング温度を上げて生成される出力の多様性を高める","利用可能なツールを追加してコミット時のスキャン範囲を広げる","コミット後に会話履歴を自動で消去して秘密の痕跡を残さないようにする","pre-commitチェックのフックで秘密パターンを検出する"],"a":3,"e":"pre-commitフックでコミットの前に秘密パターンを検出すれば、人の見落としを補える。サンプリング温度を上げても出力が変わるだけで混入は防げない。コミット後に会話履歴を消しても、すでに入った秘密はリポジトリに残る。", "qEn": "[Applied] Which mechanism prevents secrets from slipping in before a commit?", "oEn": ["Raise the sampling temperature to increase the diversity of generated output","Add tools to widen the scan scope at commit time","Automatically clear the conversation history after the commit so no trace of secrets remains","Detect secret patterns with a pre-commit check hook"], "eEn": "A pre-commit hook that detects secret patterns before the commit catches what people overlook. Raising the sampling temperature only changes the output and does not prevent leaks, and clearing the conversation history after the commit leaves the secret in the repository."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【知識】コーディングのスキルとCLAUDE.mdの読み込みタイミングの違いはどれか。","o":["両方とも常時ロードされ会話の文脈に残り続ける","両方ともオンデマンドで必要時のみ読み込まれる","スキルはオンデマンド、CLAUDE.mdは常時ロード","スキルは常時ロード、CLAUDE.mdはオンデマンド"],"a":2,"e":"スキルは必要なときに呼び出すオンデマンド、CLAUDE.mdは常時ロードされる。読み込みタイミングが違う。両方が常時ロードされるとする説明も、両方がオンデマンドとする説明も、スキルを常時ロードとする説明も誤りである。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is the difference in load timing between coding skills and CLAUDE.md?", "oEn": ["Both are always loaded and remain in the conversation context","Both are on-demand and loaded only when needed","Skills are on-demand; CLAUDE.md is always loaded","Skills are always loaded; CLAUDE.md is on-demand"], "eEn": "A skill is loaded on demand when needed, while CLAUDE.md is always loaded; the timing differs. Saying both are always loaded, both are on demand, or that skills are the always-loaded ones is wrong."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】個人用にスキルを試験的にカスタマイズする安全な方法はどれか。","o":["~/.claude/skills/ に別名で個人バリアントを作る","CLAUDE.md にスキルの手順を書き写して個人用に細かく調整する","プロジェクトの共有スキルファイルを直接書き換えて試す","元のスキルを一時的に削除して挙動の違いを確認する"],"a":0,"e":"個人バリアントを~/.claude/skills/に別名で作れば、チームに影響を与えずに試せる。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is a safe way to experimentally customize a skill for personal use?", "oEn": ["Create a personal variant under a different name in ~/.claude/skills/","Copy the skill's steps into CLAUDE.md and fine-tune them for personal use","Directly rewrite the project's shared skill file to try it","Temporarily delete the original skill to check the difference in behavior"], "eEn": "Creating a personal variant under a different name in ~/.claude/skills/ lets you experiment without affecting the team."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】argument-hint を設定する目的はどれか。","o":["サンプリング温度を下げて出力の揺らぎを抑える","引数なし呼び出し時に必要パラメータを開発者へ促す","呼び出しごとに会話の文脈を新しく分岐させる","コマンド実行中に使用可能なツールの範囲を制限する"],"a":1,"e":"argument-hintは引数未指定時に必要パラメータの入力を促すフロントマター。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the purpose of setting argument-hint?", "oEn": ["Lower the sampling temperature to suppress output fluctuation","Prompt the developer for required parameters when invoked without arguments","Branch the conversation context anew on each invocation","Restrict the range of tools available while the command runs"], "eEn": "argument-hint is frontmatter that prompts for required parameters when no arguments are given."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】allowed-tools をスキルに設定する目的はどれか。","o":["サンプリング温度を下げて出力の一貫性を高める","スキル実行中のツールアクセスを制限し破壊的操作を防ぐ","スキル呼び出しごとに会話の文脈を分岐して管理する","呼び出しに必要なパラメータを開発者へ入力するよう促す"],"a":1,"e":"allowed-toolsはスキル実行中の使用可能ツールを制限し、破壊的操作を防ぐ。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the purpose of setting allowed-tools on a skill?", "oEn": ["Lower the sampling temperature to improve output consistency","Restrict tool access while the skill runs to prevent destructive operations","Branch and manage the conversation context for each skill invocation","Prompt the developer to enter the parameters needed for invocation"], "eEn": "allowed-tools restricts the tools usable while the skill runs and prevents destructive operations."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】レビュー精度を上げるとき、曖昧な指示より明示基準が効く例として正しいのはどれか。","o":["「バグの可能性がある箇所を報告」vs「明らかな誤りだけ指摘」","「主張された挙動が実コードと矛盾するときのみフラグ」vs「コメントが正確か確認」","「潜在的なリスクを幅広く洗い出して列挙する」vs「確実に問題と言えるものだけを慎重に報告する」","「重要な問題を優先的に扱う」vs「些細な点はできるだけ後回しにする」"],"a":1,"e":"曖昧指示は解釈がぶれる。明示的・カテゴリ的な基準（矛盾時のみフラグ等）が精度を上げ、偽陽性を減らす。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] When improving review accuracy, which is a correct example of explicit criteria working better than vague instructions?", "oEn": ["\"Report spots that may be bugs\" vs. \"Point out only clear errors\"","\"Flag only when the claimed behavior contradicts the actual code\" vs. \"Check whether the comment is accurate\"","\"Broadly identify and list potential risks\" vs. \"Carefully report only what is definitely a problem\"","\"Prioritize handling important problems\" vs. \"Defer trivial points as much as possible\""], "eEn": "Vague instructions lead to varying interpretations. Explicit, categorical criteria (such as flagging only on contradiction) raise accuracy and reduce false positives."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】「保守的に」「高信頼のみ報告」のような一般的指示が精度向上に効かない理由はどれか。","o":["使用トークンが増え課金コストが上がるから","プロンプトが長くなり処理が遅くなるから","測定不能で具体的なカテゴリ基準に劣るから","モデル内部で構文エラーを引き起こすから"],"a":2,"e":"一般的指示は測定不能で解釈がぶれる。具体的なカテゴリ基準（どの問題を報告/スキップするか）が精度に効く。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Why do general instructions such as \"be conservative\" or \"report only high-confidence findings\" not improve accuracy?", "oEn": ["Because it increases the tokens used and raises billing cost","Because the prompt gets longer and processing slows down","Because they can't be measured and lose to specific category criteria","Because they cause syntax errors inside the model"], "eEn": "General instructions are unmeasurable and lead to varying interpretations. Specific categorical criteria (which problems to report or skip) improve accuracy."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】偽陽性率が開発者の信頼に与える影響として正しいのはどれか。","o":["偽陽性はレビュー結果全体には影響せず基本的に無害である","偽陽性はUIの表示レイアウトにのみ影響する","偽陽性が多いほど開発者の信頼はむしろ高まる","高偽陽性のカテゴリが、正確なカテゴリへの信頼まで損なう"],"a":3,"e":"偽陽性が多いカテゴリは、正確なカテゴリの信頼までも損なう。一時無効化や基準改善が有効。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which correctly describes the effect of false positive rate on developer trust?", "oEn": ["False positives do not affect the review results as a whole and are basically harmless","False positives only affect the display layout of the UI","The more false positives there are, the more developer trust actually increases","A high-false-positive category undermines trust even in accurate categories"], "eEn": "A category with many false positives undermines trust even in accurate categories. Temporarily disabling it and improving the criteria are effective."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】信頼度ベースのフィルタに頼らず報告対象を明確化する方法はどれか。","o":["利用可能なツールの数を増やして、より多くの観点から問題を検出できるようにする","「高い信頼度を持つ指摘だけを報告するように」といった一般的な言葉だけで指示する","報告すべき問題（バグ・セキュリティ）とスキップすべき問題（軽微なスタイル等）を明示する具体基準を書く","サンプリング温度をできるだけ下げて出力のばらつきを抑え、報告される指摘の件数が安定するように細かく調整する"],"a":2,"e":"報告すべき問題（バグ・セキュリティ）とスキップすべき問題（軽微なスタイル等）を明示する具体基準を書くと、報告対象が明確になる。「高い信頼度の指摘だけ」という一般的な言葉の指示は、モデルの自己申告の信頼度に頼るので精度が上がらない。", "qEn": "[Applied] How do you clarify what to report without relying on a confidence-based filter?", "oEn": ["Increase the number of available tools so problems can be detected from more perspectives","Instruct only with general wording such as \"report only findings with high confidence\"","Write specific criteria that explicitly state which problems to report (bugs, security) and which to skip (minor style, etc.)","Lower the sampling temperature as far as possible to suppress output variation and finely tune it so the number of reported findings is stable"], "eEn": "Writing concrete criteria that name what to report, such as bugs and security issues, and what to skip, such as minor style points, makes the reporting target clear. A vague instruction to report only high-confidence findings relies on the model's self-reported confidence and does not improve accuracy."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】偽陽性が多いカテゴリで開発者の信頼を回復しつつ改善する方法はどれか。","o":["すべてのカテゴリをまとめて無効化し検出を完全に止める","サンプリング温度を上げて出力の多様性を高め、指摘の表現を毎回変化させる","そのカテゴリを一時的に無効化し、プロンプトを改善してから再有効化する","そのカテゴリからの指摘を当面すべて無視して開発を先に進める"],"a":2,"e":"偽陽性が多いカテゴリは、一時的に無効化して開発者の信頼を回復し、その間にプロンプトを改善してから再有効化する。すべてのカテゴリをまとめて無効化すると有効な検出まで止まり、指摘を無視し続けると信頼も精度も戻らない。", "qEn": "[Applied] How do you restore developer trust and improve a category with many false positives?", "oEn": ["Disable all categories together and stop detection entirely","Raise the sampling temperature to increase output diversity and vary the wording of findings each time","Temporarily disable that category, improve the prompt, and then re-enable it","Ignore all findings from that category for now and move development forward"], "eEn": "For a category with many false positives, disable it temporarily to restore developer trust, improve the prompt in the meantime, then re-enable it. Disabling all categories stops useful detection too, and just ignoring the findings restores neither trust nor accuracy."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】重大度分類を一貫させる最も効果的な方法はどれか。","o":["「重大なものだけ報告して」と一言だけ指示する","各重大度に具体的なコード例を添えた明示基準を定義する","サンプリング温度をできる限り下げて分類のばらつきを抑える","利用可能なツールを増やして判断材料を広げる"],"a":1,"e":"各重大度に具体的なコード例を添えた明示基準を定義すると、分類の境目が揃い、一貫した判定になる。「重大なものだけ報告して」の一言では重大の意味が揺れる。温度を下げても基準自体は定まらず、ツールを増やしても判断材料にならない。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the most effective way to make severity classification consistent?", "oEn": ["Instruct only with a single phrase such as \"report only the serious ones\"","Define explicit criteria for each severity level with concrete code examples","Lower the sampling temperature as far as possible to suppress classification variation","Increase available tools to broaden the evidence for judgment"], "eEn": "Defining explicit criteria with a concrete code example for each severity level aligns the boundaries and keeps classification consistent. A one-line instruction like report only serious ones leaves the meaning of serious open, lowering temperature does not set the standard, and adding tools does not help."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】詳細な指示だけでは一貫しないとき、一貫した形式・実用的出力を得る最も効果的な技術はどれか。","o":["temperature調整","few-shot例","プロンプトの長文化","ツールの追加定義"],"a":1,"e":"few-shot例は、詳細指示だけでは一貫しない出力に対し最も効果的に一貫性と実用性をもたらす。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] When detailed instructions alone are not consistent, what is the most effective technique for getting consistent format and actionable output?", "oEn": ["Temperature adjustment","Few-shot examples","Making the prompt longer","Defining additional tools"], "eEn": "Few-shot examples most effectively bring consistency and practicality to output that detailed instructions alone cannot make consistent."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】曖昧なケースの扱い（曖昧要求でのツール選択等）を学習させるのに有効なのはどれか。","o":["利用可能なツールを追加していく","指示文を長く詳細に書き足していく","サンプリング温度を下げて出力を安定させる","曖昧ケースの扱いを示すfew-shot例"],"a":3,"e":"曖昧なケースの扱いを示すfew-shot例は、判断の仕方を実演して見せるので、新しいパターンにも判断が汎化する。指示文を長く詳細に書き足しても、ツールを追加しても、サンプリング温度を下げても、曖昧さの扱いは学習されない。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is effective for teaching how to handle ambiguous cases (such as tool selection for an ambiguous request)?", "oEn": ["Keep adding available tools","Keep adding to the instructions to make them longer and more detailed","Lower the sampling temperature to stabilize output","Few-shot examples showing how to handle ambiguous cases"], "eEn": "Few-shot examples that show how ambiguous cases are handled demonstrate the reasoning, so judgment generalizes to new patterns. Writing longer instructions, adding tools or lowering the sampling temperature does not teach how to handle ambiguity."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】few-shot例が事前指定ケースの暗記でなく汎化を促す理由はどれか。","o":["なぜその行動を選んだかの推論を示すことで新規パターンへ判断を一般化できる","処理速度が常に速く、大量の例文を短時間でまとめて一度に学習させられるから","出力の見た目が整い、開発者にとって結果が読みやすくなるから","提示された例文をそのまま丸暗記し、同じ入力に再利用するだけだから"],"a":0,"e":"few-shotは推論を伴う例で、事前指定ケースの暗記でなく新規パターンへの汎化を促す。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Why do few-shot examples promote generalization rather than memorization of pre-specified cases?", "oEn": ["By showing the reasoning for why an action was chosen, judgment can be generalized to new patterns","Because processing is always fast and a large number of examples can be learned at once in a short time","Because the output looks tidier and results are easier for developers to read","Because the given examples are simply memorized verbatim and reused for the same input"], "eEn": "Few-shot examples come with reasoning, promoting generalization to new patterns rather than memorization of pre-specified cases."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】抽出タスクでの幻覚（非公式な測定値・多様な文書構造）を減らすのに有効なのはどれか。","o":["サンプリング温度をできる限り下げて出力の揺らぎを抑える","様々な形式からの正しい抽出を示すfew-shot例","指示文をできるだけ長く詳細に書き加えていく","利用可能なツールの数を減らして選択肢を絞る"],"a":1,"e":"few-shot例は多様な文書構造の正しい抽出を示し、抽出タスクの幻覚を減らす。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is effective for reducing hallucinations in extraction tasks (informal measurements, varied document structures)?", "oEn": ["Lower the sampling temperature as far as possible to suppress output fluctuation","Few-shot examples showing correct extraction from various formats","Add to the instructions to make them as long and detailed as possible","Reduce the number of available tools to narrow the choices"], "eEn": "Few-shot examples show correct extraction from varied document structures and reduce hallucinations in extraction tasks."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】曖昧シナリオ向けのfew-shot例の作り方として最適なのはどれか。","o":["推論を含めず入力と出力だけの例を作る","例を作らず指示文だけを詳しく書き込む","できるだけ多くの例を20個以上まとめて一度に作る","なぜその行動を選んだか推論を示す例を2-4個作る"],"a":3,"e":"曖昧シナリオには、選択理由の推論を示す的を絞ったfew-shot例を2-4個作るのが効果的。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the best way to create few-shot examples for ambiguous scenarios?", "oEn": ["Create examples with only input and output, without reasoning","Create no examples and write detailed instructions only","Create as many examples as possible at once, 20 or more together","Create 2-4 examples showing the reasoning behind the choice"], "eEn": "For ambiguous scenarios, creating 2-4 targeted few-shot examples that show the reasoning behind the choice is effective."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】レビュー出力の一貫性（位置・問題・重大度・修正案）を得る方法はどれか。","o":["サンプリング温度を下げて出力を安定させる","利用可能なツールを追加して出力を整える","望ましい出力形式を示すfew-shot例を含める","望ましい形式を指示文の中で長く言葉を尽くして説明する"],"a":2,"e":"望ましい出力形式（location, issue, severity, suggested fix）を示すfew-shot例で一貫性を得る。", "qEn": "[Applied] How do you get consistent review output (location, issue, severity, suggested fix)?", "oEn": ["Lower the sampling temperature to stabilize output","Add available tools to tidy the output","Include few-shot examples showing the desired output format","Explain the desired format at great length within the instructions"], "eEn": "Few-shot examples showing the desired output format (location, issue, severity, suggested fix) bring consistency."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】許容できるコードパターンと真の問題を区別し偽陽性を減らすには。","o":["利用可能なツールを増やして判定材料を広げる","「偽陽性をできるだけ出さないように」とだけ指示文で伝える","両者を区別するfew-shot例を提供し汎化を可能にする","サンプリング温度を下げて判定のばらつきを抑える"],"a":2,"e":"許容パターンと真の問題を区別するfew-shot例が、汎化しつつ偽陽性を減らす。", "qEn": "[Applied] How do you distinguish acceptable code patterns from genuine problems and reduce false positives?", "oEn": ["Increase tools to broaden the evidence for judgment","Tell it only \"avoid false positives as much as possible\"","Provide few-shot examples that distinguish the two, enabling generalization","Lower the sampling temperature to suppress variation in judgment"], "eEn": "Few-shot examples that distinguish acceptable patterns from genuine problems reduce false positives while generalizing."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】多様な文書構造（インライン引用 vs 参考文献、本文 vs 埋め込み）の正しい処理を教えるには。","o":["利用可能なツールを増やして対応構造を広げる","多様な構造の正しい処理を示すfew-shot例を使う","サンプリング温度を下げて出力の安定性を高める","文書構造をあらかじめ一つの形式に固定してから処理させる"],"a":1,"e":"多様な構造の正しい処理を示すfew-shot例で、構造的多様性への対応を改善する。", "qEn": "[Applied] How do you teach the correct handling of varied document structures (inline citations vs. bibliography, body text vs. embedded)?", "oEn": ["Increase tools to broaden the structures supported","Use few-shot examples showing correct handling of varied structures","Lower the sampling temperature to improve output stability","Fix the document structure to a single format in advance before processing"], "eEn": "Few-shot examples showing correct handling of varied structures improve how structural diversity is handled."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】保証されたスキーマ準拠の構造化出力を得る最も信頼できる方法はどれか。","o":["tool_use とJSONスキーマ（構文エラーを排除）","アシスタント応答をプレフィルして開始文字を固定する","プロンプトで「必ずJSON形式で出力するように」と丁寧に頼む","サンプリング温度を0に設定して出力を固定する"],"a":0,"e":"tool_useとJSONスキーマがスキーマ準拠の構造化出力を保証し、構文エラーを排除する最も信頼できる方法。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is the most reliable way to get guaranteed schema-compliant structured output?", "oEn": ["tool_use with a JSON schema (eliminates syntax errors)","Prefill the assistant response to fix the starting characters","Politely ask in the prompt to \"always output in JSON format\"","Set the sampling temperature to 0 to fix the output"], "eEn": "tool_use with a JSON schema is the most reliable way to guarantee schema-compliant structured output and eliminate syntax errors."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】tool_choice の auto / any / 強制 の違いとして正しいのはどれか。","o":["autoはテキストも返しうる／anyは必ずツールを呼ぶ（選択可）／強制は特定ツールを呼ぶ","autoは常にテキストのみを返し／anyは呼ぶツールを一つに固定し／強制はツール呼び出しを禁止する","autoは必ずツールを呼ぶ／anyはテキストを返しうる／強制は選択に委ねる","autoとanyは実質的に同じ挙動で、強制指定だけが特定のツールを呼ぶ"],"a":0,"e":"autoはツールを呼ばずテキストを返しうる。anyは必ずツールを呼ぶ（どれかは選べる）。強制は特定の名指しツールを呼ぶ。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which correctly describes the difference between auto / any / forced tool_choice?", "oEn": ["auto may also return text / any always calls a tool (choice allowed) / forced calls a specific tool","auto always returns text only / any fixes the tool to call to just one / forced prohibits any tool call","auto always calls a tool / any may return text / forced leaves the choice to the model","auto and any behave essentially the same, and only forced specification calls a specific tool"], "eEn": "auto may return text without calling a tool. any always calls a tool (it can choose which). Forced calls a specifically named tool."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】tool_use による厳格JSONスキーマが排除できるものとできないものはどれか。","o":["構文エラーと意味エラーの両方をまとめて完全に排除できる","構文エラーは排除できるが、意味エラー（合計が合わない等）は防げない","構文エラーも意味エラーも防ぐことができず、どちらも出力にそのまま残る","意味エラーは排除できるが、構文エラーは残ってしまう"],"a":1,"e":"スキーマは構文エラーを排除するが、line itemが合計と合わない等の意味エラーは別途検証が要る。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What can and cannot be eliminated by a strict JSON schema with tool_use?", "oEn": ["Both syntax errors and semantic errors can be completely eliminated together","Syntax errors can be eliminated, but semantic errors (e.g., totals that do not match) cannot be prevented","Neither syntax errors nor semantic errors can be prevented at all, and both simply remain in the output as they are","Semantic errors can be eliminated, but syntax errors remain"], "eEn": "A schema eliminates syntax errors, but semantic errors such as line items that do not match the total require separate validation."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】拡張可能なカテゴリ分類のスキーマ設計はどれか。","o":["必須フィールドだけを定義して、任意の項目は一切設けない","enum を使わず、すべての値を自由記述の文字列で受け取る","enumに \"other\" + detail文字列パターンを併設する","各カテゴリを連番の数値コードだけで表現し、説明用の文字列は一切持たせない"],"a":2,"e":"enum＋\"other\"+detailパターンで、許可値で縛りつつ未知カテゴリを拡張可能に扱える。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is a schema design for extensible category classification?", "oEn": ["Define only required fields and provide no optional items at all","Do not use an enum and accept every value as a free-text string","Pair an enum with an \"other\" + detail string pattern","Represent each category only with a sequential numeric code and keep no descriptive string at all"], "eEn": "The enum + \"other\" + detail pattern constrains values to the allowed ones while still letting you handle unknown categories extensibly."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】抽出ツールから構造化データを得る正しい実装はどれか。","o":["JSONスキーマを入力パラメータに持つ抽出ツールを定義し、tool_use応答から取り出す","会話履歴をすべて消去してから、抽出結果だけを新しい応答として受け取るようにする","プロンプトでJSON出力を頼み、返答テキストから正規表現で値を抜き出す","サンプリング温度を0に設定して、モデルが返す出力の形式が毎回まったく同じになるよう細かく調整する"],"a":0,"e":"JSONスキーマを入力に持つ抽出ツールを定義し、tool_use応答から構造化データを取り出すのが確実。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the correct implementation for getting structured data from an extraction tool?", "oEn": ["Define an extraction tool whose input parameters are a JSON schema, and extract the data from the tool_use response","Clear the entire conversation history, then receive only the extraction result as a new response","Ask for JSON output in the prompt and pull out values from the response text with regular expressions","Set the sampling temperature to 0 and finely tune it so the output format the model returns is exactly the same every time"], "eEn": "Defining an extraction tool with a JSON schema as input and pulling the structured data from the tool_use response is reliable."},
    {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】特定の抽出（extract_metadata）を強化前に必ず実行させる設定はどれか。","o":["tool_choice: {\"type\":\"tool\",\"name\":\"extract_metadata\"} で強制する","tool_choice: \"auto\" に設定し、そのツールを呼び出すかどうかを毎回モデル自身の判断に完全に委ねるようにする","tool_choice: \"any\" に設定して、いずれか一つのツールを必ず呼ばせるようにする","プロンプトの中で extract_metadata を必ず先に実行するよう文章でお願いする"],"a":0,"e":"特定ツールの強制選択で、enrichment前に必ずextract_metadataを実行させられる。", "qEn": "[Applied] Which setting makes a specific extraction (extract_metadata) always run before enrichment?", "oEn": ["Force it with tool_choice: {\"type\":\"tool\",\"name\":\"extract_metadata\"}","Set tool_choice: \"auto\" and leave whether to call that tool entirely to the model's own judgment each time","Set tool_choice: \"any\" so that one of the tools is always called","Ask in the prompt, in words, to always run extract_metadata first"], "eEn": "Forcing a specific tool makes extract_metadata always run before enrichment."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】ソース文書に情報がないとき捏造を防ぐスキーマ設計はどれか。","o":["欠損に備えて予備フィールドを複数追加し冗長にスキーマ定義する","該当フィールドをoptional（nullable）にする","全フィールドをstring型に統一して型検証を省く","全フィールドを必須にして未取得時は空文字で埋める"],"a":1,"e":"全必須だとモデルが値を捏造して埋める。nullableにすれば「無い」をnullで表せ捏造を防げる。", "qEn": "[Applied] What schema design prevents fabrication when the source document lacks the information?", "oEn": ["Add multiple spare fields to prepare for missing data and define the schema redundantly","Make the relevant field optional (nullable)","Unify all fields to the string type and skip type validation","Make all fields required and fill with empty strings when not obtained"], "eEn": "If everything is required, the model fabricates values to fill them in. With nullable, \"absent\" can be expressed as null, preventing fabrication."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】曖昧ケースや拡張カテゴリに対応するenum設計はどれか。","o":["\"unclear\" を曖昧用に、\"other\"+detail を拡張用に加える","カテゴリを数値コードのみで表現し、文字列ラベルは一切持たせない","enumを使わず自由記述のstring型フィールドで受け取る","既知カテゴリのみを必須enumで定義し、想定外の入力値はすべて破棄する設計にする"],"a":0,"e":"\"unclear\"で曖昧ケース、\"other\"+detailで拡張カテゴリに対応できる。", "qEn": "[Applied] What enum design handles ambiguous cases and extensible categories?", "oEn": ["Add \"unclear\" for ambiguity and \"other\" + detail for extension","Represent categories only with numeric codes and keep no string labels at all","Don't use an enum and accept free-text string fields","Define only known categories as a required enum, and discard all unexpected input values"], "eEn": "\"unclear\" handles ambiguous cases, and \"other\" + detail handles extensible categories."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】不揃いなソース形式を厳格スキーマで扱うには何を併用するか。","o":["temperatureを上げて多様な形式に対応させる","入力前に全文書を人手で同一形式へ変換する","プロンプトに形式正規化ルールを併記する","スキーマの必須制約を外して緩く受け入れる"],"a":2,"e":"厳格スキーマと並行して、プロンプトに形式正規化ルールを併記し不揃いなソースを扱う。", "qEn": "[Applied] What should be combined with a strict schema to handle inconsistent source formats?", "oEn": ["Raise the temperature to handle diverse formats","Manually convert all documents to the same format before input","Include format normalization rules in the prompt","Remove the schema's required constraints and accept loosely"], "eEn": "In parallel with the strict schema, include format normalization rules in the prompt to handle inconsistent sources."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】retry-with-error-feedback の正しい実装はどれか。","o":["原文書・失敗した抽出・具体的な検証エラーを添えて再要求する","会話履歴をすべて消去した上で再度リクエストする","temperatureを変えて出力を揺らして再送する","同じプロンプトを一切変更せずに同一条件のままもう一度送信する"],"a":0,"e":"retry-with-error-feedbackでは、原文書と失敗した抽出結果、具体的な検証エラーを添えて再要求する。モデルが何を直すべきか分かり自己修正できる。同じプロンプトをそのまま再送しても、履歴を消しても、temperatureを変えても、失敗の原因は伝わらない。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is the correct implementation of retry-with-error-feedback?", "oEn": ["Re-request, attaching the original document, the failed extraction, and the specific validation errors","Clear all conversation history and then send the request again","Change the temperature to vary the output and resend","Send the very same prompt again, without changing anything at all, under exactly the same conditions as before"], "eEn": "In retry-with-error-feedback, you resend the request with the source document, the failed extraction and the specific validation errors, so the model knows what to fix and can correct itself. Resending the same prompt unchanged, clearing history or changing temperature does not tell it what went wrong."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】リトライが無効なケースはどれか。","o":["構造的な出力エラーが発生したとき","必要な情報がソース文書に存在しないとき","enum外の値が出力されてしまうとき","出力形式がスキーマ定義と一致しないとき"],"a":1,"e":"情報がソースに無い場合、リトライは無効。形式・構造エラーはリトライで解決しうる。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] In which case is a retry ineffective?", "oEn": ["When a structural output error occurs","When the required information does not exist in the source document","When a value outside the enum is output","When the output format does not match the schema definition"], "eEn": "When the information is not in the source, retry is ineffective. Format and structure errors can be resolved by retrying."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】偽陽性パターンを体系的に分析するためにフィードバックループに加える要素はどれか。","o":["detected_pattern フィールドで、どの構造が所見を誘発したか追跡する","各所見にfew-shot例を添えて、どのカテゴリで偽陽性が多いのかを個別に集計していく","外部レビュー用の検証ツールを複数追加して検出の網羅性を最大化する","temperatureを下げて偽陽性そのものが起きにくいようにする"],"a":0,"e":"detected_patternフィールドで誘発パターンを追跡し、開発者の却下傾向を体系的に分析できる。", "qEn": "[Applied] What element should be added to the feedback loop to analyze false-positive patterns systematically?", "oEn": ["A detected_pattern field that tracks which structure triggered the finding","Attach few-shot examples to each finding and tally individually which categories have many false positives","Add multiple verification tools for external review to maximize detection coverage","Lower the temperature so false positives themselves are less likely to occur"], "eEn": "A detected_pattern field tracks triggering patterns and enables systematic analysis of developers' dismissal tendencies."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】意味的検証エラーと構文エラーの違いとして正しいのはどれか。","o":["意味エラー（合計不一致・誤フィールド配置）は別途検証が必要／構文エラーはtool useで排除","意味エラーと構文エラーはどちらもJSONスキーマとtool useの併用だけで完全に排除できる","構文エラーは追加検証が必要で意味エラーはtool useで自動排除される","意味エラーもtool useのスキーマ検証だけで自動的に完全排除できる"],"a":0,"e":"構文エラーはtool useのスキーマで排除できるが、合計の不一致や誤ったフィールドへの配置といった意味エラーは別途の検証層が必要。意味エラーもスキーマ検証だけで完全に排除できるという説明は誤りで、構文と意味の役割を逆にした説明も誤り。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which correctly describes the difference between semantic validation errors and syntax errors?", "oEn": ["Semantic errors (mismatched totals, misplaced fields) need separate validation / syntax errors are eliminated by tool use","Both semantic and syntax errors can be completely eliminated just by combining a JSON schema with tool use","Syntax errors need additional validation and semantic errors are automatically eliminated by tool use","Semantic errors too can be completely and automatically eliminated by tool use schema validation alone"], "eEn": "Syntax errors can be eliminated with tool use and a schema, but semantic errors such as totals that do not add up or values in the wrong field need a separate validation layer. Saying schema validation alone removes semantic errors completely is wrong, and so is swapping the two roles."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】合計値の不整合を検出する自己修正検証フローはどれか。","o":["抽出後にcalculated_totalとstated_totalの平均値を単一フィールドとして出力する","stated_totalだけを抽出して記載値をそのまま信頼する構成にする","calculated_total と stated_total を両方抽出して差異をフラグする","temperatureを下げて集計時の計算ミス自体が起きにくいようにする"],"a":2,"e":"calculated_totalとstated_totalを並行抽出し差異をフラグする。conflict_detectedブール等も有効。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is a self-correcting validation flow that detects total inconsistencies?", "oEn": ["After extraction, output the average of calculated_total and stated_total as a single field","Extract only stated_total and build it to trust the stated value as is","Extract both calculated_total and stated_total and flag the discrepancy","Lower the temperature so calculation mistakes themselves are less likely during aggregation"], "eEn": "Extract calculated_total and stated_total in parallel and flag any discrepancy. A conflict_detected boolean is also effective."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】Message Batches API の特性として正しいのはどれか。","o":["処理完了までの時間について厳密なSLAを保証する仕組みである","同期APIと同じく即時応答を保証し遅延はほぼ生じない","通常より高いコストと引き換えに優先処理される","50%コスト削減・最大24時間処理・レイテンシSLAなし"],"a":3,"e":"Batches APIは50%節約・最大24時間・SLAなし。待てる処理に向く。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which correctly describes the Message Batches API?", "oEn": ["A mechanism that guarantees a strict SLA on the time until processing completes","Like the synchronous API, it guarantees immediate responses with almost no delay","It is processed with priority in exchange for a higher cost than usual","50% cost savings, up to 24-hour processing, no latency SLA"], "eEn": "The Batches API offers 50% savings, up to 24 hours, and no SLA. It suits work that can wait."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】Batches API が不適切なワークロードはどれか。","o":["マージ前チェックのようなブロッキングなワークフロー","夜間バッチで大量に処理するテストコードの自動生成タスク","週次でまとめて実行する監査ログの一括分析","夜間にまとめて生成する定期レポートの作成処理"],"a":0,"e":"レイテンシSLAがないため、開発者が結果を待つブロッキング処理には不適。非ブロッキングな夜間/週次処理に向く。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which workload is unsuitable for the Batches API?", "oEn": ["A blocking workflow such as a pre-merge check","An automatic test-code generation task processed in bulk in a nightly batch","Bulk analysis of audit logs run together weekly","Creating periodic reports generated together overnight"], "eEn": "With no latency SLA, it is unsuitable for blocking work where a developer waits for the result. It suits non-blocking nightly/weekly processing."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】Batches API の制約として正しいのはどれか。","o":["ツールを一切利用できず関数呼び出しは常に無効になる","単一リクエスト内のマルチターンのツール呼び出しをサポートしない","JSON形式の構造化出力を返すことができない仕様である","投入したすべてのバッチは処理に必ず24時間を丸ごと要する仕様である"],"a":1,"e":"Batches APIは単一リクエスト内でツールを実行して結果を返すマルチターンをサポートしない。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which correctly describes a constraint of the Batches API?", "oEn": ["No tools can be used at all, and function calling is always disabled","It does not support multi-turn tool calling within a single request","By design, it cannot return structured output in JSON format","By design, every submitted batch always takes the full 24 hours to process"], "eEn": "The Batches API does not support multi-turn, where tools are executed within a single request and the results returned."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】バッチのリクエスト/レスポンスを対応付ける仕組みはどれか。","o":["session-name フィールド","tool_choice パラメータ","custom_id フィールド","detected_pattern タグ"],"a":2,"e":"custom_idでバッチのリクエスト/レスポンス対を相関付ける。失敗時の再submitにも使う。", "qEn": "[Applied] What mechanism matches batch requests to responses?", "oEn": ["session-name field","tool_choice parameter","custom_id field","detected_pattern tag"], "eEn": "custom_id correlates batch request/response pairs. It is also used when resubmitting after a failure."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【シナリオ】ブロッキングなマージ前チェックと、夜間生成の技術的負債レポートの両方を実行中。コスト削減のため両方をBatches APIに切り替える提案をどう評価するか。","o":["両方をバッチ化した上でタイムアウト時にリアルタイム処理へ自動フォールバックさせる","両方ともリアルタイム処理のまま維持し当面はコストを据え置く","技術的負債レポートのみバッチ化し、マージ前チェックはリアルタイムを維持する","両方をバッチ化し完了はポーリングで確認する構成に統一する"],"a":2,"e":"BatchesはSLAなし最大24時間なので、待つマージ前チェックには不適。夜間レポートには最適。用途ごとにAPIを使い分ける。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You are running both a blocking pre-merge check and a nightly-generated technical debt report. How do you evaluate a proposal to switch both to the Batches API to cut costs?", "oEn": ["Batch both of them, and automatically fall back to real-time processing on timeout","Keep both on real-time processing and leave costs as they are for now","Batch only the technical debt report and keep the pre-merge check real-time","Batch both and standardize on a setup that confirms completion by polling"], "eEn": "Batches has no SLA and up to 24 hours, so it is unsuitable for a pre-merge check that someone waits on. It is ideal for the nightly report. Use the API per purpose."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】24時間バッチ処理で30時間SLA（Service Level Agreement）を保証するための投入頻度はどれか。","o":["1時間ごとに投入ウィンドウを設ける","概ね4時間ごとの投入ウィンドウを設ける","24時間ごとに投入ウィンドウを設ける","48時間ごとに一括で投入ウィンドウを設ける"],"a":1,"e":"24時間処理＋6時間の余裕で30時間SLAを満たすには、4時間ごとの投入ウィンドウが目安。", "qEn": "[Applied] To guarantee a 30-hour SLA (Service Level Agreement) with 24-hour batch processing, what submission frequency is needed?", "oEn": ["Provide a submission window every hour","Provide a submission window roughly every 4 hours","Provide a submission window every 24 hours","Provide a single bulk submission window every 48 hours"], "eEn": "To meet a 30-hour SLA with 24-hour processing plus a 6-hour margin, a submission window every 4 hours is the guideline."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】バッチ失敗時の最適な対処はどれか。","o":["失敗の有無に関わらず全リクエストをまとめて最初から再submitし直す","custom_idで失敗分のみ特定し、修正（例：超過文書のチャンキング）して再submitする","失敗したリクエストはそのまま無視して成功分だけで処理を確定させてしまう","custom_idで失敗分を特定した後、temperatureを下げて全リクエストを丸ごと再submitする"],"a":1,"e":"失敗分のみcustom_idで特定し、必要な修正（チャンキング等）を施して再submitする。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the best handling when a batch fails?", "oEn": ["Resubmit all requests from the start regardless of whether they failed","Identify only the failed ones by custom_id, fix them (e.g., chunk oversized documents), and resubmit","Ignore the failed requests as they are and finalize processing with only the successes","After identifying the failures by custom_id, lower the temperature and resubmit all the requests in full"], "eEn": "Identify only the failures by custom_id, apply the necessary fixes (chunking, etc.), and resubmit."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】大量バッチ前にコストを抑える進め方はどれか。","o":["サンプルセットでプロンプトを精緻化し初回成功率を最大化する","レビュー用のツールを増やして各件を個別に検査する","検証せずいきなり全件を一度にバッチ処理へ投入する","temperatureを下げて全件の出力を安定させてから流す"],"a":0,"e":"少数サンプルでプロンプトを磨いてから大量処理すると、初回成功率が上がり再submitコストを減らせる。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the approach to keep costs down before a large batch?", "oEn": ["Refine the prompt on a sample set to maximize the first-pass success rate","Add review tools and inspect each item individually","Submit all items to batch processing at once without validation","Lower the temperature to stabilize the output of all items before running them"], "eEn": "Polishing the prompt on a small sample before bulk processing raises the first-pass success rate and reduces resubmission cost."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】自己レビューの限界として正しいのはどれか。","o":["生成そのものに比べて計算コストが高く時間もかかりやすい","常に高速で追加のレイテンシがほぼ発生しない","生成時の推論文脈を保持し、自分の判断を疑いにくい","常に正確で見落としがほとんど起きない"],"a":2,"e":"同一セッションは生成文脈を保持し自分の判断を疑いにくい。独立インスタンスや多段レビューが有効。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which correctly describes a limitation of self-review?", "oEn": ["It has a higher computational cost than the generation itself, and it tends to take more time","It is always fast and adds almost no latency","It retains the reasoning context from generation, so it is hard to doubt its own judgments","It is always accurate and rarely misses anything"], "eEn": "The same session retains the generation context and has difficulty questioning its own judgments. An independent instance or multi-pass review is effective."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】独立レビューインスタンスが自己レビュー指示や拡張思考より優れる点はどれか。","o":["生成時の推論文脈を持たず、微妙な問題を客観検出できる","追加のコストがゼロで無料のまま実行できる","生成に用いたのと同じ文脈を引き継ぎ判断の一貫性を保てる","常に高速で応答が返り待ち時間がほぼ生じない"],"a":0,"e":"独立インスタンスは生成文脈を持たないため、自己レビューや拡張思考より微妙な問題を捉えやすい。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] How is an independent review instance better than self-review instructions or extended thinking?", "oEn": ["It has no reasoning context from generation, so it objectively detects subtle problems","It has zero additional cost and runs for free","It carries over the same context that was used for generation and keeps its judgments consistent","It always responds quickly with almost no wait time"], "eEn": "An independent instance has no generation context, so it catches subtle problems more easily than self-review or extended thinking."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】大規模レビューを多段で行う構成はどれか。","o":["全ファイルを一度の単一パスでまとめてレビューする","ファイル単位の局所パス＋クロスファイル統合パスに分割する","複数インスタンスの多数決でレビュー結果を決める","temperatureを下げて各ファイルのレビュー出力を安定化させる"],"a":1,"e":"ファイル単位の局所パスと、クロスファイルの統合パスに分けると、注意の希薄化と矛盾した所見を避けられる。全ファイルを一度の単一パスでまとめてレビューすると注意が薄まり、複数インスタンスの多数決は規模の問題を解決しない。", "qEn": "[Applied] Which structure performs a large-scale review in multiple stages?", "oEn": ["Review all files together in a single pass","Split into per-file local passes + a cross-file integration pass","Decide the review result by majority vote of multiple instances","Lower the temperature to stabilize the review for each file"], "eEn": "Splitting the review into per-file local passes and a cross-file integration pass avoids diluted attention and contradictory findings. Reviewing all files in one single pass spreads attention thin, and a majority vote among instances does not solve the problem of scale."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】校正されたレビュールーティングを可能にする検証パスはどれか。","o":["所見の重大度に関わらず全件を人間がレビューする","確信度を使わずすべての所見を一律に人間へ回す","各所見に自己申告の確信度を併記させ、ルーティングに使う","temperatureを下げて所見ごとの出力のばらつきを抑え込む"],"a":2,"e":"各所見に自己申告の確信度を併記させ、それをルーティングに使うと、確信度の低い所見だけを人間に回すなど、校正されたレビューの振り分けができる。全件を人間が見る運用や、確信度なしで一律に人間へ回す運用は、振り分けにならない。", "qEn": "[Applied] Which verification pass enables calibrated review routing?", "oEn": ["Have humans review every finding regardless of its severity","Send all findings uniformly to humans without using confidence","Have each finding carry a self-reported confidence and use it for routing","Lower the temperature to suppress the variation in output"], "eEn": "Having each finding carry a self-reported confidence and using it for routing allows calibrated review, such as sending only low-confidence findings to a person. Reviewing every finding by hand, or sending all of them to humans without confidence, is not routing at all."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】CIレビューで「コメントが実コードと矛盾するときのみ報告」のような基準が有効な理由はどれか。","o":["出力のフォーマットが自然に整い開発者にとって結果がより読みやすくなるから","処理が高速になりレビュー全体の所要時間が短くなるから","明示的・カテゴリ的基準が曖昧指示より精度を上げ偽陽性を減らすから","基準の記述が長いほど網羅性が高まり見落としが減るから"],"a":2,"e":"「コメントが実コードと矛盾するときのみ報告」のような明示的でカテゴリ的な基準は、何を報告するかが明確なので、曖昧な指示より精度が上がり偽陽性が減る。基準を長く書くほど網羅性が上がるわけではなく、フォーマットや速度の改善が目的でもない。", "qEn": "[Applied] Why is a criterion such as \"report only when a comment contradicts the actual code\" effective in CI review?", "oEn": ["Because the output format is naturally tidied and results are easier for developers to read","Because processing gets faster and the overall time required for review is shortened","Because explicit, categorical criteria raise accuracy over vague instructions and reduce false positives","Because the longer the description of the criteria, the more comprehensive it is and the fewer things are missed"], "eEn": "An explicit, categorical criterion such as report only when a comment contradicts the actual code makes clear what to report, so precision beats vague instructions and false positives drop. A longer criterion does not make coverage better, and the goal is not to improve formatting or speed."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【シナリオ】抽出で必須フィールドが空/nullになる文書がある。改善策はどれか。","o":["抽出用のツールを追加してフィールドごとに個別処理を割り当てる","必須フィールドの数をさらに増やして抽出漏れを防ぐ","多様な形式からの正しい抽出を示すfew-shot例を追加する","temperatureを下げて抽出出力のぶれを抑え込む"],"a":2,"e":"多様な形式の抽出を示すfew-shot例が、必須フィールドの空/null抽出を改善する。", "qEn": "[Scenario] Some documents leave required fields empty/null in extraction. What is the fix?", "oEn": ["Add extraction tools and assign separate processing to each field","Increase the number of required fields further to prevent extraction omissions","Add few-shot examples showing correct extraction from various formats","Lower the temperature to suppress variation in extraction output"], "eEn": "Few-shot examples showing extraction from varied formats improve empty/null extraction of required fields."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】tool_use とJSONスキーマで構造化出力を得る最大の利点はどれか。","o":["意味的な整合性エラーも同時に排除できる","追加コストがゼロで無償のまま構造化出力を得られる","処理速度が常に上がりレイテンシが縮む","スキーマ準拠を保証し構文エラーを排除できる"],"a":3,"e":"tool_use＋スキーマはスキーマ準拠を保証し構文エラーを排除する（意味エラーは別途検証）。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is the biggest advantage of getting structured output with tool_use and a JSON schema?", "oEn": ["It can also eliminate semantic consistency errors at the same time","Structured output is obtained at zero additional cost, free of charge","Processing speed always improves and latency shrinks","It guarantees schema compliance and eliminates syntax errors"], "eEn": "tool_use + schema guarantees schema compliance and eliminates syntax errors (semantic errors need separate validation)."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】nullableフィールドを使う目的はどれか。","o":["必須フィールドを増やして取得項目の網羅性を高める","画面表示を改善して抽出結果をユーザーにより見やすく整形して返す","出力生成を高速化して応答の待ち時間を短縮する","値が無い場合にnullを返させ、必須充足のための捏造を防ぐ"],"a":3,"e":"nullableにすれば「無い」をnullで表現でき、必須を満たすための捏造を防げる。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the purpose of using nullable fields?", "oEn": ["Increase the number of required fields to make the captured items more comprehensive","Improve the on-screen display and format extraction results to be easier for users to read","Speed up output generation and shorten response wait time","Return null when there is no value, so nothing is fabricated to satisfy required fields"], "eEn": "With nullable, \"absent\" can be expressed as null, preventing fabrication done to satisfy required fields."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】ゼロショットとフューショットの使い分けとして正しいのはどれか。","o":["単純はゼロショット、複雑・厳格形式は例を付ける","例を付けるかどうかは実行ごとにランダムに切り替える","どんな場合でも必ずフューショットで例を付ける","タスクの複雑さに関わらず常にゼロショットで統一する"],"a":0,"e":"単純なタスクはゼロショットで足り、複雑なタスクや厳格な形式が必要なときに例を付ける。どんな場合も必ずフューショットにする、または常にゼロショットで統一する運用は、タスクの難しさに合わず、ランダムに切り替える運用は根拠がない。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which correctly describes when to use zero-shot versus few-shot?", "oEn": ["Zero-shot for simple, examples for complex or strict formats","Randomly switch whether to include examples on each run","Always add examples with few-shot in every case","Always standardize on zero-shot regardless of complexity"], "eEn": "Simple tasks are fine with zero-shot, and examples are added for complex tasks or strict formats. Always using few-shot, or always using zero-shot, ignores how hard the task is, and switching at random has no rationale."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】プロンプトに文脈を与える効果はどれか。","o":["常に応答が高速化し遅延が縮む","画面表示が改善され結果が見やすくなる","タスク背景に即した応答を引き出す","推論のコストが確実に下がる"],"a":2,"e":"文脈を与えると、モデルがタスクの背景を踏まえた応答を返せる。文脈がないと的外れになりやすい。常に応答が高速化し遅延が縮むわけではない。文脈を足すと入力が増えるので推論のコストが確実に下がることもなく、画面表示とも関係がない。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the effect of giving context in a prompt?", "oEn": ["Responses are always faster and delay shrinks","The on-screen display improves and results are easier to read","It elicits responses that fit the task's background","The cost of inference is certain to go down"], "eEn": "Giving context lets the model respond in line with the background of the task, and without it answers tend to miss the point. It does not always make responses faster or shorten delay. Added context means more input, so it does not reliably lower inference cost, and it has nothing to do with screen display."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】段階的指示が有効な理由はどれか。","o":["常に応答が高速化して待ち時間が縮む","画面表示が改善され結果を見やすく整形できる","推論に要するコストを確実に下げられる","複雑タスクを分解し各段を確実に実行できる"],"a":3,"e":"段階的な指示は、複雑なタスクを小さな手順に分解し、各段を確実に実行させるので、一括で依頼するより完遂率が上がる。常に応答が高速化して待ち時間が縮むとは限らず、画面表示や推論コストの改善が理由でもない。", "qEn": "[Applied] Why are step-by-step instructions effective?", "oEn": ["Responses are always faster and wait time shrinks","The on-screen display improves and results can be formatted to be easier to read","The cost of inference is certain to be lowered","They break a complex task down so each step is executed reliably"], "eEn": "Step-by-step instructions break a complex task into small procedures and have each step done reliably, so the completion rate beats a single bulk request. Responses are not always faster, and display or inference cost improvements are not the reason."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】制約条件を明示する利点はどれか。","o":["推論コストを確実に削減できる","出力の範囲・長さ・形式を制御できる","画面表示が改善され結果を見やすくできる","常に応答が高速化して遅延が縮む"],"a":1,"e":"制約条件を明示すると、出力の範囲・長さ・形式をモデルに守らせて制御でき、要件への適合が高まる。推論コストが確実に減る、画面表示が見やすくなる、常に応答が速くなる、といった効果を保証するものではない。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the benefit of stating constraints explicitly?", "oEn": ["Inference cost can be reliably reduced","The scope, length, and format of the output can be controlled","The on-screen display is improved and results become easier to read","Responses are always faster and delay shrinks"], "eEn": "Stating constraints explicitly controls the scope, length and format of the output and improves fit with the requirements. It does not guarantee lower inference cost, a more readable display, or consistently faster responses."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】曖昧語を避けるべき理由はどれか。","o":["推論コストが増えるから","指示が長くなり読みにくくなるから","解釈がぶれ結果が安定しないから","画面上の表示が乱れるから"],"a":2,"e":"曖昧な語は読み手ごとに解釈が分かれ、結果が安定しない。測定できる表現にすれば出力が揃う。推論コストが増えるから、指示が長くなるから、表示が乱れるからといった理由ではない。", "qEn": "[Applied] Why should ambiguous words be avoided?", "oEn": ["Because inference cost increases","Because the instructions get longer and are harder to read","Because interpretation varies and results are unstable","Because the on-screen display becomes garbled"], "eEn": "Vague words get interpreted differently each time, so results become unstable; measurable wording keeps the output consistent. The reason is not that they raise inference cost, lengthen the instructions or break the display."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】対象読者を指定する理由はどれか。","o":["推論に要するコストを削減するため","語彙レベルや説明の深さを適切に調整するため","画面表示のレイアウトを整えるため","応答の生成速度を高速化し待ち時間を減らすため"],"a":1,"e":"対象読者を指定すると、語彙のレベルや説明の深さが読者に合うよう調整され、出力の質が上がる。画面表示のレイアウトを整えることや推論コストの削減、生成速度の向上が目的ではない。", "qEn": "[Applied] Why specify the target audience?", "oEn": ["To reduce the cost required for inference","To adjust vocabulary level and depth of explanation appropriately","To arrange the on-screen layout","To make response generation faster and reduce the time users spend waiting"], "eEn": "Specifying the target reader lets the model adjust vocabulary level and depth of explanation to that audience, which raises output quality. The aim is not to tidy the screen layout, cut inference cost or speed up generation."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】自己検証ステップを加える利点はどれか。","o":["出力前に整合性を確認させ単純な誤りを減らせる","応答が常に高速化して待ち時間が縮む","画面表示が改善され結果をより見やすく整形できる","推論に要するコストを確実に削減できる"],"a":0,"e":"出力する前に整合性を確認させる自己検証のステップを入れると、単純な誤りを自分で見つけて直せるので、誤りが減る。応答が常に高速化するわけではなく、むしろ手順が増えて時間やコストはかかる。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the benefit of adding a self-verification step?", "oEn": ["Having consistency checked before output reduces simple errors","Responses are always faster and wait time shrinks","The on-screen display improves and results can be formatted to be easier to read","The cost required for inference is reliably reduced"], "eEn": "Adding a self-check step that has the model verify consistency before answering lets it catch and fix simple mistakes, so errors drop. It does not make responses always faster; the extra step actually adds time and cost."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】出力の長さ制御が難しい理由はどれか。","o":["モデルは厳密なトークン数制御が不得手だから","出力の形式が指定されていないから","画面表示の都合で文字数が丸め込まれてしまうから","利用できるツールが不足しているから"],"a":0,"e":"モデルは厳密なトークン数を数えて止める制御が得意ではなく、指示しても長さがぶれる。出力の形式を指定しても長さの保証にはならないため、厳守したい場合は後処理で切り詰めや検証を行う。", "qEn": "[Applied] Why is it hard to control output length?", "oEn": ["Because models are poor at strict token-count control","Because the output format is not specified","Because character counts get rounded off due to on-screen display","Because there are not enough tools available"], "eEn": "Models are not good at counting tokens exactly, so the length drifts even when you state a target. Specifying an output format does not guarantee length, so enforce strict limits with post-processing such as truncation or validation."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】指示の競合を避ける理由はどれか。","o":["矛盾する指示はモデルを混乱させるから","推論に要するコストが増えるから","画面上の表示が乱れて読みにくくなるから","指示の文字数が増えてしまうから"],"a":0,"e":"矛盾する指示があるとモデルはどちらに従うべきか判断できず、出力が不安定になる。推論に要するコストが増えるからではなく、指示同士を整合させておくことが目的である。", "qEn": "[Applied] Why avoid conflicting instructions?", "oEn": ["Because contradictory instructions confuse the model","Because the cost required for inference increases","Because the on-screen display gets garbled and is hard to read","Because the number of characters in the instructions increases"], "eEn": "When instructions contradict each other, the model cannot tell which one to follow and the output becomes unstable. The point is not inference cost; it is to keep every instruction consistent with the others."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】区切り文字（デリミタ）を使う利点はどれか。","o":["画面表示が整い結果が見やすくなるから","複数項目を確実に分離・抽出できる","推論コストを削減できるから","応答が高速化し遅延が縮むから"],"a":1,"e":"デリミタで入力や出力の区切りを明示すると、複数項目を確実に分離・抽出できる。推論コストを削減できるわけではなく、画面表示を整える目的でもない。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the benefit of using delimiters?", "oEn": ["Because the on-screen display is tidied and results are easier to read","Multiple items can be separated and extracted reliably","Because inference cost can be reduced","Because responses are faster and delay shrinks"], "eEn": "Delimiters mark the boundaries of inputs and outputs, so multiple items can be separated and extracted reliably. They do not reduce inference cost, and their purpose is parsing, not making the screen look tidy."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】列挙型（enum）を使う利点はどれか。","o":["推論コストが減るから","応答が高速化するから","出力を許可値に限定できる","画面表示が見やすく整うから"],"a":2,"e":"enumは出力を事前に決めた許可値だけに限定でき、下流の分岐処理が想定外の値で壊れない。推論コストが減るわけでも応答が速くなるわけでもなく、画面表示とも無関係である。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the benefit of using an enumeration type (enum)?", "oEn": ["Because inference cost goes down","Because responses get faster","Output can be limited to the allowed values","Because the on-screen display is tidied and easier to read"], "eEn": "An enum restricts the output to a predefined set of allowed values, so downstream branching never receives an unexpected value. It does not lower inference cost or speed up responses, and it has nothing to do with screen display."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】指示の優先順位を明示する利点はどれか。","o":["競合時にどれを優先するか明確になる","推論に要するコストを削減できる","画面上の表示が整い結果が見やすくなる","応答が高速化して遅延が縮む"],"a":0,"e":"優先順位を明示しておけば、指示が競合したときにどれを優先するかが決まり、判断が一貫する。推論に要するコストを削減する効果はなく、画面表示を整えるものでもない。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the benefit of stating instruction priorities explicitly?", "oEn": ["It becomes clear which to prioritize when they conflict","The cost required for inference can be reduced","The on-screen display is tidied and results are easier to read","Responses are faster and delay shrinks"], "eEn": "Stating priorities in advance settles which instruction wins when two of them conflict, so the model decides consistently. It does not reduce inference cost, and it is not about making the display look better."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】出力の根拠提示を求める利点はどれか。","o":["検証可能性と信頼性が上がり幻覚抑制にも効く","画面上の表示が整い結果がより見やすくなるから","応答が高速化し待ち時間が縮むから","推論に要するコストを削減できるから"],"a":0,"e":"根拠を示させると、出力を原典と照合して検証でき、信頼性が上がる。根拠のない主張を出しにくくなるため幻覚の抑制にも効く。応答が高速化し待ち時間が縮むことや、推論に要するコストを削減することが目的ではない。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the benefit of asking for the basis of the output?", "oEn": ["Verifiability and reliability go up, and it helps suppress hallucination","Because the on-screen display is tidied up and the results become easier to read","Because responses are faster and wait time shrinks","Because the cost required for inference can be reduced"], "eEn": "Asking for supporting evidence lets you check the output against the source, which raises reliability. It also makes unsupported claims harder to produce, curbing hallucination. Faster responses or lower inference cost are not the goal."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】文脈注入とファインチューニングの違いはどれか。","o":["両者は完全に同じ手法で違いは呼び名だけである","どちらもモデルの重みを訓練し直す点で本質的に同一である","前者が重みを更新し後者が実行時に文脈を与える","前者は実行時に文脈を与える／後者は重みを更新する"],"a":3,"e":"文脈注入は実行時に必要な情報をプロンプトで与える方法で、重みは変わらない。ファインチューニングは訓練でモデルの重みを更新する方法である。両者を同一視する選択肢や、役割を逆にした選択肢は誤り。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is the difference between context injection and fine-tuning?", "oEn": ["They are exactly the same technique, and only the names differ","Both retrain the model's weights, so they are identical","The former updates weights; the latter provides runtime context","The former provides context at runtime / the latter updates weights"], "eEn": "Context injection supplies information in the prompt at run time and leaves the weights unchanged. Fine-tuning updates the model's weights through training. Treating the two as the same method, or swapping their roles, is wrong."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】評価セットを維持することが長期的に効く理由はどれか。","o":["応答が常に高速化して待ち時間が減るから","推論に要するコストを削減できるから","変更ごとに回帰テストして品質を守れるから","画面上の表示が整い結果が見やすくなるから"],"a":2,"e":"評価セットがあれば、プロンプトやモデルを変えるたびに同じ問題で回帰テストでき、品質の劣化をすぐ検出できる。応答が速くなるわけでも、推論に要するコストを削減できるわけでもない。", "qEn": "[Applied] Why does maintaining an evaluation set pay off over the long term?", "oEn": ["Because responses are always faster and wait time decreases","Because the cost required for inference can be reduced","Because you can regression-test each change and protect quality","Because the on-screen display is tidied and results are easier to read"], "eEn": "With an evaluation set, you can rerun the same cases after every prompt or model change and catch quality regressions right away. It does not make responses faster or reduce inference cost."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】systemプロンプトとユーザーメッセージの役割分担はどれか。","o":["systemが個別要求／userが常設方針を担う","systemは常設方針／userは個別要求","systemもuserもどちらも一時的な指示として扱われる","両者は役割が同じで扱いに違いはない"],"a":1,"e":"systemプロンプトは常に守らせる方針や役割を置く場所で、userメッセージはその都度の具体的な要求を渡す場所である。役割を分けるほど管理しやすい。両者を同じ扱いとする選択肢は誤り。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] How are roles divided between the system prompt and user messages?", "oEn": ["system handles individual requests / user handles standing policy","system is for standing policy / user is for individual requests","Both system and user are treated as temporary instructions","The two have the same role and there is no difference in handling"], "eEn": "The system prompt holds standing policy and role that should always apply, while the user message carries each specific request. Separating the two makes them easier to manage. Treating them as identical is wrong."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】プレフィルを使う目的はどれか。","o":["応答冒頭を指定して出力を誘導する","モデルの推論温度を下げて安定させる","出力形式を厳密に検証する","応答トークンの上限を自動調整する"],"a":0,"e":"プレフィルは応答の出だしを固定して誘導する。形式の完全保証はスキーマ強制が確実。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the purpose of using prefill?", "oEn": ["Guide the output by specifying how the response begins","Lower the model's temperature to stabilize it","Strictly validate the output format","Automatically adjust the response token limit"], "eEn": "Prefill guides the response by fixing its opening. Schema enforcement is the reliable way to fully guarantee the format."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】構造化出力の強制力の順序として正しいのはどれか。","o":["プレフィル（弱）＜ツールスキーマ（中）＜プロンプト指示（強）","プロンプト指示＜ツールスキーマ＜プレフィルの順で強くなる","ツールスキーマ（弱）＜プロンプト指示（中）＜プレフィル（強）","プロンプト指示（弱）＜プレフィル（中）＜ツールスキーマ（強）"],"a":3,"e":"強制力はプロンプト指示が最も弱く、プレフィルが中、ツールスキーマが最も強い。ツールスキーマは出力構造をスキーマで縛るため、プレフィルより確実に形式を守らせられる。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which correctly orders the strength of enforcement for structured output?", "oEn": ["Prefill (weak) < tool schema (medium) < prompt instruction (strong)","Strength increases in the order prompt instruction < tool schema < prefill","Tool schema (weak) < prompt instruction (medium) < prefill (strong)","Prompt instruction (weak) < prefill (medium) < tool schema (strong)"], "eEn": "Prompt instructions are the weakest way to force structure, prefill is in the middle, and a tool schema is the strongest. A tool schema constrains the output structure itself, so it holds the format more reliably than prefill."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】CIレビューで偽陽性が信頼を損なうカテゴリへの対処はどれか。","o":["一時無効化し、プロンプト改善後に再有効化する","該当カテゴリを完全に削除して二度と実行しない","偽陽性を許容範囲としてそのまま運用する","検出結果を全て手動で確認してから採用する"],"a":0,"e":"偽陽性が多いカテゴリは開発者の信頼を損なうので、いったん無効化して信頼を守り、プロンプトを改善してから再有効化する。完全削除は改善の機会を捨て、そのまま運用すれば不信が積み重なる。", "qEn": "[Applied] How do you handle a category whose false positives undermine trust in CI review?", "oEn": ["Temporarily disable it, and re-enable it after improving the prompt","Delete the category entirely and never run it again","Treat the false positives as acceptable and keep operating as is","Manually check all detection results before adopting them"], "eEn": "A category with many false positives erodes developer trust, so disable it temporarily and re-enable it once the prompt is improved. Deleting it for good throws away the chance to fix it, and keeping it as is deepens the distrust."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】重大度を一貫分類するための最善策はどれか。","o":["各重大度に具体コード例を添えた明示基準を定義する","過去の分類例を大量に集め多数決で決める","各案件ごとに担当者が個別に基準を決める","重大度の判定基準を設けずモデルの裁量に完全に委ねる"],"a":0,"e":"各重大度に具体的なコード例を添えた明示基準を定義すると、判断の拠り所が揃い一貫した分類になる。基準を設けずモデルの裁量に任せたり、案件ごとに担当者が基準を決めたりすると判定がぶれる。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the best way to classify severity consistently?", "oEn": ["Define explicit criteria for each severity with concrete code examples","Collect a large number of past classification examples and decide by majority vote","Have the person in charge decide the criteria individually for each case","Set no severity criteria and leave it entirely to the model's discretion"], "eEn": "An explicit criterion with a concrete code example for each severity level gives every judgment the same reference point, so classification stays consistent. Leaving it to the model's discretion or letting each person set criteria makes results drift."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】偽陽性パターン分析に有効なフィールドはどれか。","o":["review_category","confidence_score","detected_pattern","false_positive_id"],"a":2,"e":"detected_patternで誘発パターンを追跡し、却下傾向の体系分析を可能にする。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which field is effective for analyzing false-positive patterns?", "oEn": ["review_category","confidence_score","detected_pattern_type","false_positive_id"], "eEn": "detected_pattern tracks the triggering patterns and enables systematic analysis of dismissal tendencies."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】矛盾するソースデータを検出する自己修正フィールドはどれか。","o":["source_reliability スコア","conflict_detected ブール","ambiguity_flag ブール","validation_passed フラグ"],"a":1,"e":"conflict_detectedブールで、矛盾するソースデータの不整合を検出できる。", "qEn": "[Applied] Which self-correction field detects contradictory source data?", "oEn": ["source_reliability score field","conflict_detected boolean","ambiguity_flag boolean","validation_passed flag"], "eEn": "A conflict_detected boolean can detect inconsistencies in contradictory source data."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】Batches API のコスト・時間特性として正しいのはどれか。","o":["75%節約・最大12時間・SLA保証あり","50%割増・即時応答・SLAなし","25%節約・最大1時間・SLAあり","50%節約・最大24時間・SLAなし"],"a":3,"e":"Batches APIは通常より50%安く、結果は最大24時間以内に返り、完了時間のSLAはない。即時応答を前提にする用途には向かない。割増料金や25%・75%の節約は事実と違う。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which correctly describes the cost and time characteristics of the Batches API?", "oEn": ["75% savings, up to 12 hours, SLA guaranteed","50% surcharge, immediate response, no SLA","25% savings, up to 1 hour, SLA provided","50% savings, up to 24 hours, no SLA"], "eEn": "The Batches API costs 50% less than standard calls, returns results within 24 hours at most, and has no completion-time SLA. It does not suit uses that need an immediate reply, and the surcharge or 25% and 75% savings figures are wrong."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】Batches API が向くワークロードはどれか。","o":["対話型チャットの即時応答・入力補完","ユーザー操作に連動するリアルタイム検索","マージ前のPRブロッキングチェック","夜間レポート・週次監査・夜間テスト生成"],"a":3,"e":"Batches APIは結果が最大24時間かかるため、夜間レポートや週次監査のように待てる処理に向く。対話型チャットの即時応答やPRのブロッキングチェックは、待たされると業務が止まるので不適切。", "qEn": "[Applied] Which workloads suit the Batches API?", "oEn": ["Immediate responses and input completion in interactive chat","Real-time search linked to user operations","Blocking PR checks before merge","Nightly reports, weekly audits, nightly test generation"], "eEn": "Batch results can take up to 24 hours, so it fits work that can wait, such as nightly reports and weekly audits. Interactive chat replies and PR blocking checks stall people when results are late, so they are a poor fit."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】抽出スキーマで required と optional を適切に分ける目的はどれか。","o":["requiredとoptionalを区別せず全て同じ扱いにする","全フィールドを必須指定にして一つでも欠損すれば抽出全体を失敗として扱う","全フィールドをoptionalにして柔軟性を最大化する","存在しうる情報をoptionalにして捏造を防ぎ、必須は確実に取る"],"a":3,"e":"存在しうる情報をoptional（nullable）にすると捏造を防げる。必須は確実に取得すべき項目に限る。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the purpose of properly separating required and optional in an extraction schema?", "oEn": ["Treat required and optional all the same without distinguishing them","Make every field required and treat the entire extraction as failed if even one is missing","Make all fields optional to maximize flexibility","Make information that may exist optional to prevent fabrication, and reliably get the required ones"], "eEn": "Making information that may exist optional (nullable) prevents fabrication. Limit required fields to items that should reliably be obtained."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】リトライが成功しうるケースはどれか。","o":["必要な情報がソースに存在しない場合","参照文書がシステム外部にしかない場合","必須項目が原文から欠落している場合","形式不一致や構造的な出力エラー"],"a":3,"e":"形式不一致や構造的な出力エラーは、エラー内容を添えて再試行すれば直る可能性がある。必要な情報が原文に存在しない場合は、何度やり直しても出力できず、リトライは効かない。", "qEn": "[Applied] In which case can a retry succeed?", "oEn": ["When the required information does not exist in the source","When the reference document exists only outside the system","When a required item is missing from the original text","Format mismatches and structural output errors"], "eEn": "Format mismatches and structural output errors can be fixed by retrying with the error details attached. If the needed information is not in the source text, no number of retries can produce it, so retrying does not help."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】few-shot例を作る際の最適な個数の目安はどれか。","o":["例は使わず指示のみで統一する","考えられる全ケースを100個網羅する","曖昧シナリオに的を絞り2-4個","網羅性重視で最低でも20個以上用意する"],"a":2,"e":"few-shot例は曖昧なシナリオに絞った2〜4個が効果的で、判断の分かれ目を示せる。100個や20個以上を網羅しようとすると文脈を大きく消費し、例を使わず指示だけにすると曖昧さが残る。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is a good guideline for the number of few-shot examples?", "oEn": ["Don't use examples and standardize on instructions only","Cover all conceivable cases with 100 examples","2-4 examples focused on ambiguous scenarios","Prepare at least 20 or more, prioritizing comprehensiveness"], "eEn": "Two to four few-shot examples aimed at ambiguous scenarios work well because they show where the judgment line sits. Trying to cover 100 cases or 20 or more consumes a lot of context, and using instructions alone leaves the ambiguity."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】抽出の幻覚を減らす最も効果的な手法はどれか。","o":["抽出前に原文を要約して情報量を減らしてから渡す","出力スキーマの各項目を必須指定に変更する","多様な形式の正しい抽出を示すfew-shot例","推論温度を0にして決定的な出力にする"],"a":2,"e":"多様な形式の正しい抽出例をfew-shotで示すと、モデルは原文にある情報だけを取り出す型を学び、幻覚が減る。原文を要約して情報量を減らすと、かえって欠落や取り違えを招く。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the most effective technique for reducing extraction hallucinations?", "oEn": ["Summarize the original text before extraction to reduce the amount of information, then pass it","Change every item in the output schema to required","Few-shot examples showing correct extraction from varied formats","Set the inference temperature to 0 for deterministic output"], "eEn": "Few-shot examples of correct extraction from varied formats teach the model to pull out only what is in the text, which reduces hallucination. Summarizing the source first reduces the information and invites omissions and mix-ups."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】構造化出力で意味エラーを捕捉する方法はどれか。","o":["tool_choiceをanyに設定してモデルに出力形式の判断を委ねる","calculated_total と stated_total を併記して差異を検証する","各フィールドの型・範囲・必須制約をJSONスキーマ側で厳格に定義し出力形式を自動検証する","推論温度を0付近まで下げて数値計算の誤りを抑制し出力の一貫性を高める"],"a":1,"e":"スキーマは構文エラーのみ排除。意味エラーはcalculated/stated併記等の検証層で捕捉する。", "qEn": "[Applied] How do you catch semantic errors in structured output?", "oEn": ["Set tool_choice to any and leave the judgment of output format to the model","Record calculated_total and stated_total side by side and validate the discrepancy","Strictly define each field's type, range, and required constraints on the JSON schema side to validate the output format automatically","Lower the inference temperature to near 0 to suppress numeric calculation errors and improve output consistency"], "eEn": "A schema eliminates only syntax errors. Semantic errors are caught by a validation layer, such as recording calculated and stated values side by side."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】抽出結果をPRにインラインコメントとして自動投稿するための形式はどれか。","o":["整形前のプレーンテキスト応答","HTMLテーブル形式の出力","JSONスキーマ準拠の構造化出力","Markdown形式の自由記述テキスト"],"a":2,"e":"PRへのインラインコメントとして自動投稿するには、ファイルや行番号などの項目を機械的に読み取る必要がある。JSONスキーマに準拠した構造化出力ならそれができる。自由記述のテキストやHTMLでは解析が不安定になる。", "qEn": "[Applied] What format allows extraction results to be automatically posted as inline comments on a PR?", "oEn": ["Unformatted plain text response","HTML table output","JSON-schema-conformant structured output","Free-form descriptive text in Markdown format"], "eEn": "Posting inline PR comments automatically requires reading fields such as file and line number by machine. Structured output that conforms to a JSON schema allows that. Free-form text or HTML tables make parsing unreliable."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】tool_choice forced（強制）の用途はどれか。","o":["モデルにツールを一切使わせない","特定ツールを必ず最初に呼ばせる","ツール呼び出しをモデルの任意に委ねる","必ずテキストのみで応答させる"],"a":1,"e":"強制選択は特定ツールを必ず呼ばせる。enrichment前のextract_metadata実行などに使う。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is tool_choice forced used for?", "oEn": ["Make the model use no tools at all","Make a specific tool always be called first","Leave tool calling to the model","Make it respond with text only"], "eEn": "Forced selection always calls a specific tool. It is used, for example, to run extract_metadata before enrichment."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】明示的レビュー基準が信頼度フィルタより優れる理由はどれか。","o":["確信度の数値が高いほど常に正確だと保証されるから","閾値を一つ決めるだけで運用でき実装が単純になるから","どの問題を報告/スキップするか定義でき精度が安定するから","モデルの自己申告確信度が実際の案件の複雑さと強く相関するから"],"a":2,"e":"明示的なレビュー基準は、どの問題を報告しどれをスキップするかを定義できるので精度が安定する。モデルの自己申告の確信度は、数値が高くても正確とは限らず、案件の複雑さとも強く対応しない。", "qEn": "[Applied] Why are explicit review criteria better than a confidence filter?", "oEn": ["Because a higher confidence number is always guaranteed to be accurate","Because you only need to set one threshold to operate, which makes implementation simple","Because they can define which problems to report or skip, making accuracy stable","Because the model's self-reported confidence correlates strongly with the actual complexity of the case"], "eEn": "Explicit review criteria define which problems to report and which to skip, so precision stays stable. A model's self-reported confidence is not guaranteed accurate even when high, and it does not track how complex a case really is."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】不揃いなソース形式への対応として厳格スキーマと併用すべきものはどれか。","o":["スキーマの制約を緩めて許容範囲を広げる","入力ごとに専用スキーマを動的生成する","抽出後に別工程で形式を後処理して整える","形式正規化ルールをプロンプトに併記"],"a":3,"e":"ソースの形式が不揃いでも、厳格なスキーマに形式正規化ルールをプロンプトで併記すれば、出力を同じ形に揃えられる。スキーマの制約を緩めると、ばらついた形式がそのまま出力に残る。", "qEn": "[Applied] What should be combined with a strict schema to handle inconsistent source formats?", "oEn": ["Loosen the schema constraints to widen the tolerance","Dynamically generate a dedicated schema for each input","Tidy the format with post-processing in a separate step after extraction","Include format normalization rules in the prompt"], "eEn": "When source formats vary, pairing the strict schema with format normalization rules in the prompt brings every output into one shape. Loosening the schema constraints lets the varied formats pass straight into the output."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】few-shot例が最も効果を発揮する状況はどれか。","o":["入力形式が完全に固定された定型処理のとき","単純で一意な答えが決まっており曖昧さがない質問のとき","詳細な指示だけでは一貫した形式・出力が得られないとき","決定論的な計算処理だけで結果が導けるとき"],"a":2,"e":"詳細指示だけでは一貫しない場合に、few-shotが一貫性と実用性を最も高める。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] In which situation are few-shot examples most effective?", "oEn": ["In fixed routine processing where the input format is completely fixed","For a simple question with a single determined answer and no ambiguity","When detailed instructions alone give no consistent format or output","When the result can be derived by deterministic computation alone"], "eEn": "When detailed instructions alone are not consistent, few-shot most improves consistency and practicality."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【知識】プログレッシブ要約（逐次要約）の主なリスクはどれか。","o":["数値・割合・日付・顧客の明示的期待が曖昧な要約に圧縮されること","要約のたびにトークン消費が増えコストが上がること","会話履歴が長くなりすぎて文脈窓を超過すること","要約処理を繰り返すたびに時間がかかり全体の応答速度が低下すること"],"a":0,"e":"逐次要約は数値・日付・顧客期待などの重要事実を曖昧化するリスクがある。case factsブロックで別管理する。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is the main risk of progressive summarization?", "oEn": ["Numbers, percentages, dates, and stated customer expectations get blurred into vague summaries","Token consumption increases with each summary, raising costs","The conversation history grows too long and exceeds the context window","Each repeated round of summarization takes time and lowers the response speed of the whole system"], "eEn": "Progressive summarization risks blurring key facts such as numbers, dates, and customer expectations. Manage them separately in a case facts block."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【知識】『lost in the middle』効果とは何か。","o":["文脈窓を超えた古い情報から順に削除される現象","入力が長くなるほど末尾の情報を優先してしまう現象","長い入力の中間にある情報をモデルが取りこぼしやすい現象","長い入力では冒頭付近の情報ほど強く記憶され後半が薄れる現象"],"a":2,"e":"モデルは入力の冒頭と末尾を確実に処理するが、中間の情報を取りこぼしやすい。重要情報は両端に置く。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is the \"lost in the middle\" effect?", "oEn": ["A phenomenon where old information beyond the context window is deleted first","A phenomenon where, as input gets longer, information at the end is prioritized","A phenomenon where the model tends to miss information in the middle of a long input","A phenomenon where, in long input, information near the beginning is remembered more strongly and the latter part fades"], "eEn": "Models process the beginning and end of the input reliably but tend to miss information in the middle. Put important information at both ends."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【シナリオ】注文照会ツールが40以上のフィールドを返すが必要なのは5つだけ。文脈圧迫への対処はどれか。","o":["推論温度を下げて出力量を抑えようとする","毎ターン注文照会ツールを再実行して取り直す","返却された全フィールドをそのまま会話履歴に蓄積し続ける","蓄積前に関連フィールドのみへ絞り込む（トリミング）"],"a":3,"e":"冗長なツール出力は蓄積前に関連フィールドだけへトリミングし、文脈の無駄な消費を防ぐ。", "qEn": "[Scenario] An order lookup tool returns 40+ fields but only 5 are needed. How do you handle context strain?", "oEn": ["Try to reduce output volume by lowering the inference temperature","Re-run the order lookup tool every turn to fetch it again","Keep accumulating all the returned fields as is in the conversation history","Narrow down to only the relevant fields before accumulating (trimming)"], "eEn": "Trim verbose tool output to only the relevant fields before accumulating, preventing wasteful context consumption."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【知識】後続のAPIリクエストで会話の一貫性を保つために重要なことはどれか。","o":["直近の1ターンだけ渡す","要約した履歴だけ渡す","完全な会話履歴を渡す","毎回履歴を空にして渡す"],"a":2,"e":"APIはリクエスト間で会話の状態を保持しないため、一貫性を保つには後続のリクエストごとに完全な会話履歴を渡す。直近1ターンだけ、要約だけ、履歴なしでは、前の文脈が失われる。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is important for keeping conversations consistent in subsequent API requests?", "oEn": ["Pass only the most recent one turn","Pass only the summarized history","Pass the full conversation history so far","Pass an empty history every time"], "eEn": "The API does not keep conversation state between requests, so to stay consistent you pass the full conversation history with each later request. Sending only the last turn, only a summary, or an empty history loses earlier context."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】複数ターンにわたり取引事実（金額・日付・注文番号・ステータス）を確実に保持する方法はどれか。","o":["会話履歴を毎ターン要約し直し、その要約テキストだけに事実の保持を全面的に頼る","必要になるたびに注文照会ツールを再実行して取引事実を取り直す","推論温度を下げてモデルが事実を取り違えないよう安定させる","要約履歴の外に『case facts』ブロックを設け各プロンプトに含める"],"a":3,"e":"取引事実はcase factsブロックとして要約履歴の外で永続化し、各プロンプトに含めることで失われない。", "qEn": "[Applied] How do you reliably retain transaction facts (amounts, dates, order numbers, statuses) across multiple turns?", "oEn": ["Re-summarize the conversation history every turn and rely entirely on that summary text to retain facts","Re-run the order lookup tool whenever needed to fetch the transaction facts again","Lower the inference temperature so the model does not mix up facts","Set up a \"case facts\" block outside the summarized history and include it in every prompt"], "eEn": "Persist transaction facts as a case facts block outside the summarized history and include it in every prompt so they are not lost."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】複数イシューのセッションで構造化イシューデータ（注文ID・金額・ステータス）を扱う方法はどれか。","o":["会話の要約テキストに混ぜて保持する","別の文脈レイヤーに抽出・永続化する","不要になり次第すべて破棄する","各ターンごとにツールで再取得する"],"a":1,"e":"注文IDや金額、ステータスのような構造化データは、要約テキストに混ぜると情報が欠けたり混ざったりする。別の文脈レイヤーに抽出して永続化すれば、複数イシューが続いても取り違えない。", "qEn": "[Applied] How do you handle structured issue data (order ID, amount, status) in a multi-issue session?", "oEn": ["Keep it mixed into the summary text","Extract and persist it in its own context layer","Discard it all once it is no longer needed","Re-fetch it with a tool on every turn"], "eEn": "Structured data such as order IDs, amounts, and statuses gets lost or mixed up when folded into a summary. Extracting it into a separate context layer and keeping it persistent prevents confusion across several issues."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】位置効果（position effects）を緩和する集約入力の組み方はどれか。","o":["詳細データを冒頭に集め要点は末尾にまとめて記載する","所見をランダムな順序で並べて偏りをなくすよう配置する","重要な情報を入力全体の中間にまとめて配置し前後を詳細で挟んで整理する","重要な所見サマリーを冒頭に置き、詳細はセクション見出しで整理する"],"a":3,"e":"重要サマリーを冒頭に、詳細をセクション見出しで整理すると、lost in the middleの影響を緩和できる。", "qEn": "[Applied] How should aggregated input be structured to mitigate position effects?", "oEn": ["Gather the detailed data at the beginning and put the key points together at the end","Arrange findings in random order to eliminate bias","Place the important information together in the middle of the whole input, sandwiched by details before and after","Put the key findings summary at the beginning and organize details under section headings"], "eEn": "Putting the key summary first and organizing details under section headings mitigates the lost in the middle effect."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】下流エージェントの文脈予算が限られるとき、上流エージェントはどう変えるべきか。","o":["冗長な内容・推論連鎖でなく、構造化データ（要点・引用・関連度）を返す","取得した原文の全文をそのまま下流エージェントに渡し判断をすべて委ねる","推論温度を下げて出力を短くまとめ情報量を絞り込んで返す","推論の過程と中間ステップをすべて含めて詳細に報告する"],"a":0,"e":"下流の文脈予算が限られる場合、上流は構造化データ（key facts・citations・relevance scores）を返すよう変える。", "qEn": "[Applied] When a downstream agent's context budget is limited, how should the upstream agent change?", "oEn": ["Return structured data (key points, citations, relevance) instead of verbose content and reasoning chains","Pass the full text of the retrieved source as is to the downstream agent and leave all judgment to it","Lower the inference temperature to summarize the output briefly and return a narrowed amount of information","Report in detail, including the whole reasoning process and all intermediate steps"], "eEn": "When the downstream context budget is limited, the upstream agent changes to return structured data (key facts, citations, relevance scores)."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【知識】適切なエスカレーションの契機として正しいのはどれか。","o":["顧客の人間要求・ポリシーの例外/欠如・進展不能","顧客の苛立ちや感情の強さが一定を超えたとき","案件が複雑で処理に時間がかかると判断された場合全般","モデルの自己申告確信度が閾値を下回ったとき"],"a":0,"e":"エスカレーションは人間要求・ポリシー例外/欠如・進展不能が契機。複雑なだけ・感情・自己申告確信度は不適。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which correctly describes appropriate triggers for escalation?", "oEn": ["A customer request for a human, a policy exception or gap, or inability to progress","The customer's frustration or emotional intensity exceeds a certain level","In general, whenever a case is judged to be complex and likely to take a long time to handle","When the model's self-reported confidence falls below a threshold"], "eEn": "Escalation is triggered by a human request, a policy exception/gap, or inability to make progress. Mere complexity, emotion, or self-reported confidence are not appropriate."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【シナリオ】顧客が明示的に人間対応を要求した。正しい対応はどれか。","o":["調査を試みず直ちにエスカレーションする","案件の確信度を計算して閾値と比較する","顧客の感情を分析してから対応を決める","まず自律的に解決を試みてから必要なら判断する"],"a":0,"e":"顧客が人間の対応を明示的に求めたなら、その意思を尊重して調査を挟まず直ちにエスカレーションする。自律解決を先に試したり、感情や確信度を計算して判断したりするのは、要求を無視することになる。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A customer explicitly asked for a human. What is the correct response?", "oEn": ["Escalate immediately without attempting an investigation","Calculate the case's confidence and compare it with a threshold","Analyze the customer's emotions before deciding how to respond","First try to resolve it autonomously, then decide if necessary"], "eEn": "When a customer explicitly asks for a human, respect that request and escalate at once without investigating first. Trying to resolve it autonomously, or analyzing sentiment or computing confidence first, ignores what the customer asked."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【シナリオ】顧客が苛立っているが問題はエージェントの能力内。最適な対応はどれか。","o":["感情スコアが閾値を超えたら自動的にエスカレーションする","苛立ちを受け止め解決を提案し、再度人間を求めたらエスカレーションする","苛立ちを検知した時点で自律解決を試みず即座に人間へエスカレーションする","解決を試みず謝罪だけして対応を打ち切り会話を終了する"],"a":1,"e":"能力内なら苛立ちを認めつつ解決提案し、顧客が再度人間を求めた場合のみエスカレーションする。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A customer is frustrated, but the issue is within the agent's capability. What is the best response?", "oEn": ["Escalate automatically when the sentiment score exceeds a threshold","Acknowledge the frustration and offer a resolution, and escalate if they ask for a human again","Escalate to a human immediately upon detecting frustration, without attempting autonomous resolution","Apologize only without attempting to resolve, cut off the interaction, and end the conversation"], "eEn": "If it is within capability, acknowledge the frustration while offering a resolution, and escalate only if the customer asks for a human again."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【知識】感情ベースのエスカレーションや自己申告確信度が不適切な理由はどれか。","o":["追加の計算が必要でコストが増えるから","実際の案件複雑さと相関せず校正も不正確だから","感情や確信度の数値をUIに表示できないから","処理に時間がかかり全体の応答速度が大きく低下するから"],"a":1,"e":"感情や自己申告確信度は案件の複雑さと相関せず校正も悪いため、複雑さの代理指標として不適切。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Why are emotion-based escalation and self-reported confidence inappropriate?", "oEn": ["Because extra computation is needed and costs increase","Because they do not correlate with actual case complexity and are poorly calibrated","Because emotion and confidence values cannot be displayed in the UI","Because processing takes time and greatly lowers the response speed of the system as a whole"], "eEn": "Emotion and self-reported confidence do not correlate with case complexity and are poorly calibrated, so they are inappropriate proxies for complexity."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【シナリオ】ツール結果が複数顧客にマッチした。正しい対応はどれか。","o":["追加の識別子を求めて明確化する","ヒューリスティクスで1件に絞る","先頭の候補をそのまま採用する","最も一致度の高い候補を自動で選ぶ"],"a":0,"e":"複数マッチ時は追加識別子を求めて明確化する。ヒューリスティック選択は誤認のリスク。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A tool result matched multiple customers. What is the correct response?", "oEn": ["Ask for additional identifiers to disambiguate","Narrow it down to one with a heuristic","Adopt the first candidate as is","Automatically select the candidate with the highest match score"], "eEn": "When there are multiple matches, ask for additional identifiers to clarify. Heuristic selection risks misidentification."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【シナリオ】ポリシーが自社サイトの価格調整のみ規定し、顧客が競合価格マッチを要求した。対応はどれか。","o":["ポリシーが沈黙・曖昧な事項なのでエスカレーションする","ポリシーに明記がないので一律で拒否して終える","案件の確信度を計算して閾値を基準に判断する","明文化された規定がなくても妥当と判断して独断で承認する"],"a":0,"e":"ポリシーが自社サイトの価格調整しか定めていないとき、競合価格マッチは規定の外にある。沈黙や曖昧さがある事項は、一律拒否や独断の承認ではなく、人間へエスカレーションするのが妥当。", "qEn": "[Scenario] The policy only covers price adjustments on the company's own site, and a customer requested a competitor price match. What is the response?", "oEn": ["Escalate, since the policy is silent or ambiguous on the matter","Since it is not stated in the policy, uniformly refuse and end it","Calculate the case's confidence and judge based on a threshold","Judge it reasonable and approve it on your own even without a written provision"], "eEn": "The policy only covers price adjustments on the company's own site, so a competitor price match falls outside it. When a policy is silent or ambiguous, escalate to a human rather than refusing outright or approving on your own."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【シナリオ】Web検索サブエージェントがタイムアウトした。コーディネーターの知的回復を可能にする最善のエラー伝播はどれか。","o":["空の結果を正常な成功レスポンスとして呼び出し元に返す","指数バックオフで数回再試行した後に汎用の『検索不可』ステータスだけを返す","例外をそのまま最上位に投げて全ワークフローを直ちに終了する","失敗種別・試行クエリ・部分結果・代替案を含む構造化エラー文脈を返す"],"a":3,"e":"構造化エラー文脈はコーディネーターが再試行・代替・部分結果での続行を判断できる。汎用ステータスは文脈を隠し、空成功は回復を妨げ、全終了は不要に過剰。", "qEn": "[Scenario] A web search subagent timed out. What is the best error propagation that lets the coordinator recover intelligently?", "oEn": ["Return an empty result to the caller as a normal success response","After retrying a few times with exponential backoff, return only a generic \"search unavailable\" status as the result","Throw the exception as is to the top level and terminate the entire workflow immediately","Return a structured error context with the failure type, attempted query, partial results, and alternatives"], "eEn": "A structured error context lets the coordinator decide whether to retry, use an alternative, or continue with partial results. A generic status hides context, an empty success prevents recovery, and terminating everything is unnecessarily excessive."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【知識】アクセス失敗と有効な空結果を区別する理由はどれか。","o":["前者は再試行判断が必要／後者はマッチなしの成功で扱いが異なるから","区別してもUI表示が変わるだけで実際の益はないから","両者を区別する処理は複雑で応答が遅くなるだけだから","どちらも最終的に結果が空である点で本質的に同じ扱いにしてよいから"],"a":0,"e":"アクセス失敗（取れなかった）と空結果（無かった）は意味が異なる。区別しないと適切な回復判断ができない。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Why distinguish an access failure from a valid empty result?", "oEn": ["Because the former requires a retry decision, while the latter is a success with no matches, so they are handled differently","Because distinguishing them only changes the UI display and has no real benefit","Because the processing to distinguish them is complex and only slows responses","Because both ultimately have an empty result and may be treated essentially the same"], "eEn": "An access failure (could not retrieve) and an empty result (nothing there) mean different things. Without distinguishing them, appropriate recovery decisions cannot be made."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【知識】汎用エラーステータス（『search unavailable』）の問題はどれか。","o":["エラー通知のコストが増加する","コーディネーターから貴重な文脈を隠す","処理が高速になり応答時間が短縮される","再試行の要否をログから追跡できなくする"],"a":1,"e":"汎用ステータスは失敗種別・試行内容・部分結果といった文脈を隠し、知的な回復判断を妨げる。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is the problem with a generic error status (\"search unavailable\")?", "oEn": ["The cost of error notification increases","It hides valuable context from the coordinator","Processing gets faster and response time shrinks","It makes it impossible to track from logs whether a retry is needed"], "eEn": "A generic status hides context such as the failure type, what was attempted, and partial results, preventing intelligent recovery decisions."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【知識】多エージェント系のアンチパターンの組み合わせはどれか。","o":["失敗箇所での局所的な回復と、解決不能時に部分結果を添えた上位への伝播","構造化エラー文脈の返却と、失敗種別に応じた再試行判断","エラーの黙殺（空を成功扱い）と、単一失敗での全ワークフロー終了","試行クエリの記録と、代替案を含めた上位への丁寧な報告"],"a":2,"e":"エラーの黙殺と単一失敗での全終了はいずれもアンチパターン。局所回復・部分結果伝播・構造化エラーが正しい。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which combination is an anti-pattern in multi-agent systems?", "oEn": ["Local recovery at the point of failure, and propagating to the higher level with partial results when unresolvable","Returning a structured error context, and retry decisions based on the failure type","Silently swallowing errors (treating empty as success), and terminating the entire workflow on a single failure","Recording attempted queries, and politely reporting upward with alternatives"], "eEn": "Silently swallowing errors and terminating everything on a single failure are both anti-patterns. Local recovery, partial-result propagation, and structured errors are correct."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】サブエージェントが一時的失敗に遭遇したときの正しい振る舞いはどれか。","o":["局所回復を試み、解決不能なら試行内容と部分結果を添えて伝播する","再試行も局所回復も行わず即座に全ワークフローを終了させて処理を止める","失敗を無視して次のステップへそのまま処理を進める","空の結果を正常な成功として返し失敗を呼び出し元に隠す"],"a":0,"e":"サブエージェントは一時的な失敗にまず局所回復を試み、解決できなければ試行内容と部分結果を添えて上位へ伝播する。即座に全体を止めたり、失敗を隠して空の結果を成功として返したりしてはいけない。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the correct behavior when a subagent encounters a transient failure?", "oEn": ["Attempt local recovery, and if unresolvable, propagate with the attempted actions and partial results","Do neither retries nor local recovery, and immediately terminate the entire workflow to stop processing","Ignore the failure and proceed to the next step as is","Return an empty result as a normal success and hide the failure from the caller"], "eEn": "A subagent should first try local recovery from a transient failure, and if that fails, propagate it upward with what was tried and any partial results. It must not halt the whole workflow at once or hide the failure by returning an empty result as success."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】統合出力でカバレッジを明示するにはどうするか。","o":["すべての所見を裏付けの強さや情報源の量に関わらず同等の確度として扱う","情報源が不足している領域を明示せず結論に含めてしまう","どの所見が十分裏付けられ、どの領域が情報源不足でギャップかを注記する","推論温度を下げて出力の表現を統一し全体を断定的にまとめる"],"a":2,"e":"統合出力では、どの所見が十分に裏付けられ、どの領域が情報源不足のギャップかを注記する。すべてを同等の確度で扱ったり、不足を明示せず結論に含めたりすると、読み手が確度を誤解する。", "qEn": "[Applied] How do you make coverage explicit in the synthesized output?", "oEn": ["Treat all findings as equally certain regardless of strength of support or amount of sources","Include areas with insufficient sources in the conclusion without making it explicit","Annotate which findings are well supported and which areas are gaps due to insufficient sources","Lower the temperature to unify the output wording and summarize everything assertively"], "eEn": "In a synthesized output, note which findings are well supported and which areas are gaps for lack of sources. Treating everything as equally certain, or folding gaps into the conclusion unmarked, leads readers to misjudge confidence."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【知識】長い探索セッションでの文脈劣化の兆候はどれか。","o":["トークン消費が減りAPIコストが徐々に下がっていく","以前発見した具体的クラスでなく『典型的パターン』を参照し始める","処理速度が徐々に上がり応答が以前のセッションより速く返るようになる","出力の書式が崩れ整形されない応答が徐々に増えていく"],"a":1,"e":"文脈劣化は、具体的に発見した情報でなく一般的な『典型パターン』への参照が増える形で現れる。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is a sign of context degradation in a long exploration session?", "oEn": ["Token consumption decreases and API cost gradually falls","It starts referring to \"typical patterns\" instead of the specific classes found earlier","Processing speed gradually increases and responses come back faster than in previous sessions","More responses with broken output formatting and no formatting appear gradually"], "eEn": "Context degradation shows up as more references to generic \"typical patterns\" instead of specifically discovered information."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】文脈境界を越えて主要所見を保持する手段はどれか。","o":["推論温度を下げて出力を安定させ記憶を保つ","参照ツールを増やして都度取得し直す","スクラッチパッドファイルに記録し後続で参照する","全会話履歴を文脈窓に残したまま常に保持し続ける"],"a":2,"e":"スクラッチパッドファイルに主要所見を永続化し参照することで、文脈劣化を打ち消せる。", "qEn": "[Applied] What means preserves key findings across context boundaries?", "oEn": ["Lower the inference temperature to stabilize output and retain memory","Add reference tools and re-fetch each time","Record them in a scratchpad file and refer to it later","Keep the entire conversation history in the context window at all times"], "eEn": "Persisting key findings to a scratchpad file and referring to it counteracts context degradation."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】冗長な探索出力を隔離しつつ主エージェントが高レベル理解を保つ方法はどれか。","o":["temperatureを下げて出力量を制御する","全出力を主エージェントの文脈に保持し続ける","検索ツールの呼び出し回数を制限する","サブエージェントに委譲して冗長出力を隔離する"],"a":3,"e":"サブエージェント委譲で冗長な探索出力を隔離し、主エージェントは高レベルの調整に専念できる。", "qEn": "[Applied] How can verbose exploration output be isolated while the main agent keeps a high-level understanding?", "oEn": ["Control output volume by lowering the temperature","Keep all output in the main agent's context","Limit the number of search tool calls","Delegate to a subagent to isolate the verbose output"], "eEn": "Delegating to a subagent isolates verbose exploration output, so the main agent can focus on high-level coordination."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】クラッシュ復旧のための構造化状態永続化はどれか。","o":["各エージェントの状態を単一の共有メモリ変数へ集約し全エージェントが直接読み書きする","各エージェントが既知の場所へ状態をエクスポートし、再開時にマニフェストを読み込む","状態を各プロセスのメモリ上にのみ保持しプロセス終了時に破棄する","チェックポイントを取らずログ出力だけで進捗を推測して再開する"],"a":1,"e":"各エージェントが状態をエクスポートし、コーディネーターが再開時にマニフェストを読み込みプロンプトへ注入する。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is structured state persistence for crash recovery?", "oEn": ["Consolidate each agent's state into a single shared memory variable that all agents read and write directly","Each agent exports its state to a known location, and a manifest is loaded on resume","Keep state only in each process's memory and discard it when the process ends","Take no checkpoints and resume by guessing progress from log output alone"], "eEn": "Each agent exports its state, and on resume the coordinator loads the manifest and injects it into the prompt."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】拡張探索セッションで文脈が冗長な発見出力で埋まったときの対処はどれか。","o":["冗長な発見出力をそのまま文脈に蓄積し続ける","/compact で文脈使用量を削減する","temperatureを上げて出力の多様性を高める","利用するツールの数を増やして対応する"],"a":1,"e":"/compactは会話履歴を要約して文脈の使用量を減らすコマンドで、冗長な発見出力で膨らんだ拡張探索セッションに有効である。そのまま蓄積し続けると文脈が溢れ、temperatureやツール数を変えても解決しない。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the remedy when the context in an extended exploration session fills with verbose discovery output?", "oEn": ["Keep accumulating the verbose discovery output in context as is","Reduce context usage with /compact","Raise the temperature to increase output diversity","Increase the number of tools used to cope"], "eEn": "The /compact command summarizes the conversation to reduce context usage, which helps an extended exploration session bloated with verbose findings. Letting them pile up overflows the context, and changing temperature or tool count does not fix that."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】次フェーズのサブエージェントを起動する前に行うべきことはどれか。","o":["前フェーズの全ログをそのまま次段へ引き渡す","前フェーズの主要所見を要約し初期文脈へ注入する","前フェーズのtemperature設定を引き継いで調整する","何も引き継がず各サブエージェントを独立に起動する"],"a":1,"e":"次フェーズのサブエージェントには、前フェーズの主要所見を要約して初期文脈へ注入する。全ログをそのまま渡すと文脈が劣化し、何も引き継がなければ前の成果が使えない。", "qEn": "[Applied] What should be done before launching the next phase's subagent?", "oEn": ["Hand over the entire log of the previous phase to the next stage exactly as it is","Summarize the previous phase's key findings and inject them as initial context","Carry over and adjust the previous phase's temperature setting","Carry over nothing and launch each subagent independently"], "eEn": "Before launching a next-phase subagent, summarize the key findings from the previous phase and inject them into its initial context. Passing the full logs degrades the context, and passing nothing leaves earlier results unused."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【シナリオ】全体精度97%だが特定の文書型・フィールドで事故が頻発する懸念がある。最適な検証はどれか。","o":["合格基準となる精度しきい値を引き上げて再評価する","文書型・フィールド別に層化抽出し、セグメントごとの精度を測る","全評価サンプルを単一の集計指標にまとめて平均精度だけを報告する","評価データ件数を倍に増やし全体精度の信頼区間を狭める"],"a":1,"e":"集計精度は特定セグメントの低精度を隠す。文書型・フィールド別の層化抽出で弱点を露見させる。", "qEn": "[Scenario] Overall accuracy is 97%, but there is concern that errors frequently occur in specific document types and fields. What is the best validation?", "oEn": ["Raise the accuracy threshold used as the pass criterion and re-evaluate","Use stratified sampling by document type and field, and measure accuracy per segment","Combine all evaluation samples into a single aggregate metric and report only the average accuracy","Double the number of evaluation data points to narrow the confidence interval of overall accuracy"], "eEn": "Aggregate accuracy hides low accuracy in particular segments. Stratified sampling by document type and field exposes weaknesses."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【知識】高信頼抽出の誤り率測定と新規パターン検出に有効な手法はどれか。","o":["全件を人間がレビュー","各バッチの先頭数件を確認","層化ランダムサンプリング","無作為に1件だけ確認"],"a":2,"e":"層化ランダムサンプリングは高信頼抽出の継続的な誤り率測定と新規パターン検出に有効。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which technique is effective for measuring the error rate of high-confidence extraction and detecting new patterns?", "oEn": ["Have humans review everything","Check the first few items of each batch","Stratified random sampling","Check just one item at random"], "eEn": "Stratified random sampling is effective for continuous error-rate measurement of high-confidence extraction and detection of new patterns."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】レビュー注意を適切に振り向けるためのスコアはどれか。","o":["モデルのtemperature設定値をそのまま確信度とみなすスコア","各出力テキストの文字数に基づいて算出した長さスコア","呼び出したツールの総数から求めた複雑性スコア","ラベル付き検証セットで校正したフィールド単位の確信度スコア"],"a":3,"e":"フィールド単位の確信度を検証セットで校正し、レビュー閾値の設定とルーティングに使う。", "qEn": "[Applied] Which score allocates review attention appropriately?", "oEn": ["A score that treats the model's temperature setting directly as confidence","A length score calculated from the character count of each output text","A complexity score derived from the total number of tools called","A field-level confidence score calibrated on a labeled validation set"], "eEn": "Calibrate field-level confidence on a validation set and use it to set review thresholds and for routing."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】高信頼抽出の自動化前に確認すべきことはどれか。","o":["全体の平均精度だけが目標値を超えているか","文書型・フィールドセグメント別に精度が一貫しているか","1件あたりの平均処理速度が要件を満たすか","文書1件を処理するのにかかる推論コストが予算内に収まるか"],"a":1,"e":"自動化前に、文書型・フィールド別の精度の一貫性を検証する。全体精度だけでは不十分。", "qEn": "[Applied] What should be confirmed before automating high-confidence extraction?", "oEn": ["Whether only the overall average accuracy exceeds the target","Whether accuracy is consistent across document type and field segments","Whether the average processing speed per item meets the requirement","Whether the inference cost of processing one document fits within budget"], "eEn": "Before automating, verify the consistency of accuracy by document type and field. Overall accuracy alone is not enough."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】限られたレビュー能力を優先配分する方法はどれか。","o":["低確信度や矛盾/曖昧なソースの抽出を人間レビューへ回す","抽出結果を全件そのまま人間レビューへ回す","確信度の高い抽出結果から順に優先して人間レビューへ回す","処理した順に先頭から一定件数をレビューへ回す"],"a":0,"e":"低確信度・矛盾/曖昧ソースの抽出を優先的に人間レビューへ回し、限られた能力を有効活用する。", "qEn": "[Applied] How do you prioritize allocation of limited review capacity?", "oEn": ["Route low-confidence extractions and extractions from contradictory/ambiguous sources to human review","Route all extraction results as is to human review","Route extraction results to human review in order, starting with those of highest confidence","Send a fixed number of items from the front, in the order processed, to review"], "eEn": "Prioritize routing low-confidence and contradictory/ambiguous-source extractions to human review to make effective use of limited capacity."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【知識】要約ステップで出典帰属が失われる原因はどれか。","o":["要約時にtemperatureが高く設定されているから","利用するツールの数が多く出力が複数に分散してしまうから","所見を読み手向けのUI表示に合わせて整形する過程で出典情報が省かれるから","claim-sourceマッピングを保持せずに所見を圧縮するから"],"a":3,"e":"claim-sourceマッピングを保持せず圧縮すると、要約で出典帰属が失われる。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What causes source attribution to be lost in a summarization step?", "oEn": ["Because the temperature is set high during summarization","Because many tools are used and the output gets split across several","Because source information is omitted while formatting findings for the reader's UI display","Because findings are compressed without retaining the claim-source mapping"], "eEn": "Compressing without retaining the claim-source mapping loses source attribution in the summary."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】統合時に出典帰属を保つには何が必要か。","o":["統合の段階で出典情報を省略して所見の本文だけを結合してまとめる","各サブエージェントが全文テキストをそのまま統合エージェントへ渡す","サブエージェントが構造化claim-sourceマッピングを出力し下流が保持する","各サブエージェントの出力を要約モデルに通し出典を含めずに簡潔化してから全体を統合する"],"a":2,"e":"構造化claim-sourceマッピング（URL・文書名・抜粋）を出力し、下流が統合を通じて保持する。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is needed to preserve source attribution during synthesis?", "oEn": ["Omit the source information at the synthesis stage and merge only the body text of the findings","Have each subagent pass its full text as is to the synthesis agent","Subagents output a structured claim-source mapping, and downstream retains it","Run each subagent's output through a summarization model to condense it without sources, then synthesize everything"], "eEn": "Output a structured claim-source mapping (URL, document name, excerpt), and downstream retains it through synthesis."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【シナリオ】信頼できる複数ソースで統計値が矛盾した。正しい扱いはどれか。","o":["最も新しい日付のソースの値を採用する","出典付きで矛盾を注記し、恣意的に1値を選ばない","複数ソースの値の単純平均を代表値とする","信頼度が低いと判断した側のソースを結果から除外する"],"a":1,"e":"矛盾は出典付きで注記し、恣意的な単一値選択を避ける。コーディネーターが調停を判断できるようにする。", "qEn": "[Scenario] Statistics from multiple reliable sources contradict each other. What is the correct handling?", "oEn": ["Adopt the value from the source with the latest date","Annotate the contradiction with sources and do not arbitrarily pick one value","Use the simple average of the values from the multiple sources as the representative value","Exclude from the result the source judged to have lower reliability"], "eEn": "Annotate contradictions with sources and avoid arbitrarily selecting a single value. Let the coordinator decide how to reconcile."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【知識】時系列データを構造化出力に含める際の注意点はどれか。","o":["日付フィールドを省いて数値だけを構造化出力に含める","公開日/収集日を含め、時間差を矛盾と誤解しないようにする","最新の時点の値だけを残して古い時点の値は破棄する","複数時点の値を時系列にわたって平均し単一の代表値に統合する"],"a":1,"e":"公開日/収集日を含めることで、時間差による値の違いを矛盾と誤解せず正しく解釈できる。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is a caution when including time-series data in structured output?", "oEn": ["Omit the date fields and include only numbers in the structured output","Include publication/collection dates so time differences are not mistaken for contradictions","Keep only the latest point's value and discard older values","Average the values across multiple time points and merge them into a single representative value"], "eEn": "Including publication/collection dates lets value differences caused by timing be interpreted correctly rather than mistaken for contradictions."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】合成出力でコンテンツ型ごとの適切な描画とはどれか。","o":["財務データは表、ニュースは散文、技術的所見は構造化リストで描画する","財務データもニュースも技術的所見もすべて連続した散文にまとめて描画する","全てのコンテンツを表形式に変換して統一的に描画する","コンテンツ型に関わらず全ての出力を単一の共通形式で描画する"],"a":0,"e":"財務データは表、ニュースは散文、技術的所見は構造化リストと、内容の型に合う形で描画すると読みやすい。すべてを散文や表、単一の形式に一律変換すると、型ごとの情報が伝わりにくくなる。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is appropriate rendering per content type in a synthesized output?", "oEn": ["Render financial data as tables, news as prose, and technical findings as structured lists","Render financial data, news, and technical findings all together as one continuous run of prose","Convert all content into table format and render it uniformly","Render all output in a single common format regardless of content type"], "eEn": "Rendering financial data as a table, news as prose, and technical findings as a structured list fits each content type and reads well. Converting everything into prose, tables, or one common format makes each type's information harder to grasp."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】文書分析で矛盾値が見つかったときの扱いはどれか。","o":["矛盾値の一方をサブエージェント側で削除して報告する","矛盾する複数の値を平均してひとつの代表値に置き換える","矛盾値を含め明示的に注記し、調停はコーディネーターに委ねる","矛盾値には触れず片方の値だけを採用して残りは出力から取り除く"],"a":2,"e":"文書分析は矛盾値を含め明示注記して完了し、調停は統合前にコーディネーターへ委ねる。", "qEn": "[Applied] How should contradictory values found in document analysis be handled?", "oEn": ["Delete one of the contradictory values on the subagent side and report","Average the contradictory values and replace them with a single representative value","Include the contradictory values with an explicit note, and leave reconciliation to the coordinator","Say nothing about the contradiction, adopt only one of the values, and remove the other from the output"], "eEn": "Document analysis is complete once it explicitly annotates the contradictory values, and reconciliation is left to the coordinator before synthesis."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】レポートで確立された所見と争点のある所見を扱う方法はどれか。","o":["争点のある所見はレポートから省き確立された所見だけを掲載する","明示的セクションで両者を区別し、元の出典の特徴づけと方法論的文脈を保つ","確立された所見も争点のある所見も区別せず同じ節にまとめて記述する","両者を一つの結論に統合し出典や方法論的文脈は省いて簡潔にまとめて提示する"],"a":1,"e":"確立済みと争点ありを明示セクションで区別し、原典の特徴づけと方法論的文脈を保持する。", "qEn": "[Applied] How do you handle established findings and contested findings in a report?", "oEn": ["Omit contested findings from the report and publish only established findings","Separate them into explicit sections, keeping the original source's characterization and methodological context","Describe both in the same section without distinguishing established from contested findings","Merge the two into a single conclusion and present it concisely, leaving out the sources and methodological context"], "eEn": "Distinguish established from contested findings in explicit sections, preserving the original sources' characterization and methodological context."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】サブエージェントの構造化出力に含めるべきメタデータはどれか。","o":["描画に使うUIテーマの設定","生成に用いたmax_tokens","日付・ソース位置・方法論的文脈","モデルのtemperature値"],"a":2,"e":"下流の正確な統合を支えるため、日付・ソース位置・方法論的文脈をメタデータとして含める。", "qEn": "[Applied] What metadata should be included in a subagent's structured output?", "oEn": ["UI theme settings used for rendering","The max_tokens value that was used for generation","Dates, source locations, methodological context","The model's temperature value"], "eEn": "Include dates, source locations, and methodological context as metadata to support accurate downstream synthesis."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【シナリオ】数日にわたるタスクでセッションをまたいで状態を保持したい。最適な手段はどれか。","o":["セッションごとにゼロから状態を再構築して開始する","会話履歴をすべてプロンプトへ連結し毎回モデルに全量を渡し続ける","外部ストアへ永続化するメモリ手段で窓を超えて保存・再参照する","全ての履歴を単一のコンテキスト窓の中に保持し続ける"],"a":2,"e":"窓内メモリは揮発的。長期保持には外部ストアへの永続化が要る。全履歴保持は破綻、再構築は非効率。", "qEn": "[Scenario] You want to retain state across sessions in a task spanning several days. What is the best means?", "oEn": ["Start each session by rebuilding state from scratch","Concatenate the entire conversation history into the prompt and keep passing the whole thing to the model every time","Use a memory mechanism that persists to an external store, saving and re-referencing beyond the window","Keep all history within a single context window"], "eEn": "In-window memory is volatile. Long-term retention requires persisting to an external store. Keeping all history breaks down, and rebuilding is inefficient."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】長文中間の重要指示が無視される問題への対処はどれか。","o":["指示のフォントや装飾を変更する","重要情報を長文の中間に配置する","重要情報を複数箇所に分散させて繰り返し配置する","重要情報を冒頭または末尾に配置する"],"a":3,"e":"lost in the middle対策として、重要情報を入力の両端に配置する。", "qEn": "[Applied] How do you address the problem of important instructions in the middle of a long text being ignored?", "oEn": ["Change the font or decoration of the instructions","Place the important information in the middle of the long text","Spread the important information out and place it repeatedly in multiple spots","Place the important information at the beginning or the end"], "eEn": "As a countermeasure to lost in the middle, place important information at both ends of the input."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】非決定的なエージェント出力を本番反映前に検査する最善策はどれか。","o":["出力をそのまま本番へ反映しログだけを残す","temperatureを0にすれば検査は不要になる","決定的な検証層で検査し、不合格は反映しない","エージェント自身の自己検証だけで十分とする"],"a":2,"e":"非決定性はコードによる決定的検証層で囲む。temperature 0でも非決定性は残り、自己検証はバイアスを含む。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the best way to check non-deterministic agent output before it goes into production?", "oEn": ["Apply the output to production as is and keep only logs","Setting the temperature to 0 means that checking is no longer necessary at all","Check with a deterministic validation layer and don't apply failures","Rely on the agent's own self-verification alone"], "eEn": "Wrap non-determinism in a deterministic validation layer built in code. Non-determinism remains even at temperature 0, and self-verification carries bias."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】依存先APIの連続失敗で連鎖障害が起きた。最適なパターンはどれか。","o":["リトライの回数をさらに増やして呼び出す","各リクエストのタイムアウト時間を延ばす","サーキットブレーカーで一時遮断し回復を待つ","失敗した依存先へ即座に再接続を繰り返し試みる"],"a":2,"e":"連続失敗時はサーキットブレーカーで遮断し、負荷集中と連鎖障害を防ぐ。リトライ増は悪化させる。", "qEn": "[Applied] Consecutive failures of a dependent API caused a cascading failure. What is the best pattern?", "oEn": ["Increase the number of retries further and keep calling","Extend each request's timeout","Temporarily cut off with a circuit breaker and wait for recovery","Immediately and repeatedly try to reconnect to the failing dependency"], "eEn": "On consecutive failures, cut off with a circuit breaker to prevent load concentration and cascading failure. More retries make it worse."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】リトライとフォールバックの違いはどれか。","o":["リトライは同手段の再試行／フォールバックは代替手段への切替","リトライは代替手段への切替でフォールバックは同手段の再試行","リトライは処理を中断する仕組みでフォールバックも同様に処理を停止する","リトライもフォールバックも同一の再試行処理を指す用語である"],"a":0,"e":"リトライは同じ手段をもう一度試すことで、フォールバックは別の代替手段に切り替えることである。リトライを代替手段への切替とする選択肢や、両者を同じ再試行とする選択肢は定義が逆または混同している。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the difference between retry and fallback?", "oEn": ["Retry is re-attempting the same method / fallback is switching to an alternative method","Retry is switching to an alternative method, and fallback is re-attempting the same method","Retry is a mechanism that aborts processing, and fallback likewise stops processing","Retry and fallback are terms for the same re-attempt process"], "eEn": "A retry runs the same method again, while a fallback switches to a different alternative method. Calling a retry a switch to an alternative, or treating both as the same repeated attempt, reverses or confuses the definitions."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【知識】冪等性が信頼性に寄与する理由はどれか。","o":["処理をより高速に実行できるから","APIの呼び出しコストを常に削減できるから","リトライ時の重複副作用を防げるから","出力のUI表示を整えられるから"],"a":2,"e":"冪等な操作は何度実行しても結果が同じなので、リトライしても二重課金や重複登録のような副作用が出ない。そのため安心して再試行でき、信頼性が上がる。処理速度やUI表示、呼び出しコストとは関係がない。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Why does idempotency contribute to reliability?", "oEn": ["Because processing can run faster","Because it can always lower the cost of calling the API","Because it prevents duplicate side effects on retry","Because it can tidy the UI display of the output"], "eEn": "An idempotent operation gives the same result no matter how many times it runs, so retrying causes no duplicate side effects such as double charges or repeated records. That makes retries safe and improves reliability. It is unrelated to speed, UI display, or call cost."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】グレースフルデグラデーション（優雅な劣化）とは何か。","o":["落とす機能をランダムに選んで段階的に停止させる","障害が起きても全機能を落とさず完全な状態を維持し続ける","一部の障害が起きた時点でシステム全体を完全に停止する","一部機能が落ちても全体停止せず限定機能で稼働を続ける"],"a":3,"e":"グレースフルデグラデーションは、一部の機能が落ちてもシステム全体を止めず、限定した機能で稼働を続ける設計で、可用性を保てる。全機能を維持し続けることや、一部の障害で全停止することとは異なる。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is graceful degradation?", "oEn": ["Randomly choosing which features to drop and stopping them step by step","Keep maintaining a complete state without dropping any features when a failure occurs","Completely stopping the whole system as soon as a partial failure occurs","Continuing with limited functionality instead of halting entirely when some features fail"], "eEn": "Graceful degradation keeps a system running with limited functions when some parts fail, instead of stopping everything, which preserves availability. It is not about keeping every function intact, and it is the opposite of halting completely at the first failure."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】ヘルスチェックが信頼性に寄与する理由はどれか。","o":["処理全体をより高速に実行できるようになるから","利用者向けのUI表示を見やすく整えられるから","障害を早期検出し復旧やフェイルオーバーを起動できる","システム全体の運用コストを継続的に削減できるようになるから"],"a":2,"e":"ヘルスチェックは障害の早期検出を可能にし、復旧・フェイルオーバーのトリガーになる。", "qEn": "[Applied] Why do health checks contribute to reliability?", "oEn": ["Because they let the whole process run faster","Because they tidy the user-facing UI display","They detect failures early and can trigger recovery or failover","Because they continuously reduce the operating cost of the whole system"], "eEn": "Health checks enable early detection of failures and serve as triggers for recovery and failover."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【シナリオ】コーディネーターが研究を3サブタスクに分けたが、各サブエージェントは成功しているのに最終レポートが一領域に偏った。最初に見るべきはどれか。","o":["文書分析サブエージェントが用いた関連性の判定基準","最終レポートを組み立てる統合エージェントの指示","コーディネーターの分解ログ（割当範囲が網羅的か）","各Web検索で用いた検索クエリの品質"],"a":2,"e":"各サブが割当内で正常なら、偏りは分解の狭さが原因。まずコーディネーターの分解ログを見る。", "qEn": "[Scenario] The coordinator split the research into 3 subtasks, and every subagent succeeded, yet the final report skewed toward one area. What should you look at first?", "oEn": ["The criteria for judging relevance that were used by the document analysis subagent","The instructions of the synthesis agent that assembles the final report","The coordinator's decomposition log (whether the assigned scope is comprehensive)","The quality of the search queries used in each web search"], "eEn": "If each subagent works properly within its assignment, the skew is caused by a narrow decomposition. First look at the coordinator's decomposition log."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】サブエージェントへ完全な前段所見をプロンプトに含める理由はどれか。","o":["文脈を自動継承しないため明示的に渡す必要があるから","サブエージェントの応答をより高速にするため","利用者向けのUI上に前段の所見を分かりやすく表示するため","全体のトークン消費量とコストを削減できるため"],"a":0,"e":"サブエージェントは親文脈を自動継承しないため、前段の所見はプロンプトに明示的に含める。", "qEn": "[Applied] Why include the complete previous findings in the subagent's prompt?", "oEn": ["Because they don't inherit context automatically, so they must be passed explicitly","To make the subagent's response faster","To display the previous findings in an easy-to-understand way on the UI shown to users","Because it can reduce overall token consumption and cost"], "eEn": "Subagents do not automatically inherit parent context, so the previous findings must be included explicitly in the prompt."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【知識】エージェントループが終了すべきstop_reasonはどれか。","o":["tool_use","end_turn","max_tokens","pause_turn"],"a":1,"e":"stop_reasonがend_turnならループ終了、tool_useなら継続。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] For which stop_reason should the agent loop terminate?", "oEn": ["tool_use","end_turn","max_tokens","pause_turn"], "eEn": "If stop_reason is end_turn, the loop ends; if tool_use, it continues."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【応用】コーディネーターのallowedToolsに必須の項目はどれか（サブエージェント生成のため）。","o":["\"Bash\"","\"Grep\"","\"Read\"","\"Task\""],"a":3,"e":"サブエージェント生成にはallowedToolsへ\"Task\"を含める必要がある。", "qEn": "[Applied] Which item is required in the coordinator's allowedTools (to spawn subagents)?", "oEn": ["\"Bash\"","\"Grep\"","\"Read\"","\"Task\" tool"], "eEn": "To spawn subagents, \"Task\" must be included in allowedTools."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】MCP（Model Context Protocol）リソースの主用途はどれか。","o":["副作用のある書き込み操作を実行するために使う","コンテンツカタログを公開し探索的ツール呼び出しを減らす","認証情報や秘密鍵を安全に保持しておくために使う","クライアント側のユーザーインターフェースを描画するために使う"],"a":1,"e":"MCPリソースは読み取り中心でカタログを公開し、探索的ツール呼び出しを削減する。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the main use of MCP (Model Context Protocol) resources?", "oEn": ["Used to carry out write operations that have side effects","Expose a content catalog and cut exploratory tool calls","Used to securely hold credentials and secret keys","Used to render the client-side user interface"], "eEn": "MCP resources are read-oriented, expose a catalog, and reduce exploratory tool calls."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【シナリオ】タイムアウトを返すツールのerrorCategoryはどれか。","o":["business","transient","validation","permission"],"a":1,"e":"タイムアウトは待てば回復しうる一時的な障害なので、errorCategoryはtransientとなり再試行が妥当。businessは業務ルール違反、validationは入力不正、permissionは権限不足を表し、タイムアウトとは別物である。", "qEn": "[Scenario] Which errorCategory applies to a tool that returns a timeout?", "oEn": ["business","transient (retry)","validation","permission"], "eEn": "A timeout is a temporary failure that may recover, so its errorCategory is transient and a retry is appropriate. Business means a business-rule violation, validation means invalid input, and permission means missing authorization, none of which describe a timeout."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【応用】tool_choice: \"any\" の効果はどれか。","o":["必ずいずれかのツールを呼ばせる","特定の1つのツールを強制的に呼ばせる","モデルにツールを一切呼ばせない","呼び出すツールをモデルの判断に任せる"],"a":0,"e":"tool_choiceをanyにすると、モデルはどれかのツールを必ず呼び出し、テキストだけで返すことができなくなる。どのツールにするかはモデルが選ぶ。特定の1つを強制するのは名前指定、ツールを使わせないのはnoneの役割である。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the effect of tool_choice: \"any\"?", "oEn": ["Makes the model always call one of the tools","Forces a specific single tool to be called","Makes the model call no tools at all","Leaves which tool to call up to the model's judgment"], "eEn": "Setting tool_choice to any forces the model to call some tool, so it cannot reply with plain text only, but the model still chooses which one. Forcing one specific tool is done by naming it, and preventing tool use is the job of none."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【シナリオ】チーム共有のスラッシュコマンドの置き場所はどれか。","o":["~/.claude/commands/","プロジェクトのCLAUDE.md",".claude/commands/","リポジトリ直下のconfig.json"],"a":2,"e":"チーム共有はプロジェクトの.claude/commands/に置き、VCSで配布する。", "qEn": "[Scenario] Where do team-shared slash commands go?", "oEn": ["~/.claude/commands/","The project's CLAUDE.md",".claude/commands/","config.json at the repository root"], "eEn": "Team-shared commands go in the project's .claude/commands/ and are distributed via VCS."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【応用】散在するテストファイルに規約を自動適用する手段はどれか。","o":[".claude/rules/ の **/*.test.* globパターン","実行のたびに各開発者が手動で呼び出すスキルによる規約の適用","ルートのCLAUDE.mdだけに記述した共通規約からモデルが推論して適用すること","各テストディレクトリに個別に配置したCLAUDE.mdによる指示"],"a":0,"e":"散在ファイルにはglobパターンのパス別ルールが最適。位置に依らず自動適用される。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the way to automatically apply conventions to scattered test files?", "oEn": ["A **/*.test.* glob pattern in .claude/rules/","Applying conventions through a skill that each developer invokes manually on every run","The model inferring and applying common conventions written only in the root CLAUDE.md","Instructions from CLAUDE.md files placed individually in each test directory"], "eEn": "For scattered files, path-specific rules with glob patterns are best. They apply automatically regardless of location."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【知識】CIで非対話実行するフラグはどれか。","o":["--batch オプション","--headless","-p（--print）","--daemon モード"],"a":2,"e":"Claude Codeをプロンプト付きで一度だけ実行して結果を出力し終了するのが-p（--print）で、CIのような非対話環境で使う。--batchや--headless、--daemonはその正式なフラグではない。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which flag runs non-interactively in CI?", "oEn": ["--batch option","--headless","-p (--print)","--daemon mode"], "eEn": "The -p (--print) flag runs Claude Code once with a prompt, prints the result, and exits, which suits non-interactive environments such as CI. --batch, --headless, and --daemon are not the official flags for this."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】スキーマ準拠の構造化出力を保証する最も確実な方法はどれか。","o":["プロンプトで丁寧に依頼する方法","アシスタント応答をプレフィルする","tool_use とJSONスキーマ","temperatureを0に設定する"],"a":2,"e":"tool_useとJSONスキーマを組み合わせると、出力がスキーマの構造に従うよう強制され、構文エラーも排除できる。丁寧な依頼やプレフィル、temperatureを0にする方法は、構造の遵守までは保証しない。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] What is the most reliable way to guarantee schema-compliant structured output?", "oEn": ["Politely asking in the prompt","Prefilling the assistant response","tool_use and a JSON schema","Setting temperature to 0"], "eEn": "Combining tool_use with a JSON schema forces the output to follow the schema's structure and eliminates syntax errors. Polite requests, prefilling the response, or setting temperature to 0 do not guarantee adherence to the structure."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【応用】値が無いときの捏造を防ぐスキーマ設計はどれか。","o":["欠損しやすい項目ごとにフィールドを追加で増やして補うようにする","全てのフィールドを必須（required）にする","nullable（optional）フィールドにする","値を全て文字列型（string）に統一する"],"a":2,"e":"nullableにすれば『無い』をnullで表せ、必須充足のための捏造を防げる。", "qEn": "[Applied] What schema design prevents fabrication when a value is absent?", "oEn": ["Add extra fields for each item prone to being missing to compensate","Make all fields required","Make them nullable (optional) fields","Unify all values to the string type"], "eEn": "With nullable, \"absent\" can be expressed as null, preventing fabrication to satisfy required fields."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【知識】Batches APIの特性として正しいのはどれか。","o":["100%割引・最大72時間・SLA保証あり","リアルタイム応答・SLAあり","コスト増・即時応答・SLAなし","50%節約・最大24時間・SLAなし"],"a":3,"e":"Batches APIは50%節約・最大24時間・SLAなし。非ブロッキング処理に向く。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which correctly describes the Batches API?", "oEn": ["100% discount, up to 72 hours, SLA guaranteed","Real-time response, with SLA","Higher cost, immediate response, no SLA","50% savings, up to 24 hours, no SLA"], "eEn": "The Batches API is 50% savings, up to 24 hours, no SLA. It suits non-blocking processing."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【知識】lost in the middle対策として正しい配置はどれか。","o":["重要情報を末尾だけにまとめて置く","重要情報を文脈の中間に置く","重要情報を全体にランダムに置く","重要情報を冒頭または末尾に置く"],"a":3,"e":"長い文脈では中間にある情報が見落とされやすい（lost in the middle）ため、重要情報は冒頭か末尾に置く。中間に置いたり、全体にランダムに散らしたりすると取りこぼしやすい。", "qEn": "[Knowledge] Which placement is correct as a countermeasure to lost in the middle?", "oEn": ["Put the important information only at the end","Put the important information in the middle","Scatter the important information randomly throughout","Put the important information at the beginning or the end"], "eEn": "In a long context, information in the middle is easily overlooked (lost in the middle), so put key information at the beginning or the end. Placing it in the middle or scattering it randomly makes it easier to miss."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【応用】矛盾する統計値の正しい扱いはどれか。","o":["複数の統計値を平均して代表値とする","信頼度が低い側の統計値を結果から取り除く","最も新しい時点の統計値を採用する","出典付きで両論併記し恣意的選択を避ける"],"a":3,"e":"矛盾する統計値は、出典を付けて両論併記し、読み手が判断できるようにする。平均して代表値にしたり、一方を取り除いたり、新しいものだけを採用したりすると、恣意的な選択になり情報が失われる。", "qEn": "[Applied] What is the correct handling of contradictory statistics?", "oEn": ["Average the statistics and use that as the representative value","Remove the statistics from the side with lower reliability from the result","Adopt the statistic from the most recent point in time","Present both sides with sources and avoid arbitrary selection"], "eEn": "When statistics conflict, present both with their sources so the reader can judge. Averaging them into one value, dropping one side, or adopting only the newest one is an arbitrary choice that discards information."}];

// ===== シナリオ演習：6つの本番想定シナリオ（公式ガイド準拠）=====
// 各シナリオは文脈（context）を持ち、複数の紐づく問題を出題する。30問×5セットで構成。
const SCENARIOS = {
  s1: { ja:"【シナリオ1：顧客サポート解決エージェント】Claude Agent SDKで顧客サポート解決エージェントを構築している。返金・請求紛争・アカウント問題など高曖昧度の要求を、MCPツール（get_customer / lookup_order / process_refund / escalate_to_human）経由のバックエンド接続で処理する。目標は80%以上の初回解決率と、適切なエスカレーション判断。",
        en:"[Scenario 1: Customer Support Resolution Agent] You are building a customer support resolution agent with the Claude Agent SDK. It handles high-ambiguity requests (returns, billing disputes, account issues) via backend MCP tools (get_customer / lookup_order / process_refund / escalate_to_human). The target is 80%+ first-contact resolution with sound escalation." },
  s2: { ja:"【シナリオ2：Claude Codeによるコード生成】Claude Codeで開発を加速している。チームはコード生成・リファクタリング・デバッグ・ドキュメント化に利用。カスタムスラッシュコマンド・CLAUDE.md設定でワークフローに統合し、プランモードと直接実行を使い分ける。",
        en:"[Scenario 2: Code Generation with Claude Code] You use Claude Code to accelerate development—code generation, refactoring, debugging, documentation. You integrate it via custom slash commands and CLAUDE.md, choosing between plan mode and direct execution." },
  s3: { ja:"【シナリオ3：マルチエージェント研究システム】Claude Agent SDKでマルチエージェント研究システムを構築。コーディネーターが専門サブエージェント（Web検索・文書分析・統合・レポート生成）へ委譲し、出典付きの包括的レポートを生成する。",
        en:"[Scenario 3: Multi-Agent Research System] You build a multi-agent research system with the Claude Agent SDK. A coordinator delegates to specialized subagents (web search, document analysis, synthesis, report generation) to produce comprehensive, cited reports." },
  s4: { ja:"【シナリオ4：開発者生産性ツール】Claude Agent SDKで開発者生産性ツールを構築。不慣れなコードベースの探索・レガシー理解・ボイラープレート生成・反復作業の自動化を支援し、組み込みツール（Read/Write/Bash/Grep/Glob）とMCPサーバーを使う。",
        en:"[Scenario 4: Developer Productivity] You build developer-productivity tools with the Claude Agent SDK to explore unfamiliar codebases, understand legacy systems, generate boilerplate, and automate repetitive tasks, using built-in tools (Read/Write/Bash/Grep/Glob) and MCP servers." },
  s5: { ja:"【シナリオ5：CI/CDのClaude Code】Claude CodeをCI/CDパイプラインに統合。自動コードレビュー・テスト生成・PRフィードバックを実行する。実用的なフィードバックを与えつつ偽陽性を最小化するプロンプト設計が求められる。",
        en:"[Scenario 5: Claude Code for CI] You integrate Claude Code into a CI/CD pipeline running automated code reviews, test generation, and PR feedback. You must design prompts that give actionable feedback while minimizing false positives." },
  s6: { ja:"【シナリオ6：構造化データ抽出】Claudeで構造化データ抽出システムを構築。非構造化文書から情報を抽出し、JSONスキーマで検証して高精度を維持する。エッジケースを優雅に扱い、下流システムと統合する。",
        en:"[Scenario 6: Structured Data Extraction] You build a structured data extraction system with Claude. It extracts from unstructured documents, validates output via JSON schemas, maintains high accuracy, handles edge cases gracefully, and integrates downstream." },
};
const SCEN_BANK = [
  {"s":"s1","d":"D1","q":"本番データで、12%のケースでエージェントがget_customerを飛ばし、顧客の名乗った名前だけでlookup_orderを呼び、口座誤認と誤返金が起きている。最も効果的な対策はどれか。","qEn":"In 12% of cases the agent skips get_customer and calls lookup_order using only the customer's stated name, causing misidentified accounts and incorrect refunds. What most effectively fixes this?","o":["本人確認を必ず最初に行うよう指示する文言をsystemプロンプトに追加し、口座の誤認や誤返金が起きた場合の注意喚起と正しい手順の詳しい説明も併せて明記する","get_customerを常に最初に呼び出す正しい手順を示すfew-shot例を複数用意し、名乗った名前だけで進めてしまった失敗例も対比として加える","リクエストの種別を判定し、それぞれの状況に適したツールだけを有効化するルーティング分類器を実装して、不要なツール呼び出しを事前に抑制する","get_customerが検証済み顧客IDを返すまでlookup_orderとprocess_refundをプログラム的に遮断する前提ゲートを設ける"],"oEn":["Add wording to the system prompt instructing the agent to always perform identity verification first, and note the correct procedure and warnings for cases where accounts were misidentified or refunds issued in error","Provide multiple few-shot examples showing the correct procedure of always calling get_customer first, including contrasting failure cases that proceeded on the stated name alone","Implement a routing classifier that identifies the request type and enables only the tools suited to each situation, suppressing unnecessary tool calls in advance","Add a programmatic prerequisite that blocks lookup_order and process_refund until get_customer returns a verified customer ID"],"a":3,"e":"金銭的影響のある重要な順序制御は前提ゲートで決定的に保証する。プロンプトやfew-shotは確率的で失敗率が残り、ルーティングは順序でなく可用性の問題に対処してしまう。注意喚起の文言を足してもモデルが手順を飛ばす余地は消えず、返金のような取り返しのつかない操作では一度の失敗が損失になる。","eEn":"Critical ordering with financial impact needs deterministic prerequisite gating. Prompt/few-shot are probabilistic; routing addresses availability, not ordering. Adding warning text does not remove the chance that the model skips a step, and for irreversible operations like refunds a single failure is a real loss."},
  {"s":"s1","d":"D2","q":"get_customerとlookup_orderの説明が共に最小限（「顧客情報を取得」「注文詳細を取得」）で、注文番号付きの質問でも誤ってget_customerを呼ぶ。選択信頼性を上げる最も効果的な第一歩はどれか。","qEn":"Both tools have minimal descriptions ('Retrieves customer information'/'Retrieves order details') and the agent often calls get_customer for order queries. Best first step to improve selection reliability?","o":["両方のツールを単一のlookup_entityツールに統合して選択の余地をなくす","正しいツール選択を示すfew-shot例を5〜8個ほど用意し、注文番号を含む質問での呼び分けパターンを学習させる","各ツールの説明に入力形式・例クエリ・エッジケース・使い分け境界を加えて拡充する","利用者の入力を解析して適切なツールを事前に選び出すルーティング層を実装する"],"oEn":["Consolidate both tools into a single lookup_entity tool so there is no selection to get wrong","Add 5-8 few-shot examples of correct tool selection, teaching the calling pattern to use for queries that include an order number","Expand each tool's description with input formats, example queries, edge cases, and when-to-use boundaries","Implement a routing layer that parses user input and pre-selects the appropriate tool before the agent acts"],"a":2,"e":"ツール説明はLLMの選択の主機構。最小説明が根本原因なので、説明拡充が低労力・高レバレッジの第一歩。few-shotはトークン増、ルーティングは過剰、統合は第一歩には労力過大。説明が最小のままではfew-shotを足しても根本原因が残り、2つのツールを統合しても入力の判別が1つのツールの内側へ移るだけである。","eEn":"Tool descriptions are the primary selection mechanism. Expanding them is the low-effort, high-leverage first step; few-shot adds tokens, routing is over-engineered, consolidation is too much for a 'first step.' If descriptions stay minimal, adding few-shot examples leaves the root cause in place, and merging the two tools only moves the input disambiguation inside a single tool."},
  {"s":"s1","d":"D1","q":"エージェントの初回解決率が55%で目標80%を大きく下回る。簡単な案件（写真証拠付きの標準的な破損交換）をエスカレーションし、ポリシー例外を要する複雑案件を無理に自律処理している。最も効果的な改善はどれか。","qEn":"First-contact resolution is 55% vs an 80% target. It escalates easy cases (standard damage replacements with photo evidence) while auto-handling complex policy-exception cases. Best improvement?","o":["いつ解決しいつエスカレーションするかの明示基準とfew-shot例をsystemプロンプトに追加する","顧客メッセージの感情分析で不満の強さを測り、一定の閾値を超えたら自動でエスカレーションする","過去の対応チケットで訓練した別の分類器を用いて、案件ごとにエスカレーション要否を事前予測させる","各応答の前に確信度を1〜10で自己申告させ、設定した閾値を下回ったら自動的に人間へ引き継ぐ運用にする"],"oEn":["Add explicit escalation criteria with few-shot examples to the system prompt","Run sentiment analysis on customer messages and auto-escalate when negativity passes a threshold","Use a separate classifier trained on past tickets to predict per-case whether escalation is needed","Have the agent self-report confidence (1-10) and route to a human below a set threshold"],"a":0,"e":"根本原因は判断境界の曖昧さ。明示基準＋few-shotが比例的な第一対応。自己申告確信度は校正が悪く、分類器は過剰、感情は複雑さと無相関。不満の強さは案件の複雑さと別物で、穏やかな文面の複雑案件は自律処理に残り、強い不満を伴う簡単案件は不要にエスカレーションされる。","eEn":"Root cause is unclear decision boundaries. Explicit criteria + few-shot is the proportionate fix; self-confidence is poorly calibrated, a classifier is over-engineered, sentiment doesn't correlate with complexity. Frustration is separate from case complexity: a calmly worded complex case stays in autonomous handling while an angry but simple case is escalated needlessly."},
  {"s":"s1","d":"D1","q":"返金額が方針上限の$500を超える操作だけを確実に止めて人間へ回したい。最適な実装はどれか。","qEn":"You must reliably block only refunds over the $500 policy limit and route them to a human. Best implementation?","o":["モデルのtemperatureを下げて出力を安定させ慎重な判断を促す","送出ツール呼び出しを傍受するフックで閾値超過を検出しエスカレーションへリダイレクトする","上限を超える大きな返金を丁寧に断るfew-shot例を複数見せて判断を学習させる","systemプロンプトに『$500を超える返金は必ず承認を得ること』という指示を明記して従わせる"],"oEn":["Lower the model's temperature to stabilize outputs and encourage more cautious decisions","A hook that intercepts outgoing tool calls, detects threshold breach, and redirects to escalation","Show several few-shot examples that politely decline large refunds above the limit so the agent learns the judgment","State in the system prompt that any refund over $500 must obtain approval, and require the agent to comply"],"a":1,"e":"閾値強制のような業務ルールはツール呼び出し傍受フックで決定的に行う。プロンプトやfew-shot、temperatureは確率的で保証できない。temperatureを下げても出力が安定するだけで、$500超の操作が実行される可能性は消えない。指示文やfew-shotには、守られなかった場合に実行を止める仕組みがない。","eEn":"Threshold enforcement is a business rule best done with a deterministic tool-interception hook; prompt/few-shot/temperature are probabilistic. Lowering temperature only stabilizes output and does not remove the chance of an over-$500 operation running; prompt instructions and few-shot examples have no mechanism to block execution if ignored."},
  {"s":"s1","d":"D2","q":"process_refundがタイムアウトを返した。errorCategoryの分類と対処の正しい組み合わせはどれか。","qEn":"process_refund returns a timeout. Correct errorCategory and handling?","o":["恒久的な失敗と判断し、再試行せずその場で処理を諦める","validation と分類し、引数の形式を修正してから同じ呼び出しを再試行する","permission と分類し、再試行せず直ちに人間へエスカレーションする","transientと分類し指数バックオフ付きで上限まで再試行する"],"oEn":["Treat it as a permanent failure and give up on the spot without retrying","Classify as validation and retry the same call after fixing the argument format","Classify as permission and escalate to a human immediately without retrying","Classify as transient and retry with exponential backoff up to a limit"],"a":3,"e":"タイムアウトは一時的障害＝transient。同じ引数で待機して再試行する。validationは引数誤り、permissionは権限不足。タイムアウトを恒久的な失敗とみなして再試行せず諦めると、待てば成功し得る処理を取りこぼす。","eEn":"Timeouts are transient; retry with backoff. Validation is bad input; permission is access denial. Treating a timeout as permanent and giving up without retrying throws away an operation that could succeed after a wait."},
  {"s":"s1","d":"D5","q":"複数ターンの対話で、返金額・日付・注文番号など取引事実が逐次要約で曖昧化していく。確実に保持する設計はどれか。","qEn":"Across turns, transactional facts (amounts, dates, order numbers) get blurred by progressive summarization. How to reliably preserve them?","o":["会話履歴の要約を毎ターン細かく作り直し、その要約だけを頼りに事実を保持する","要約履歴の外に『case facts』ブロックを設け各プロンプトに含める","モデルのtemperatureを下げて出力のぶれを抑え曖昧化を防ぐ","必要になるたびにツールを呼び直して取引事実を毎回取得し直す"],"oEn":["Rebuild a detailed summary of the conversation each turn and rely on that summary alone to preserve the facts","Maintain a 'case facts' block outside summarized history, included in each prompt","Lower the model's temperature to reduce output variance and prevent the facts from blurring","Re-call the tools to re-fetch the transactional facts fresh every single time they are needed"],"a":1,"e":"取引事実はcase factsブロックとして要約の外で永続化し各プロンプトに含めると失われない。要約を毎ターン作り直すほど細部は劣化し、temperatureを下げても失われた事実は戻らない。ツールの再取得は遅延とコストを増やし、会話中に出た事実の保持にもならない。","eEn":"Persist transactional facts in a 'case facts' block outside summarization, included each prompt. Re-summarizing every turn degrades details further, lowering temperature does not restore lost facts, and re-fetching via tools adds latency and cost and does not preserve facts stated in the conversation."},
  {"s":"s1","d":"D5","q":"顧客が明示的に「人間につないでほしい」と要求した。エージェントの正しい対応はどれか。","qEn":"The customer explicitly demands a human agent. Correct behavior?","o":["調査を試みず、ただちに人間へエスカレーションする","まず自律的に解決を試み、無理だと分かった時点で人間へ回す","顧客の感情を分析してから対応方針を決める","確信度スコアを計算し、低い場合に限って人間へつなぐ"],"oEn":["Escalate to a human immediately without attempting investigation","First attempt autonomous resolution and hand off to a human only if that fails","Analyze the customer's sentiment before deciding how to respond","Compute a confidence score and connect to a human only when it is low"],"a":0,"e":"顧客の明示的な人間要求は調査を挟まず直ちに尊重する。まず自律解決を試みると顧客の明示的な要求を無視することになり、感情分析や確信度の算出も、要求が明確な場面では不要な遅れを生む。","eEn":"Honor an explicit request for a human immediately, without first investigating. Attempting autonomous resolution first ignores the customer's explicit request, and emotion analysis or confidence scoring only adds needless delay when the request is clear."},
  {"s":"s1","d":"D5","q":"lookup_orderが複数の顧客にマッチした。エージェントの正しい振る舞いはどれか。","qEn":"lookup_order returns multiple matching customers. Correct behavior?","o":["エラーとして処理を止める","先頭のレコードを採用する","ヒューリスティクスで1件に絞る","追加の識別子をユーザーに求めて明確化する"],"oEn":["Stop processing and return an error","Adopt the first record in the result set","Pick a single record using internal heuristics","Ask the user for additional identifiers to disambiguate"],"a":3,"e":"複数マッチ時は追加識別子を求める。ヒューリスティック選択は誤認のリスク。先頭レコードの採用や推測による絞り込みは別の顧客の情報を扱うおそれがあり、エラーとして止めるのは追加の識別子で解決できる状況に対して過剰である。","eEn":"On multiple matches, request more identifiers; heuristic selection risks misidentification. Taking the first record or narrowing by guesswork risks handling another customer's data, and stopping with an error is excessive when an additional identifier can resolve it."},
  {"s":"s1","d":"D1","q":"返金・アカウント問題・請求疑義を一度に訴える顧客。最適なアプローチはどれか。","qEn":"A customer raises a refund, an account issue, and a billing dispute at once. Best approach?","o":["懸念ごとに文脈を共有しない別々のセッションを立てて個別に対応する","個別項目に分解し共有文脈で各々を並行調査してから統一的な解決に統合する","顧客が最初に述べた懸念だけを処理し、残りは範囲外として扱って会話を終える","すべての懸念を一つの曖昧な指示にまとめて一括で処理させる"],"oEn":["Spin up separate sessions per concern with no shared context and handle each one in isolation","Decompose into items, investigate each in parallel with shared context, then synthesize a unified resolution","Handle only the concern raised first and end the conversation, treating the rest as out of scope","Combine all concerns into a single vague instruction and process them together in one pass"],"a":1,"e":"複数懸念は分解→共有文脈で並行調査→統一解決へ統合する。文脈を共有しない別セッションでは返金と請求疑義の関連が見えず、矛盾した対応になりうる。最初の懸念だけの処理や曖昧な一括指示は、残りの懸念を取りこぼす。","eEn":"Decompose, investigate in parallel with shared context, then synthesize one resolution. Separate sessions without shared context cannot see how the refund and billing issues relate and may give conflicting answers, while handling only the first concern or one vague bundled instruction drops the rest."},
  {"s":"s1","d":"D1","q":"人間へエスカレーションするが、相手は会話の文字起こしを参照できない。最適な引き継ぎはどれか。","qEn":"You escalate to a human who cannot see the transcript. Best handoff?","o":["顧客とのやり取りの生ログ全体を一切加工せず担当者に転送して判断を委ねる","顧客IDだけを渡し、詳細は担当者が自分で調べる前提にする","顧客ID・根本原因・返金額・推奨アクションを含む構造化サマリーを渡す","『この案件をそのまま対応してください』とだけ伝えて引き継ぐ"],"oEn":["Forward the entire raw transcript of the customer exchange unaltered and leave the judgment to the agent","Pass only the customer ID and assume the agent will look up the details themselves","A structured summary with customer ID, root cause, refund amount, recommended action","Hand off by saying only 'please handle this case as-is' with nothing more"],"a":2,"e":"文字起こしを見られない人間には、構造化された引き継ぎサマリーが必要。生ログの丸ごと転送は担当者に読み解く負担を残し、顧客IDだけの引き継ぎや「そのまま対応を」だけの依頼では、状況や根拠が伝わらず調べ直しになる。","eEn":"For a human without the transcript, compile a structured handoff summary. Forwarding the raw log leaves the agent to decode it, and passing only a customer ID or a bare 'please handle this' conveys neither the situation nor the grounds, forcing a re-investigation."},
  {"s":"s1","d":"D2","q":"あるツールが『該当データなし』と『アクセス失敗』をどちらも空配列で返す。本番で最も深刻な問題はどれか。","qEn":"A tool returns both 'no data' and 'access failure' as an empty array. Most serious production problem?","o":["認証処理が二重に走ってしまい余計なコストが発生する","返される結果が常に大きすぎて文脈窓を圧迫してしまう","tool_choiceによるツールの強制指定が正しく効かなくなる","失敗を成功と誤認し、必要な再試行やエスカレーションが発火しない"],"oEn":["Authentication runs twice, incurring unnecessary extra cost","The returned results are always too large and overflow the context","Forcing a specific tool via tool_choice stops working correctly","Failure is mistaken for success, so needed retries/escalation never fire"],"a":3,"e":"空成功への偽装で回復処理が起動しない。構造化エラーで区別する。認証の二重実行によるコスト、結果の肥大化、tool_choiceの不具合は、空配列で失敗と該当なしの区別がつかなくなる問題とは別の話である。","eEn":"Disguising failure as empty success prevents recovery; distinguish with structured errors. Duplicate authentication cost, oversized results, and tool_choice misbehavior are separate matters from the inability to tell failure from an empty result when both return an empty array."},
  {"s":"s1","d":"D2","q":"返金額が方針上限超の業務エラーを、エージェントが顧客へ適切に伝えられるようにツールが返すべきものはどれか。","qEn":"For a business-rule violation (over-limit refund), what should the tool return so the agent can communicate well?","o":["例外を内部で完全に握りつぶし、処理が成功したかのような応答を返す","retriable: false と顧客向けの分かりやすい説明を含む構造化エラー","エラーの種別や原因を区別せず、一律の『処理に失敗しました』という汎用メッセージを返す","データが存在しない場合と全く同じように空の配列をそのまま返す"],"oEn":["An internally swallowed exception with a response that looks as if it succeeded","A structured error with retriable: false and a customer-friendly explanation","A generic 'operation failed' message that ignores the error type or cause, returned uniformly","The same empty array returned exactly as when no matching data exists"],"a":1,"e":"業務エラーはretriable:falseと顧客向け説明を含めて返す。例外の握りつぶしや汎用メッセージ、空配列では、顧客に伝えるべき理由が失われ、再試行しても無意味であることも判断できない。","eEn":"Return business errors with retriable:false and a customer-friendly explanation. Swallowing the exception, a generic message, or an empty array loses the reason to tell the customer and gives no signal that retrying is pointless."},
  {"s":"s2","d":"D3","q":"チームの標準レビューを実行する /review スラッシュコマンドを、clone/pullした全開発者が使えるようにしたい。どこに作るか。","qEn":"You want a /review slash command running the team checklist, available to every developer on clone/pull. Where do you create it?","o":["プロジェクトルートに置く CLAUDE.md ファイル内","プロジェクトの .claude/commands/ ディレクトリ",".claude/config.json の commands 配列に定義する","各開発者のホームにある ~/.claude/commands/ ディレクトリ"],"oEn":["Inside the CLAUDE.md file at the project root","The project's .claude/commands/ directory","A commands array defined in .claude/config.json","Each developer's home ~/.claude/commands/ directory"],"a":1,"e":"プロジェクトスコープのコマンドは.claude/commands/に置き、VCSで全員へ共有される。他は個人用・指示用・存在しない仕組み。~/.claude/commands/は各開発者のホーム内にありcloneやpullでは共有されない。CLAUDE.mdは指示を書く場所でコマンドの定義先ではなく、config.jsonのcommands配列という仕組みもない（2026年10月時点）。","eEn":"Project-scoped commands live in .claude/commands/ and are shared via VCS; others are personal, for instructions, or nonexistent. ~/.claude/commands/ lives in each developer's home directory and is not shared by clone or pull, CLAUDE.md holds instructions rather than command definitions, and there is no commands array in config.json (as of October 2026)."},
  {"s":"s2","d":"D3","q":"モノリスをマイクロサービスへ再構成する（多数ファイルに影響、サービス境界の判断が必要）。最適な進め方はどれか。","qEn":"You must restructure a monolith into microservices (dozens of files, service-boundary decisions). Best approach?","o":["プランモードで探索・依存理解・設計を行ってから変更する","直接実行で少しずつ変更しながらサービス境界を自然に発見する","直接実行で始め、複雑になった段階でプランモードへ切り替える","構造を最初に全指定した包括的な指示を渡して直接実行する"],"oEn":["Enter plan mode to explore, understand dependencies, and design before changing","Use direct execution, changing bit by bit and discovering service boundaries naturally along the way","Start with direct execution and switch to plan mode once it becomes complex","Pass comprehensive up-front instructions that fully specify the structure and execute directly"],"a":0,"e":"大規模・多アプローチ・アーキ判断はプランモード。直接実行は手戻りリスク、複雑さは要件に既に明示されている。サービス境界の判断を後回しにして直接実行で進めると、多数のファイルに及ぶ変更をやり直す事態になりやすい。包括的な指示でも、探索の前に構造を決め打ちする点は変わらない。","eEn":"Large-scale, multi-approach, architectural work calls for plan mode; direct execution risks rework, and the complexity is already stated. Postponing the service-boundary decision and proceeding by direct execution invites redoing changes across many files, and a comprehensive instruction still fixes the structure before any exploration."},
  {"s":"s2","d":"D3","q":"領域別に異なる規約があり、テストファイルは各コードの隣に散在する。場所に依らず全テストへ同じ規約を自動適用したい。最も保守的な方法はどれか。","qEn":"Different areas have different conventions; test files are scattered next to code. You want all tests to follow one convention regardless of location. Most maintainable?","o":["テストファイルが置かれている各サブディレクトリに個別の CLAUDE.md をそれぞれ配置して管理する","コードの種別ごとに対応する規約を記した SKILL.md を持つ専用スキルをそれぞれ用意して適用する","ルートの CLAUDE.md に領域ごとの見出しを設け、そこにすべてのテスト規約をまとめて記述し、場所を問わず一律に適用されるよう管理する",".claude/rules/ にYAMLフロントマターのglobパターン（**/*.test.tsx）で条件適用するルールを作る"],"oEn":["Place a separate CLAUDE.md in each subdirectory that holds test files and manage them individually","Create a dedicated skill per code type, each with a SKILL.md that records the matching conventions, and apply them","In the root CLAUDE.md, add per-area headings and gather all test conventions under them to apply uniformly everywhere","Create .claude/rules/ files with YAML glob patterns (**/*.test.tsx) for conditional application"],"a":3,"e":"散在テストにはglobパターンのパス別ルールが最適。CLAUDE.mdは推論依存・ディレクトリ束縛、スキルは手動呼び出しで自動適用にならない。テストの隣へCLAUDE.mdを置くと同じ規約を場所ごとに複製することになり、ルートのCLAUDE.mdに一括記載すると該当しないコードの作業でも常に読み込まれる。","eEn":"Scattered tests need glob-pattern path rules; CLAUDE.md relies on inference and is directory-bound, skills require manual invocation. Placing CLAUDE.md next to each test duplicates the same convention per location, and putting everything in the root CLAUDE.md loads the rules even when working on unrelated code."},
  {"s":"s2","d":"D3","q":"単一ファイルのバグ修正で、明確なスタックトレースがある。最適な進め方はどれか。","qEn":"A single-file bug fix with a clear stack trace. Best approach?","o":["直接実行","計画フェーズ","並列処理","投票方式"],"oEn":["Direct execution","Planning phase","Parallel passes","Voting scheme"],"a":0,"e":"スコープが明確な単純変更は直接実行。プランモードは過剰。並列処理や投票方式は、独立した複数作業の分担や複数案の比較に使う手法で、原因が特定できている単一ファイルの修正では手間が増えるだけである。","eEn":"A clear, well-scoped change calls for direct execution; plan mode is overkill. Parallel processing and voting are for splitting independent work or comparing several candidates, and for a single-file fix with a known cause they only add overhead."},
  {"s":"s2","d":"D3","q":"巨大なCLAUDE.mdを整理したい。推奨される方法はどれか。","qEn":"You want to organize a large CLAUDE.md. Recommended?","o":["内容を細かく分割せず、すべての規約をこれまで通り一つの CLAUDE.md ファイルにまとめて記述し続け、肥大化しても分割はせず今後もそのままの運用を維持する方針とする","肥大化した CLAUDE.md を思い切って全て削除し、必要な指示はその都度プロンプトで直接渡す運用に切り替える方針とする","ファイルそのものは一切分割せず、肥大化した CLAUDE.md の中身をコメント行で見出しごとに区切って整理し続ける運用にする",".claude/rules/ にトピック別ファイル（testing.md, api-conventions.md, deployment.md）として分割する"],"oEn":["Keep all conventions in one CLAUDE.md as before, and even as it grows leave it unsplit and keep that arrangement","Boldly delete the bloated CLAUDE.md entirely and switch to passing any needed instructions directly in each prompt","Don't split the file at all; keep organizing the bloated CLAUDE.md by separating sections with comment lines","Split into topic files under .claude/rules/ (testing.md, api-conventions.md, deployment.md)"],"a":3,"e":"モノリシックなCLAUDE.mdはトピック別ファイルへ分割すると保守しやすい。一つのファイルのまま置き続けても、コメントで区切っても、毎回すべてが読み込まれる構造は変わらない。全削除すると共有すべき規約が失われ、毎回プロンプトで渡す手間が生じる。","eEn":"Split a monolithic CLAUDE.md into topic-specific files for maintainability. Keeping it as one file or dividing it with comments still loads everything every time, and deleting it all loses shared conventions and forces them into every prompt."},
  {"s":"s2","d":"D5","q":"対話セッションが長引き精度低下・コスト増した。最適な対処はどれか。","qEn":"A long session shows degraded accuracy and rising cost. Best response?","o":["要約して新セッション開始、または /clear で文脈リセット","モデルのtemperatureを上げて多様な出力を促す","利用できるツールをさらに追加して能力を補おうとする","何も対処せずそのまま放置し、同じ長いセッションのまま作業を続行する"],"oEn":["Summarize and start fresh, or /clear to reset context","Raise the model's temperature to encourage more varied output","Add more available tools to make up for the capability","Do nothing and keep working in the same long session"],"a":0,"e":"履歴肥大は精度低下とコスト増を招く。要約しての再開や/clearが対処。temperatureを上げても履歴の肥大は解消せず、ツールを増やすと選択精度が落ちて入力も増える。放置すれば精度低下とコスト増が続く。","eEn":"Bloated history hurts accuracy and cost; summarize-and-restart or /clear. Raising temperature does not shrink the bloated history, adding tools lowers selection accuracy and increases input, and doing nothing leaves the accuracy loss and cost growth in place."},
  {"s":"s2","d":"D3","q":"編集のたびにフォーマットとテストを『確実に』実行させたい。プロンプト依頼では時々スキップされる。最も確実な手段はどれか。","qEn":"You want format+test to run on every edit reliably; prompting sometimes skips. Most reliable?","o":["PostToolUse等のフックでイベント駆動の決定的強制として自動実行する","編集専用のスラッシュコマンドを用意し、編集のたびに開発者が忘れず手動で実行する","プランモードで実行計画を立てたうえで毎回手動で流すようにする","CLAUDE.md に『編集後は必ず実行せよ』と強調して記載する"],"oEn":["Use a hook (e.g., PostToolUse) for deterministic, event-driven enforcement","Create a slash command and have the developer run it manually after every edit","Draw up an execution plan in plan mode and then run it manually every time","In CLAUDE.md, emphatically state 'always run this after editing'"],"a":0,"e":"必須処理の確実な実行はフックで決定的に強制する。コマンドは手動、CLAUDE.md記述は依頼に留まる。手動で毎回実行する運用は、忘れたときに防げない。CLAUDE.mdで強調してもプロンプトと同じ依頼にすぎず、スキップされる可能性は残る。","eEn":"Guaranteed mandatory steps need a hook for deterministic enforcement; commands are manual, CLAUDE.md text is just a request. A manual run each time cannot prevent forgetting, and emphasizing it in CLAUDE.md is still just a request, as with the prompt, so skipping remains possible."},
  {"s":"s2","d":"D3","q":"新メンバーがチームの指示を受け取れない。最も疑うべき原因はどれか。","qEn":"A new teammate isn't receiving team instructions. Most likely cause?","o":["会話の履歴が長くなりすぎたため、初期に与えた指示が文脈から抜け落ちている","指示がプロジェクトレベルでなくユーザーレベル（~/.claude/CLAUDE.md）にある","モデルのtemperatureが低く設定されているため、与えた指示が出力に反映されにくくなっている","有効化されているツールが多すぎて、指示が埋もれて届かなくなっている"],"oEn":["The conversation history has grown too long, so early instructions dropped out of context","Instructions are at user level (~/.claude/CLAUDE.md), not project level","The model's temperature is set too low, so the given instructions barely affect the output","Too many tools are enabled, so the instructions get buried and never reach the model"],"a":1,"e":"ユーザーレベルの設定は個人にしか適用されずVCSで共有されない。チーム共有はプロジェクトレベルへ。新メンバーのセッションは履歴が新しいため文脈からの脱落ではなく、temperatureの設定やツールの多さも、指示が届くかどうかとは関係しない。","eEn":"User-level settings apply only to that user and aren't shared via VCS; team config belongs at project level. A new member's session has fresh history, so it is not context loss, and temperature or the number of tools has no bearing on whether instructions reach the model."},
  {"s":"s2","d":"D3","q":"冗長な出力を出すスキル（コードベース解析）を主会話から隔離したい。最適なフロントマター設定はどれか。","qEn":"You want a verbose skill (codebase analysis) isolated from the main conversation. Best frontmatter?","o":["context: shared に設定して主会話と文脈を共有する","context: fork で隔離サブエージェント文脈で実行する","argument-hint を付けて引数の入力例を提示する","allowed-tools の項目を空にしてスキルが使えるツールを制限する"],"oEn":["Set context: shared to share context with the main conversation","context: fork to run in an isolated subagent context","Add an argument-hint to show example input for the arguments","Empty the allowed-tools field to restrict the tools the skill can use"],"a":1,"e":"context: forkは隔離サブ文脈で実行し、出力が主会話を汚さない。context: sharedという設定はなく、argument-hintは引数の入力例を示すだけで、allowed-toolsは使えるツールの制限であり、いずれも出力を主会話から隔離しない（2026年10月時点）。","eEn":"context: fork runs in an isolated context so output doesn't pollute the main session. There is no context: shared setting, argument-hint only shows example arguments, and allowed-tools only restricts available tools; none of them isolates output from the main conversation (as of October 2026)."},
  {"s":"s2","d":"D5","q":"多段タスクで冗長な発見フェーズにより文脈窓が枯渇しそうだ。最適な手段はどれか。","qEn":"A multi-phase task risks context exhaustion from a verbose discovery phase. Best tool?","o":["Exploreサブエージェントで発見出力を隔離し要約を返す","モデルのtemperatureを上げて探索を効率化する","会話履歴により多くの情報を追加して文脈を厚くしていく","発見フェーズで得た全出力をそのまま主会話の履歴に残し続ける"],"oEn":["Use the Explore subagent to isolate discovery output and return summaries","Raise the model's temperature to make the exploration more efficient","Add more information to the conversation history to thicken the context","Keep all output from the discovery phase in the main conversation's history as-is"],"a":0,"e":"Exploreサブエージェントは冗長な発見出力を隔離し要約を返して文脈枯渇を防ぐ。発見出力を履歴にそのまま残し続けたり、情報をさらに足したりすると窓の枯渇が早まる。temperatureを上げても探索の効率は変わらない。","eEn":"The Explore subagent isolates verbose discovery and returns summaries to preserve context. Leaving all discovery output in the history or adding more information exhausts the window sooner, and raising temperature does not make exploration more efficient."},
  {"s":"s3","d":"D1","q":"「AIが創造産業に与える影響」を調査したが、各サブエージェントは成功しているのに最終レポートが視覚芸術のみを扱い、音楽・執筆・映画を欠いた。コーディネーターのログは「デジタルアート」「グラフィックデザイン」「写真」の3サブタスクへ分解していた。最も可能性の高い根本原因はどれか。","qEn":"Researching 'AI's impact on creative industries,' each subagent succeeds but the report covers only visual arts, missing music, writing, film. The coordinator decomposed into 'digital art,' 'graphic design,' 'photography.' Most likely root cause?","o":["文書分析が厳しすぎる関連性の基準で結果を過剰にフィルタしている","コーディネーターの分解が狭すぎ、関連領域を網羅しないサブタスク割当になっている","最終レポートを統合するエージェントに、抜けや欠落を検出するための指示が与えられていない","Web検索サブエージェントの検索クエリが網羅的になっていない"],"oEn":["Document analysis over-filters the results using an overly strict relevance bar","The coordinator's decomposition is too narrow, missing relevant domains","The agent that synthesizes the final report was given no instructions to detect gaps or omissions","The web-search subagent's search queries are not comprehensive"],"a":1,"e":"各サブが割当内で正常なら、偏りは分解の狭さが原因。下流エージェントを責めるのは誤り。ログでは3つのサブタスクがすべて視覚芸術に偏っており、文書分析のフィルタや検索クエリ、統合側の指示を直しても、そもそも割り当てられていない音楽・執筆・映画は拾えない。","eEn":"With subagents working within scope, the gap stems from narrow decomposition, not downstream agents. The log shows all three subtasks confined to visual arts, so fixing the document-analysis filter, the search queries, or the synthesis instructions cannot recover music, writing, and film that were never assigned."},
  {"s":"s3","d":"D5","q":"Web検索サブエージェントがタイムアウトした。コーディネーターの知的回復を可能にする最善のエラー伝播はどれか。","qEn":"The web-search subagent times out. Best error propagation for intelligent coordinator recovery?","o":["失敗種別・試行クエリ・部分結果・代替案を含む構造化エラー文脈を返す","空の結果を成功として扱いコーディネーターへそのまま返す","例外を最上位まで投げてワークフロー全体を終了させる","指数バックオフで数回再試行した後、原因を示さない汎用の『検索不可』を返す"],"oEn":["Return structured error context: failure type, attempted query, partial results, alternatives","Treat the empty result as a success and return it to the coordinator as-is","Throw the exception up to the top level and terminate the entire workflow","Retry with exponential backoff a few times, then return a generic 'search unavailable' with no cause"],"a":0,"e":"構造化エラー文脈で再試行・代替・部分結果続行を判断できる。汎用は文脈を隠し、空成功は回復を妨げ、全終了は過剰。再試行後に原因を示さない汎用の「検索不可」を返すと、コーディネーターは代替クエリや部分結果での続行を判断する材料を持てない。","eEn":"Structured error context enables recovery decisions; generic hides context, empty-success blocks recovery, termination is excessive. Returning a generic 'search unavailable' after retries gives the coordinator nothing to judge alternative queries or continuing with partial results."},
  {"s":"s3","d":"D2","q":"統合エージェントが頻繁に簡単な事実確認（日付・名前・統計）を要し、毎回コーディネーター経由で40%遅延する。85%は単純、15%は深い調査。最適策はどれか。","qEn":"The synthesis agent often needs simple fact-checks (dates, names, stats), adding 40% latency via coordinator round-trips. 85% simple, 15% deep. Best approach?","o":["検証が必要になった項目はすべて末尾にまとめておき、処理の最後にまとめてバッチで一括確認し、不足があれば補うようにする","統合エージェントに範囲限定の verify_fact ツールを与え、複雑な検証のみコーディネーター経由を維持する","統合エージェントにすべてのWeb検索ツールをそのまま与えて自由に呼び出せるようにする","Web検索側があらかじめすべての余分な文脈を大量にキャッシュしておき、統合の段階に十分備えておく"],"oEn":["Batch all items needing verification at the end and confirm them together in one pass at the very end, filling any gaps","Give the synthesis agent a scoped verify_fact tool; keep complex verification via the coordinator","Give the synthesis agent all the web-search tools as-is and let it call them freely","Have the web-search side pre-cache lots of extra context in advance to prepare for the synthesis stage"],"a":1,"e":"最小権限の原則。85%の単純ケースに範囲限定ツールを与え、複雑ケースは既存パターンを維持。全付与は責務分離違反、バッチはブロッキング依存、投機キャッシュは予測不能。大量の文脈を事前にキャッシュしても、統合時にどの日付や名前を確認するかは事前に分からず、当たらない分は無駄になる。","eEn":"Least privilege: scoped tool for the 85% common case, coordinator for complex ones. Full access breaks separation; batching blocks; speculative caching can't predict needs. Pre-caching lots of context cannot predict which dates or names will need checking during synthesis, so what misses is wasted."},
  {"s":"s3","d":"D1","q":"独立したサブエージェントを同時に走らせたい。最適な起動方法はどれか。","qEn":"You want independent subagents to run concurrently. Best way to launch?","o":["モデルのtemperatureを上げて並行して動かそうとする","それぞれのターンを分けて、サブエージェントを一つずつ順番に起動していく","各サブエージェントを直列にチェイニングしてつないでいく","1つのコーディネーター応答内で複数のTaskツール呼び出しを発行する"],"oEn":["Raise the model's temperature to try to run them concurrently","Split into separate turns and launch the subagents one at a time in order","Chain each subagent sequentially, connecting them one after another","Emit multiple Task tool calls in a single coordinator response"],"a":3,"e":"並列起動は単一応答内で複数Task呼び出しを発行する。ターン分割は直列化を招く。temperatureはサンプリングの設定で並行実行とは無関係である。サブエージェントを一つずつ起動したり直列にチェイニングしたりすると、独立した処理を待たせることになる。","eEn":"Parallelism comes from multiple Task calls in one response; separate turns serialize. Temperature is a sampling setting unrelated to concurrency, and launching subagents one at a time or chaining them serially makes independent work wait."},
  {"s":"s3","d":"D1","q":"サブエージェントへ前段のWeb検索・文書分析結果を渡したい。正しい方法はどれか。","qEn":"You must pass prior web-search and document-analysis findings to a subagent. Correct method?","o":["モデルのtemperatureを上げて内容を推測させる","前段の結果をsystemプロンプトに焼き込んで渡す","文脈は自動的に継承されるので、特に何も渡さずそのまま実行する","前段の完全な所見をサブエージェントのプロンプトに直接含める"],"oEn":["Raise the model's temperature and let it infer the content","Bake the prior stage's results into the system prompt and pass them that way","Context is inherited automatically, so run it as-is without passing anything","Include the complete prior findings directly in the subagent's prompt"],"a":3,"e":"サブエージェントは文脈を自動継承しないため明示的に含める。何も渡さなければ前段の所見は届かず、temperatureを上げて推測させても事実は復元できない。systemプロンプトへの焼き込みは、タスクごとに変わる所見の受け渡し方として適さない。","eEn":"Subagents don't inherit context automatically; include findings explicitly. Without explicit passing, earlier findings never arrive, raising temperature to make the model guess cannot restore facts, and baking them into the system prompt is unsuitable for findings that change per task."},
  {"s":"s3","d":"D5","q":"統合段で出典帰属を保つにはサブエージェントの出力をどう設計するか。","qEn":"To preserve attribution through synthesis, how should subagent output be designed?","o":["出典の情報は省略し、要約された主張の内容だけをまとめて下流へ渡す","構造化claim-sourceマッピング（URL・文書名・抜粋）を出力し下流が保持する","モデルのtemperatureを下げて出力される帰属を安定させる","各サブエージェントが根拠となった文書の全文を一切加工せずそのまま下流の統合段へ渡していく"],"oEn":["Omit the source information and pass only the summarized claims downstream together","Output structured claim-source mappings (URL, doc name, excerpt) preserved downstream","Lower the model's temperature to stabilize the attribution in the output","Have each subagent pass the full text of the source documents downstream to synthesis, entirely unmodified"],"a":1,"e":"構造化claim-sourceマッピングを出力し統合を通じて保持する。出典を省くと帰属が失われ、temperatureを下げても帰属は安定しない。根拠の全文をそのまま渡すと下流の文脈を圧迫し、どの主張がどの出典に基づくかも対応づけられない。","eEn":"Emit structured claim-source mappings preserved through synthesis. Omitting sources loses attribution, lowering temperature does not stabilize attribution, and passing full source text unprocessed burdens the downstream context without mapping which claim rests on which source."},
  {"s":"s3","d":"D5","q":"信頼できる複数ソースで統計値が矛盾した。正しい扱いはどれか。","qEn":"Credible sources report conflicting statistics. Correct handling?","o":["一方の値を誤りとみなして削除する","複数の値の平均を取って一つにまとめる","出典付きで矛盾を注記し、恣意的に1値を選ばない","最も新しい値を正しいものとして採用し一つに統一する"],"oEn":["Treat one of the conflicting values as an error and delete it","Take the average of the multiple values and merge into one","Annotate the conflict with attribution; don't arbitrarily pick one","Adopt the newest value as the correct one and unify to a single figure"],"a":2,"e":"矛盾は出典付きで注記し恣意的選択を避け、調停判断を委ねる。一方を誤りとして削除したり平均で一つにまとめたりすると、実在しない数値や恣意的な選択が混じる。最新値への統一も、測定方法や対象期間の違いによる矛盾を見えなくする。","eEn":"Annotate conflicts with attribution rather than arbitrarily selecting. Deleting one value or averaging them introduces an invented number or arbitrary choice, and unifying to the newest value hides contradictions caused by differing measurement methods or periods."},
  {"s":"s3","d":"D1","q":"コーディネーターが常に全パイプライン（検索→分析→統合→生成）を経由し、単純質問でも遅く高コスト。改善策はどれか。","qEn":"The coordinator always runs the full pipeline, slow and costly even for simple queries. Improvement?","o":["利用するサブエージェントの数をさらに増やして対応する","モデルのtemperatureを下げて処理を高速化する","単純な質問でも、常にすべてのサブエージェントを並列で起動する","クエリ要件を分析し必要なサブエージェントのみ動的に選択して呼び出す"],"oEn":["Respond by increasing the number of subagents used even further","Lower the model's temperature to speed up the processing","Always launch every subagent in parallel, even for simple queries","Analyze query requirements and dynamically select only needed subagents"],"a":3,"e":"コーディネーターはクエリの複雑さを評価し必要なサブエージェントだけ動的に選ぶ。サブエージェントを増やしたり、常に全員を並列起動したりすると、単純な質問でも不要な処理が増えてコストはさらに膨らむ。temperatureは処理経路の長さとは無関係である。","eEn":"The coordinator should assess complexity and dynamically select only needed subagents. Adding subagents or always launching all of them in parallel adds unneeded work even for simple questions and raises cost further, and temperature has no bearing on the length of the processing path."},
  {"s":"s3","d":"D5","q":"統合出力でカバレッジを明示するにはどうするか。","qEn":"How to make coverage explicit in synthesis output?","o":["全所見について情報源の件数を集計し件数が多い順にランク付けして提示する","どの所見が十分裏付けられ、どの領域が情報源不足でギャップかを注記する","最も確信度の高い所見だけを抽出し他は省略して簡潔に示す","各所見に長さを揃えた要約を付与し全体を均一な粒度で並べる"],"oEn":["Aggregate the count of sources per finding and present them ranked from most to fewest","Annotate which findings are well-supported vs which areas have gaps from unavailable sources","Extract only the highest-confidence findings and omit the rest for a concise summary","Attach uniform-length summaries to every finding and list them at a single granularity"],"a":1,"e":"統合出力にカバレッジ注記を付け、裏付けの強弱とギャップを明示する。情報源の件数順ランキングは件数が多いだけの所見を優先し、確信度の高い所見だけに絞ると不足領域が見えなくなる。均一な粒度の要約も裏付けの強弱を隠す。","eEn":"Add coverage annotations distinguishing well-supported findings from gaps. Ranking by source count favors findings that merely have many sources, keeping only high-confidence findings hides gaps, and uniform-granularity summaries conceal how strong the support is."},
  {"s":"s3","d":"D1","q":"研究範囲をサブエージェント間で分担し重複を最小化したい。最善の設計はどれか。","qEn":"You want to partition research scope across subagents to minimize duplication. Best design?","o":["全エージェントに全範囲を広く探索させ最後に結果の重複を排除する","各エージェントに同一の情報源を割り当て回答を多数決で選ぶ","オーケストレーターが全サブタスクを順番に一つずつ処理する","各エージェントに異なるサブトピックや情報源タイプを割り当てる"],"oEn":["Have every agent explore the full scope broadly and dedupe results at the end","Give every agent the same sources and pick the answer by majority vote","Let the orchestrator process all subtasks sequentially one at a time","Assign distinct subtopics or source types to each agent"],"a":3,"e":"重複を最小化するにはサブトピック・情報源タイプを明示分割する。全員に全範囲を探索させる方法や同じ情報源を多数決する方法は、作業の重複をむしろ前提にしている。順番に一つずつ処理する方法は分担そのものにならない。","eEn":"Minimize duplication by assigning distinct subtopics/source types. Having everyone explore the full scope or voting over the same sources presupposes duplicated work, and processing subtasks one by one is not a division of labor at all."},
  {"s":"s4","d":"D2","q":"コードベースを効率よく理解する進め方はどれか。","qEn":"Best way to build codebase understanding efficiently?","o":["READMEと設定ファイルだけを読み全体のアーキテクチャを推測して進める","各ファイルの行数を数えて大きい順に上位のファイルから内容を確認していく","ディレクトリ構造をGlobで一覧化してから主要な拡張子のファイルを端から順番に開いて内容を読む","Grepで入口を見つけ、Readでimportを辿り流れを追う（全ファイル一括読みしない）"],"oEn":["Read only the README and config files, then infer the overall architecture from them","Count each file's line length and review the largest files first, working down the list","List the directory tree with Glob, then open and read files of the main extensions one by one from the top","Grep for entry points, then Read to follow imports and trace flows (not reading all files upfront)"],"a":3,"e":"段階的にGrepで入口特定→Readで追跡が効率的。一括読みは文脈を浪費。READMEからの推測は実装と食い違うことがあり、行数の多いファイルが重要とは限らない。Globで列挙した順に端から開く方法は、無関係なファイルで文脈を消費する。","eEn":"Incrementally Grep for entry points then Read to trace; bulk reading wastes context. Guessing from the README may diverge from the implementation, large files are not necessarily important, and opening files in Glob order consumes context on irrelevant ones."},
  {"s":"s4","d":"D2","q":"Editが一意なテキストを見つけられず失敗した。信頼できる代替はどれか。","qEn":"Edit fails on a non-unique text match. Reliable fallback?","o":["sedコマンドを使って行番号を指定し該当行を書き換える","Read + Write で全体を読み込んで書き換える","replace_allフラグを付けて一致箇所を全て置換する","より長い前後の文脈を含めて一意になるように置換対象を指定し直す"],"oEn":["Use sed to target the line number and rewrite that line","Read + Write to load and rewrite the file","Add the replace_all flag to replace every matching occurrence","Include more surrounding context so the target match becomes unique"],"a":1,"e":"Editが一意マッチを得られない場合、Read+Writeが信頼できるフォールバック。sedで行番号を指定する方法は行のずれで別の行を書き換えるおそれがあり、replace_allは一致した全箇所を書き換えてしまう。文脈を長くして再指定するのは同じEditの延長で、一意なアンカーが取れない状況では解決にならない。","eEn":"When Edit lacks a unique anchor, Read+Write is the reliable fallback. Specifying line numbers with sed risks rewriting the wrong line if lines shift, replace_all rewrites every match, and re-specifying with longer context is still Edit, which does not help when no unique anchor exists."},
  {"s":"s4","d":"D2","q":"GrepとGlobの使い分けとして正しいのはどれか。","qEn":"Correct distinction between Grep and Glob?","o":["GrepもGlobも同様にファイル内容を対象に検索し結果を行単位で返す","Grepは内容検索（関数名・エラー文字列）、Globはパスパターン一致（ファイル名・拡張子）","Grepはファイルパスのパターン一致を行い、Globはファイル内容を対象に全文検索を実行して返す","GrepもGlobもファイル名やパスのパターン一致だけを行い内容は見ない"],"oEn":["Both Grep and Glob search file contents alike and return their results on a line-by-line basis","Grep searches contents (function names, error strings); Glob matches path patterns (names, extensions)","Grep matches file path patterns while Glob performs full-text search over file contents","Both Grep and Glob only match file name and path patterns and never inspect file contents"],"a":1,"e":"Grepは内容検索、Globはパスパターン一致。両方が内容を検索する、両方がパスだけを見る、という説明はどちらも片方の機能を落としている。Grepがパス一致でGlobが全文検索という説明は役割が逆である。","eEn":"Grep is content search; Glob is path-pattern matching. Saying both search content, or both look only at paths, drops one tool's function, and describing Grep as path matching and Glob as full-text search reverses their roles."},
  {"s":"s4","d":"D2","q":"高機能なMCP（Model Context Protocol）ツールより組み込みのGrepが好まれてしまう。是正策はどれか。","qEn":"The agent prefers built-in Grep over a more capable MCP (Model Context Protocol) tool. Fix?","o":["MCPツールの説明を強化し能力と出力を詳細に説明する","システムプロンプトでMCPツールを優先せよと強く指示する","MCPツールの入力スキーマを簡素化して引数を減らす","組み込みのGrepツールを無効化してMCPツールだけを残す"],"oEn":["Enhance the MCP tool's description to detail capabilities and outputs","Instruct in the system prompt to strongly prefer the MCP tool","Simplify the MCP tool's input schema to reduce its arguments","Disable the built-in Grep tool and leave only the MCP tool available"],"a":0,"e":"MCPツール説明を詳細化すれば組み込みより適切に選ばれる。システムプロンプトでの強い優先指示は説明の不足を補わず、スキーマの簡素化は選択の根拠を増やさない。Grepの無効化は選択の問題を避けるだけで、組み込みツールの有用な機能も失う。","eEn":"Detailing the MCP tool's description makes it preferred over built-ins. A strongly worded priority instruction in the system prompt does not make up for a thin description, simplifying the schema adds no basis for selection, and disabling Grep avoids the selection problem while also losing a useful built-in."},
  {"s":"s4","d":"D2","q":"探索的なツール呼び出しを減らすため、課題サマリーや文書階層・DBスキーマをエージェントに見せたい。最適なMCP（Model Context Protocol）要素はどれか。","qEn":"To cut exploratory tool calls, you want to expose issue summaries, doc hierarchies, DB schemas. Best MCP (Model Context Protocol) element?","o":["ルート（作業ディレクトリの宣言）","MCPリソース（コンテンツカタログの公開）","MCPプロンプト（再利用可能なテンプレート）","サンプリング（モデル呼び出し委譲）"],"oEn":["Roots (declaring accessible directories)","MCP resources (exposing content catalogs)","MCP prompts (reusable templates)","Sampling (delegating model calls to the client)"],"a":1,"e":"MCPリソースは読み取り中心でカタログを公開し探索的呼び出しを減らす。ルートは作業ディレクトリの範囲の宣言、プロンプトは再利用できるテンプレート、サンプリングはサーバーからのモデル呼び出しの依頼であり、課題サマリーやスキーマのカタログを公開する要素ではない。","eEn":"MCP resources expose catalogs to reduce exploratory tool calls. Roots declare working directory scope, prompts are reusable templates, and sampling lets a server request a model call; none of them publishes a catalog such as issue summaries or schemas."},
  {"s":"s4","d":"D1","q":"共有のコードベース分析を基点に、2つの異なるリファクタリング方針を並行検討したい。最適な手段はどれか。","qEn":"From a shared codebase analysis, you want to explore two refactoring approaches in parallel. Best mechanism?","o":["conversation_idを共有し両方針を1つの履歴に交互に書き込む","毎回まっさらな新規セッションを開始し分析を最初からやり直す","fork_sessionで共有ベースラインから独立ブランチを作る","同一セッションを--resumeで再開し方針を順番に試す"],"oEn":["Share a conversation_id and interleave both approaches into one history","Start a fresh new session each time and redo the analysis from scratch","fork_session to branch independently from a shared baseline","--resume the same session and try each approach in turn"],"a":2,"e":"fork_sessionは共有ベースラインから独立ブランチを作り発散探索に向く。1つの履歴に交互に書くと2つの方針が混ざり、毎回新規セッションにすると共有の分析をやり直すことになる。--resumeで順番に試すと、前の方針の履歴が次に残る。","eEn":"fork_session branches from a shared baseline for divergent exploration. Writing alternately into one history mixes the two approaches, starting a fresh session each time redoes the shared analysis, and trying them in turn with --resume leaves the first approach's history in the second."},
  {"s":"s4","d":"D3","q":"権限を事前許可する際、破壊的操作の扱いとして最適なのはどれか。","qEn":"When pre-authorizing permissions, best handling of destructive operations?","o":["読み取りも書き込みも含め全操作に毎回手動承認を求める","読み取りは広く自動許可、書き込みは絞り、破壊的操作は承認必須","破壊的操作を含む全ての操作を事前にまとめて自動許可に設定する","操作の種類は区別せず実行のたびにランダムに許可を判定する"],"oEn":["Require manual approval on every operation, including reads and writes","Auto-allow reads broadly, scope writes, require approval for destructive ops","Auto-allow every operation upfront in one batch, including destructive ones","Ignore the operation type and decide each permission at random per call"],"a":1,"e":"リスクの非対称性に応じ配分する。一律自動許可は危険、一律承認は非効率。実行のたびにランダムに許可を判定する方法は、同じ操作でも結果が変わり、安全を保証する根拠にならない。","eEn":"Allocate by risk asymmetry; blanket auto-allow is risky, blanket approval is inefficient. Deciding permission at random each time gives different outcomes for the same operation, so it offers no basis for safety."},
  {"s":"s4","d":"D1","q":"レガシーコードベースに包括的なテストを追加する開放的タスク。最適な分解はどれか。","qEn":"Open-ended task: add comprehensive tests to a legacy codebase. Best decomposition?","o":["複数エージェントに同じテストを書かせ多数決で最終版を選ぶ","構造を把握し高インパクト領域を特定し、依存発見に応じて適応する動的分解","テストの作成を固定の直列パイプラインと定め着手前に全ての工程を確定させる","全ファイルを対象に単一プロンプトでテスト一式をまとめて生成させる"],"oEn":["Have several agents write the same tests and pick the final version by majority vote","Dynamic decomposition: map structure, find high-impact areas, adapt as dependencies surface","Treat test creation as a fixed sequential pipeline with all stages locked in upfront","Generate the entire test suite for all files in a single prompt at once"],"a":1,"e":"開放的タスクは中間発見に基づく動的適応分解が適する。複数エージェントに同じテストを書かせて多数決を取っても探索の役には立たず、固定の直列パイプラインは途中の発見に応じて計画を変えられない。全ファイルを単一プロンプトに載せる方法は注意が薄まる。","eEn":"Open-ended tasks suit dynamic decomposition adapting to discoveries. Having several agents write the same tests and vote does not help exploration, a fixed serial pipeline cannot change the plan as discoveries arrive, and putting every file in a single prompt dilutes attention."},
  {"s":"s4","d":"D2","q":"汎用の analyze_document が誤用される。推奨される設計はどれか。","qEn":"A generic analyze_document is misused. Recommended design?","o":["呼び出し側のプロンプトでanalyze_documentツールの正しい使い方と適切な入力例を毎回具体的に詳しく指示して示す","analyze_documentをそのまま残し入力パラメータにmodeやtypeやformatを追加して要求に応じ振る舞いを条件分岐して切り替える","analyze_documentツールの説明文を大幅に長くし想定される全ユースケースを具体例つきでもれなく詳細に列挙する","extract_data_points・summarize_content・verify_claim_against_source 等、目的別ツールに分割する"],"oEn":["Instruct the caller in the prompt, every time and in concrete detail, on the correct usage and proper input examples for analyze_document","Keep analyze_document and add mode/type/format input parameters so it branches its behavior internally at runtime based on the request","Greatly expand the analyze_document tool's description, enumerating every anticipated use case in exhaustive detail with examples","Split into purpose-specific tools (extract_data_points, summarize_content, verify_claim_against_source)"],"a":3,"e":"汎用ツールは入出力契約が定義された目的別ツールへ分割すると精度・保守性が上がる。プロンプトでの毎回の指示や説明文の長大化は、曖昧な契約のまま使い方を補う対症療法で、modeなどの引数を足して内部で切り替える方法も、入出力の契約が1つのツールに混在したままになる。","eEn":"Split generic tools into purpose-specific ones with defined I/O contracts. Repeated prompt instructions or a lengthened description patch an ambiguous contract symptomatically, and adding mode-style parameters that branch internally still leaves several input/output contracts mixed in one tool."},
  {"s":"s4","d":"D2","q":"18個あったツールを5個に統合したら選択精度は上がったが、ある複合操作だけ失敗が増えた。最も妥当な解釈はどれか。","qEn":"Consolidating 18 tools to 5 raised selection accuracy but one complex operation now fails more. Best interpretation?","o":["ツール数の削減は無関係で失敗はモデルの偶発的なばらつきによる","統合後のツール説明が長すぎてモデルが指示を読み飛ばしている","過度な統合で粒度が粗くなり、その操作に必要な細かい制御が失われた","その操作だけ入力トークンが多くコンテキスト長の上限に達している"],"oEn":["Tool count is irrelevant; the failure is just random variance in the model","The consolidated tool descriptions got too long, so the model skips instructions","Over-consolidation made granularity too coarse, losing fine control for that operation","Only that operation has many input tokens and is hitting the context-length limit"],"a":2,"e":"統合しすぎると粒度が粗くなり柔軟性を失う。その操作だけ粒度を見直す。全体の選択精度は上がっており、悪化したのは特定の複合操作だけである。説明文の長さや入力トークンの上限は全操作に等しく影響するため、その操作だけを説明できない。","eEn":"Over-consolidation coarsens granularity; revisit granularity for that operation. Overall selection accuracy improved and only one compound operation got worse; description length and input token limits affect all operations alike, so they cannot explain that single operation."},
  {"s":"s5","d":"D4","q":"自動コードレビューの偽陽性率が分類で大きく異なる。セキュリティ/正確性8%、性能18%、スタイル/命名52%、ドキュメント48%。多くの開発者が「半分は誤り」として所見を無視し始め、高偽陽性分類が正確な分類への信頼まで損ねている。信頼を回復しつつ改善する最善策はどれか。","qEn":"False positive rates vary widely: security/correctness 8%, performance 18%, style/naming 52%, docs 48%. Developers dismiss findings as 'half wrong,' undermining trust in accurate categories. Best approach to restore trust while improving?","o":["全分類に一律の厳格度低減を適用し全体の偽陽性率を許容できる水準まで一様に下げる","高偽陽性分類（スタイル・命名・ドキュメント）を一時無効化し高精度分類のみ動かしながらプロンプトを改善する","全分類を有効に保ったままfew-shot例を各分類に追加し数週間かけて各分類の偽陽性率を段階的に着実に下げる","全分類を有効なまま残し各所見に確信度スコアを併記して採否の判断を開発者に委ねる"],"oEn":["Apply a uniform strictness reduction across all categories to bring the overall false-positive rate down to an acceptable level","Temporarily disable high-FP categories (style, naming, docs); run only high-precision ones while improving prompts","Keep all categories enabled, add few-shot examples per category, and reduce each category's false-positive rate gradually over several weeks","Keep all categories enabled and attach a confidence score to each finding, leaving the accept/reject decision to developers"],"a":1,"e":"高偽陽性分類は信頼を損ねるため一時無効化し、高精度分類で信頼を保ちながらプロンプトを改善する。確信度表示や一律調整は根本のカテゴリ別偏りに対処しない。全分類に一律の調整をかけると、すでに8%程度と精度の高い分類まで弱めてしまう。全分類を有効のまま数週間かけて改善すると、その間も開発者の不信が続く。","eEn":"High-FP categories erode trust; temporarily disable them and run high-precision ones while improving prompts. Confidence scores or uniform tweaks don't address per-category bias. A uniform adjustment across all categories would also weaken categories that are already precise at about 8%, and improving every category while leaving all enabled prolongs developer distrust in the meantime."},
  {"s":"s5","d":"D4","q":"コスト削減のため、(1)マージ前の必須ブロッキングチェックと(2)夜間生成の技術的負債レポートの両方をMessage Batches APIへ切り替える提案をどう評価するか。","qEn":"To cut costs, a proposal switches both (1) a blocking pre-merge check and (2) an overnight tech-debt report to the Message Batches API. How to evaluate?","o":["両方をバッチ化し処理が完了するまでクライアント側で定期的にポーリングして確認する","技術的負債レポートのみバッチ化し、マージ前チェックはリアルタイムを維持する","両方ともリアルタイム処理のまま維持しコスト削減は別の方法で図る","両方をバッチ化し規定時間を超えたらリアルタイム処理へフォールバックする"],"oEn":["Batch both and poll the client side periodically until processing completes","Use batch only for the tech-debt reports; keep real-time for pre-merge checks","Keep both in real-time processing and pursue cost savings by other means","Batch both, falling back to real-time if a set time limit is exceeded"],"a":1,"e":"BatchesはSLAなし最大24時間で、待つマージ前チェックには不適。夜間レポートには最適。用途ごとに使い分ける。ポーリングで完了を待つ方法はマージ前の開発者を最大24時間待たせうる。規定時間後にリアルタイムへ戻すフォールバックでは、待機時間とバッチ分の費用の両方が無駄になる。","eEn":"Batches has no SLA, up to 24h—unfit for blocking pre-merge checks but ideal for overnight reports. Match API to use case. Polling for completion could leave developers waiting up to 24 hours before merging, and falling back to real-time after a deadline wastes both the wait and the batch cost."},
  {"s":"s5","d":"D3","q":"14ファイルを変更するPRを単一パスでレビューすると深さがばらつき矛盾も生じる。最適な再構成はどれか。","qEn":"Single-pass review of a 14-file PR yields inconsistent depth and contradictions. Best restructuring?","o":["より大きな文脈窓を持つモデルで14ファイル全体を1パスでレビューする","同じレビューを3回独立に実行し2回以上指摘された項目だけ採用する","開発者にPRを3〜4ファイル単位に分割して提出させる運用へ変える","各ファイル個別の局所パス＋別途クロスファイル統合パスに分割する"],"oEn":["Review all 14 files in a single pass using a larger-context-window model","Run the same review three times independently and keep only items flagged in two or more","Change the process so developers submit PRs split into 3-4 files each","Split into per-file local passes plus a separate cross-file integration pass"],"a":3,"e":"注意の希薄化が根本原因。個別パス＋統合パスに分割する。文脈窓拡大は注意の質を解決せず、多数決は実バグを抑制する。開発者にPRを3〜4ファイルに分割させる運用は負担を移すだけで、分割後もファイル間の整合性を見る統合パスが別途必要になる。","eEn":"Attention dilution is the cause; split into per-file plus integration passes. Bigger context doesn't fix attention quality; voting suppresses real bugs. Having developers split the PR into 3-4 files merely shifts the burden onto them, and a separate integration pass is still needed to check consistency across the pieces."},
  {"s":"s5","d":"D4","q":"コードレビューは反復的に動作し、Claudeが変更ファイルを分析後、関連ファイル（import・基底クラス・テスト）をツール呼び出しで取得して文脈を理解してから最終フィードバックを返す。バッチ処理を検討する際の主要な技術的制約はどれか。","qEn":"The review works iteratively: Claude analyzes a file, then requests related files (imports, base classes, tests) via tool calls before final feedback. Considering batch processing, the primary technical constraint?","o":["バッチ処理はリクエストごとの相関IDを持たず結果を対応づけられない","バッチAPIはリクエストパラメータにツール定義を含められない","非同期モデルは処理途中でツールを実行し結果を返す（マルチターン）ことができない","バッチ処理の最大24時間というレイテンシはPRフィードバックの用途には遅すぎる"],"oEn":["Batch processing has no per-request correlation IDs to map results back","The batch API can't include tool definitions in the request parameters","The async model can't execute tools mid-request and return results (multi-turn)","Batch's up-to-24-hour latency is too slow for the PR feedback use case"],"a":2,"e":"このワークフローはツール呼び出しで途中結果を取り込む反復型。Batches APIは単一リクエスト内のマルチターンのツール呼び出しを支援しないため、これが主要制約。相関IDはcustom_idで可能、レイテンシは別の制約、ツール定義自体は含められる。遅延の長さは用途の適否に関わる運用上の問題で、ツールの結果を途中で取り込めないという実行モデル上の制約とは性質が異なる。","eEn":"The workflow is iterative with mid-request tool calls. Batches doesn't support multi-turn tool calling within a request—the primary constraint. custom_id gives correlation; latency is a different issue; tool defs can be included. The length of the latency is an operational suitability issue, different in nature from the execution-model limitation that tool results cannot be incorporated mid-request."},
  {"s":"s5","d":"D3","q":"パイプラインで claude \"...\" を実行するとジョブが無限に待機する。対話入力待ちが原因。正しい対処はどれか。","qEn":"Running claude \"...\" in CI hangs indefinitely waiting for interactive input. Correct fix?","o":["起動コマンドに--batchフラグを付けて非対話で実行する","標準入力を/dev/nullにリダイレクトして入力待ちを回避する","-p（--print）フラグを付けて非対話モードで実行する","環境変数CLAUDE_HEADLESSをtrueに設定して起動する"],"oEn":["Add a --batch flag to run non-interactively","Redirect standard input from /dev/null to avoid the wait","Add -p (--print) for non-interactive mode","Set the CLAUDE_HEADLESS environment variable to true"],"a":2,"e":"-p（--print）は非対話実行の正式手段。他は存在しない機能やUnix回避策。--batchフラグとCLAUDE_HEADLESS環境変数はClaude Codeにない。/dev/nullへのリダイレクトは入力待ちを避ける回避策にすぎず、正式な非対話実行の手段ではない（2026年10月時点）。","eEn":"-p (--print) is the documented non-interactive flag; others are nonexistent features or workarounds. Claude Code has no --batch flag or CLAUDE_HEADLESS variable, and redirecting from /dev/null is only a workaround for the input wait, not the documented way to run non-interactively (as of October 2026)."},
  {"s":"s5","d":"D4","q":"「保守的に判断せよ」「高信頼のみ報告」が精度向上に効かない理由はどれか。","qEn":"Why do 'be conservative'/'report only high-confidence' fail to improve precision?","o":["モデルがこの種の指示を常に無視するよう学習されているから","温度設定と競合して出力が不安定になるから","再現率を犠牲にして見逃しを増やすから","測定不能で具体的なカテゴリ基準に劣るから"],"oEn":["The model has been trained to ignore this kind of instruction","They conflict with the temperature setting and destabilize output","They sacrifice recall and increase missed detections","They're unmeasurable and inferior to specific categorical criteria"],"a":3,"e":"曖昧語は解釈がぶれる。具体的カテゴリ基準（報告/スキップの定義）が精度に効く。モデルが指示を無視するのではなく、何を報告するかの基準が定まらないことが問題で、温度設定とも関係がない。","eEn":"Vague terms vary in interpretation; specific categorical criteria (what to report vs skip) improve precision. The model does not ignore the instruction; the problem is that what to report is left undefined, and it has nothing to do with the temperature setting."},
  {"s":"s5","d":"D4","q":"レビュー出力の一貫性（位置・問題・重大度・修正案）を得る最も効果的な方法はどれか。","qEn":"Most effective way to get consistent review output (location, issue, severity, fix)?","o":["望ましい形式を指示文で長く詳細に説明する","望ましい出力形式を示すfew-shot例を含める","利用可能なツールの数を増やして選択肢を広げる","temperatureを0に近づけて出力を安定させる"],"oEn":["Describe the desired format at length in prose","Include few-shot examples showing the desired output format","Increase the number of available tools to widen options","Bring temperature close to 0 to stabilize the output"],"a":1,"e":"望ましい形式を示すfew-shot例が一貫性に最も効く。形式を文章で長く説明するより、実際の出力例のほうが位置・問題・重大度・修正案の並びを正確に示せる。ツールを増やしてもtemperatureを0に近づけても、形式のばらつきは直接は抑えられない。","eEn":"Few-shot examples of the desired format best drive consistency. A concrete output example shows the order of location, issue, severity, and fix more precisely than a long prose description, and neither adding tools nor lowering temperature directly curbs format variation."},
  {"s":"s5","d":"D4","q":"24時間バッチ処理で30時間SLA（Service Level Agreement）を保証するための投入頻度の目安はどれか。","qEn":"With 24h batch processing, what submission frequency guarantees a 30h SLA (Service Level Agreement)?","o":["30分ごとの投入ウィンドウ","12時間ごとの投入ウィンドウ","概ね4時間ごとの投入ウィンドウ","6時間ごとの投入ウィンドウ"],"oEn":["Every 30 minutes","Every 12 hours or so","Roughly every 4 hours","Every 6 hours or so"],"a":2,"e":"24時間処理＋余裕で30時間SLAを満たすには4時間ごとの投入が目安。12時間ごとでは待ち時間が最大12時間加わり、処理の24時間と合わせて36時間となり30時間を超える。6時間ごとでは合計がちょうど30時間で余裕がなく、30分ごとは頻度が過剰でバッチにまとめる利点が薄れる。","eEn":"24h processing plus margin meets a 30h SLA with ~4-hour windows. With 12-hour windows the wait adds up to 12 hours to the 24-hour processing for 36 hours, exceeding 30; 6-hour windows total exactly 30 hours with no margin, and 30-minute windows are excessively frequent and weaken the benefit of batching."},
  {"s":"s5","d":"D4","q":"バッチ失敗時の最適な対処はどれか。","qEn":"Best handling of batch failures?","o":["バッチ全体を最初から破棄して成功した分も含めた全てのリクエストをまとめて再度submitする","失敗したリクエストは無視し成功したものの結果だけを採用して処理を先へ進める","custom_idで失敗分のみ特定し修正（超過文書のチャンキング等）して再submitする","エラーの内容に関わらず一定回数だけバッチ全体を自動でリトライし続ける"],"oEn":["Discard the whole batch from scratch and resubmit all requests together, including the successful ones","Ignore the failed requests and proceed using only the results from the successful ones","Identify failures by custom_id and resubmit only those with fixes (e.g., chunking oversized docs)","Regardless of the error, keep auto-retrying the entire batch a fixed number of times"],"a":2,"e":"失敗分のみcustom_idで特定し必要な修正を施して再submitする。成功分まで含めて全体を再投入すると費用が無駄になり、失敗分を無視すると結果が欠落する。原因を問わない全体リトライは、文書が長すぎるなど同じ理由で再び失敗する。","eEn":"Use custom_id to resubmit only failed items with appropriate fixes. Resubmitting everything including successes wastes cost, ignoring failures leaves gaps in the results, and retrying the whole batch regardless of cause fails again for the same reason, such as an oversized document."},
  {"s":"s5","d":"D3","q":"レビュー再実行時に同じ指摘を何度も投稿しないための指示はどれか。","qEn":"How to avoid re-posting the same review comments on re-runs?","o":["過去の所見を文脈に含め、新規・未対応のみ報告させる","投稿前にコメントの文面をランダムに言い換えて重複を隠す","実行のたびに全ての指摘を毎回まとめて再投稿する","重複を避けるため以降のレビューを一切行わない"],"oEn":["Include prior findings in context; report only new or unaddressed issues","Randomly reword each comment before posting to hide the duplicates","Re-post every finding in full on each run, all bundled together","To avoid duplicates, skip performing any further reviews altogether"],"a":0,"e":"過去所見を文脈に入れ新規・未対応のみ報告させ重複を防ぐ。コメントを言い換えても重複自体は消えず、毎回すべてを再投稿すれば同じ指摘が積み重なる。以降のレビューを止めると新しい問題を見逃す。","eEn":"Include prior findings; report only new/unaddressed to avoid duplicates. Rephrasing comments does not remove the duplication, reposting everything each run piles up the same findings, and stopping further reviews misses new problems."},
  {"s":"s6","d":"D4","q":"スキーマ準拠の構造化出力を得る最も信頼できる方法はどれか。","qEn":"Most reliable way to get schema-compliant structured output?","o":["プロンプトで「必ずJSON形式で出力して」と明確に依頼する","temperatureを0に設定して出力のぶれをなくす","アシスタント応答をプレフィルして開き括弧から始めさせる","tool_use とJSONスキーマ（構文エラーを排除）"],"oEn":["Clearly ask in the prompt to always output in JSON format","Set temperature to 0 to remove output variability","Prefill the assistant reply to start from an opening brace","tool_use with JSON schemas (eliminates syntax errors)"],"a":3,"e":"tool_use＋JSONスキーマがスキーマ準拠を保証し構文エラーを排除する。プロンプトでの依頼やtemperature 0、プレフィルは、形式を促すだけでスキーマ準拠も構文の正しさも保証しない。","eEn":"tool_use with JSON schemas guarantees compliance and eliminates syntax errors. A prompt request, temperature 0, and prefill only encourage the format and guarantee neither schema compliance nor valid syntax."},
  {"s":"s6","d":"D4","q":"ソース文書に情報がないとき値の捏造を防ぐスキーマ設計はどれか。","qEn":"Schema design to prevent fabrication when info is absent from the source?","o":["該当フィールドをoptional（nullable）にする","全てのフィールドの型をstringに統一して柔軟に受け取る","各フィールドにもっともらしい既定値をあらかじめ設定しておく","全てのフィールドを必須にしてモデルに必ず値を出力させる"],"oEn":["Make the field optional (nullable)","Make all field types a uniform string to receive them flexibly","Preset a plausible default value on each field in advance","Make every field required to force the model to always output a value"],"a":0,"e":"全必須だと捏造して埋める。nullableなら『無い』をnullで表せ捏造を防ぐ。型をstringに統一しても「無い」を表す手段にならず、もっともらしい既定値を設定すると、実在しない値がそのまま出力に混入する。","eEn":"All-required invites fabrication; nullable lets the model return null for missing data. Unifying types to string gives no way to express absence, and setting plausible default values lets non-existent values slip straight into the output."},
  {"s":"s6","d":"D4","q":"tool_useの厳格JSONスキーマが排除できるものとできないものはどれか。","qEn":"What do strict JSON schemas via tool_use eliminate and not?","o":["意味的な誤りは確実に排除できるが構文エラーの方は依然として残る","構文エラーも意味エラーもどちらも防ぐことはできない","構文エラーと意味エラーの両方を完全に排除できる","構文エラーは排除できるが意味エラー（合計不一致等）は防げない"],"oEn":["They reliably eliminate semantic errors, but syntax errors still remain","They can prevent neither syntax errors nor semantic errors","They completely eliminate both syntax errors and semantic errors","Eliminate syntax errors but not semantic errors (e.g., totals that don't sum)"],"a":3,"e":"スキーマは構文を排除するが、合計不一致等の意味エラーは別途検証が要る。意味的な誤りを確実に排除できるという説明は逆で、スキーマが保証するのは形の正しさまでである。両方を完全に排除できる、あるいはどちらも防げないという説明も誤りである。","eEn":"Schemas remove syntax errors; semantic errors need separate validation. The claim that semantic errors can be reliably eliminated is backwards, as a schema guarantees only well-formedness, and claims that it removes both or neither kind are also wrong."},
  {"s":"s6","d":"D4","q":"検証失敗時に再試行で自己修正を導く最適な方法はどれか。","qEn":"Best way to guide self-correction on validation failure?","o":["会話履歴を全て消去し文脈をリセットしてから再送する","temperatureを上げて出力の多様性を高めてから再送する","全く同じプロンプトを変更せずにそのまま繰り返し再送する","原文書・失敗した抽出・具体的な検証エラーを添えて再要求する"],"oEn":["Clear the entire conversation history to reset context, then resend","Raise the temperature to boost output diversity before resending the request","Resend the exact same prompt without any changes and keep retrying it as-is","Resend with the original doc, the failed extraction, and the specific validation error"],"a":3,"e":"検証エラーを具体的に添えた再要求が自己修正を導く。履歴を消すと失敗の手掛かりも失われ、同じプロンプトの繰り返しでは同じ誤りが再現しやすい。temperatureを上げても誤りの原因は伝わらない。","eEn":"Re-request with specific validation errors to guide correction. Clearing the history discards the clues about the failure, repeating the same prompt tends to reproduce the same error, and raising temperature does not convey what went wrong."},
  {"s":"s6","d":"D4","q":"リトライが無効なケースはどれか。","qEn":"When are retries ineffective?","o":["必要な情報がソース文書に存在しないとき","JSONの構造が壊れているとき","値がenumの範囲外になったとき","抽出した結果の形式が想定と一致しないとき"],"oEn":["When the required info is absent from the source","When the returned JSON structure is broken","When a value falls outside the enum range","When the extracted output's format doesn't match expectations"],"a":0,"e":"情報がソースに無い場合リトライは無効。形式・構造エラーは解決しうる。JSONの構造崩れ、enum範囲外、形式の不一致は、エラーを添えた再試行で出力を直せる。情報そのものが無い場合だけ、再試行しても出力が改善しない。","eEn":"Retries fail when info is absent; format/structural errors are fixable. Broken JSON structure, out-of-range enum values, and format mismatches can be fixed by retrying with the error attached; only when the information itself is absent does retrying not improve the output."},
  {"s":"s6","d":"D4","q":"合計値の不整合を検出する自己修正検証フローはどれか。","qEn":"Self-correction flow to detect total mismatches?","o":["calculated_totalのみを抽出し明細から合計を毎回計算し直す","stated_totalのみを抽出し記載された値を唯一の正しい合計として無検証でそのまま採用する","temperatureを下げることで合計値の計算精度そのものを引き上げる","calculated_total と stated_total を両方抽出して差異をフラグする"],"oEn":["Extract only calculated_total, recomputing the sum from line items each time","Extract only stated_total and accept it, unverified, as the one correct sum","Lower the temperature to raise the accuracy of the total's computation itself","Extract both calculated_total and stated_total and flag discrepancies"],"a":3,"e":"両値を併記し差異をフラグ。conflict_detectedブール等も有効。calculated_totalだけに頼ると記載値との食い違いに気づけず、stated_totalを無検証で採用すると誤った合計がそのまま通る。","eEn":"Extract both and flag discrepancies; conflict_detected booleans also help. Relying only on calculated_total hides any mismatch with the stated value, and accepting stated_total unverified lets a wrong total pass through."},
  {"s":"s6","d":"D4","q":"拡張可能なカテゴリ分類を実現しつつ未知も取りこぼさないenum設計はどれか。","qEn":"Enum design for extensible categorization without missing unknowns?","o":["未知の値は既存のenumの中で最も近いカテゴリとして自動的に丸め込んで扱う","カテゴリを数値コードのみで表現しenumそのものは一切定義しない設計にする","enumは使わず全てのカテゴリを制約のない自由記述のテキストとしてモデルから受け取る設計にする","enumに \"other\" + detail文字列を併設し、未知は other+説明で受ける"],"oEn":["Round unknown values to the nearest existing enum category automatically","Represent categories with numeric codes only and define no enum whatsoever","Use no enum at all and take every category as unconstrained free-text from the model","Add \"other\" + a detail string; capture unknowns as other+explanation"],"a":3,"e":"許可値で縛りつつotherとdetailで未知に対応する。未知の値を最も近いenumに丸めると誤分類が黙って混ざる。全て自由記述にすると値が揺れ、スキーマで縛る意味がなくなる。","eEn":"Constrain with enum while handling unknowns via other+detail. Rounding an unknown value to the nearest enum member silently introduces misclassification, and fully free-text output drops the constraint that keeps values consistent."},
  {"s":"s6","d":"D5","q":"全体精度97%だが特定の文書型・フィールドで事故が頻発する懸念がある。最適な検証はどれか。","qEn":"97% overall accuracy but specific doc types/fields fail often. Best validation?","o":["文書型・フィールド別に層化抽出しセグメントごとの精度を測る","評価用のサンプル件数を倍に増やしてから全体精度をもう一度測定し直す","合格とみなす精度の閾値を95%から98%へ引き上げる","全体の平均精度をさらに引き上げるようプロンプトを調整する"],"oEn":["Stratified sampling by doc type/field to measure per-segment accuracy","Double the evaluation sample size and re-measure the overall accuracy again","Raise the passing accuracy threshold from 95% to 98%","Tune the prompt to push the average overall accuracy even higher"],"a":0,"e":"集計精度は特定セグメントの低精度を隠す。層化抽出で弱点を露見させる。サンプル数を倍にしても閾値を98%に上げても測るのは全体精度のままで、セグメント別の欠陥は見えない。","eEn":"Aggregate accuracy masks weak segments; stratified sampling reveals them. Doubling the sample or raising the threshold to 98% still measures only the aggregate, so segment-level failures stay hidden."},
  {"s":"s6","d":"D5","q":"高信頼抽出を自動化する前に確認すべきことはどれか。","qEn":"What to verify before automating high-confidence extractions?","o":["1件あたりの処理コストが予算内に収まるかどうか","全体の平均精度が設定した目標値を上回っているかどうかだけ","文書型・フィールドセグメント別に精度が一貫しているか","1件あたりの処理速度が十分に速いかどうか"],"oEn":["Whether the per-item processing cost stays within budget","Only whether the overall average accuracy exceeds the target","Whether accuracy is consistent across doc types and field segments","Whether the per-item processing speed is fast enough"],"a":2,"e":"自動化前に文書型・フィールド別の一貫性を検証する。全体精度だけでは不十分。コストや処理速度は運用面の指標で、抽出結果が信頼できるかどうかは示さない。","eEn":"Verify per-type/field consistency before automating; overall accuracy isn't enough. Cost and speed are operational metrics and say nothing about whether the extraction is reliable."},
  {"s":"s6","d":"D4","q":"不揃いなソース形式を厳格スキーマで扱うには何を併用するか。","qEn":"To handle inconsistent source formats with a strict schema, what to combine?","o":["temperatureを上げて表現の揺れを吸収させる","プロンプトに形式正規化ルールを併記する","スキーマの制約を緩めて幅広い形式を許容する","利用するツールの数を増やして対応形式を広げる"],"oEn":["Raise the temperature to absorb variation in representation","Include format-normalization rules in the prompt alongside the schema","Loosen the schema constraints to allow a wide range of formats","Increase the number of tools used to widen format coverage"],"a":1,"e":"厳格スキーマと形式正規化ルールを併用し不揃いなソースを扱う。temperatureを上げても出力のばらつきが増えるだけで形式は揃わない。スキーマを緩めると、構造を保証する目的が失われる。","eEn":"Pair the strict schema with format-normalization rules in the prompt. Raising temperature only adds output variance, and loosening the schema gives up the structural guarantee a strict schema provides."}];
// シナリオ演習バンク（英訳・選択肢シャッフル適用済み）
